    {
      "@graph": [
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Adventurer's Pack"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This item is the starter kit for an adventurer, containing the essential items for exploration and survival. The Bulk value is for the entire pack together, but see the descriptions of individual items as necessary. The pack contains the following items: a backpack, a bedroll, 10 pieces of chalk, flint and steel, 50 feet of rope, 2 weeks' rations, soap, 5 torches, and a waterskin.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Adventurer's Pack",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1094",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Final Blade"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A Large or smaller restrained or willing creature can be executed by a final blade. Destruction A final blade can be destroyed via the rare ritual, blunt the final blade.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Final Blade",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Artifact",
            "aonprd:Trait-Death",
            "aonprd:Trait-Evil",
            "aonprd:Trait-Necromancy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=11",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Chain"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Chain",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=114",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Giant Scorpion Venom"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The venom of a giant scorpion is excruciating and its effects are somewhat debilitating. Maximum Duration 6 rounds; Stage 1 2d6 poison damage and enfeebled 1 (1 round); Stage 2 2d8 poison damage and enfeebled 1 (1 round); Stage 3 2d10 poison damage and enfeebled 2 (1 round)",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Giant Scorpion Venom",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Injury",
            "aonprd:Trait-Poison"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=12",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Chalk"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Chalk",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1206",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Silencer"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "One of the more prolifically used devices developed in the infamous Alkenstar Gunworks, these small firearm components are capable of muffling most of the weapons' explosive sound when fired. Without a silencer, a firearm's shot makes a loud and distinctive bang, which can easily be heard through doors and thin walls, but firearms equipped with silencers only make a quiet noise when fired. Due to engineering constraints, a silencer can't be attached to any firearm with the scatter trait. Attaching a silencer to a firearm takes 1 minute, and the silencer is consumed the first time a shot is fired through it.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Silencer",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1207",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tripod"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Tripods are designed for use with kickback weapons, as a way for gunslingers with lower strength to accurately use these more powerful weapons by sacrificing mobility instead. They can be set up and attached to a firearm with a single Interact action using one hand, setting the tripod in your square. I the kickback weapon requires two hands, you can change your grip on the weapon as part of this action. hile this sturdy piece of engineering is in use, you don't take the –2 penalty for firing a kickback weapon, even if your Strength isn't high enough to avoid the penalty. However, you must retrieve the tripod with a single Interact action before you can move the firearm to a different position. Normally, when you're hidden or undetected, you become observed if you do anything except Hide, Sneak, or Step. However, deploying or retrieving a tripod with an Interact action doesn't automatically make you observed, so long as you don't set up or remove the tripod when it's in a spot where creatures can see the tripod itself.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Tripod",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1294",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stanching"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "These symbols close bloody wounds. Armor with this rune reduces the DC of the flat check to end persistent bleed damage from 15 to 12 (7 with particularly effective assistance).",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Stanching",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Necromancy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1343",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cane"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A cane is a straight length of wood with a curved handle, shaped like the tip of a hook. Its simple design helps with balance and only slightly assists with taking weight off the affected opposite leg. The cane is typically 2 to 3 feet long but can be lengthened or shortened as needed.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Cane",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1344",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Crutch"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Crutches come as singles or as a pair depending on how much support you need while walking. A crutch fits under your armpit, and you use your hand and the swing of your arm to move with them.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Crutch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1352",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Prosthesis"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A prosthesis replaces a missing or damaged body part. Typical prostheses include artificial feet, eyes, hands, and limbs, though a basic prosthesis can be designed as a replacement for any body part. Advancements in the prosthetic field mean that even the most basic of prostheses can provide the full range of functionality for a missing body part. A prosthesis has a number of belts or cuffs that keep it attached to your body. You can attach or remove a prosthesis as an Interact action.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Prosthesis",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=14",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Climbing Kit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This satchel includes 50 feet of rope, pulleys, a dozen pitons, a hammer, a grappling hook, and one set of crampons. Climbing kits allow you to attach yourself to the wall you're Climbing, moving half as quickly as usual (minimum 5 feet) but letting you attempt a DC 5 flat check whenever you critically fail to prevent a fall. A single kit has only enough materials for one climber; each climber needs their own kit. If you wear your climbing kit, you can access it as part of a Climb action.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Climbing Kit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=148",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Warleader's Bulwark"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This +1 resilient breastplateis made from shining bronze overlaid with reinforcing golden panels emblazoned with images of loyal soldiers. Wearing this breastplate grants you a commanding aura. You gain a +2 item bonus to Diplomacy checks, but you take a –2 item penalty to Stealth checks to Hide and Sneak and Deception checks to Impersonate. —Command Bravery [one-action] (concentrate);",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Warleader's Bulwark",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=15",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Clothing"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Ordinary clothing is functional with basic tailoring, such as peasant garb, monk's robes, or work clothes. More expensive finery or clothes for specific climes cost more.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Clothing",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=156",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Moonlit Chain"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This +1 silver chain shirt has a collar adorned with stitched images of the phases of the moon. You can see in moonlight as though you had low-light vision. —Dim Sight [one-action] (manipulate);",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "7",
          "aonprd:name": "Moonlit Chain",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=16",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Compass"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A compass helps you Sense Direction or navigate, provided you're in a location with uniform magnetic fields. Without a compass, you take a –2 item penalty to these checks (similar to using a shoddy item).",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Compass",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1671",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cat"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Cat",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1682",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Horse"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Horse",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=17",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cookware"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Cookware",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1716",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Gloaming Arc"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This black +2 striking scimitar reflects light only along its edge, like a thin crescent moon. It grants a +1 item bonus to Stealth while you're holding it, increasing to a +2 item bonus if it has a +3 weapon potency rune. Critical Success The target is unaffected. Success The target is enfeebled 1 for 1 round. Failure The target is enfeebled 2 for 1 minute and drained 1. The target doesn't cast a shadow until it is no longer drained. Critical Failure As failure, but drained 2.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "11",
          "aonprd:name": "Gloaming Arc",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Evocation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Shadow",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=179",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Oil of Potency"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you apply this thick, viscous oil to a weapon or suit of armor, that item immediately becomes magically potent. If the item is a weapon, it temporarily becomes a +1 striking weapon, or, if it's armor, it temporarily becomes +1 resilient armor. This lasts for 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Oil of Potency",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oil"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=18",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Crowbar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When Forcing Open an object that doesn't have an easy grip, a crowbar makes it easier to gain the necessary leverage. Without a crowbar, prying something open takes a –2 item penalty to the Athletics check to Force Open.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Crowbar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1818",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shadewither Key"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This palm-sized talisman hangs on a string of braided bark fibers. It resembles a leaf from some unknown tree similar to oak, carved from jade and then dipped halfway into black ink that looks wet despite feeling completely dry. The gate key was originally created to open the aiudara known as the Seventh Arch. In recent years, corrupting magic has given it additional, stranger powers. When you wear and invest the Shadewither Key, shadows gather around you. You gain a +1 item bonus to Stealth checks. However, this boon comes with great risk: any elf who touches the Shadewither Key is immediately afflicted with the obnubilate curse. —Umbral Double [three-actions] (concentrate, manipulate); Destruction The Shadewither Key’s magic can be destroyed by exposing the artifact to uncontained teleportation energies. If touched to an unlinked or malfunctioning aiudara, the Shadewither Key causes the gate to connect to a new counterpart. If this happens, the key’s magic leaves it, rendering the item useless (as described in the book).",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "22",
          "aonprd:name": "Shadewither Key",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-unique",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Artifact",
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursed",
            "aonprd:Trait-Illusion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Shadow",
            "aonprd:Trait-Unique"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=186",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Healing Potion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A healing potion is a vial of a ruby-red liquid that imparts a tingling sensation as the drinker's wounds heal rapidly. When you drink a healing potion, you regain the listed number of Hit Points.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Healing Potion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Potion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vitality"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=19",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Disguise Kit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This small wooden box contains cosmetics, false facial hair, spirit gum, and a few simple wigs. You usually need a disguise kit to set up a disguise in order to Impersonate someone using the Deception skill. If you've crafted a large number of disguises, you can replenish your cosmetics supply with replacement cosmetics suitable for the type of your disguise kit. You can draw and replace a worn disguise kit as part of the action that uses it.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Disguise Kit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=1973",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bomb Coagulant Alembic"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This apparatus increases the viscosity of the reagents in alchemical bombs, to deadly effect. As a 10-minute activity that has the manipulate trait, you can use a bomb coagulant alembic to distill the contents of one infused alchemical bomb that deals splash damage into a stickier substance. After distilling, the bomb deals no splash damage but instead deals persistent damage equal to and of the same type as its original splash damage. If the bomb already deals persistent damage, distilling increases that damage by the bomb’s original splash damage.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Bomb Coagulant Alembic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemist's Toolkit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This mobile collection of vials and chemicals can be used for simple alchemical tasks. If you wear your alchemist's toolkit, you can draw and replace them as part of the action that uses them.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemist's Toolkit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=21",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Flint and Steel"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Flint and steel are useful in creating a fire if you have the time to catch a spark, though using them is typically too time-consuming to be practical during an encounter. Even in ideal conditions, using flint and steel to light a flame requires using at least 3 actions, and often significantly longer.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Flint and Steel",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=22",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Formula Book (Blank)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A formula book holds the formulas necessary to make items other than the common equipment from this chapter; characters of the alchemist class typically get one for free. Each formula book can hold the formulas for up to 100 different items. Formulas can also appear on parchment sheets, tablets, and almost any other medium; there's no need for you to copy them into a specific book as long as you can keep them on hand to reference them.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Formula Book (Blank)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=23",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Grappling Hook"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can throw a grappling hook with a rope tied to it to make a climb easier. To anchor a grappling hook, make a ranged attack roll using your simple weapon proficiency against a DC depending on the target, typically at least DC 20. This attack has the secret trait. On a success, your hook has a firm hold, but on a critical failure, the hook seems like it will hold but actually falls when you're partway up.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Grappling Hook",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2368",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ursine Avenger Hood"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Note from Nethys: This item is a constituent part of the Ursine Avenger Hood archetype using the archetype artifact rules. A gift passed from warrior to warrior, this cowl is made from a cave bear's skull and fur. Once invested, the wearer gains a +1 item bonus to Nature checks to Command an Animal, which increases to +2 if the animal is a bear. The wearer of the hood feels a constant longing for the wilderness and wild places and takes a –1 item penalty to all Diplomacy checks to Gather Information or Make an Impression if they go more than 5 days inside a large town or city without spending at least 4 hours in the wilderness. Destruction Soak the Ursine Avenger Hood in the blood of a linnorm that is at least 16th level and then burn it in a fire that uses only oak and chrysanthemum as fuel.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Ursine Avenger Hood",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-unique",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Artifact",
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Unique"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2369",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Gelid Shard"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Note from Nethys: This item is a constituent part of the Gelid Shard archetype using the archetype artifact rules. This crystal shard shimmers with its own light even as it seems to draw the heat out of its surroundings. Plunging it into your heart grants you the tranquil lethality of deepest winter, but the more you draw upon its power, the colder your heart grows. Your frozen heart dulls your emotions. When you gain a bonus from an emotion effect, that bonus is reduced by 1, to a minimum of 0. At 10th level, the bonus is reduced by 2. Your dulled emotions make it hard to relate to others; the DC of checks to Make an Impression or Request a favor of other creatures, or to Aid in such attempts, is increased by +2. You gain resistance to cold equal to your level and a +2 status bonus to all saves against emotion effects. Destruction The gelid shard must be left exposed in the Plane of Fire for a week and a day, then smashed with an adamantine hammer by someone who felt true love for the shard's creator.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Gelid Shard",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Arcane",
            "aonprd:Trait-Artifact",
            "aonprd:Trait-Cold",
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=24",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hammer"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Hammer",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=246",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Trident of Lightning"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This item looks like a normal trident carved with Gozren motifs. If thrown without being activated, it wobbles in the air and fails to strike true. When you Activate the trident, the carvings crackle with electricity. You then hurl the trident. It shatters immediately after leaving your hand and unleashes its magic as a 4th-rank lightning bolt originating from your space. The bolt deals 5d12 electricity damage and has a basic Reflex save DC of 25.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Trident of Lightning",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Electricity",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2475",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "The Big Sky"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The Big Sky represents widespread change or liberation. As long as you have The Big Sky invested, you gain a +2 item bonus to Perception checks made while you are flying outside during the day and to any check made to Escape. The bonus increases to +3 if you are at least 17th level.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "The Big Sky",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-unique",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Abjuration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Artifact",
            "aonprd:Trait-Harrow-Court",
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Unique"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=249",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spacious Pouch"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Though it appears to be a cloth bag decorated with panels of richly colored silk or stylish embroidery, a spacious pouch opens into a magical space larger than its outside dimensions. The Bulk held inside the bag doesn't change the Bulk of the spacious pouch itself. The amount of Bulk the bag's extradimensional space can hold depends on its type. You can Interact with the spacious pouch to stow items in it or remove them just like a mundane sack. Though the bag can hold a great amount of material, an object still needs to be able to fit through the opening of the sack to be stored inside. If the bag is overloaded or broken, it ruptures and is ruined, causing the items inside to be lost forever. If it's turned inside out, the items inside spill out unharmed, but the bag must be put right before it can be used again. A living creature placed inside the bag has enough air for 10 minutes before it begins to suffocate, and it can attempt to Escape against a DC of 13. An item inside the bag provides no benefits unless it's retrieved first. An item in the bag can't be detected by magic that detects only things on the same plane.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Spacious Pouch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Extradimensional",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=25",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Healer's Toolkit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This kit of bandages, herbs, and suturing tools is necessary for Medicine checks to Administer First Aid, Treat Disease, Treat Poison, or Treat Wounds. If you wear your healer's toolkit, you can draw and replace them as part of the action that uses them.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Healer's Toolkit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2517",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "The Uprising"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you have The Uprising invested, you gain a +2 item bonus to all saving throws against affects that attempt to control you or restrain you. This item bonus increases to +3 if you are 20th level.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "The Uprising",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-unique",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Artifact",
            "aonprd:Trait-Conjuration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Unique"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=255",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Everlight Crystal"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "An everlight crystal is one of the most common applications of permanent magic. This stone or gem sheds magical bright light constantly in a 20-foot radius (and dim light for the next 20 feet). The light requires no oxygen, generates no heat, and can’t be extinguished, though the crystal can be covered.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Everlight Crystal",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Light",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=26",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Primal Symbol"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Primal spellcasters, especially druids, often wear adornments of natural materials to symbolize their connection to nature, such as rings of woven plants, tokens made from animal parts, or other symbols related to a druidic order or nature philosophy.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Primal Symbol",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=266",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Skeleton Key"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A grinning skull tops the bow of this macabre key. This key can be used in place of a thieves' toolkit when attempting to Pick a Lock, and it grants a +1 item bonus to the Thievery check. If the skeleton key becomes broken due to a critical failure on the check, it works as a normal thieves' toolkit and loses its benefits until repaired. —Loosen Lock [free-action] (manipulate);",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Skeleton Key",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2665",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spore Shepherd's Staff"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This staff is constructed from a magically grown amanita mushroom, with a shaft that spreads into a bright red cap speckled in white. While wielding the staff you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Nature checks to identify fungus.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Spore Shepherd's Staff",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Conjuration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Staff",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2700",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Adventurer's Pack"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This item is the starter kit for an adventurer, containing the essential items for exploration and survival. The Bulk value is for the entire pack together, but see the descriptions of individual items as necessary. The pack contains the following items: a backpack, a bedroll, 10 pieces of chalk, flint and steel, 50 feet of rope, 2 weeks' rations, soap, 5 torches, and a waterskin.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Adventurer's Pack",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2702",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemist's Toolkit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This mobile collection of vials and chemicals can be used for simple alchemical tasks. If you wear your alchemist's toolkit, you can draw and replace them as part of the action that uses them.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemist's Toolkit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2708",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Caltrops"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "These four-pronged metal spikes can damage a creature's feet. You can scatter caltrops in an empty square adjacent to you with an Interact action. The first creature that moves into that square must succeed at a DC 14 Acrobatics check or take 1d4 piercing damage and 1 persistent bleed damage. A creature taking persistent bleed damage from caltrops takes a –5-foot penalty to its Speed. Spending an Interact action to pluck the caltrops free reduces the DC to stop the bleeding. Once a creature takes damage from caltrops, enough are ruined that other creatures moving into the square are safe. Deployed caltrops can be salvaged and reused if no creatures took damage from them. Otherwise, enough are ruined that they can't be salvaged.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Caltrops",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=271",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Adamantine"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Mined from rocks that fell from the heavens, adamantine is one of the hardest metals known. It has a shiny, black appearance, and it is prized for its amazing resiliency and ability to hold an incredibly sharp edge. Adamantine Items Adamantine ItemsHardnessHPBT Thin Items Standard-grade104020 High-grade135226 Items Standard-grade145628 High-grade176834 Structure Standard-grade2811256 High-grade3413668 Rules for Special MaterialsMaterial UsesAdamantine Armor Adamantine Shield Adamantine Weapon",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Adamantine",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Precious",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2713",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Climbing Kit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This satchel includes 50 feet of rope, pulleys, a dozen pitons, a hammer, a grappling hook, and one set of crampons. Climbing kits allow you to attach yourself to the wall you're Climbing, moving half as quickly as usual (minimum 5 feet) but letting you attempt a DC 5 flat check whenever you critically fail to prevent a fall. A single kit has only enough materials for one climber; each climber needs their own kit. If you wear your climbing kit, you can access it as part of a Climb action.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Climbing Kit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2715",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Clothing"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Ordinary clothing is functional with basic tailoring, such as peasant garb, monk's robes, or work clothes. More expensive finery or clothes for specific climes cost more.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Clothing",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2717",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cookware"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Cookware",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2718",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Crowbar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When Forcing Open an object that doesn't have an easy grip, a crowbar makes it easier to gain the necessary leverage. Without a crowbar, prying something open takes a –2 item penalty to the Athletics check to Force Open.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Crowbar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=272",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cold Iron"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Weapons made from cold iron are deadly to demons and fey alike. Cold iron looks like normal iron but is mined from particularly pure sources and shaped with little or no heat. This process is extremely difficult, especially for high-grade cold iron items. Cold Iron Items Cold Iron ItemsHardnessHPBT Thin Items Low-grade52010 Standard-grade72814 High-grade104020 Items Low-grade93618 Standard-grade114422 High-grade145628 Structure Low-grade187236 Standard-grade228844 High-grade2811256 Rules for Special MaterialsMaterial UsesCold Iron Armor Cold Iron Shield Cold Iron Weapon",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Cold Iron",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Precious"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2721",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dueling Cape"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can pull a dueling cape you're wearing from your shoulder and wrap it around your arm with an Interact action. While wielding the dueling cape this way, the cape uses that arm and hand, and you can't hold anything else in that hand. While you do so, you can spend an action to hold it in a protective position, giving you a +1 circumstance bonus to AC and to Deception checks to Feint until the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Dueling Cape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2724",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Formula Book (Blank)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A formula book holds the formulas necessary to make items other than the common equipment from this chapter; characters of the alchemist class typically get one for free. Each formula book can hold the formulas for up to 100 different items. Formulas can also appear on parchment sheets, tablets, and almost any other medium; there's no need for you to copy them into a specific book as long as you can keep them on hand to reference them.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Formula Book (Blank)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2725",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Grappling Hook"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can throw a grappling hook with a rope tied to it to make a climb easier. To anchor a grappling hook, make a ranged attack roll using your simple weapon proficiency against a DC depending on the target, typically at least DC 20. This attack has the secret trait. On a success, your hook has a firm hold, but on a critical failure, the hook seems like it will hold but actually falls when you're partway up.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Grappling Hook",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2727",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Healer's Toolkit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This kit of bandages, herbs, and suturing tools is necessary for Medicine checks to Administer First Aid, Treat Disease, Treat Poison, or Treat Wounds. If you wear your healer's toolkit, you can draw and replace them as part of the action that uses them.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Healer's Toolkit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2730",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lantern"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A lantern sheds bright light and requires 1 pint of oil to function for 6 hours.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Lantern",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2731",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lock"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Picking a poor lock requires two successful DC 15 Thievery checks, a simple lock requires three successful DC 20 Thievery checks, an average lock requires four successes at DC 25, a good lock requires five successes at DC 30, and a superior lock six successes at DC 40.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Lock",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2733",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Manacles"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can manacle someone who is willing or otherwise at your mercy as an exploration activity taking 10–30 seconds depending on the creature's size and how many manacles you apply. A two-legged creature with its legs bound takes a –15-foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds, and a two-handed creature with its wrists bound has to succeed at a DC 5 flat check any time it uses a manipulate action or else that action fails. This DC may be higher depending on how tightly the manacles constrain the hands. A creature bound to a stationary object is immobilized. For creatures with more or fewer limbs, the GM determines what effect manacles have, if any. Freeing a creature from poor manacles requires two successful DC 17 Thievery checks, simple manacles requires three successes at DC 22, average manacles require four successes at DC 27, good manacles require five successes at DC 32, and superior manacles require six successes at DC 42.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Manacles",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2737",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Musical Instrument"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Handheld instruments include bagpipes, a small set of chimes, small drums, fiddles and viols, flutes and recorders, small harps, lutes, trumpets, and similarly sized instruments. The GM might rule that an especially large handheld instrument (like a tuba) has greater Bulk. Heavy instruments such as large drums, a full set of chimes, and keyboard instruments are less portable and generally need to be stationary while being played. A virtuoso instrument is more finely made and gives a +1 item bonus to Performance checks using that instrument.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Musical Instrument",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2745",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Religious Symbol"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This piece of wood or silver is emblazoned with an image representing a deity. Some divine spellcasters, such as clerics, can use a religious symbol to use certain abilities. A religious symbol can be worn on the body on a chain or pin, or can be held.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Religious Symbol",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2747",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Repair Toolkit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A repair toolkit allows you to perform simple repairs while traveling. It contains a portable anvil, tongs, woodworking tools, a whetstone, and oils for conditioning leather and wood. You can use a repair toolkit to Repair items using the Crafting skill. You can draw and replace a worn repair toolkit as part of the action that uses it.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Repair Toolkit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2748",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rope"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Rope",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=275",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dawnsilver"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Dawnsilver is renowned for its lightness, durability, and effectiveness against a range of creatures including devils and werecreatures. It has the same sheen as silver but a slightly lighter hue. Dawnsilver weapons and armor are treated as if they were silver for the purpose of damaging creatures with weakness to silver. A metal item made of dawnsilver is lighter than one made of iron or steel: the item's Bulk is reduced by 1 (reduced to light Bulk if its normal Bulk is 1, with no effect on an item that normally has light Bulk). The Price of an item made of this material is based on the item's normal Bulk, not its reduced Bulk for being made of dawnsilver, but reduce the Bulk before making any further Bulk adjustments for the size of the item. Dawnsilver Dawnsilver ItemsHardnessHPBT Thin Items Standard-grade52010 High-grade83216 Items Standard-grade93618 High-grade124824 Structure Standard-grade187236 High-grade249648 Rules for Special MaterialsMaterial UsesDawnsilver Armor Dawnsilver Shield Dawnsilver Weapon",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Dawnsilver",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Precious",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2753",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spellbook (Blank)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A spellbook holds the written knowledge necessary to learn and prepare various spells, a necessity for wizards (who typically get one for free) and a useful luxury for other spellcasters looking to learn additional spells. Each spellbook can hold up to 100 spells. The Price listed is for a blank spellbook.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Spellbook (Blank)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2758",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Thieves' Toolkit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You need a thieves' toolkit to Pick Locks or Disable Devices (of some types) using the Thievery skill. If your thieves' toolkit is broken, you can repair it by replacing the lock picks with replacement picks appropriate to your toolkit; this doesn't require using the Repair action. If you wear your thieves' toolkit, you can draw and replace it as part of the action that uses it.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Thieves' Toolkit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2760",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Torch"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A torch sheds bright light in a 20-foot radius (and dim light to the next 20 feet) for 1 hour. It can be used as an improvised weapon that deals 1d4 bludgeoning damage plus 1 fire damage.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Torch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2762",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Writing Set"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Using a writing set, you can draft correspondence and scribe scrolls. A set includes stationery, including a variety of paper and parchment, as well as ink, a quill or ink pen, sealing wax, and a simple seal. If you've written a large amount, you can refill your kit with extra ink and paper.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Writing Set",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=277",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Silver"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Silver weapons are a bane to creatures ranging from devils to werewolves. Silver items are less durable than steel items, and low-grade silver items are usually merely silver-plated. Silver Items Silver ItemsHardnessHPBT Thin Items Low-grade3126 Standard-grade52010 High-grade83216 Items Low-grade52010 Standard-grade72814 High-grade104020 Structure Low-grade104020 Standard-grade145628 High-grade208040 Rules for Special MaterialsMaterial UsesSilver Armor Silver Shield Silver Weapon",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Silver",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Precious"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=278",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Armor Potency"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Magic wards deflect attacks. Increase the armor's item bonus to AC by 1. The armor can be etched with one property rune. You can upgrade the armor potency rune already etched on a suit of armor using the normal process for upgrading items and runes.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Armor Potency",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2788",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Energy-Resistant"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "These symbols convey protective forces from the Elemental Planes. You gain resistance 5 to acid, cold, electricity, or fire. The crafter chooses the damage type when creating the rune. Multiple energy-resistant runes can be etched onto a suit of armor; rather than using only the strongest effect, each must provide resistance to a different damage type. For instance, a +2 acid-resistant greater fire-resistant breastplate would give you acid resistance 5 and fire resistance 10.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Energy-Resistant",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=279",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Resilient"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Resilient runes imbue armor with additional protective magic. This grants the wearer a +1 item bonus to saving throws. You can upgrade the resilient rune already etched on a suit of armor using the normal process for upgrading items and runes.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Resilient",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2791",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Raiment"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This armor can be disguised with a mere thought. —Costume Change [one-action] (concentrate);",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Raiment",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Illusion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=280",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Striking"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A striking rune stores destructive magic in the weapon, increasing the weapon damage dice it deals to two instead of one. For instance, a +1 striking dagger would deal 2d4 damage instead of 1d4 damage. You can upgrade the striking rune already etched on a weapon to a stronger version, increasing the values of the existing rune to those of the new rune. The Price of the upgrade is the difference between the two runes' Prices.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Striking",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2804",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Magic Armor"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A suit of magic armor is simply a suit of armor or explorer’s clothing etched with fundamental runes. An armor potency rune increases the armor’s item bonus to AC, and a resilient rune adds an item bonus to saving throws. The Prices here are for all types of armor. You don’t need to adjust the Price from leather armor to full plate or the like. These armors are made of standard materials, not precious materials such as dawnsilver.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Magic Armor",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=281",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Weapon Potency"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Magical enhancements make this weapon strike true. Attack rolls with this weapon gain a +1 item bonus, and the weapon can be etched with one property rune. You can upgrade the weapon potency rune already etched on a weapon to a stronger version, increasing the values of the existing rune to those of the new rune. The Price of the upgrade is the difference between the two runes' prices.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Weapon Potency",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2829",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Striking"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A striking rune stores destructive magic in the weapon, increasing the weapon damage dice it deals to two instead of one. For instance, a +1 striking dagger would deal 2d4 damage instead of 1d4 damage. You can upgrade the striking rune already etched on a weapon to a stronger version, increasing the values of the existing rune to those of the new rune. The Price of the upgrade is the difference between the two runes' Prices.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Striking",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=283",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Energy-Resistant"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "These symbols convey protective forces from the Elemental Planes. You gain resistance 5 to acid, cold, electricity, or fire. The crafter chooses the damage type when creating the rune. Multiple energy-resistant runes can be etched onto a suit of armor; rather than using only the strongest effect, each must provide resistance to a different damage type. For instance, a +2 acid-resistant greater fire-resistant breastplate would give you acid resistance 5 and fire resistance 10.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Energy-Resistant",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2830",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Weapon Potency"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Magical enhancements make this weapon strike true. Attack rolls with this weapon gain a +1 item bonus, and the weapon can be etched with one property rune. You can upgrade the weapon potency rune already etched on a weapon to a stronger version, increasing the values of the existing rune to those of the new rune. The Price of the upgrade is the difference between the two runes' prices.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Weapon Potency",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2834",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Corrosive"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Acid sizzles across the surface of the weapon etched with this rune. When you hit with the weapon, add 1d6 acid damage to the damage dealt. In addition, on a critical hit, the target's armor (if any) takes 3d6 acid damage (before applying Hardness); if the target has a shield raised, the shield takes this damage instead.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Corrosive",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Acid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2838",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Flaming"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A weapon with this rune is empowered by flickering flame. The weapon deals an additional 1d6 fire damage on a successful Strike, plus 1d10 persistent fire damage on a critical hit.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Flaming",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=284",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ethereal"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "An ethereal rune replicates armor on the Ethereal Plane.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "Ethereal",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Conjuration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2840",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ghost Touch"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A weapon etched with this rune can harm creatures without physical form. A ghost touch weapon is particularly effective against incorporeal creatures, which almost always have a specific vulnerability to ghost touch weapons. Incorporeal creatures can touch, hold, and wield ghost touch weapons (unlike most physical objects).",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Ghost Touch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2841",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Grievous"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When your attack roll with this weapon is a critical hit and gains the critical specialization effect, you gain an additional benefit depending on the weapon group. Axe You can damage a third creature, with the same restrictions. Bow The Athletics check to pull the missile free is DC 20. Brawling The target takes a –4 circumstance penalty to its save. Club You can knock the target up to 15 feet away. Crossbow If the target of the critical hit is adjacent to a surface, it gets stuck to that surface by the missile, as the bow critical specialization. Dart The base persistent bleed damage increases to 2d6. Firearm The target takes a –4 circumstance penalty to its save. Flail You move the target 5 feet. You can't move it away from you, but you can move it in another direction of your choice. Hammer You can also knock the target 5 feet away from you. Knife The target takes a –5-foot status penalty to its Speed while it has the persistent bleed damage. Pick The extra damage from the critical specialization effect increases to 4 per weapon damage die. Polearm You can move the target up to 10 feet. Shield You can knock the target up to 10 feet away. Sling The target also takes a –10-foot status penalty to its Speed for 1 round if it fails the save. Spear The clumsy condition lasts for 2 rounds. Sword The target is off-guard until the end of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Grievous",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2847",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shock"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Electric arcs crisscross shock weapons, dealing an extra 1d6 electricity damage on a hit. On a critical hit, electricity arcs out to deal an equal amount of electricity damage to up to two other creatures of your choice within 10 feet of the target.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Shock",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Electricity",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2853",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vorpal"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Originally created as a means of slaying the legendary jabberwock, vorpal weapons prove equally effective against nearly any foe with a head. —Snicker-Snack [reaction] (concentrate, death, incapacitation) ;",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "Vorpal",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2861",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Magic Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A magic weapon is a weapon etched with only fundamental runes. A weapon potency rune gives an item bonus to attack rolls with the weapon, and a striking rune increases the weapon's number of weapon damage dice. The Prices here are for all types of weapons. You don't need to adjust the Price from a club to a greataxe or the like. These weapons are made of standard materials, not precious materials such as cold iron.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Magic Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2870",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Searing Blade"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This +2 greater striking flaming longsword has an ornate brass hilt and a blade shaped like stylized flames. When wielded, the blade projects illumination resembling shimmering firelight, emitting dim light in a 10-foot radius. —Shoot Fire [two-actions] (concentrate, manipulate);",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Searing Blade",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2879",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Antidote"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "An antidote protects you against toxins. Upon drinking an antidote, you gain an item bonus to Fortitude saving throws against poisons for 6 hours.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Antidote",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Elixir",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=288",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shadow"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Armor etched with this rune takes on a hazy black appearance. You gain a +1 item bonus to Stealth checks while wearing the armor.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Shadow",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Shadow"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2880",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Antiplague"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Antiplague can fortify the body's defenses against diseases. Upon drinking an antiplague, you gain an item bonus to Fortitude saving throws against diseases for 24 hours; this applies to your daily save against a disease's progression.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Antiplague",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Elixir",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2887",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Elixir of Life"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Elixirs of life accelerate a living creature's natural healing processes and immune system. Upon drinking this elixir, you regain the listed number of Hit Points and gain an item bonus to saving throws against diseases and poisons for 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Elixir of Life",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Elixir",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=289",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Slick"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This property makes armor slippery, as though it were coated with a thin film of oil. You gain a +1 item bonus to Acrobatics checks to Escape and Squeeze.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Slick",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2915",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Adamantine"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Mined from rocks that fell from the heavens, adamantine is one of the hardest metals known. It has a shiny, black appearance, and it is prized for its amazing resiliency and ability to hold an incredibly sharp edge. Adamantine Items Adamantine ItemsHardnessHPBT Thin Items Standard-grade104020 High-grade135226 Items Standard-grade145628 High-grade176834 Structure Standard-grade2811256 High-grade3413668 Rules for Special MaterialsMaterial UsesAdamantine Armor Adamantine Shield Adamantine Weapon",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Adamantine",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Precious",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2916",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cold Iron"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Weapons made from cold iron are deadly to demons and fey alike. Cold iron looks like normal iron but is mined from particularly pure sources and shaped with little or no heat. This process is extremely difficult, especially for high-grade cold iron items. Cold Iron Items Cold Iron ItemsHardnessHPBT Thin Items Low-grade52010 Standard-grade72814 High-grade104020 Items Low-grade93618 Standard-grade114422 High-grade145628 Structure Low-grade187236 Standard-grade228844 High-grade2811256 Rules for Special MaterialsMaterial UsesCold Iron Armor Cold Iron Shield Cold Iron Weapon",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Cold Iron",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Precious"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2917",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dawnsilver"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Dawnsilver is renowned for its lightness, durability, and effectiveness against a range of creatures including devils and werecreatures. It has the same sheen as silver but a slightly lighter hue. Dawnsilver weapons and armor are treated as if they were silver for the purpose of damaging creatures with weakness to silver. A metal item made of dawnsilver is lighter than one made of iron or steel: the item's Bulk is reduced by 1 (reduced to light Bulk if its normal Bulk is 1, with no effect on an item that normally has light Bulk). The Price of an item made of this material is based on the item's normal Bulk, not its reduced Bulk for being made of dawnsilver, but reduce the Bulk before making any further Bulk adjustments for the size of the item. Dawnsilver Dawnsilver ItemsHardnessHPBT Thin Items Standard-grade52010 High-grade83216 Items Standard-grade93618 High-grade124824 Structure Standard-grade187236 High-grade249648 Rules for Special MaterialsMaterial UsesDawnsilver Armor Dawnsilver Shield Dawnsilver Weapon",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Dawnsilver",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Precious",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2919",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Orichalcum"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The most rare and valuable skymetal, orichalcum is coveted for its incredible time-related magical properties. This dull, coppery metal isn't as physically sturdy as adamantine, but orichalcum's time-bending properties protect it, granting it greater Hardness and Hit Points. If an orichalcum item takes damage but isn't destroyed, it repairs itself completely 24 hours later. Orichalcum Items Orichalcum ItemsHardnessHPBT Thin Items High-grade166432 Items High-grade187236 Structure High-grade3514070 Rules for Special MaterialsMaterial UsesOrichalcum Armor Orichalcum Shield Orichalcum Weapon",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "Orichalcum",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Precious",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2920",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Silver"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Silver weapons are a bane to creatures ranging from devils to werewolves. Silver items are less durable than steel items, and low-grade silver items are usually merely silver-plated. Silver Items Silver ItemsHardnessHPBT Thin Items Low-grade3126 Standard-grade52010 High-grade83216 Items Low-grade52010 Standard-grade72814 High-grade104020 Structure Low-grade104020 Standard-grade145628 High-grade208040 Rules for Special MaterialsMaterial UsesSilver Armor Silver Shield Silver Weapon",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Silver",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Precious"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=294",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vitalizing"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A vitalizing weapon pulses with vital energy, dealing an extra 1d6 persistent vitality damage to undead. On a critical hit, the undead is also enfeebled 1 until the end of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Vitalizing",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=2944",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Invisibility Potion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "An invisibility potion is colorless and oddly lightweight. Upon drinking it, you gain the effects of a 2nd-rank invisibility spell.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Invisibility Potion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Illusion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Potion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=295",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Flaming"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A weapon with this rune is empowered by flickering flame. The weapon deals an additional 1d6 fire damage on a successful Strike, plus 1d10 persistent fire damage on a critical hit.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Flaming",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=297",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ghost Touch"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A weapon etched with this rune can harm creatures without physical form. A ghost touch weapon is particularly effective against incorporeal creatures, which almost always have a specific vulnerability to ghost touch weapons. Incorporeal creatures can touch, hold, and wield ghost touch weapons (unlike most physical objects).",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Ghost Touch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=299",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Holy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A holy weapon commands powerful celestial energy. Strikes made with it gain the holy trait and deal an extra 1d4 spirit damage, or an extra 2d4 against an unholy target. If you are unholy, you are enfeebled 2 while carrying or wielding this weapon. —Holy Healing [reaction] concentrate, healing, vitality;",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "11",
          "aonprd:name": "Holy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Holy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=300",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Keen"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The edges of a keen weapon are preternaturally sharp. Attacks with this weapon are a critical hit on a 19 on the die as long as that result is a success. This property has no effect on a 19 if the result would be a failure.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Keen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=3021",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Everlight Crystal"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "An everlight crystal is one of the most common applications of permanent magic. This stone or gem sheds magical bright light constantly in a 20-foot radius (and dim light for the next 20 feet). The light requires no oxygen, generates no heat, and can’t be extinguished, though the crystal can be covered.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Everlight Crystal",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Light",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=3069",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cloak of Illusions"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This cloak flows, covering and concealing the wearer's body. The cloak allows you to cast figment as an occult innate cantrip. Although naturally a dull gray, while invested the cloak picks up colors and patterns from its surroundings, granting a +1 item bonus to Stealth checks. —Draw Hood [two-actions] (manipulate);",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "7",
          "aonprd:name": "Cloak of Illusions",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=307",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unholy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "An unholy rune instills fiendish power into the etched weapon. Strikes made with it gain the unholy trait and deal an extra 1d4 spirit damage, or an extra 2d4 against a holy target. If you are holy, you are enfeebled 2 while carrying or wielding this weapon. —Unholy Bloodshed [reaction] (concentrate);",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "11",
          "aonprd:name": "Unholy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Unholy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=308",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vorpal"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Originally created as a means of slaying the legendary jabberwock, vorpal weapons prove equally effective against nearly any foe with a head. —Snicker-Snack [reaction] (concentrate, death, incapacitation) ;",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "Vorpal",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=3086",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Handwraps of Mighty Blows"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As you invest these embroidered strips of cloth, you must meditate and slowly wrap them around your hands. These handwraps have weapon runes etched into them to give your unarmed attacks the benefits of those runes, making your unarmed attacks work like magic weapons. For example, +1 striking handwraps of mighty blows would give you a +1 item bonus to attack rolls with your unarmed attacks and increase the damage of your unarmed attacks from one weapon die to two (normally 2d4 instead of 1d4, but if your fists have a different weapon damage die or you have other unarmed attacks, use two of that die size instead). You can upgrade, add, and transfer runes to and from the handwraps just as you would for a weapon, and you can attach talismans to the handwraps. Treat the handwraps as melee weapons of the brawling group with light Bulk for these purposes. Property runes apply only when they would be applicable to the unarmed attack you're using. For example, a property that must be applied to a slashing weapon wouldn't function when you attacked with a fist, but you would gain its benefits if you attacked with a claw or some other slashing unarmed attack. The entries below list the most typical combinations of fundamental runes.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Handwraps of Mighty Blows",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=32",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Manacles"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can manacle someone who is willing or otherwise at your mercy as an exploration activity taking 10–30 seconds depending on the creature's size and how many manacles you apply. A two-legged creature with its legs bound takes a –15-foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds, and a two-handed creature with its wrists bound has to succeed at a DC 5 flat check any time it uses a manipulate action or else that action fails. This DC may be higher depending on how tightly the manacles constrain the hands. A creature bound to a stationary object is immobilized. For creatures with more or fewer limbs, the GM determines what effect manacles have, if any. Freeing a creature from poor manacles requires two successful DC 17 Thievery checks, simple manacles requires three successes at DC 22, average manacles require four successes at DC 27, good manacles require five successes at DC 32, and superior manacles require six successes at DC 42.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Manacles",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=3228",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Animal Pheromones"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "These chemicals convey myriad signals. Many varieties of these alchemical cocktails exist, each tailored for the unique chemistry of a specific type of animal. You can, for example, make wolf pheromones, but not pheromones that affect all animals. The pheromones don’t work on creatures that are similar to the specific kind of animal, but aren’t actually animals—for example, wolf pheromones don’t work on werewolves. When you learn the formula for animal pheromones, you learn the formulas for all common animals. If no animals of a kind are common, you must learn the formula for it separately, and the formula has the same rarity as the least-rare creature of that kind. You Activate animal pheromones by rubbing them on yourself or a creature within reach. The pheromones last for 24 hours or until scrubbed clean with 1 minute of work (consisting of multiple Interact actions). During this time, the pheromones exude a subtle aroma in a 15-foot radius that calms and influences the designated animals. A designated animal that ends its turn within the affected area must attempt a Will saving throw with the following effects. The animal is then temporarily immune to the pheromones for 24 hours. The effect lasts for the duration of the pheromones, even after the creature leaves the affected area. Critical Success The animal is unaffected. It doesn’t necessarily become aware of the pheromones, although intelligent animals might become suspicious if they observe others of their kind being affected. Success The animal’s attitude toward the affected creature improves by one step. If this improves its attitude to at least indifferent, it can’t take hostile actions against the affected creature, though the change in attitude ends as soon as the affected creature takes a hostile action against the animal or its allies. Failure As success, but the attitude increases by two steps. Critical Failure As success, but the attitude increases to helpful.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Animal Pheromones",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Olfactory"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=328",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alarm Snare"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You create an alarm snare by rigging one or more noisy objects to a trip wire or pressure plate. When you create an alarm snare, you designate a range between 100 to 500 feet at which it can be heard. When a Small or larger creature enters the square, the snare makes a noise loud enough that it can be heard by all creatures in the range you designated.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Alarm Snare",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mechanical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Snare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Trap"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=3286",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Acid Flask"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This flask filled with corrosive acid deals 1 acid damage, the listed persistent acid damage, and the listed acid splash damage. Many types grant an item bonus to attack rolls.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Acid Flask",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Acid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Bomb",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Splash"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=3287",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemist's Fire"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Alchemist's fire is a combination of volatile liquids that ignite when exposed to air. Alchemist's fire deals the listed fire damage, persistent fire damage, and splash damage. Many types grant an item bonus to attack rolls.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemist's Fire",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Bomb",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Splash"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=3288",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Blasting Stone"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When this pebble hits a creature or a hard surface, it explodes with a deafening bang. A blasting stone deals the listed sonic damage and sonic splash damage, and each creature within 10 feet of the space in which the stone exploded must succeed at a Fortitude saving throw with the listed DC or be deafened until the end of its next turn. Many types of blasting stones grant an item bonus to attack rolls.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Blasting Stone",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Bomb",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sonic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Splash"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=33",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Material Component Pouch"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This pouch contains material components for those spells that require them. Though the components are used up over time, you can refill spent components during your daily preparations.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Material Component Pouch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=3308",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Elixir of Life"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Elixirs of life accelerate a living creature's natural healing processes and immune system. Upon drinking this elixir, you regain the listed number of Hit Points and gain an item bonus to saving throws against diseases and poisons for 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Elixir of Life",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Elixir",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=3360",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Smoke Ball"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "With a sharp twist of this item, you instantly create a screen of thick, opaque smoke in a burst centered on one corner of your space. All creatures within that area are concealed, and all other creatures are concealed to them. The smoke lasts for 1 minute or until dispersed by a strong wind.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Smoke Ball",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=3585",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Map"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "These are various types of maps used by explorers",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Map",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=359",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Staff of Phantasms"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This ornate metal staff shines with precious inlays of gold. When you Cast a Spell from the staff, the illusory image of something you desire flashes across its surface. While wielding the staff, you gain a +2 status bonus to checks to disbelieve an illusion.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Staff of Phantasms",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Staff"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=362",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Staff of the Magi"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Sigils and runes of ancient and powerful magic cover the iron cladding on this long wooden staff. A staff of the magi is a +3 major striking staff, and when wielding it you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against spells. Voluntarily destroying a staff of the magi unleashes a truly devastating wave of arcane energy that surges out, dissipating with distance. When wielding the staff, you can break it using an Interact action. This releases a 30-foot‑burst magical explosion centered on the staff. This deals 2d10 force damage per charge remaining in the staff (DC 40 basic Reflex save), You automatically critically fail your save. The explosion continues to echo beyond the initial blast zone, dealing half as much damage to creatures beyond 30 feet but within a 60-foot burst. A creature reduced to 0 Hit Points by this damage dies instantly; this is a death effect. Cantrip detect magic, light, mage hand, telekinetic projectile 1st lock 2nd enlarge, glitterdust, invisibility, knock, telekinetic maneuver, web 3rd dispel magic, fireball, lightning bolt 4th invisibility, enlarge, fireball, wall of fire, web 5th cone of cold, passwall, telekinetic haul 6th disintegrate, dispel magic, fireball, lightning bolt 7th cone of cold, passwall, plane shift, wall of fire 8th fireball, mage armor 9th dispel magic, meteor swarm, summon dragon",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Staff of the Magi",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Evocation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Staff"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=37",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Musical Instrument"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Handheld instruments include bagpipes, a small set of chimes, small drums, fiddles and viols, flutes and recorders, small harps, lutes, trumpets, and similarly sized instruments. The GM might rule that an especially large handheld instrument (like a tuba) has greater Bulk. Heavy instruments such as large drums, a full set of chimes, and keyboard instruments are less portable and generally need to be stationary while being played. A virtuoso instrument is more finely made and gives a +1 item bonus to Performance checks using that instrument.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Musical Instrument",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=374",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Adamantine Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Adamantine weapons have a shiny black appearance and cut through lesser items with ease. They treat any object they hit as if it had half as much Hardness as usual, unless the object's Hardness is greater than that of the adamantine weapon.Base MaterialAdamantine",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "11",
          "aonprd:name": "Adamantine Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=375",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cold Iron Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Cold iron weapons deal additional damage to creatures with weakness to cold iron, like demons and fey.Base MaterialCold Iron",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Cold Iron Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=379",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Silver Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Silver weapons deal additional damage to creatures with weakness to silver, like werewolves, and ignore the resistances of some other creatures, like devils.Base MaterialSilver",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Silver Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=399",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Belt of Long Life"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This thick leather belt is engraved with imagery of an ancient tree. You gain 15 temporary Hit Points the first time you invest the belt in a day. When you invest the belt, you either increase your Constitution modifier by 1 or increase it to +4, whichever would give you a higher value. —Call Upon the Ancient Life [one-action] (manipulate);",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "Belt of Long Life",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Apex",
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=4",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Backpack"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A backpack holds up to 4 Bulk of items, and the first 2 Bulk of these items don't count against your Bulk limits. If you're carrying or stowing the pack rather than wearing it on your back, its Bulk is light instead of negligible.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Backpack",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=40",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rations"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Rations",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=407",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Aeon Stone"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times. When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an aeon stone with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again. There are various types of aeon stones, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each aeon stone also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a wayfinder",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Aeon Stone",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Earth",
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=41",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Religious Symbol"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This piece of wood or silver is emblazoned with an image representing a deity. Some divine spellcasters, such as clerics, can use a religious symbol to use certain abilities. A religious symbol can be worn on the body on a chain or pin, or can be held.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Religious Symbol",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=43",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Repair Toolkit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A repair toolkit allows you to perform simple repairs while traveling. It contains a portable anvil, tongs, woodworking tools, a whetstone, and oils for conditioning leather and wood. You can use a repair toolkit to Repair items using the Crafting skill. You can draw and replace a worn repair toolkit as part of the action that uses it.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Repair Toolkit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=44",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rope"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Rope",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=45",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sack"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A sack can hold up to 8 Bulk worth of items. A sack containing 2 Bulk or less can be worn on the body, usually tucked into a belt. You can carry a sack with one hand, but must use two hands to transfer items in and out.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Sack",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=455",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Charm of Resistance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This charm, normally hung from the belt or worn around the neck, grants you resistance 5 against one type of energy damage: acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic. Each charm is crafted to protect against a particular type of energy damage, and its design usually embodies the type of energy it protects the wearer from in some way. For instance, a charm of cold resistance could be carved in the shape of a yeti, whereas a charm of fire resistance would be made from volcanic glass.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Charm of Resistance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=468",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ventriloquist's Ring"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This elegant copper ring has miniature images of songbirds engraved around its circumference. You gain a +1 item bonus to Deception checks. —Throw Voice [two-actions] (manipulate);",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "3",
          "aonprd:name": "Ventriloquist's Ring",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=50",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Signal Whistle"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When sounded, a signal whistle can be heard clearly up to half a mile away across open terrain.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Signal Whistle",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=51",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Snare Kit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This kit contains tools and materials for creating snares. A snare kit allows you to Craft snares using the Crafting skill. You can draw and replace a worn snare kit as part of the action to use it.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Snare Kit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=52",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Soap"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Soap",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=543",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemist's Lab"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You need an alchemist's lab to Craft alchemical items during downtime.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemist's Lab",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=560",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Aluum Charm"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This ornate pendant of brass is adorned with a vibrant blue gemstone. An aluum charm grants control over a particular aluum and lesser influence over other such constructs. As long as you wear an aluum’s linked aluum charm, that aluum follows your verbal commands, including somewhat nuanced orders like “subdue this target” or “strike anyone wearing a blue robe.”",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Aluum Charm",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Enchantment",
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=57",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tent"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Tent",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=58",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Thieves' Toolkit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You need a thieves' toolkit to Pick Locks or Disable Devices (of some types) using the Thievery skill. If your thieves' toolkit is broken, you can repair it by replacing the lock picks with replacement picks appropriate to your toolkit; this doesn't require using the Repair action. If you wear your thieves' toolkit, you can draw and replace it as part of the action that uses it.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Thieves' Toolkit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=6",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Basic Crafter's Book"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This book contains formulas for Crafting the 0-level common items in this chapter.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Basic Crafter's Book",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=60",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Torch"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A torch sheds bright light in a 20-foot radius (and dim light to the next 20 feet) for 1 hour. It can be used as an improvised weapon that deals 1d4 bludgeoning damage plus 1 fire damage.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Torch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=618",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Serithtial"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Perception +28; normal vision and hearing within 60 feet Communication empathy (partner only) Skills Iomedae Lore +29, Religion +26, Zon-Kuthon Lore +29 Int +2, Wis +1, Cha +2 Will +30The legendary blade Serithtial is said to have been forged by Iomedae, goddess of honor, justice, and valor. She is an intelligent +4 major striking holy bastard sword. Although the sword is made of steel, Serithtial is also treated as cold iron and silver, allowing her to deal more damage to certain supernatural creatures. She glows as bright as a torch, but you or Serithtial can suppress or resume this glow as a single action, which has the concentrate trait. In addition, Strikes with Serithtial deal an additional 2d6 damage against creatures that are worshippers of Zon-Kuthon. While wielding Serithtial, against effects created by followers of Zon-Kuthon you gain the benefit of unfettered movement, a +4 status bonus to saves against death and void effects, void resistance 10, and suppress the doomed condition. Serithtial was forged as a bastard sword, and she reverts to this shape when no one wields her, but she can also detect what sort of blade her current wielder prefers and transform into it (choosing from dagger, shortsword, longsword, scimitar, falchion, greatsword, rapier, or bastard sword) using an action, which she does when first held. The wielder can empathically tell Serithtial to transform at any time by using a single action, which has the concentrate trait, after which Serithtial uses an action to transform. Serithtial is willing to work with almost any partner as long as they are dedicated to defeating the great wyrm Kazavon and the forces of Zon-Kuthon. If you ignore those threats and pursue your own agenda instead, before long Serithtial attempts to seize control of your body (DC 45 Will save to resist her control), though she typically remains in control for only long enough to find a more worthy partner. You can attempt a new Will save each day to retake control of your body. —Grace of the Inheritor (concentrate); Destruction If Kazavon or a great wyrm shadow dragon who is a worshipper of Zon-Kuthon uses its dragon breath on Serithtial while she is unattended, the sword melts into a pool of mundane iron.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "23",
          "aonprd:name": "Serithtial",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-unique",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Artifact",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Intelligent",
            "aonprd:Trait-Unique"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=62",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Waterskin"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When it's full, a waterskin contains roughly 1 day's worth of water for a Small or Medium creature.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Waterskin",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=63",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Writing Set"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Using a writing set, you can draft correspondence and scribe scrolls. A set includes stationery, including a variety of paper and parchment, as well as ink, a quill or ink pen, sealing wax, and a simple seal. If you've written a large amount, you can refill your kit with extra ink and paper.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Writing Set",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=680",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dueling Cape"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can pull a dueling cape you're wearing from your shoulder and wrap it around your arm with an Interact action. While wielding the dueling cape this way, the cape uses that arm and hand, and you can't hold anything else in that hand. While you do so, you can spend an action to hold it in a protective position, giving you a +1 circumstance bonus to AC and to Deception checks to Feint until the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Dueling Cape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=687",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ghost Charge"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "These spring-loaded metal canisters contain a mixture of chemicals and salts that drain and disintegrate nearby undead creatures. A ghost charge deals the listed vitality damage and splash damage, though as usual for vitality damage, this damage harms only undead and creatures with void healing. Ghost charges are designed to explode even on contact with a spiritual substance, making them ideal for damaging incorporeal undead. A primary target that takes damage from a ghost charge becomes enfeebled until the start of your next turn. Many types grant an item bonus to attack rolls.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Ghost Charge",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Bomb",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Splash",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vitality"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=7",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bedroll"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Bedroll",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=740",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Predictable Silver Piece"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This seemingly unremarkable, weathered silver coin bears the bust of an unnamed monarch on the face and a majestic bird on the tail. You can toss the coin without activating it, in which case it follows the normal laws of probability. —Cheat Fate [one-action] (manipulate);",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Predictable Silver Piece",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=741",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ready"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A ready rune draws component pieces of a suit of armor toward one another, making it extremely fast to get into. You can don light armor with a ready rune as a single action, or medium or heavy armor with a ready rune as a 2-action activity.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Ready",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=78",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Glue Bomb"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A glue bomb is a harmless explosive mechanism bursting with sticky substances. When you hit a creature with a glue bomb, that creature takes a status penalty to its Speeds for 1 minute. Many types of glue bomb also grant an item bonus to attack rolls. On a critical hit, a creature in contact with a solid surface becomes stuck to the surface and immobilized for 1 round, and a creature flying via wings has its wings tangled, causing it to fall safely to the ground and become unable to Fly again for 1 round. Glue bombs aren't effective when used on a creature that's in water. The target can end any effects by Escaping or spending a total of 3 manipulate actions to carefully remove the sticky substances. These manipulate actions don't have to be consecutive, and other creatures can provide the actions as well.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Glue Bomb",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Bomb",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=80",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Antidote"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "An antidote protects you against toxins. Upon drinking an antidote, you gain an item bonus to Fortitude saving throws against poisons for 6 hours.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Antidote",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Elixir",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=81",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Antiplague"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Antiplague can fortify the body's defenses against diseases. Upon drinking an antiplague, you gain an item bonus to Fortitude saving throws against diseases for 24 hours; this applies to your daily save against a disease's progression.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Antiplague",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Elixir",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=824",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Harrow Deck"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Used by gamblers and seers alike, this deck of cards comes in several varieties. Simple harrow decks are made from low-quality paper and typically have only an icon and a number to signify the suit and alignment. These simple decks are mostly used for games of chance, as the actual image and significance of the cards are irrelevant for such games. Common harrow decks are made from higher-quality paper and feature illustrations—harrow readers typically use these decks. Fine harrow decks are made from a variety of materials, such as high-quality paper, woods, bone, ivory, or metal.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Harrow Deck",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=9",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Caltrops"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "These four-pronged metal spikes can damage a creature's feet. You can scatter caltrops in an empty square adjacent to you with an Interact action. The first creature that moves into that square must succeed at a DC 14 Acrobatics check or take 1d4 piercing damage and 1 persistent bleed damage. A creature taking persistent bleed damage from caltrops takes a –5-foot penalty to its Speed. Spending an Interact action to pluck the caltrops free reduces the DC to stop the bleeding. Once a creature takes damage from caltrops, enough are ruined that other creatures moving into the square are safe. Deployed caltrops can be salvaged and reused if no creatures took damage from them. Otherwise, enough are ruined that they can't be salvaged.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Caltrops",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=91",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Elixir of Life"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Elixirs of life accelerate a living creature's natural healing processes and immune system. Upon drinking this elixir, you regain the listed number of Hit Points and gain an item bonus to saving throws against diseases and poisons for 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Elixir of Life",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Elixir",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=924",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Thresholds of Truth"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Zarmavdian's spellbook, Thresholds of Truth, was once a straightforward treatise on arcane and occult lore containing several useful spells. It's been so heavily annotated, however, that the original text is hard to read. It's clear that Zarmavdian wanted to prevent eldritch creatures from manipulating innocent minds, but his spellbook is a treasure trove for those seeking dangerous or inscrutable lore. The bookseller Morlibint currently keeps this book in his collection at Odd Stories. Thresholds of Truth provides access to the Eldritch Researcher archetype and contains the following spells. Cantrips: chill touch, dancing lights, daze, detect magic, electric arc, ghost sound, mage hand, light, prestidigitation, read aura, shield 1st Level: alarm, charm, color spray, mage armor, magic missile, true strike, unseen servant 2nd Level: comprehend language, dispel magic, false life, glitterdust, web 3rd Level: haste, lightning bolt, locate, paralyze, slow 4th Level: clairvoyance, daydreamer's curse, resilient sphere",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "0",
          "aonprd:name": "Thresholds of Truth",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-unique",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Unique"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=927",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Drover's Band"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This black leather wrist guard has a bright red gem on the inside of the wrist. Faint glyphs and words of domination in Infernal swim inside the gem. Your words become harsh and clipped when you have this magic item invested. Critical Success The target creature is unaffected. Success The target creature is slowed 1 for 1 round as its responses are muddled by your commands. Failure The creature is controlled by you for 1 hour, although it doesn't follow commands that are obviously self-destructive. Critical Failure As failure, but the duration is 1 day.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "7",
          "aonprd:name": "Drover's Band",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Enchantment",
            "aonprd:Trait-Incapacitation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=942",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fulcrum Lenses"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Fulcrum lenses are unique magical crystals that each contain a sliver of Nhimbaloth's essence. They belong to a larger set of lenses created to manipulate or even bind the Empty Death; most of the other lenses are long lost and likely destroyed. The Haruvex family came into possession of four of the lenses, and they knew that bringing them together focused Nhimbaloth's attention in unprecedented and dangerous ways. Belcorra brought all four lenses to the Abomination Vaults with her, intending to install them in Gauntlight for her ultimate revenge upon Absalom. She also created a special receptacle called the Fulcrum Lattice to hold the lenses so that their power could be focused together. She realized the danger of keeping the fulcrum lenses too close together until the right time and spread them out among loyal groups in the Abomination Vaults' lowest levels for safekeeping. Belcorra keeps only the most powerful lens, the Ebon Fulcrum Lens, with her—indeed, as a ghost, it's the only one she can carry. If the heroes can bring the other three lenses to bear against Belcorra, they can draw Nhimbaloth's dread glare to the sorcerer. Despite her loyalty, Belcorra can't hope to keep her spirit intact when Nhimbaloth gazes directly upon it. The fulcrum lenses are more than mere receptacles of Nhimbaloth's essence. Each grants those who use it a fragment of the Great Old One's power.",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Fulcrum Lenses",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-unique",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Enchantment",
            "aonprd:Trait-Invested",
            "aonprd:Trait-Necromancy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Negative",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Unique"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Equipment.aspx?ID=95",
          "@type": "aonprd:Equipment",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Leaper's Elixir"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "This tingly solution increases the elasticity and contraction of your leg muscles. For 1 minute after drinking this elixir, you can High Jump or Long Jump as a single action instead of 2 actions. If you do, you don’t perform the initial Stride (nor do you fail if you don’t Stride 10 feet).",
          "aonprd:itemLevel": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Leaper's Elixir",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Consumable",
            "aonprd:Trait-Elixir"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "@id": "aonprdg:equipment"
    },
    {
      "@graph": [
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=100",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Efficient Alchemy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Thanks to the time you've spent studying and experimenting, you know how to scale your formulas into larger batches that don't require any additional attention. Increase the number of items you can create each day with advanced alchemy to 6 + your Intelligence modifier. In addition, when you Craft alchemical consumables during downtime, you can produce twice as many alchemical items in a single batch without spending additional preparatory time. For instance, if you are creating elixirs of life, you can craft up to eight elixirs in a single batch using downtime, rather than four. This doesn't change the amount of alchemical reagents or other ingredients required to craft each item, nor does it change your rate of progress for days past the base downtime spent.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-advanced-alchemy",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Efficient Alchemy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=102",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Combine Elixirs"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can add the full ingredients of a second elixir to an elixir you make to create a hybrid concoction. You must expend an additional versatile vial to make this combined elixir, and the ingredients must be for an elixir of the same level or lower that you could create with Quick Alchemy. When this combination elixir is consumed, both the constituent elixirs take effect. For example, you can combine two lesser elixirs of life to create a combined elixir that heals twice the normal amount, or you can combine a lesser darkvision elixir with a lesser eagle-eye elixir to both gain darkvision and find secret doors.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Combine Elixirs",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Additive",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=104",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Directional Bombs"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can lob bombs with great force and a precise trajectory to angle the splash in a cone that sprays in a single direction, potentially allowing you to avoid allies and splash deeper into enemy lines. When throwing an alchemical bomb with the splash trait, instead of splashing all squares adjacent to the target, you can create a splash in a 15-foot cone. You choose the cone's direction, but its first square must be a square in the target's space.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Directional Bombs",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=105",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mutant Physique"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Basic mutagens that affect your physical form can bring out the beast within you, turn you nigh invincible, or make your body more elastic. While you're affected by one of the listed mutagens, you get an additional benefit. Bestial Mutagen You gain the mutagen's item bonus to your Intimidation checks. In addition, you increase the damage die size of your claws and jaws by one step, and they gain the deadly d10 trait.Juggernaut Mutagen You gain resistance to all physical damage equal to half your level.Quicksilver Mutagen You can stretch your legs and Step up to 10 feet, and you can squish and compress your body, allowing you to make it through tight spaces as if you were one size smaller, in addition to any effect from Squeezing.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Mutant Physique",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=107",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sticky Bomb"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can mix in a sticky additive to an alchemical bomb to make its contents adhere and continue to deal damage. A creature hit by a sticky bomb also takes persistent damage equal to and of the same type as the bomb's splash damage. If the bomb already deals persistent damage, combine the two amounts. Use the splash damage amount listed in the bomb's stat block, even if you used an ability to change the splash damage dealt.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Sticky Bomb",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Additive",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=109",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Expanded Splash"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can throw bombs at just the right trajectory to create especially large and powerful explosions. When you throw an alchemical bomb and that bomb has the splash trait, you can have the splash damage affect all creatures within 10 feet of the target instead of 5 feet. If you do, you gain a status bonus to the bomb's splash damage equal to your Intelligence modifier. If you have the bomber 5th-level field discovery, this additional damage applies even if you caused your bomb to deal splash damage equal to your Intelligence modifier instead of the normal amount, allowing your bombs to deal splash damage equal to double your Intelligence modifier.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Expanded Splash",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1102",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Magaambyan Attendant Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You devote much of your study to halcyon magic. You gain the ability to cast a single arcane or primal cantrip of your choice, (as is normal for cantrips, it is heightened to a spell level equal to half your level, rounded up). If you weren’t already, you become trained in that tradition’s spell DCs and spell attack rolls, with Intelligence as your spellcasting ability if you choose arcane or Wisdom as your spellcasting ability if you choose primal. Regardless of whether you choose an arcane or primal cantrip, you also either become trained in Arcana or Nature, or an expert in one of those skills in which you were already trained. When you gain this feat, choose to affiliate with the Cascade Bearers, Emerald Boughs, Rain–Scribes, Tempest-Sun Mages, or Uzunjati. This grants you additional feats available to only that branch.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-arcana-or-nature-member-of-the-magaambya-of-attendant-rank",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Magaambyan Attendant Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=111",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Merciful Elixir"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=111#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You mix a special additive into your elixir that calms the drinker's body and mind. The elixir of life attempts to counteract one fear effect or one effect imposing the paralyzed condition on the drinker, using the item's level and a counteract modifier equal to your class DC – 10.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Merciful Elixir",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Additive-2",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=111#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=114",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Invincible Mutagen"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The fortifying additives you brew into your mutagens make your juggernaut form impervious. Whenever you’re affected by a juggernaut mutagen, you gain resistance to all physical damage equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 0).",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Invincible Mutagen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1144",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "False Faith"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Droskar knows you may need to disguise yourself in societies that oppose your faith. After spending 1 hour in prayer to Droskar, you can cast spells using the religious symbol of a different deity as your divine focus, and you can address verbal prayers to that deity. Droskar intercepts your prayers and answers them without the named god knowing. This ability applies to the religious symbol of only one god at a time—making a different religious symbol work in this fashion requires another hour of prayer and causes the old one to cease functioning. You can always use a religious symbol of Droskar without affecting this ability.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worshipper-of-droskar",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "False Faith",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1146",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Crystal Keeper Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can use Arcana, Occultism, Religion, or Society to Decipher Writing by meditating before a crystal, regardless of the type of writing. When you Decipher Writing and roll a critical failure, you get a failure instead, and when you Decipher Writing and roll a success, you get a critical success instead. Additionally, you gain resistance 10 to damage from hazards associated with crystals.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-society-or-elven-lore",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Crystal Keeper Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1147",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Crystal Ward Spells"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your study of crystals and the energies held within a gem’s facets grants you special arcane crystal ward spells, which are a type of focus spell. It costs 1 Focus Point to cast a focus spell, and you start with a focus pool of 1 Focus Point. You refill your focus pool when you make your next daily preparations, and you can regain 1 Focus Point by spending 10 minutes using the Refocus activity to research and memorize the properties of gems. Focus spells are automatically heightened to half your level rounded up. Certain feats can give you more focus spells and increase the size of your focus pool, though your focus pool can never hold more than 3 Focus Points. You gain the electrified crystal ward focus spell, and you are trained in arcane spell attack rolls and spell DCs. Your spellcasting ability is Intelligence.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-crystal-keeper-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Crystal Ward Spells",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1148",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Simple Crystal Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As long as you meditate before a gemstone worth at least 10 gp as part of your daily preparations, you are capable of seeing magic as flowing runes that reveal information about magic objects, and you can scribe a personal rune that represents you. You gain the read aura and sigil cantrips. You cast these cantrips as arcane innate spells at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell level equal to half your level rounded up.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-crystal-keeper-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Simple Crystal Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1149",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Armor Rune Shifter"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn the secrets of armor runes by viewing them through gems and can alter them at your discretion. Once per day when you make your daily preparations, you can focus on a rune’s magical energies through a crystal’s facets to alter a single property rune on one suit of armor in your possession to suppress its normal effects and make it function as a different property rune. You can temporarily alter the rune to function as one of the following runes: energy-resistant, fortification, glamered, invisibility, shadow, or slick. The property rune remains altered until you make your next daily preparations. The armor must meet the prerequisites for the temporary rune, and any other runes that required the suppressed rune are also suppressed while the rune is transformed. The rune is obviously altered, and thus the armor can’t be sold as though it had the temporary rune.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-crystal-keeper-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Armor Rune Shifter",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1150",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Weapon-Rune Shifter"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn how to alter the magic of weapon runes by using a crystal as a focusing component. Once per day during your daily preparations, you can focus on a rune’s magical energies through a crystal’s facets to alter a single property rune on one weapon in your possession to suppress its normal effects and make it function as a different property rune. You can temporarily alter the rune to function as one of the following runes: corrosive, flaming, frost, ghost touch, grievous, returning, shock, thundering, or wounding. The property rune remains altered until you make your next daily preparations. The weapon must meet the prerequisites for the temporary rune, and any other runes that required the suppressed rune are also suppressed while the rune is transformed. The rune is obviously altered, and thus the weapon can’t be sold as though it had the temporary rune.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-crystal-keeper-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Weapon-Rune Shifter",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1151",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Deadly Poison Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your poisons are devastatingly potent. When you apply a simple poison with Poison Weapon, the poison deals 4d4 poison damage instead of 1d4 poison damage. When you apply an injury poison to your weapon, the DC to resist that poison increases by 2, to a maximum of your class DC.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-improved-poison-weapon",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Deadly Poison Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1152",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Pesh Skin"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1152#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your plant form sprouts hundreds of spines, and your blood causes mild hallucinations in creatures exposed to it. Each time a creature touches you, hits you with an unarmed attack, or hits you with a melee weapon attack while adjacent to you, that creature takes 1d6 piercing damage. Increase the damage to 2d6 if the polymorph spell is 8th level or higher, or to 3d6 if it’s 10th level. When an adjacent creature damages you with piercing or slashing damage, it must succeed at a Fortitude save against your class DC or become stupefied 1 (or stupefied 2 on a critical failure) until the end of its next turn. These benefits last until you’re no longer polymorphed into a plant.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Pesh Skin",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Morph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1152#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1153",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shaped Contaminant"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Through a combination of careful manipulation and precise breath control, you can deploy inhaled toxins precisely. When you activate an inhaled poison, you can cause it to fill a 20-foot line that’s 5 feet tall rather than a 10-foot cube. You gain a +3 status bonus to saving throws against inhaled poisons that you activate.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Shaped Contaminant",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1154",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Zephyr Guard Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As a Zephyr Guard, you’re always vigilant against crime and threats to the city’s safety. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Perception checks against attempts to Palm an Object, Steal, or Conceal an Object (including you’re Seeking concealed objects). You become trained in Society and Katapesh Lore; if you were already trained, you become an expert instead.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Zephyr Guard Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1155",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Decry Thief"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you attempt to Demoralize, you can make it harder for the target to flee, in place of the action’s normal effects. Critical Success For 1 round, the target takes a –10-foot status penalty to Speed and a –4 status penalty to Stealth. Success For 1 round, the target takes a –5-foot status penalty to Speed and a –2 status penalty to Stealth.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-zephyr-guard-dedication-trained-in-intimidation",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Decry Thief",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1156",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Know the Beat"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You become trained in your choice of Guild Lore, Legal Lore, Mercantile Lore, or Underworld Lore. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks to Gather Information and to checks made to investigate crimes.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-zephyr-guard-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "3",
          "aonprd:name": "Know the Beat",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1157",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Relentless Disarm"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you succeed, but don’t critically succeed, at a check to Disarm a creature, your circumstance bonus to further checks to Disarm that creature is +4 instead of +2. Other creatures gain only the normal bonus. When you critically succeed at a Disarm check, you can immediately Demoralize your target as a reaction.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-zephyr-guard-dedication-trained-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Relentless Disarm",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1158",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unfazed Assessment"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1158#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have witnessed hundreds of fighting styles and quickly adapt to defend against complicated maneuvers. Choose a creature within 30 feet who you’re aware of, and attempt a Perception check against that target’s Will DC. If you succeed, you size up their fighting style, gaining a +1 circumstance bonus to AC and saving throws against that creature’s attacks (or a +2 circumstance bonus for a critical success). These benefits last until the end of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-zephyr-guard-dedication-expert-in-perception",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Unfazed Assessment",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1158#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1160",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Apex Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can call upon the essence of every individual animal of a particular species to temporarily transform your animal into an exemplar of its kind. You learn the apex companion order spell. Increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Apex Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1161",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Aura of Unbreakable Virtue"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are a paragon of all that is good, your overwhelming aura causing evildoers to cower. All evil creatures within 15 feet of you take a –1 status penalty to checks and DCs that target you or your allies. This penalty is –2 against creatures you have taken an oath against (such as dragons if you have the Dragonslayer Oath feat). You can choose to suppress or resume this aura as an action, which has the concentrate trait.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-tenets-of-good",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Aura of Unbreakable Virtue",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1162",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bloodline Metamorphosis"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have learned to manipulate the innate power of your bloodline and adapt it to your needs. When making your daily preparations, you can swap out a single spell of 9th level or lower for another spell of the same level. You can’t swap out spells granted specifically by your bloodline.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Bloodline Metamorphosis",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1163",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Efficient Alchemy (Paragon)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your daily preparations are particularly efficient and plentiful. When using your infused reagents to create alchemical items during your daily preparations, you make a batch of three of a given item instead of a batch of two, or a batch of four if your field normally lets you create three of that item.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Efficient Alchemy (Paragon)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1164",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Emblazon Divinity"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your sacred etchings imbue objects with power. It takes you only 1 minute to emblazon a symbol using Emblazon Armament, and you can have up to four symbols emblazoned at a time. Each item can still have only one symbol emblazoned upon it, and if you exceed the limit of four, the oldest symbol disappears. These symbols can benefit even those who don’t follow the deity, provided they aren’t directly opposed (as determined by the GM). You can select a different benefit for each emblazoned symbol, chosen from any you have from Emblazon Armament or other feats such as Emblazon Energy or Emblazon Antimagic.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-emblazon-armament",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Emblazon Divinity",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1165",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Enduring Debilitation"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1165#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can make your debilitation last an exceptionally long time. The triggering debilitation lasts for 1 minute instead of until the end of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-debilitating-strike",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Enduring Debilitation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1165#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1166",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Golden Body"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You perfect your body, refining the flex of every muscle and the bend of every joint to maximum efficiency. Your unarmed Strikes gain the deadly d12 trait, and you have fast healing 20, causing you to regain 20 HP at the start of each of your turns provided you have at least 1 HP.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Golden Body",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1168",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Song of the Fallen"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The moving power of your songs can stir the spirits of the dead to rise once more and fight alongside you. You learn the song of the fallen composition spell. Increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-focus-pool",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Song of the Fallen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=117",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Greater Merciful Elixir"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your additives contain panaceas that can remedy a plethora of maladies. When you use Merciful Elixir, your elixir can instead attempt to counteract the blinded, deafened, sickened, or slowed condition.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-merciful-elixir",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Greater Merciful Elixir",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1170",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Superior Sight"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your senses are peerless. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks, and you gain low-light vision. If you already have low-light vision, gain darkvision instead. Furthermore, when you target an enemy, you automatically succeed at the flat check if that enemy is concealed, hidden, or undetected.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Superior Sight",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1187",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Juggler Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You become trained in Performance; if you were already trained in Performance, you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You also gain the Juggle skill feat, even if you don’t meet its prerequisites.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dexterity-14",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Juggler Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1188",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Focused Juggler"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1188#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You continue Juggling until the end of your next turn. Increase the maximum number of items you can Juggle by one.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-juggler-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Focused Juggler",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1188#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1189",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Juggler"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you start to Juggle or add another item to those you are Juggling, you add two items instead of one. Increase the maximum number of items you can Juggle by one.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-performance-juggler-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Juggler",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1190",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reflexive Catch"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1190#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You grab the triggering item. If you are Juggling, you can immediately add the item to the objects you’re Juggling as a free action, which has the concentrate and manipulate traits.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-acrobatics-juggler-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Reflexive Catch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1190#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1191",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lobbed Attack"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1191#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You make a thrown ranged Strike with the required weapon, using the weapon’s normal range increment. This attack doesn’t trigger reactions, and if the target has never seen you use this feat before, the target is flat-footed against this attack.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-performance-juggler-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Lobbed Attack",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1191#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1192",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Opportune Throw"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1192#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You make a thrown ranged Strike with the required weapon against the triggering creature. If you critically succeed and the trigger was a manipulate action, you disrupt that action. This Strike doesn’t count against your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn’t apply to this Strike.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-legendary-in-performance-juggler-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Opportune Throw",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1192#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1193",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Staff Acrobat Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you High Jump, Leap, or Long Jump while wielding your staff, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to any Athletics check required and add 5 feet to the distance you can Leap vertically and horizontally. You can Shove and Trip even if you don’t have a free hand, provided you are wielding your staff. Finally, when you roll a success on a check to Balance while wielding your staff, you get a critical success instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dexterity-16-trained-in-acrobatics-and-athletics-trained-with-at-least-one-of-the-following-weapons-staff-bo-staff-halfling-sling-staff-or-any-weapon-in-the-spear-or-polearm-group-referred-to-in-this-archetype-as-your-staff",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Staff Acrobat Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1194",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bullying Staff"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can attempt to Shove or Trip creatures up to two sizes larger than you. If you have master proficiency with your staff, you can attempt to Shove or Trip creatures up to three sizes larger than you.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-staff-acrobat-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Bullying Staff",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1195",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Staff Sweep"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1195#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You sweep your foes away with your staff. Roll an Athletics check to Shove or Trip, and compare the result to the appropriate DCs of up to two foes, each of whom must be within your reach and no more than 5 feet apart.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-staff-acrobat-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Staff Sweep",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1195#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1196",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Levering Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1196#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Make a Strike with your staff. As long as you don’t critically fail, the target becomes flat-footed and takes a –2 circumstance penalty to its DC against Shove, Trip, and Tumble Through attempts until the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-staff-acrobat-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Levering Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Press",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1196#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1197",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Whirlwind Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1197#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You use your staff as a defensive implement as well as an offensive one. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to AC as long as you remain in this stance.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-staff-acrobat-dedication-expert-proficiency-in-your-staff",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Whirlwind Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1197#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1198",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Pivot Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1198#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You Leap and then Strike using your staff. You gain a circumstance bonus to damage for the Strike equal to twice the number of weapon damage dice. Regardless of whether your Strike hit, you can then attempt to Shove or Trip the target.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-staff-acrobat-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Pivot Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Attack",
            "aonprd:Trait-Open",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1198#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1199",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Juggle"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1199#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can Juggle items and still use your hands between tosses. You can use the Juggle action in several ways. You can start to Juggle with a single stored item, an item you were carrying, or an unattended item within your reach. The item must be of light or negligible Bulk. You Juggle the item until the end of your next turn, unless you use this feat against next turn to continue Juggling (see below). While you are Juggling, you can use this action again to add another item to the Juggle, which must meet all the same requirements. You can Juggle a number of items equal to one more than the number of hands you are using to Juggle. You can also use this action to continue Juggling as long as you aren’t fatigued. When you do, you continue to Juggle until the end of your next turn. If you do not continue Juggling by the end of your turn, you cease Juggling and you drop all the items. You become fatigued if you continue Juggling for more than 10 minutes (60 rounds) within the course of an hour. As long as you’re Juggling fewer than your maximum number of items, you have a free hand. You can wield weapons you are Juggling (but not shields or other items) as long as they can be wielded in one hand. For example, while you Juggle a dagger in one hand and wield a shield in the other, you are wielding the dagger but still have a free hand to Cast a Spell with a material component. Juggling two or more weapons with one hand doesn’t allow you to use feats that require two weapons each held in a different hand.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dexterity-16-trained-in-performance",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Juggle",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1199#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1201",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Animal Trainer Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the services of a young animal companion that travels with you and obeys simple commands as best as it can. This trained animal is trained in Performance instead of the skill listed for its type.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-nature",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Animal Trainer Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1202",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Beast Speaker"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You constantly have the effects of speak with animals as a 2nd-level innate primal spell. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks to Make a Request of animals while this spell is active.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-trainer-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Beast Speaker",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1203",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mature Trained Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your animal companion grows up, becoming a mature animal companion. Increase its proficiency rank in Performance to expert instead of one of the three skill increases for mature. It gains the Mesmerizing Performance advanced maneuver, rather than the normal advanced maneuver for its type. Mesmerizing Performance [one-action] Uncommon Concentrate Emotion Source Pathfinder #152: Legacy of the Lost God pg. 76 Requirements The companion’s last action was a successful Performance check to Perform. The companion maintains its performance to captivate a single target within 30 feet that witnessed its successful performance. The target must attempt a Will save. Success The target is unaffected and temporarily immune for 1 hour Failure The target is fascinated by the companion for its next action and then is temporarily immune for 1 hour. Critical Failure The target is fascinated by the companion for 1 round. While it remains fascinated, it can’t use reactions.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-trainer-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Mature Trained Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1207",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Insistent Command"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you roll a success to Command an Animal, you get a critical success; if you roll a critical failure, you get a failure.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-nature-animal-trainer-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Insistent Command",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1208",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Splendid Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your animal companion continues to develop. It becomes a nimble or savage animal companion (your choice), gaining abilities determined by its type. Increase its proficiency rank in Performance to master instead of Athletics or Acrobatics.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mature-trained-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Splendid Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1209",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Specialized Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The animal companion you gain from the Animal Trainer Dedication feat gains one specialization of your choice. Increase its proficiency rank in Performance to legendary instead of one of the specialization's skill increases.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-splendid-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Specialized Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1213",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ravening's Desperation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your study of the Beast of Gluttondark has taught you how to make do in the most trying of circumstances rather than succumb to weakness. As long as your current Hit Points are less than half your maximum Hit Points, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Survival and Stealth checks. If your current Hit Points are less than a quarter your maximum Hit Points, the circumstance bonus is +2 instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-zevgavizeb-lore",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Ravening's Desperation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1214",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dig Quickly"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1214#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your hands work as effectively as shovels when you need to dig a quick hole. You dig a shallow pit in the square you currently occupy, turning the square into difficult terrain (including for you). In addition, you also kick up a cloud of grit in a direction of your choice. The cloud extinguishes small, unattended, non-magical fires and helps smother the flames on burning creatures located within the cone; creatures in this cone that are taking persistent fire damage can immediately attempt an additional flat DC 15 check to end the persistent damage.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Dig Quickly",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1214#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1215",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Esteemed Visitor"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your polite manners and natural ability to comfort others make it easy for you to break down cultural barriers and earn strangers’ trust. While you are in a settlement, when you roll a critical failure on a Diplomacy check to Gather Information or Make an Impression, you get a failure instead.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Esteemed Visitor",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1216",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Handy with Your Paws"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Crafting checks to Repair non-magical items, and you don’t need a repair kit for such repairs as long as you have any amount of junk, spare parts, or debris at your disposal.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Handy with Your Paws",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1217",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Improvisational Defender"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are always prepared for fights that frequently disrupt seemingly peaceful times. When you use an improvised weapon or a shoddy weapon, you don’t take the –2 item penalty to attack rolls.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Improvisational Defender",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1218",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Scamper Underfoot"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are used to ducking under foes and can scurry around the battlefield with ease. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Acrobatics checks to Tumble Through the spaces of Medium or larger enemies, and the presence of an enemy doesn’t make the squares difficult terrain.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Scamper Underfoot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1219",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shoony Lore"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Growing up in shoony society, you learned the value of honesty, friendship, and hard work, even during trying times. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Diplomacy and Survival. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You also become trained in Shoony Lore.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Shoony Lore",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=122",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Persistent Mutagen"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've trained your physical form to remain stable. Once per day, when you consume an alchemical item with the infused and mutagen traits, you can extend its duration to last until the next time you make your daily preparations instead of its normal duration. Unlike with the normal extension from Extend Elixir, this can exceed the duration of an item created with Quick Alchemy beyond its normal 10-minute limit.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-extend-elixir",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Persistent Mutagen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1220",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Loyal Empath"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have incredible empathy for your friends and family, and you have an innate timing for helping others in distress. You can use the Aid reaction to grant a bonus to another creature’s Will saving throw. As usual for Aid, you need to prepare by using an action on your turn to encourage the creature to bravely withstand the effect.",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Loyal Empath",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1221",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Practiced Paddler"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’re skilled at navigating bogs and marshes, even for a paddler shoony. You gain a swim Speed of 15 feet.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-paddler-shoony",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Practiced Paddler",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1222",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tough Tumbler"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve taken your share of licks while scurrying around the battlefield and know how to defend yourself against opportunistic attackers. Your movement ends only when you critically fail an Acrobatics check to Tumble Through an enemy’s space (or when you don’t have enough Speed to move all the way through its space). You still trigger reactions on a failure to Tumble Through, but you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC against attacks that you trigger in this way.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-scamper-underfoot",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Tough Tumbler",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1223",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Improvisational Warrior"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you use an improvised weapon, you apply the critical specialization of a brawling weapon to it. Depending on the shape and nature of the improvised weapon, your GM might determine another weapon group’s critical specialization is more appropriate.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-improvisational-defender",
          "aonprd:level": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Improvisational Warrior",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1224",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sodbuster"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Years toiling in soil have made you an expert digger. You gain a burrow Speed of 10 feet through loose soil or dirt.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dig-quickly",
          "aonprd:level": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Sodbuster",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1225",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Steadfast Ally"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your presence alone is enough to provide your allies with emotional support. You can use the Aid reaction to grant a bonus to another creature’s Will saving throw even when you haven’t prepared to help.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-loyal-empath",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Steadfast Ally",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1226",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unrivaled Builder"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Building things is like solving a puzzle, and you know how to use anything at your disposal to get the job done. You gain creation as a 5th-level innate primal spell. You must have an equivalent Bulk of material to create an item, such as wood or scrap metal to make a wheelbarrow. You can cast this spell once each day.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-handy-with-your-paws",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Unrivaled Builder",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Shoony"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1227",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Golem Grafter Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your flesh has been specially treated with the same arcane and alchemical processes used to toughen the skin of flesh golems. Increase your maximum Hit Points by an amount equal to your level. You gain resistance to physical damage (except adamantine) equal to your number of class feats from the golem grafter archetype.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-arcana-and-crafting-or-an-ally-with-expert-proficiency-in-those-skills-willing-to-augment-you",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Golem Grafter Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1228",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Accursed Clay Fist"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have replaced one of your forearms with one made of clay and infused with cursed arcane magic. When you make an unarmed Strike with your clay fist and hit, your target takes a –2 status penalty to saving throws against curse effects for 1 hour.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-golem-grafter-dedication-expert-in-unarmed-attacks",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Accursed Clay Fist",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Curse"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1229",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quicken Heartbeat"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1229#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve replaced your heart with one made of animated quicksilver and living adamantine. You reduce your slowed condition by 1. Alternatively, if you are not slowed, you are quickened 1 during your next turn, and can use your extra action to Stride or Strike.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-golem-grafter-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Quicken Heartbeat",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1229#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1230",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Legs of Stone"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain a +2 status bonus to your Fortitude and Reflex DCs against attempts to Shove or Trip you. You can Shove creatures even if you don’t have a hand free. When you successfully Shove a foe, you can Stride away from your opponent (instead of toward it), but you must move the same distance in the opposite direction from where you Shoved it.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-golem-grafter-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Legs of Stone",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1231",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Iron Lung"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your lungs are infused with the resilience of iron. Treat the result of your save against an inhaled poison as one degree of success better than you rolled. Additionally, you gain the following ability. Exhale Poison (arcane, necromancy, poison) [two-actions] Frequency once per hour; Requirement You were within the area of an inhaled poison within the last minute; Effect You sharply exhale the poison that previously surrounded you in a 15-foot cone. Creatures in the area are affected by the poison; the poison's DC and effects are unchanged.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-golem-grafter-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Iron Lung",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1232",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Turpin Rowe Lumberjack Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your logging training has made you intimately familiar with all aspects of forestry, and you have trained extensively to reach around trees and utilize their bulk to your advantage. You become trained in Milling Lore and Forest Lore, or an expert if you were already trained. You can always Take Cover when you are within forest terrain to gain cover, even if you’re not next to an obstacle you can Take Cover behind. In addition, any enemy who gains standard cover from a tree gains only lesser cover against your attacks (or only standard cover, if the enemy otherwise gains greater cover).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-survival",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Turpin Rowe Lumberjack Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1233",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Axe Climber"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you are climbing a wooden surface and have a hatchet or battle axe in each hand, you have a climb Speed equal to half your normal Speed. You must still have both legs available to climb and can’t use either of the axes in combat while climbing. This feat can also be used to climb a surface of ice if you have a light pick in each hand.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-turpin-rowe-lumberjack-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Axe Climber",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1234",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Log Roll"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1234#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You shuffle your feet to dislodge the surface beneath you or otherwise cause your opponent to become unsteady. Attempt an Acrobatics check against the adjacent creature’s Reflex saving throw DC. On a success, the creature falls. On a critical failure, you fall.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-turpin-rowe-lumberjack-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Log Roll",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1234#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1235",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Axe Thrower"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have mastered the weight and balance of a variety of axes and can lob them with ease. Any one-handed axe weapon you wield has the thrown trait with a range of 10 feet. For axes that already have the thrown trait, the range increases by 10 feet. When you critically succeed at an attack roll with a thrown axe weapon, you apply the axe’s critical specialization effect.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-turpin-rowe-lumberjack-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Axe Thrower",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1236",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Widen the Gap"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Once you have penetrated a foe’s defenses, you can home in on the same spot to exploit your opponent’s wound and deal some serious damage. The second time you hit and deal damage with a melee axe Strike to the same opponent or object during your turn, you ignore half of the opponent’s or object’s Hardness, if any. If you hit and deal damage with a melee axe Strike to the same opponent or object a third or fourth time during your turn, you ignore all of its Hardness, if any.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-turpin-rowe-lumberjack-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Widen the Gap",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1240",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Annihilating Swing"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1240#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have embraced brute destructive power. You make a melee Strike that ignores any resistances the target has. If you target a solid unattended object or surface with your Strike, you might automatically destroy it without an attack roll. If you target any object or surface with Hardness 20 or less that isn't a magic item or the effect of a spell, you destroy it. If the target object or surface is a magic item or the effect of a spell, you attempt to counteract it using your attack bonus with the Strike for the counteract check. Your counteract rank is 10th. On a successful counteract check, you destroy the object or surface unless it has Hardness greater than 20, in an artifact, or is similarly difficult to destroy. You destroy up to a 5-foot cube of an object or surface larger than Medium.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Annihilating Swing",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1240#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1241",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Astonishing Explosion"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1241#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your bomb incorporates an explosive spark of wonder that leaves witnesses dumbfounded. Any target hit by your Strike with the bomb is fascinated by you for 1 round. On a critical success, the target is also stunned 1.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Astonishing Explosion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Additive-2",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1241#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1242",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Banishing Blow"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1242#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The erratic teleportation magic you experienced in the Kortos Mounts has taught you a few tricks. You attempt an Athletics check to Shove the fiend that triggered your champion's reaction; on a success, the target can't teleport or summon creatures for 1 minute. On a critical success, the target is also stunned 1 and can't teleport or summon creatures for 1 hour, and if you are on your home plane and the target is a fiend of level 18 or lower from another plane, it is also banished to its home plane. Your multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this attack.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-fiendsbane-oath",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Banishing Blow",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1242#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1243",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Denier of Destruction"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1243#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can manipulate the same energies that the aeon orbs use to sustain life. You cast heal on the triggering target. Instead of its normal effects, the heal spell reduces the triggering damage by an amount equal to the Hit Points a 1-action heal spell of that level would have recovered. As usual, if this reduces the damage to 0, it might also remove additional effects of the triggering attack, such as injury poisons.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-healing-font",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Denier of Destruction",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1243#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1244",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Endurance of the Rooted Tree"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Just as the Vale of Aroden retains light and life despite inhospitable surroundings, you can sustain yourself regardless of your environment. You don't need to eat, drink, or breathe. In addition, you can cast the wholeness of body ki spell almost effortlessly. You can cast it as a free action that triggers at the start of your turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-wholeness-of-body",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Endurance of the Rooted Tree",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1245",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mimic Protections"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "By adopting resonant reflections, you have learned to copy the abilities of other creatures as well. When you use Hunt Prey on a foe within 100 feet, you gain resistance 10 to all damage types that target has resistance or immunity to for as long as the foe remains within 100 feet.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Mimic Protections",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1246",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reclaim Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1246#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have learned to manipulate reflections of magic, similar to the resonant reflections. You reclaim the magic of an ongoing spell, using it reprepare a spell with a duration. You Dismiss a Spell of 4th level or lower that you cast today from a spell slot with at least half its duration remaining, even if that spell can't normally be Dismissed. You can then spend 10 minutes to reprepare the spell in that spell slot, as Reprepare Spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-reprepare-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Reclaim Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1246#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1247",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reflecting Riposte"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1247#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You attempt to counteract the triggering spell using powerful magical techniques observed in the Kortos Mounts. Use your attack roll modifier with your shield or parrying weapon for your counteract check. If you counteract the spell, it is reflected upon the caster. If the spell targeted individual creatures, it targets the caster only. If the spell targeted an area centered on a point, the new area is centered on the caster. If the spell was a cone or line, the cone or line emanates from you toward the caster. If the spell has a save DC, it uses your class DC, and if it requires a spell attack roll, use the same attack roll modifier as the counteract check.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dueling-riposte-mirror-shield-or-twin-riposte",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Reflecting Riposte",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1247#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1248",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ringmaster's Introduction"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1248#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You announce the triggering ally with a litany of their legendary achievements, spurring them to action. The target is quickened this turn and can spend the extra action to Stride, Strike, Demoralize, Feint, or Perform.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Ringmaster's Introduction",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1248#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1249",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Steal Essence"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1249#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Being in the presence of the aeon orbs as they deteriorated has taught you how to siphon energy, and you do so with the required magic item. The DC to steal the properties of a magic item is equal to the DC for the item's level or the normal DC to Steal the item, whichever is higher. The targeted item then becomes temporarily immune for 24 hours. If the object was on a creature, that creature is also temporarily immune (which prevents you from attempting to Steal the Essence of another object on it). If you successfully steal the properties of an item, it loses its magical properties for 24 hours and you can move those properties to a non-magical object of the same general kind (such as moving a hat's properties to another piece of headgear or moving a weapon's properties to another weapon) for the same length of time. If the moved properties are counteracted, they return immediately to the original item. You automatically fail to Steal the Essence of an artifact, cursed item, or similar item.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-legendary-in-thievery-or-master-in-arcana-nature-occultism-or-religion",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Steal Essence",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1249#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=125",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Miracle Worker"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your alchemical mastery can resuscitate the recently slain. You can administer a major or true elixir of life to a creature who has been dead for no more than 2 rounds. When you do, that creature is immediately returned to life with 1 Hit Point and becomes wounded 1.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Miracle Worker",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1250",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tenacious Blood Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1250#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have learned how to invest magic more deeply by witnessing Aroden's works. The triggering blood magic effect lasts for 1 minute instead of 1 round.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Tenacious Blood Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1250#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1251",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Verdant Presence"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1251#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The life-giving properties of the aeon orbs flourish within you. Small plants or fungi magically appear on all surfaces in a 60-foot emanation around you. This life withers after 1 day unless the environment can support it. You can choose one of the following options each time you use this feat. You can cause any number of 5-foot squares in the area to be light undergrowth, which is difficult terrain and provides lesser cover.You can cause a tree or giant mushroom to appear in any unoccupied location in the area; it occupies an entire 5-foot square and provides standard cover. The tree or mushroom has 5 Hardness and 50 Hit Points.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Verdant Presence",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1251#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=127",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Craft Philosopher's Stone"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your research has paid off, culminating in the legendary philosopher's stone. You learn the formula for the philosopher's stone and can add it to your formula book.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Craft Philosopher's Stone",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=128",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mega Bomb"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can add a highly explosive additive to an alchemical bomb to turn it into a mega bomb. Throwing this bomb takes a 2-action activity instead of a Strike. This isn't a Strike, and you don't make an attack roll. The mega bomb explodes in a 30-foot burst within 60 feet. It deals damage as if each creature were the primary target, with a basic Reflex save. On a failed save, a creature also takes any extra effects that affect a primary target (such as off-guard from bottled lightning). Though all targets in the area take splash damage as primary targets, there is no further splash beyond that area.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Mega Bomb",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Additive",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=129",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Perfect Mutagen"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have enhanced the formulas for your mutagens, aligning them perfectly to your physiology. When under the effect of a mutagen you crafted, you do not suffer its drawback.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Perfect Mutagen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=132",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Raging Intimidation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your fury fills your foes with fear. While you are raging, your Demoralize and Scare to Death actions (from the Intimidation skill and an Intimidation skill feat, respectively) gain the rage trait, allowing you to use them while raging. As soon as you meet the prerequisites for the skill feats Intimidating Glare and Scare to Death, you gain these feats.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Raging Intimidation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=134",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sudden Charge"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=134#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With a quick sprint, you dash up to your foe and swing. Stride twice. If you end your movement within melee reach of at least one enemy, you can make a melee Strike against that enemy. You can use Sudden Charge while Burrowing, Climbing, Flying, or Swimming instead of Striding if you have the corresponding movement type.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Sudden Charge",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=134#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=136",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Furious Finish"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=136#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Desperate to finish the fight, you pour all your rage into one final blow. Make a Strike. If it hits, you gain a circumstance bonus to damage equal to the number of rounds remaining in your Rage (maximum 10). After this Strike, your Rage immediately ends, and you are fatigued until you rest for at least 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Furious Finish",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=136#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=137",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "No Escape"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=137#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You keep pace with a retreating foe. Stride up to your Speed, following the enemy and keeping it in reach throughout its movement until it stops moving or you've moved your full Speed. You can use No Escape to Burrow, Climb, Fly, or Swim instead of Stride if you have the corresponding movement type.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "No Escape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=137#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=140",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fast Movement"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your rage is a frenzy of rapid movements. While you are raging, you gain a +10-foot status bonus to your Speed.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Fast Movement",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=144",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Animal Skin"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your proficiency in unarmored defense increases to expert. When you are raging and unarmored, your skin transforms into a thick hide. You gain a +2 item bonus to AC (+3 if you have the greater juggernaut class feature). The thickness of your hide gives you a Dexterity modifier cap to your AC of +3. This item bonus to AC is cumulative with armor potency runes on your explorer's clothing, mystic armor, and bands of force.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-instinct",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Animal Skin",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Morph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1447",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Known Weaknesses"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Whenever you Devise a Stratagem, you can also attempt a check to Recall Knowledge as part of that action before rolling the d20. If you critically succeed at the Recall Knowledge check, you notice a weakness and can convey the information to allies to grant each of them a +1 circumstance bonus to their next attack roll against the subject, as long as their attack is made before the beginning of your next turn. If you choose an attack stratagem, this bonus applies to that attack roll too.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Known Weaknesses",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1449",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "That's Odd"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you enter a new location, such as a room or corridor, you immediately notice one thing out of the ordinary. The GM determines what it is, or whether there's nothing reasonable to pick up, skipping obvious clues that can be easily noticed without a check or specifically looking for them. You learn only that an area or object is suspicious, but not why it's suspicious. For example, if you entered a study with a large bloodstain on the ground, the bloodstain is so obviously suspicious it's evident to you already, so the GM might note that there's something suspicious about the desk drawer instead. You would then need to investigate the drawer further to find out what specifically is out of the ordinary. If you wish, you can Pursue a Lead concerning this detail even if you have Pursed a Lead less than 10 minutes ago. That's Odd doesn't reveal whether creatures are suspicious. You don't typically get any benefit when you leave and come back to a place, though if a major change has happened there and time has passed, the GM might determine that you do.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "That's Odd",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=145",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reactive Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=145#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You lash out at a foe that leaves an opening. Make a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If your attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, you disrupt that action. This Strike doesn't count toward your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Reactive Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=145#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1456",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemical Discoveries"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've devoted extra time in the lab to improve your knowledge of alchemy. You learn the formulas for two alchemical items each time you level up instead of one; these must still be elixirs or tools. The number of versatile vials you can create each day increases by one if you're an expert in Crafting, two if you're a master, or three if you're legendary.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-alchemical-sciences-methodology",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemical Discoveries",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1460",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Scalpel's Point"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your stratagems benefit from your precise knowledge of anatomy. When you critically hit with an attack on which you substituted your attack roll due to Devising a Stratagem, if your attack dealt piercing or slashing damage, you also deal 1d6 persistent bleed damage to your target.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-forensic-medicine-methodology",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Scalpel's Point",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1463",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Predictive Purchase"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have just the thing for the situation. You gain the Prescient Planner and Prescient Consumable feats. When using Prescient Planner, you can pull out the item as a 2-action activity to remove your backpack (or a similar container) and draw the item, rather than taking 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Predictive Purchase",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1464",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Thorough Research"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have comprehensive knowledge in your fields of interest. When you succeed at a Recall Knowledge check, you gain additional information or context. When you critically succeed at a check to Recall Knowledge, you get additional information or context or can ask an additional follow-up question (the GM chooses which).",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Thorough Research",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1475",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Strategic Bypass"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your plans account for your foes' resistances, enabling you to strike a telling blow. When you hit with a Strike on which you substituted your attack roll due to Devising a Stratagem, you ignore an amount of resistance equal to your Intelligence modifier for each resistance that applies against your attack.",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Strategic Bypass",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1477",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Implausible Purchase"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "It seems impossible, but you've analyzed every angle and are able to just keep pulling out exactly the item you need, even in far-flung locations. You can use Prescient Planner even if you have already used it after purchasing goods, and you can use it as a single action instead of a 2-action activity, during which you Interact to draw the item. In addition, five times per day, you can use Prescient Planner to pull out a common consumable item up to 6 levels lower than your level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-predictive-purchase",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Implausible Purchase",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1478",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reconstruct The Scene"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You spend 1 minute surveying a small location (such as a single room) to get an impression of events that occurred there in the last day. This involves moving about the area and studying footprints, spilled drinks or blood, and so forth. You get an indistinct mental impression of significant events that happened there. This gives you clues and details of the past, including the overall events and their time frame, but it’s not a perfect record. This also isn’t enough to identify who was involved in these events if you weren’t already aware the person was there. As determined by the GM, you also pick out various seemingly small details that could serve as important clues, like a memorable weapon someone used for a murder or the type of cloak someone wore when passing through.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Reconstruct The Scene",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1487",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Divine Aegis"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1487#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "A barrier offers protection against other magic but leaves you exposed to divine energy. Until the beginning of your next turn, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against nondivine magical effects, but you also take a –1 circumstance penalty to saves against divine effects.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Divine Aegis",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1487#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1491",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Whispers of Weakness"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1491#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Voices whisper to you how to best lay a creature low. You target one creature within 60 feet; if it has any weaknesses, you learn them, as well as which of its saving throw modifiers is lowest. You also come to understand its movements, gaining a +2 status bonus to your next attack roll (or skill check made as part of an attack action) against that foe before the end of your turn. The target is then temporarily immune for 1 day.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Whispers of Weakness",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1491#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1492",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced Revelation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Divine power reveals greater mysteries to you. You learn the advanced revelation spell associated with your mystery.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-initial-revelation-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced Revelation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1496",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Read Disaster"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You spend 10 minutes and open yourself to the divine mysteries of the world, peering into the most sinister portents of the future. You gain the effects of augury, except you learn only about the dangers ahead; any results of “good” are instead “nothing,” and results of “mixed” are instead “bad.” If you are legendary in Religion, you take only 1 minute to Read Disaster.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Read Disaster",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exploration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Prediction"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1497",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Oracular Warning"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1497#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have a premonition about impending danger that you use to warn your allies. Each ally within 20 feet gains a +2 status bonus to their initiative roll and gains temporary Hit Points equal to half your level, which last for 1 minute. If you are cursebound 2 when you use Oracular Warning, the bonus increases to +3, and if you are cursebound 3, the bonus increases to +4.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Oracular Warning",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1497#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1499",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Surging Might"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1499#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You focus the power of your spell to overcome enemies' resistances. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell, the spell ignores an amount of the target's resistance equal to your level against the following types of damage: spirit, vitality, and void. This applies to all damage the spell deals, including persistent damage and damage caused by an ongoing effect of the spell. This doesn't cause the spell to ignore immunities, only resistances.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Surging Might",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1499#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1501",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Greater Revelation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You unlock deeper revelations hidden within your mystery. You gain your mystery’s greater revelation spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-initial-revelation-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Greater Revelation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1505",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Diverse Mystery"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have broadened your understanding of the divine and can tap into the wonders of a different mystery. Select one revelation spell from a mystery other than your own. You can choose only an initial revelation spell or an advanced revelation spell. This spell gains the cursebound trait for you, and when you cast it, you gain the cursebound 1 effects of its mystery in addition to your normal curse effects. Any ability that lets you use a cursebound ability without increasing the severity of your curse also prevents you from gaining this additional curse effect. You can't cast your chosen revelation spell if any of the following conditions are true: its mystery's curse effects directly conflict with or negate the effects of your own mystery's curse, the curse would have no effect on you (for example, removing an ability from your original mystery that you lack), or if either of these criteria would be met once you finish Casting the Spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Diverse Mystery",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1506",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Portentous Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1506#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your spellcasting is rife with strange lights, mild fumes, and other captivating effects that befuddle your foes. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell, any creature that attempts to use a reaction triggered by your Cast a Spell activity takes a –2 circumstance penalty to attack rolls and skill checks rolled as part of the reaction. In addition, if the spell includes a spell attack or requires a saving throw, creatures you hit or that fail their saves are fascinated with you until the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Portentous Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1506#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1507",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Blaze of Revelation"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1507#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your mind and body can, for a short time and with great peril, surpass the final limits of your curse. For 1 minute, you shed torrential flames, become surrounded by spirits, or otherwise overflow with divine power in a way that suits your mystery. On each of your turns during that time, you can cast one revelation spell without spending Focus Points. At the end of the minute, the durations of any revelation spells you cast during that time end, and you must attempt a DC 40 Fortitude save. Critical Success You aren’t otherwise affected. Success You are drained 2 and can't reduce or remove this condition until your next preparations. Failure You are drained 4 and can't reduce or remove this condition until your next preparations. Critical Failure You die.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Blaze of Revelation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1507#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1508",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Divine Effusion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The power of your mystery surges through you like a font of divine energy, even when your own magic dwindles. Twice per day, you can cast a spell after you've run out of spell slots of the appropriate spell rank; the two spells you cast with this feat must be of different spell ranks.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Divine Effusion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=151",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Animal Rage"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=151#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You transform into your animal. You gain the effects of the 3rd-level animal form spell except you use your own statistics, temporary Hit Points, and unarmed attacks instead of those granted by animal form. You also retain the constant abilities of your gear. If your animal is a frog, your tongue’s reach increases to 15 feet. Dismissing the transformation gains the rage trait.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-instinct",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Animal Rage",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Polymorph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage",
            "aonprd:Trait-Transmutation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=151#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1513",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Disarming Flair"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You knock weapons from the hands of your foes with style. When you Disarm, the action gains the bravado trait.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Disarming Flair",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1517",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Goading Feint"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your tricks make foes overextend their attacks. On a Feint, you can use the following success and critical success effects instead of any other effects you would gain when you Feint; if you do, other abilities that adjust the normal effects of your Feint no longer apply. You can choose whether to use the Goading Feint benefits or the normal benefits each time you Feint a given foe. Critical Success The target takes a –2 circumstance penalty to all attack rolls against you before the end of its next turn. Success The target takes a –2 circumstance penalty to its next attack roll against you before the end of its next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Goading Feint",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1525",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tumble Behind (Swashbuckler)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your tumbling puts your foes on the back foot. When you Tumble Through successfully, the foe you Tumbled Through is off-guard against the next attack you make before the end of your turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Tumble Behind (Swashbuckler)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1527",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Flamboyant Athlete"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your panache allows you to perform incredible feats: climbing, swimming, and leaping far beyond your normal capacity. While you have panache, you gain the following benefits. You gain climb and swim Speeds equal to half your land Speed.The DCs of your High Jumps and Long Jumps decrease by 10. This doesn't combine with other abilities that reduce those DCs.The distance you can move with a vertical Leap increases to 5 feet. Your distance for a horizontal Leap increases to 15 feet if your Speed is at least 15 feet, or to 20 feet if your Speed is at least 30 feet.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Flamboyant Athlete",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1533",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Agile Maneuvers"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your easily maneuver against your foes. Your Disarm, Grapple, Reposition, Shove, and Trip actions have a lower multiple attack penalty. Even if your weapon or unarmed attack doesn't have the agile trait, the penalty is –4 if the action is your second attack on your turn, or –8 if it's your third or subsequent attack. If your weapon or unarmed attack is agile and you have panache, the penalty is reduced further, to –3 if it's the second attack on your turn or –6 if it's the third or subsequent.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Agile Maneuvers",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1544",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Derring-do"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you compound panache with even more derring-do, it somehow tends to work out. When you already have panache, you can roll twice and use the higher result on checks to which the circumstance bonus from stylish combatant applies (Tumble Through and any skill actions with the bravado trait).",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Derring-do",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1546",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reflexive Riposte"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can riposte almost without a thought. At the start of each of your turns when you regain your actions, you gain an additional reaction that can be used only to perform an Opportune Riposte.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-opportune-riposte",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Reflexive Riposte",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1550",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Flamboyant Leap"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1550#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You stylishly leap and deliver a powerful finisher. Make a Leap, High Jump, or Long Jump and attempt one single-action finisher at any point during your jump; the finisher can't be one that includes other movement, such as Mobile Finisher. Immediately after the finisher, you fall to the ground if you're in the air, even if you haven't reached the maximum distance of your jump. If the distance you fall is no more than the height of your jump, you take no damage and land upright. When attempting a High Jump or Long Jump during a Flamboyant Leap, determine the DC using the Long Jump DCs, and increase the maximum distance to double your Speed, rather than just your Speed.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-flamboyant-athlete",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Flamboyant Leap",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1550#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1555",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Felicitous Riposte"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You take advantage of your foe's openings with uncanny odds. When you make an Opportune Riposte, roll twice on the attack roll and take the better result.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Felicitous Riposte",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1562",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cauldron"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can brew magic in your cauldron, creating useful magical concoctions. You can use the Craft activity to create oils and potions. You immediately gain the formulas for four common 1st-level oils or potions. At 4th level and every 2 levels beyond that, you gain the formula for a common oil or potion of that level or lower (a 4th-level potion if you’re 4th level, a 6th-level potion if you’re 6th level, and so on). If you have a familiar, you can have your familiar learn these formulas rather than storing them in a formula book. Your familiar can learn new formulas in the same way it learns new spells, and these formulas are transferred from a slain familiar to a new familiar in the same way spells are. During your daily preparations, you can create one temporary oil or potion using a formula you know. If you have master proficiency in spell DC, you can create a batch of two temporary oils or potions during your daily preparations, and if you have legendary proficiency, you can create a batch of three. Any items you create this way become inert bottles of liquid the next time you make your daily preparations, and any remaining effects of the temporary items end. A temporary oil or potion has no value.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Cauldron",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1565",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Basic Lesson"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your patron grants you a special lesson, revealing a hidden facet of its nature. Choose a basic lesson from the list here. You gain its associated hex, and your familiar learns the associated spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Basic Lesson",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1574",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Greater Lesson"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your patron grants you greater knowledge. Choose a greater or basic lesson from the list here. You gain its associated hex, and your familiar learns the associated spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Greater Lesson",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1578",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Witch’s Bottle"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You spend 10 minutes and 1 Focus Point brewing a special potion containing the power of one of your hexes that targets a creature. A creature that consumes this potion is targeted by the hex. If the hex has a sustained duration and you have cackle, you can cast cackle into the bottle just before you seal it. If you do, the hex's duration is extended as if you had cast cackle the round after the hex was cast (typically this extends the duration by 1 round). Your cackling laugh sounds out when the potion is unsealed. Any potion you create this way loses its power the next time you make your daily preparations. While the potion is in your possession, you can render it inert using a single action that has the concentrate trait. You can't regain the Focus Point you spent to create the potion (or the Focus Point you spent to cast cackle) until the potion is consumed or loses its magic.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-cauldron",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Witch’s Bottle",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1579",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Major Lesson"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your patron grants you even greater secrets. Choose a major, greater, or basic lesson from the list here. You gain its associated hex, and your familiar learns the associated spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Major Lesson",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1583",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hex Focus"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your patron’s teachings have allowed you to achieve a deeper focus. Whenever you Refocus, completely refill your focus pool.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Hex Focus",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=161",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Terrifying Howl"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=161#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You unleash a terrifying howl. Attempt Intimidation checks to Demoralize each enemy within 30 feet: you don't take a penalty if the creature doesn't understand your language. Regardless of the results of your checks, each target is then temporarily immune to Terrifying Howl for 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Terrifying Howl",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=161#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1633",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Martial Performance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your muse has taught you how to handle a wider variety of weapons than most bards, empowering you to effortlessly blend your performance into combat tools. When you have a courageous anthem composition cantrip active, and you damage an enemy with a Strike, the spell’s duration is extended by 1 round. You can extend an individual casting only once in this way. If you gain the rallying anthem or song of strength composition cantrips, you can apply this benefit to those cantrips as well.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warrior-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Martial Performance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=164",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Predator's Pounce"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=164#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You close the distance to your prey in a blur, pouncing on the creature before it can react. You Stride up to your Speed and make a Strike at the end of your movement.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-instinct",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Predator's Pounce",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=164#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1665",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Iron Repercussions"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Disobeying your Iron Command has lasting consequences. If an enemy refuses to kneel to you, you can deal persistent mental damage instead of normal mental damage. You must decide whether the mental damage will be persistent before your enemy chooses whether to kneel or not. The amount of damage is unchanged.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-obedience-cause",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Iron Repercussions",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=170",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Whirlwind Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=170#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You lash out in a blur of motion, attacking all nearby adversaries. Make a melee Strike against each enemy within your melee reach. Each attack counts toward your multiple attack penalty, but you do not increase your penalty until you have made all your attacks.",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Whirlwind Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=170#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1733",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Gorilla Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1733#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You lower yourself to the ground and take an imposing, knuckle-walking stance. While in this stance, the only Strikes you can make are gorilla slam unarmed attacks. These deal 1d8 bludgeoning damage; are in the brawling group; and have the backswing, forceful, grapple, nonlethal, and unarmed traits. While you are in Gorilla Stance, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to Climb, and if you roll a success on an Athletics check to Climb, you get a critical success instead.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Gorilla Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1733#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=179",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bardic Lore"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your studies make you informed on every subject. You are trained in Bardic Lore, a special Lore skill that can be used only to Recall Knowledge, but on any topic. If you have legendary proficiency in Occultism, you gain expert proficiency in Bardic Lore, but you can’t increase your proficiency rank in Bardic Lore by any other means.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-enigma-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Bardic Lore",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=180",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lingering Composition"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "By adding a flourish, you make your compositions last longer. You learn the lingering composition focus spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-maestro-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Lingering Composition",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=181",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reach Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=181#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can extend your spells’ range. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that has a range, increase that spell’s range by 30 feet. As is standard for increasing spell ranges, if the spell normally has a range of touch, you extend its range to 30 feet.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Reach Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=181#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1812",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Entreat with Forebears"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Something about your presence causes creatures of your bloodline to, consciously or not, recognize you as one of their own, and you become inured to their tricks. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy, Deception, and Intimidation checks when interacting with creatures that have the trait corresponding to your bloodline, and you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Perception and saving throws against such creatures. For example, an aberrant bloodline sorcerer would gain this benefit against creatures with the aberration trait. The GM is the final arbiter of which creatures match your bloodline.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-a-bloodline-that-corresponds-with-a-creature-trait",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Entreat with Forebears",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=182",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Versatile Performance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can rely on the grandeur of your performances rather than ordinary social skills. You can use Performance instead of Diplomacy to Make an Impression and instead of Intimidation to Demoralize. You can also use an acting Performance instead of Deception to Impersonate. In addition, you can use your proficiency rank in Performance to meet the prerequisites of skill feats that require a particular proficiency rank in Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-polymath-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Versatile Performance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=185",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Uplifting Overture"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn the uplifting overture composition cantrip, which aids your allies’ skills with the inspiring nature of your performance.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-maestro-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Uplifting Overture",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=190",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Triple Time"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn the triple time composition cantrip, which speeds up you and your allies for a round.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Triple Time",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=1952",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dual-Weapon Reload"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You carry your ammunition in a way that allows you to reload while holding two weapons. While you're wielding two one-handed weapons, each in a different hand, you don't need a free hand to reload a one-handed ranged weapon you're wielding.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dual-weapon-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Dual-Weapon Reload",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=197",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Know-It-All"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you succeed at a check to Recall Knowledge, you gain additional information or context. When you critically succeed at a check to Recall Knowledge, you get additional information or context or can ask an additional follow-up question (the GM chooses which).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bard-enigma-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Know-It-All",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=203",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Allegro"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can quicken your allies with a fast-paced performance. You learn the allegro composition cantrip.",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Allegro",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=206",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Effortless Concentration"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=206#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can maintain a spell with hardly a thought. You immediately gain the effects of the Sustain action, allowing you to extend the duration of one of your active spells.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Effortless Concentration",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Summoner",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=206#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2074",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Snarecrafter Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have studied the art of crafting snares and laying traps, and few have shown more talent in these arts than you. You gain the Snare Crafting feat. When you set a snare, the DC of any saving throw it requires uses the higher of your class DC or the snare's DC. If a snare normally takes 1 minute to Craft, you can Craft it with 3 Interact actions instead. Each day during your daily preparations, you can prepare four snares from your formula book for quick deployment (increasing to six snares if you're a master in Crafting and eight if you're legendary). Snares prepared in this way don't cost you any resources to Craft. When you increase your proficiency rank in Crafting to expert, master, or legendary, add three additional snare formulas to your formula book. The snares must be of your level or lower.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Snarecrafter Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2114",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bon Mot"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2114#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You launch an insightful quip at a foe, distracting them. Choose a foe within 30 feet and roll a Diplomacy check against the target's Will DC. Critical Success The target is distracted and takes a –3 status penalty to Perception and Will saves for 1 minute. The target can end the effect early with a retort to your Bon Mot. This can either be a single action that has the concentrate trait or an appropriate skill action to frame their retort. The GM determines which skill actions qualify, though they must take at least 1 action. Typically, the retort needs to use a linguistic Charisma-based skill action. Success As critical success, but the penalty is –2. Critical Failure Your quip is atrocious. You take the same penalty an enemy would take had you succeeded. This ends after 1 minute or if you issue another Bon Mot and succeed.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-diplomacy",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Bon Mot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2114#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2128",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Forensic Acumen"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You understand principles of forensic medicine, making you better at examining a body to determine the cause of death or injury. You can perform a forensic examination on a body, as described under Recall Knowledge in the Medicine skill, in half the normal amount of time (to a minimum of 5 minutes). If you succeed at your check, you can attempt an immediate check to Recall Knowledge to follow up on something you found, with a +2 circumstance bonus. This check is usually related to the cause of injury or death, such as a Crafting check to identify a poison or weapon used or an additional Medicine check to identify a specific disease. If you prefer, you can instead attempt to Recall Knowledge about the type of creature whose body you examined, using the appropriate skill and gaining the same circumstance bonus. The circumstance bonus increases to +3 if you have master proficiency in Medicine and +4 if you have legendary proficiency.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-medicine",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Forensic Acumen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2139",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "No Cause for Alarm"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2139#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You attempt to reduce panic. Attempt a Diplomacy check, comparing it to the Will DC of creatures in a 10-foot emanation around you who are frightened. Each of them is temporarily immune for 1 hour. Critical Success Reduce the creature's frightened value by 2. Success Reduce the creature's frightened value by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-diplomacy",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "No Cause for Alarm",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2139#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=214",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Deity's Domain"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You embody an aspect of your deity. Choose one of your deity's domains. You gain the domain's initial domain spell as a devotion spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Deity's Domain",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=216",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unimpeded Step"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "With a burst of divine liberation, your ally's movement from your Liberating Step is unaffected by difficult terrain, greater difficult terrain, narrow surfaces, and uneven ground. If you have the exalted reaction benefit, this applies to everyone who Steps.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-liberation-cause",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Unimpeded Step",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2172",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bright Lion Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You become trained in your choice of Deception or Diplomacy and in Mzali Lore; if you were already trained, you become an expert instead. You incorporate enough worship of Walkena in your daily life to avoid suspicion. You typically don't need to Lie or Impersonate to pass yourself off as a worshipper of Walkena. Against careful inspection, you gain a +4 circumstance bonus to Deception checks specifically to pass yourself off as a version of yourself faithful to Walkena.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-member-of-the-bright-lions-not-a-worshipper-of-walkena-trained-in-stealth",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Bright Lion Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=218",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Divine Grace"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=218#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You call upon your deity's grace, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to the save.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Divine Grace",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=218#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=221",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shining Oath"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve sworn an oath to put the undead to rest. You gain the following edict: “You must end the existence of undead you encounter as long as you have a reasonable chance of success; in the unlikely event you find an undead that isn't unholy, you can try to work out a more peaceful way to help it recover from its undead state rather than destroying it in combat, such as helping it complete its unfinished business and find peace.” Your Retributive Strike gains a +4 circumstance bonus to damage against an undead, or +6 if you have master proficiency with the weapon you used. Your Glimpse of Redemption’s resistance against damage from an undead is 7 + your level. If you use Liberating Step triggered by an undead, your ally gains a +4 circumstance bonus to checks granted by your Liberating Step, and the ally can Step twice afterward. You don’t consider undead to be legitimate authorities, even in nations ruled by undead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-tenets-of-good",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Shining Oath",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oath"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=223",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Aura of Courage"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You stand strong in the face of danger and inspire your allies to do the same. Whenever you become frightened, reduce the condition value by 1 (to a minimum of 0). At the end of your turn, each ally in your champion's aura reduces its frightened value by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-champions-aura-holy",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Aura of Courage",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=225",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mercy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your touch soothes the body or mind. You can cast lay on hands targeting a living creature using 2 actions instead of 1. If you do, you can attempt to counteract one condition of your choice affecting the target. When you select this feat, choose one of the following options, which determines the conditions you can choose: Mercy of the Body blinded, dazzled, deafened, enfeebled, sickened; Mercy of Grace clumsy, grabbed, paralyzed; Mercy of the Mind fleeing, frightened, stupefied.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-lay-on-hands",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Mercy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2269",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rain of Embers Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2269#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter the stance of an enraged phoenix, holding your fingers as rigid as deadly talons while moving with quick, flickering gestures that dance with biting flames. The only Strikes you can make are fire talon Strikes. These deal 1d4 fire damage; are in the brawling group; and have the agile, finesse, fire, nonlethal, and unarmed traits. While in Rain of Embers Stance, you gain a +1 status bonus to AC and fire resistance equal to half your level (minimum 1).",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Rain of Embers Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2269#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=227",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Litany Against Wrath"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You excoriate a foe for its wrath against goodly creatures. You can cast the litany against wrath devotion spell. Increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-devotion-spells-tenets-of-good",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Litany Against Wrath",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2277",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ghost Hunter Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have focused your training on hunting and defeating ghosts, spirits, and all manner of haunts. Pick Spirit Lore or Haunt Lore; you become trained in this skill. If you were already trained in both skills, you become trained in a new Lore skill of your choice. Choose two cantrips from the occult spell list. Each cantrip must have the divination, enchantment, or necromancy trait. You can cast these spells as innate occult spells. You gain access to the Cast a Spell activity if you didn't have it already. You're trained in occult spell attack rolls and spell DCs. You can usually replace material components with somatic components, so you don't need a spell component pouch. Your key spellcasting ability for these spells is Charisma.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-occultism-or-religion",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Ghost Hunter Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2278",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Grave's Voice"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can use your choice of Spirit Lore or Haunt Lore to Make an Impression or Request things of incorporeal creatures. At the GM's discretion, an incorporeal spirit might be willing to hear you out.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ghost-hunter-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Grave's Voice",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2279",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Investigate Haunting"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are skilled at noticing the telltale signs of ghosts and hauntings. Even when you aren't Investigating in exploration mode, you get a check to Recall Knowledge about incorporeal undead and haunts active in the area. You also gain a +2 circumstance bonus to skill checks to disable haunts.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ghost-hunter-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Investigate Haunting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2280",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spirit Spells"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your ability to confront incorporeal menaces develops into full-fledged spellcasting. Choose a 1st-level occult spell. You can Cast this Spell as an innate occult spell. At 6th level, you gain a 2nd-level occult spell, and at 8th level, you gain a 3rd-level occult spell. Each of these spells must have the divination, enchantment, or necromancy trait. You can cast each of these spells once per day.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ghost-hunter-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Spirit Spells",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2281",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ghost Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2281#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Once per day, you can infuse a weapon you are carrying with magical energies that allow it to strike true against incorporeal undead. The weapon gains the effects of the ghost touch property rune for 10 minutes. At 10th level, you can apply this effect to two weapons instead of one.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ghost-hunter-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Ghost Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2281#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2282",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Peer Beyond"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have uncanny insight into the way ghosts and haunts manifest, manipulate the mind, and rejuvenate. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to saving throws against mental effects caused by incorporeal undead and haunts, and you can roll a Spirit Lore or Haunt Lore check for initiative if you know that an incorporeal undead or a haunt is present. If you are present when a spirit or haunt is defeated, you instantly gain a flash of insight into how it can be permanently put to rest. Typically, this flash manifests as a vision that presents a quick scene closely linked to the source of the spirit or haunt's creation. Attempt a Spirit Lore or Haunt Lore check, respectively, with a DC appropriate for the spirit or haunt's level. On a success, you gain a hint about how to put the spirit to rest or permanently disable the haunt; on a critical success, you learn the exact method of doing so.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ghost-hunter-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Peer Beyond",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2296",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Truespeech"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "It is paramount that you are understood and you understand others; language need not impede your message. You can cast tongues as a 5th-level divine innate spell once per day on yourself only. You gain a +1 status bonus to Diplomacy checks for the duration of the spell when speaking to creatures with whom you already shared a language before casting.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-angelkin",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Truespeech",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Aasimar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=236",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sense Unholiness"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You sense the truly wicked as a queasy or foreboding feeling. You can sense the presence of creatures with the unholy trait within 120 feet. This functions as a vague sense, similar to humans’ sense of smell. An unholy creature using a disguise or otherwise trying to hide its presence attempts a Deception check against your Perception DC to hide its sanctification from you. If the creature succeeds at its Deception check, it is then temporarily immune to your Sense Unholiness for 1 day.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Sense Unholiness",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=237",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Devoted Focus"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your devotion is strong enough to increase your focus to incredible heights. Whenever you Refocus, completely refill your focus pool.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-devotion-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Devoted Focus",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=247",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lasting Doubt"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you cast doubt upon your foes, the effect lasts longer than usual. After being enfeebled 2 by your Glimpse of Redemption, the foe is enfeebled 1 for 1 minute. If you have Weight of Guilt, after being stupefied 2 by your Glimpse of Redemption, the foe is stupefied 1 for 1 minute or until the flat check from stupefied causes it to lose a spell, whichever comes first.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-redeemer-cause",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Lasting Doubt",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=248",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Liberating Stride"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Instead of you taking a Step at the end of your Liberating Step, the triggering ally can Stride up to half their Speed. Even if you have exalt, only the triggering ally gains this benefit.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-liberator-cause",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Liberating Stride",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=260",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ultimate Mercy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mercy transcends the bounds of life and death. Add ultimate mercy to the types of mercy you can provide. When you use Mercy, you can target a creature that died since your last turn to return it to life. The target returns to life with 1 Hit Point and becomes wounded 1. You can't return the target to life if it died from disintegrate or a death effect. The creature gains the other benefits of lay on hands after it returns to life.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mercy",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Ultimate Mercy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=264",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Deadly Simplicity"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you are wielding your deity’s favored weapon, increase the damage die size of that weapon by one step. If your deity’s favored weapon is an unarmed attack (such as a fist, if you worship Irori) and its damage die is smaller than d6, instead increase its damage die size to d6.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-deity-with-a-simple-or-unarmed-attack-favored-weapon-trained-with-your-deitys-favored-weapon",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Deadly Simplicity",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=265",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Domain Initiate"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your deity bestows a special spell related to their powers. Select one domain—a subject of particular interest to you within your religion—from your deity’s list. You gain an initial domain spell for that domain, a spell unique to the domain and not available to other clerics. Domain spells are a type of focus spell. It costs 1 Focus Point to cast a focus spell, and you start with a focus pool of 1 Focus Point. You refill your focus pool during your daily preparations, and you can regain 1 Focus Point by spending 10 minutes using the Refocus activity to pray to your deity or do service toward their causes. Focus spells are automatically heightened to half your level rounded up, much like cantrips. Focus spells don’t require spell slots, and can’t be cast using spell slots. Your focus pool can hold one Focus Point for each focus spell you have, up to 3 points. The full rules for focus spells appear here.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Domain Initiate",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2658",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Eldritch Researcher Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the ability to cast a single arcane or occult cantrip of your choice (which is heightened to a spell level equal to half your level rounded up). If you weren't already, you become trained in that tradition's spell DCs and spell attack rolls with Intelligence as your spellcasting ability. Regardless of whether you choose an arcane or occult cantrip, you also become an expert in your choice of either Arcana or Occultism. You also gain a +1 circumstance bonus to checks you attempt with the chosen skill when Investigating or Identifying Magic.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-arcana-and-occultism",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Eldritch Researcher Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2659",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Seeker of Truths"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your devotion to discovering and hoarding abstruse truths borders on the fanatical, and you can bring this devotion to bear. You gain the cleric's Domain Initiate feat but must select knowledge, secrecy, or truth as your domain. You cast that domain's domain spell as a focus spell of the same tradition as your cantrip from Eldritch Researcher Dedication, and you Refocus by contemplating abstruse mysteries rather than praying to a god. When an ability would manifest a divine symbol—such as the word of truth focus spell—it instead manifests as a strange shape unique to you that seems to defy geometry.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-eldritch-researcher-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Seeker of Truths",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2660",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Strange Script"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have such familiarity with obscure texts that you can compel them to reveal their secrets. Once per day, you can touch a single text (such as a tome, a wall of hieroglyphics, or something similar) and understand its meaning for 1 hour. If the text is in multiple languages, you gain the ability to understand them all for only the purposes of reading the text. If the text is in a code or cypher, you don't automatically understand the text, but you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to checks to decipher it.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-eldritch-researcher-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Strange Script",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2661",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Scholarly Defense"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your knowledge of strange creatures and their bizarre anatomy allows you to anticipate their physical attacks and reduce the damage you take from them. You gain resistance to physical damage from melee attacks made by aberrations and oozes. This resistance is equal to one-third your level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-eldritch-researcher-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Scholarly Defense",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2662",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Able Ritualist"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your readings on rituals make you a skilled participant. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to primary and secondary checks you attempt as part of casting a ritual.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-eldritch-researcher-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Able Ritualist",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2663",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lorefinder"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You know that fate sometimes conspires to keep dangerous knowledge or items from the eyes of those most able to understand them. You deny fate the ability to conceal truths from you. You can cast locate as an innate occult spell once per day. When you reach 14th level, this spell is heightened to 5th level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-eldritch-researcher-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Lorefinder",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2664",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Know it All"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your knowledge of abstruse topics is unparalleled. When you succeed at a check to Recall Knowledge, you gain additional information or context. When you critically succeed at a Knowledge check, at the GM's discretion you might gain even more additional information or context than normal.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-eldritch-researcher-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Know it All",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2665",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced Seeker of Truths"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have unlocked deeper secrets to uncovering and hoarding lore. You gain an advanced domain spell from one domain you selected with Seeker of Truths. Increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-eldritch-researcher-dedication-seeker-of-truths",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced Seeker of Truths",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2666",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Words of Unraveling"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have unlocked abstruse methods to tangle with reality itself, altering the fate of a single individual. Once per day as an occult innate spell, you can cast daydreamer's curse, outcast's curse, or savant's curse. At the GM's discretion, you can substitute or add additional occult curse spells of 4th level or lower to this list. You can choose a different spell from the list each time you use this ability. If you couldn't already cast occult spells, these spells use Intelligence as your spellcasting ability, and you become trained in spell attack rolls and spell DCs for occult spells; if you could already cast occult spells, your proficiency in spell attack rolls and spell DCs for occult spells increases to expert.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-eldritch-researcher-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Words of Unraveling",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2667",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Entities from Afar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can call in aberrations to fight for you or to answer questions. You can cast summon entity as an innate occult spell once per day. If you couldn't already cast occult spells, these spells use Intelligence as your spellcasting ability, and you become trained in spell attack rolls and spell DCs for occult spells; if you could already cast occult spells, your proficiency in spell attack rolls and spell DCs for occult spells increases to expert. As soon as the aberration arrives, instead of giving it any other commands, you can demand that it help you with a single question you pose to it. For the creature to effectively answer, you must Sustain the Spell for 1 minute, and you must understand and be understood by the aberration. If you do, the aberration gives you a cryptic clue as provided by the read omens spell, except that the clue is even more enigmatic than normal; the creature then immediately returns from whence it came without providing you any other benefit. At 16th level and every 2 levels thereafter, the summon entity spell is heightened by 1 level (to a maximum of 8th level when you reach 20th level).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-eldritch-researcher-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Entities from Afar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2668",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Incredible Recollection"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2668#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can sift through knowledge locked within your mind at an incredible pace. You instantly use up to 5 Recall Knowledge actions. If you have any special abilities or free actions that would normally be triggered when you Recall Knowledge, you can't use them for these actions.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-eldritch-researcher-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Incredible Recollection",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2668#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2683",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Crossbow Infiltrator Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have mastered stealthy weapons that allow you to strike carefully from a distance far enough to avoid reprisal, yet close enough to confirm your kills. You have familiarity with the gauntlet bow, hand crossbow, and repeating hand crossbow, treating the repeating hand crossbow as a martial weapon for the purposes of proficiency and the gauntlet bow as a simple weapon for the purposes of proficiency. If you're at least an expert in any of these weapons, you gain access to that weapon's critical specialization effect. You also gain the Infiltrator's Draw action. Infiltrator's Draw [one-action] Frequency once per round; Effect You Interact to draw a gauntlet bow, hand crossbow, or repeating hand crossbow, then Strike with it. Alternatively, you can Strike with a loaded hand crossbow or repeating hand crossbow you're already holding and then Interact to stow it.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-stealth",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Crossbow Infiltrator Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2684",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Repeating Hand Crossbow Training"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The specific needs of your organization or mission warrant your use of the latest in ingenious crossbow technology. You gain access to repeating hand crossbows and repeater bandoliers. If you have Running Reload or a similar feat that allows you to reload and perform another action or activity as a single action, you can use that action more efficiently with a repeating weapon. You can use the action as a 3-action activity to reload a magazine into a repeating weapon after you perform its other granted action, or as a 2-action activity if you use a magazine from a repeater bandolier.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-crossbow-infiltrator-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Repeating Hand Crossbow Training",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2685",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reloading Trick"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2685#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can fire off a single shot even when it seems like you are unprepared. You Interact to reload your hand crossbow or gauntlet bow and attempt a ranged Strike with it.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-crossbow-infiltrator-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Reloading Trick",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2685#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2686",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lethargy Poisoner"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've learned more than the use of hand crossbows. During your daily preparations, you can prepare a dose of lethargy poison from ordinary materials in a wilderness or urban area. If you're an expert in Crafting, you can instead craft a dose of stupor poison. You can prepare two doses (of either poison) if you're a master in Crafting and three doses if you're legendary in Crafting. The save DC for this poison is equal to your class DC. Only you can use these poisons, and they expire the next time you make your daily preparations. The GM might decide that the area you're in is too barren to provide the materials you need for this feat.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-crossbow-infiltrator-dedication-trained-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Lethargy Poisoner",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2689",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Syu Tak-Nwa's Skillful Tresses"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can expertly control your living hair and use it to perform various tasks. You can perform simple Interact actions with your hair such as opening an unlocked door or picking up objects. Your hair can't perform actions that require fingers or significant manual dexterity, including any action that would require a check to accomplish. Your hair can hold items of up to 1 Bulk, but can't Activate or attack with any items it's holding.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-living-hair",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Syu Tak-Nwa's Skillful Tresses",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2690",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Syu Tak-Nwa's Deadly Hair"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your hair unarmed attack deals 1d6 bludgeoning damage and gains the grapple trait.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-living-hair",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Syu Tak-Nwa's Deadly Hair",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2691",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Syu Tak-Nwa's Hexed Locks"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your hair unarmed attack gains the reach trait. You can deliver hexes through your hair. When you successfully cast a hex focus spell that requires 2 or more actions to cast and that doesn't require a spell attack roll, if your target is within your reach, as part of the spellcasting activity you can make a hair Strike against the foe before applying any effects of the hex. If this Strike misses, the hex has no effect.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-living-hair",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Syu Tak-Nwa's Hexed Locks",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2692",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Entwined Energy Ki"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can transform your inner power into a type of energy to empower your ki abilities. When you gain this feat, choose either acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic damage. When you cast ki blast, you can choose to have the spell deal the type of damage you chose instead of force damage. When you cast ki form or ki strike, add the type of damage you chose to the list of damage types you can select for the spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Entwined Energy Ki",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2693",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Wronged Monk's Wrath"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the wronged monk's wrath ki spell. Increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ki-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Wronged Monk's Wrath",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2704",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Butterfly Blade Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You become trained in Deception and Stealth; if you were already trained, you become an expert instead. Whenever your proficiency rank in any weapon increases to expert or beyond, you also gain that new proficiency rank with butterfly swords. You gain access to butterfly swords.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-butterfly-swords",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Butterfly Blade Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2705",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Butterfly's Kiss"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can make nonlethal Strikes with a butterfly sword without taking a penalty.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-butterfly-blade-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Butterfly's Kiss",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2706",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Butterfly's Sting"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the sneak attack class feature. You don't increase the number of dice as you gain levels.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-butterfly-blade-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Butterfly's Sting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2707",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mastermind's Eye"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you succeed at identifying a creature using Recall Knowledge, that creature is flat-footed against your attacks until the start of your next turn; if you critically succeed, it's flat-footed against your attacks for 1 minute. This feat serves as the rogue's mastermind racket for the purpose of meeting prerequisites.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-butterfly-blade-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Mastermind's Eye",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2708",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Deadly Butterfly"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain access to the butterfly sword's critical specialization effect. If you already had access to the critical specialization effect or you gain the effect at a later time, you also gain the critical specialization effect for knives when you critically hit with a butterfly sword. You can benefit from only one critical specialization effect at a time.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-butterfly-blade-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Deadly Butterfly",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2709",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Innocent Butterfly"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You know how to alter the perceptions of others. You can cast aura of the unremarkable once per day as an innate arcane spell. The spell uses your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-butterfly-blade-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Innocent Butterfly",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2710",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ghost Eater Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have trained as a ghost eater, a hunter specialized in the destruction of spirits. You know how to channel your own spiritual energy to harm spirits. Your weapon and unarmed attack Strikes become magical. Against incorporeal creatures, they also gain the effects of a ghost touch property rune.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-occultism-or-religion",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Ghost Eater Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2711",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reach Beyond"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've learned to move your spiritual energy past yourself to attack spirits where others can't. You can make melee Strikes against incorporeal creatures that are inside solid objects as long as the object is within your reach. An incorporeal creature inside of a solid object is hidden, requiring you to succeed at a DC 11 flat check when you target it. You can spend an action, which has the concentrate trait, to focus on a creature inside of a solid object. If you do, the next melee Strike you make this turn requires you to succeed at only a DC 6 flat check to affect the creature.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ghost-eater-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Reach Beyond",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2712",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Disrupting Strikes"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2712#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You call forth positive energy from within to help you destroy undead. Your weapon and unarmed Strikes gain the effects of a disrupting property rune until the start of your next turn. If you're 14th level or higher, your Strikes instead gain the effects of a greater disrupting property rune. The DC for the rune's effect is equal to your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ghost-eater-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Disrupting Strikes",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2712#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2713",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cross the Threshold"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can cast ethereal jaunt as an occult innate spell once per day. You don't need to Sustain the Spell; instead, it lasts for 10 minutes or until you choose to return to your material form as a free action.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ghost-eater-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Cross the Threshold",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2730",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sense Ki"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can read the presence of ki in your area. You gain imprecise lifesense out to a range of 30 feet.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ki-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Sense Ki",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2731",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shift Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2731#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You move the spell's area to a new location within 120 feet. The spell's remaining duration is reduced by half. The spell no longer affects its previous area.",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Shift Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2731#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2732",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Electric Counter"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2732#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You gain resistance to electricity equal to your level until the start of your next turn. If the triggering damage was electricity, this resistance applies to it. If the triggering damage was from a melee attack, the attacker takes 3d6 electricity damage.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-wild-winds-initiate",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Electric Counter",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Electricity",
            "aonprd:Trait-Evocation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2732#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2733",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Effortless Reach"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Focusing the powers of your ki to augment your blows, you stretch and lengthen your body in ways that defy logic. Your unarmed attacks gain the reach trait.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Effortless Reach",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2734",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Golden League Xun Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are a xun for the Golden League, aiding the organization. You gain expert proficiency in two of the following skills (or in two other skills of your choice in which you're trained, if you were already an expert in the listed skills): Athletics, Deception, Intimidation, or Stealth. In addition, if you use Underworld Lore to Earn Income or Recall Knowledge, when you get a success, you get a critical success instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-underworld-lore",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Golden League Xun Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2735",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Beneath Notice"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are skilled at hiding from your foes and targets among the common populace. You gain the Quick Disguise and Slippery Secrets skill feats. In addition, while in a crowd, you can Impersonate a nondescript member of the crowd as a three action activity (one action if you are legendary in Deception).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-golden-league-xun-dedication-expert-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Beneath Notice",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2736",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Menacing Prowess"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Scaring off multiple people at once is your specialty. When you Demoralize, you can target up to 2 creatures within 30 feet of you at once. If you are a master of Intimidation, you can Demoralize up to 4 creatures at once; if you're legendary, you can Demoralize up to 8 creatures at once.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-golden-league-xun-dedication-expert-in-intimidation",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Menacing Prowess",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2737",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rope Mastery"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Ropes are your tool of choice, and you deploy them in versatile ways. When Climbing a rope, you move 5 more feet on a success and 10 more feet on a critical success, to a maximum of your Speed. This additional movement stacks with the effects of Quick Climb. In addition, you can use a rope to hamper your foes. When holding a rope, you can attempt an Athletics check to Disarm, Grapple, or Trip a creature up to 10 feet away instead of only adjacent creatures. If you critically fail such a check while holding a rope, you can drop the rope to take the effects of a failure instead of a critical failure.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-golden-league-xun-dedication-expert-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Rope Mastery",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2738",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Silent Sting"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2738#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You quickly hide your weapon to make it difficult to pin the attack on you. You attempt to Conceal an Object to hide the triggering weapon. Your Stealth check is compared to the Perception DC of all creatures within 30 feet that can see you. You automatically succeed against creatures farther than 30 feet. The target of your Strike gains a +4 circumstance bonus to their Perception DC for this check. If your Stealth check is a success, you hide your weapon so well that the creature can't clearly determine where the attack originated.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-golden-league-xun-dedication-expert-in-stealth",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Silent Sting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2738#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2739",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sixth Pillar Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You use your physical discipline to channel your magic. If your proficiency rank in unarmed attacks is at least expert, your proficiency rank in spell attacks increases to expert. Likewise, if your proficiency rank in spell attacks is at least expert, your proficiency rank in unarmed attacks improves to expert. You become an expert in Athletics, or in another trained skill if you were already expert in Athletics.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dexterity-14-expert-in-acrobatics-ability-to-cast-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Sixth Pillar Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=274",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Panic the Dead"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Vitality strikes terror in the undead. When you use a heal spell to damage undead, any undead that fails its saving throw is also frightened 1. If it critically failed, the creature also gains the fleeing condition until the start of your next turn. Mindless undead are not immune to this effect due to being mindless.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Panic the Dead",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fear",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2740",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Six Pillars Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2740#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You stand firm, steeling your mind and body, allowing you to use your magic unperturbed. While in this stance, you gain a +4 circumstance bonus to AC against reactions triggered by using actions with the concentrate or manipulate traits. In addition, when you cast a spell that requires one or more actions while in this stance, your unarmed Strikes gain a +1 circumstance bonus to damage.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-sixth-pillar-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Six Pillars Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2740#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2741",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Maneuvering Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2741#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You instantly tap into the magical power of a spell you're casting to quickly pounce around the battlefield. You Step, Leap, or Stand. This action can be before or after you Cast the Spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-sixth-pillar-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Maneuvering Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2741#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2744",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "All the Time in the World"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2744#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your firsthand experience of the subjective nature of time and space has given you new observational insights. Your mind processes information so quickly that time appears to stop for all creatures but you. You can take up to 9 actions in 3 sets of up to 3 actions each. During this time, you can use purely mental and observational abilities such as Recall Knowledge, Seek, and Devise a Stratagem, and you can use an action to move a mental projection of yourself to a location within a 60- foot radius to observe objects more closely and from different angles, though you can't affect your surroundings in any way (for instance, you could move your mental projection more closely to a distant door to read a minute inscription on its handle, but you could not open it to observe the other side). When the duration elapses, time resumes its normal flow.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "All the Time in the World",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2744#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2745",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dance of Intercession"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2745#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You either performed in or stood witness to the dance used to invoke the Celestial Dragon and can harness a sliver of their power. You Stride in a dance up to half your Speed, attempting a DC 35 Performance check. You can perform this dance up to three times per day. The second time you do so in the same day, use the degree of success one worse than your actual roll on the Performance check. The third time in a day, use the degree of success two lower than your actual roll. Critical Success You perform the movements of the Dance of Intercession so gracefully that you evoke a glimmer of the memory of the Celestial Dragon's awesome power. You cast the 3-action version of either 9th-level harm or heal at any point during your Stride. This does not use any spell slots. Success As critical success, but the spell is 7th level instead of 9th as you stumble through the movements. Failure As critical success, but the spell is 5th level instead of 9th as you stumble through the movements. Critical Failure You fail to remember the steps of the dance. You gain no additional effect beyond Striding half your Speed, and you can't attempt the Dance of Intercession again until your next daily preparations.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-performance",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Dance of Intercession",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2745#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2746",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Demon's Hair"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your hair constantly wriggles and writhes like that of your rival, Syu Tak-nwa. Your damage die of your hair unarmed Strike increases by one step and it gains the reach and versatile slashing traits. Your familiar assumes partial control over your hair; as long as your familiar is alive and within 30 feet, you are permanently quickened, and you can use the extra action only to make a hair Strike. You can deliver hexes through your hair. When you successfully cast a non-cantrip hex that requires 2 or more actions to cast and that doesn't require a spell attack roll, if your target is within your reach, as part of the spellcasting activity you can make a hair Strike against them before applying any effects of the hex. If this Strike misses, the hex has no effect.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-living-hair",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Demon's Hair",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2747",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Everdistant Defense"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2747#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The spatial barrier of Syndara's Island has taught you that distance can foil enemies better than any armor. You warp space, causing each square within your aura that the attack or creature would move through to count as triple the distance. If this reaction is used on a ranged attack, the attack takes range increment penalties based on the adjusted range and fails if this would cause it to exceed its maximum range.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Everdistant Defense",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Abjuration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2747#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2748",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Extradimensional Stash"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you perform sleight of hand, you fold space so that objects really do disappear. You create a small extradimensional space somewhere within in your clothing that can hold up to 5 Bulk worth of objects. The space functions as a bag of holding, but can hold only up to 5 Bulk, has no Bulk of its own, and can be Interacted with using only one hand. In addition, when you Palm an Object, you can place it directly into this extradimensional space as long as the space has sufficient free space to hold the object.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-legendary-in-thievery",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Extradimensional Stash",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Extradimensional",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2749",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Head of the Night Parade"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2749#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You remember the revelry of the Night Parade and call them to your aid in a riotous display. You Perform and cast 8th-level mad monkeys three times, except that the spell calls various apparitions such as dancing tsukumogami or drinking oni rather than monkeys. Each casting can produce a different kind of mischief. You can Sustain all three Spells each round using a single Perform action.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Head of the Night Parade",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2749#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2750",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Heart of the Kaiju"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Witnessing the might of the kaiju King Mogaru, Alru, and Toraloa up close awoke a new ferocity within you. When you transform using Monstrosity Shape, you can take on a kaiju form. When you take this feat, choose acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic damage; this is the damage your breath weapon deals. You can't change this later. The battle form is Gargantuan size with the following specific abilities; the damage values already include the extra die from being a 9th-level spell. Kaiju Speed 40 feet; physical resistance 5; Melee [one-action] jaws (reach 20 feet), Damage 3d12+20 piercing; Melee [one-action] claws (agile, reach 20 feet), Damage 3d8+20 slashing; Breath Weapon [two-actions] (evocation, primal) Each creature in a 60-foot cone takes 15d6 damage (of your chosen damage type), with a basic Reflex save against your spell DC. Once activated, your breath weapon can't be used again for 1d4 rounds.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-monstrosity-shape",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Heart of the Kaiju",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2751",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Plum Deluge"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2751#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have learned to saturate an area with poison in imitation of the techniques of your rival, Blue Viper. As part of this ability, you Interact to draw three vials of the same contact poison and throw them in the air, where they shatter and spread a poisonous deluge affecting a 20-foot burst within 60 feet. All creatures in the burst are automatically exposed to the poison, immediately bypassing any onset time, and must attempt a saving throw against that poison. The three vials must be identical, even if the poison can come in multiple types or different levels.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Plum Deluge",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2751#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2752",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ruby Resurrection"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2752#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "In a burst of flame, you return to health like a phoenix rising from the ashes. Change your current Hit Points to 30 and cast a 6th-level fireball centered on yourself. This fireball doesn't affect you. Your hair turns brilliant red for 1 hour. If you haven't used Ruby Resurrection and you die, you stay in initiative order and Ruby Resurrection triggers automatically at the start of your next turn, bringing you back to life at 0 HP before having its normal effects. This happens only if there are some remains to resurrect; for instance, if you were killed by disintegrate you wouldn't return.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Ruby Resurrection",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Necromancy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2752#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2753",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Scapegoat Parallel Self"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2753#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Seeing Syndara superimpose creatures with similar metaphysical properties, you've realized a way to manipulate the effects of your oracular curse. You immediately change your curse to its minor, moderate, or major stage, or back to its mild form, exchanging the curse effect with that of a parallel version of yourself in another reality.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Scapegoat Parallel Self",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Necromancy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2753#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2754",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sever Space"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2754#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You destroy the space between you and your targets, allowing you to strike with your melee weapons at great range. Make a melee Strike with the required weapon or unarmed attack. The attack gains an 80-foot reach for this Strike. After the Strike, regardless of whether it succeeded, the world rushes to fill the space you destroyed, bringing you and the target adjacent to each other. You can choose to teleport to the closest space adjacent to the target or to attempt to teleport the target adjacent to you. If you choose the target, they can negate the teleportation if they succeed at a Fortitude save against your class DC.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Sever Space",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Conjuration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Teleportation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2754#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2755",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Time Dilation Cascade"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2755#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You borrow a bit of time from the future to act now. Make six Strikes. Your multiple attack penalty applies normally to these Strikes. If you successfully hit a creature with multiple Strikes, combine those Strikes' damage for the purpose of resistances and weaknesses. On your next turn, you regain 1 action instead of 3. This is before any alteration in your actions due to the quickened, slowed, and stunned conditions.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Time Dilation Cascade",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2755#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2756",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vitality-Manipulating Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2756#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have learned to attack meridians and pressure points like your rival Shino Hakusa. You gain a vitality blast ranged unarmed Strike that deals 1d4 negative damage, has a range of 30 feet, and has the unarmed and versatile positive traits. Additionally, when you use Stunning Fist, instead of saving against being stunned, you can choose to have the target make a Fortitude save against your class DC with the following results. You must choose to do this before the target rolls its save. Critical Success The target is unaffected. Success The target's muscles become temporarily weaker. For 1 round, the target is enfeebled 2, and any time it attempts to take an action with the manipulate trait, the action is disrupted unless it succeeds at a flat check with a DC equal to 5 + its enfeebled value. Failure As success, but the duration is 1 minute. Critical Failure As success, but the duration is 1 minute, the flat check is DC 11, and the target takes –10-foot status penalty to all Speeds for the duration.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Vitality-Manipulating Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2756#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2757",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vivacious Afterimage"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2757#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You move so quickly that you create a short-lived afterimage, looks exactly like you, in front of you or behind you. You Stride. At any point along your movement, you leave an afterimage of yourself behind. Alternatively, you can stop moving and send your afterimage forward instead, up to the remainder of your Speed. A creature that spends actions to engage with your afterimage can attempt to disbelieve it with a Will save against your class DC. Once an enemy has disbelieved any of your afterimages, they are temporarily immune to all of your Vivacious Afterimages for 10 minutes. As long as a creature has not disbelieved the afterimage, the afterimage counts as a creature for flanking. The afterimage lasts until the beginning of your next turn or until you use Vivacious Afterimage again, whichever comes first.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-vivacious-speed",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Vivacious Afterimage",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Illusion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2757#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2758",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Whirlwind Toss"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2758#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You whirl a foe to smash into all nearby creatures before throwing them far away. You Thrash. During this Thrash, your Collateral Thrash feat applies to all other enemies adjacent to you. You can then throw the grabbed creature 10 feet, where they fall prone. If the enemy you choose for Collateral Thrash is also adjacent to you, it attempts only one save and takes the damage only once.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-collateral-thrash",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Whirlwind Toss",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2758#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2759",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Worldsphere Gravity"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2759#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Though creating demiplanes usually requires lengthy rituals, you know how to establish minor planar effects in imitation of Syndara's masterpieces. If your next action is to Cast a Spell of at least 5th level from your spell slots that affects an area, you can apply one of the following planar effects to a 20-foot burst centered within the spell's area. The effect persists for 1 minute. Gravitational Morass The pull of gravity is amplified here, creating greater difficult terrain. Flying creatures that pass through the area must succeed at a Reflex save against your spell DC or fall to the ground, taking bludgeoning damage equal to half the distance fallen.Flowing Time Erratic timestreams aid you within this space. A creature that starts its turn in the burst is affected by haste on that turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Worldsphere Gravity",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Metamagic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2759#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=282",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Divine Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=282#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You siphon residual spell energy into a weapon you’re wielding. Until the end of your turn, the weapon deals an additional 1d4 spirit damage. If you are holy or unholy, Strikes with the weapon also gain that trait, and the additional damage increases to 2d4 against creatures of the opposing trait.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Divine Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=282#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=283",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Selective Energy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As you call down divine power, you can prevent some enemies from benefiting or some allies from being hurt. When you cast a version of harm or heal that has an area, you can designate up to 5 creatures in the area. They are not targeted by the spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Selective Energy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2848",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Raise a Tome"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2848#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You raise up the book you're holding and flip it open to defend yourself and expedite your studies. The book remains raised until the start of your next turn. While you have a book raised, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to AC and a +1 circumstance bonus to Recall Knowledge to identify creatures using a skill related to the subject of the book (Arcana if you're using your spellbook). This bonus is in addition to any item bonus the book normally gives to the check. If you have Shield Block, you can use the tome for that feat (Hardness 3, HP 12, BT 6) as though it were a shield. Whenever you use an ability that allows you to Raise a Shield, such as Emergency Targe, you can Raise a Tome instead, changing any requirements that normally require a shield to apply to your book.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Raise a Tome",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2848#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2849",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Expansive Spellstrike"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can blast the energy of a spell out around the target of your attack. When you Spellstrike with a spell that has an area of a burst, cone, or line, the spell creates an area instead of affecting only the target. The target must be in the area. A burst is centered on a corner of the target’s square; if the target is Large or larger, the burst use the square corner closest to the center of the target and choose the corner if more than one is eligible. A cone or line emits from you and must include the target; if you’re not adjacent to the target (using a reach weapon or starlit span, for example), choose any square adjacent to the target as the source. The spell affects all creatures in the area as normal, but the Strike still targets only one creature.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-spellstrike",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Expansive Spellstrike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2850",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Force Fang"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can turn your attack into an unerring blur of force. You learn the force fang conflux spell. Increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-focus-pool",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Force Fang",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2853",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Devastating Spellstrike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2853#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your Spellstrike sweeps are so wide and devastating, they splash onto nearby foes. Make a Spellstrike. Foes adjacent to the target take splash damage equal to 2 + the extra damage from Arcane Cascade. The damage type is the same as Arcane Cascade; if the spell already deals splash damage of the same type, combine the damage together before applying weaknesses or resistances.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-arcane-cascade-inexorable-iron-hybrid-study-spellstrike",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Devastating Spellstrike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2853#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2854",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Distracting Spellstrike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2854#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You weave distracting magic with one hand to enhance your Spellstrike. Make a Spellstrike and Feint against the target of your Strike. Do this immediately before making the Strike, but after choosing your target. The Feint gains the arcane, illusion, and visual traits, and it always has the basic effects of a Feint, rather than applying any adjustments or alternate effects from other feats or abilities.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-laughing-shadow-hybrid-study-spellstrike",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Distracting Spellstrike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2854#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2856",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Starlit Eyes"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Starlight shines in your sight, enhancing your perception and range. When you make a ranged Strike while in Arcane Cascade stance, you lower the DC of your flat check to target a creature that's concealed or hidden from you. The DC is reduced to 3 instead of 5 against a concealed creature and to 9 instead of 11 against a hidden one. When you cast shooting star and target a hidden creature, you don't have to attempt the flat check for targeting a hidden creature with a ranged Strike.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-arcane-cascade-starlit-span-hybrid-study",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Starlit Eyes",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2864",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fused Staff"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you prepare a staff, you can hold it up to a weapon to merge the two items. You can switch the fused item's form from the weapon to the staff or vice versa as a single action, which has the concentrate trait. When the item is in staff form, you can Cast the Spells from the staff and benefit from any other abilities the staff grants. The staff and the weapon share their fundamental runes, using whichever weapon potency and whichever striking rune is higher level. They don't share any other runes or specific abilities. You can Cast Spells from the staff as part of a Spellstrike even when the staff is in weapon form. Otherwise, you can't cast the staff's spells while it's in weapon form. The fusion lasts until your next daily preparations, though you can spend 10 minutes to separate the two items and meld the staff into a different weapon. The melding works for you alone. A different wielder can use the staff in its current form but can't transform it, get the benefit of the shared runes, or use its spells for a Spellstrike if it's in weapon form.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-spellstrike",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Fused Staff",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Arcane",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Transmutation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2865",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Runic Impression"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can temporarily replicate the effects of a property rune for your weapon or unarmed attacks. You learn the runic impression conflux spell. Increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-focus-pool",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Runic Impression",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2866",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spell Swipe"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2866#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You attack in an arc and enact your spell against everyone you hit. Make a Spellstrike, but roll separate Strikes to attack two creatures, each of whom must be within your melee reach and adjacent to each other. If your spell could affect two or more targets, your spell affects whichever foes you hit, not just the first target; otherwise, choose one target to affect with the spell. A Spell Swipe counts as two attacks for your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until after you make both attacks. If you're using a weapon that has the sweep trait, its circumstance bonus applies against both targets. You can use this activity with only melee Strikes, even if you have the starlit span hybrid study or a similar ability. If you use Expansive Spellstrike to Spellstrike with an area spell, apply the area as described in Expansive Spellstrike, choosing one of the creatures you Strike to determine the area and whether the spell fails due to a critically failed Strike. If you use Expansive Spellstrike to Spellstrike with a targeted spell, the spell is lost completely only if both Strikes are critical failures.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-spellstrike",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Spell Swipe",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2866#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2886",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced Weaponry"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your eidolon's attack evolves. Choose one of your eidolon's starting melee unarmed attacks. It gains one of the following traits, chosen when you gain the feat: disarm, grapple, nonlethal, shove, trip, or versatile bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced Weaponry",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Evolution",
            "aonprd:Trait-Summoner"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2891",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Glider Form"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2891#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your eidolon evolves wings, a buoyant body, or some other means to control descent. It glides slowly toward the ground, 5 feet down and up to 25 feet forward through the air. As long as it spends at least 1 action gliding each round and has not yet reached the ground, it remains in the air at the end of your turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Glider Form",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Eidolon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Evolution",
            "aonprd:Trait-Move",
            "aonprd:Trait-Summoner"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2891#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2897",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ranged Combatant"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Spines, flame jets, and holy blasts are just some of the ways your eidolon might strike from a distance. It gains a ranged unarmed attack with a range increment of 30 feet that deals 1d4 damage and has the magical and propulsive traits. When you select this feat, choose a damage type: acid, bludgeoning, cold, electricity, fire, negative, piercing, positive, or slashing. If your eidolon is a celestial, fiend, or monitor with an alignment other than true neutral, you can choose a damage type in its alignment.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Ranged Combatant",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Evolution",
            "aonprd:Trait-Summoner"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2898",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reinforce Eidolon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You buffer your eidolon. You gain the reinforce eidolon link cantrip.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Reinforce Eidolon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Summoner"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2903",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lifelink Surge"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn the lifelink surge link spell. Increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Lifelink Surge",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Summoner"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2915",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tandem Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2915#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You and your eidolon each attack, seamlessly targeting the same foe without interfering with each other's movements. Your eidolon makes a melee Strike, and then you make a melee Strike against the same creature. Both attacks count toward your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until after both attacks have been made.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Tandem Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Summoner",
            "aonprd:Trait-Tandem"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2915#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2962",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tattoo Artist"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can craft tattoos, including magical tattoos. When you select this feat, you gain the formulas for four common magical tattoos of 2nd level or lower. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Crafting checks to Craft tattoos. If you're a master in Crafting, this bonus increases to +2 and you gain the formulas for four common magical tattoos of 7th level or lower.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Tattoo Artist",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2970",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fire Lung"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A lifetime of proximity to flames has inured your lungs and eyes to smoke. You can breathe normally in areas of ash and smoke without risk of suffocation, and you ignore the concealed condition from smoke. You need only a successful DC 10 flat check to recover from persistent fire damage, rather than DC 15 (and the DC when receiving particularly effective assistance is 5 instead of 10).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-flame-order",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Fire Lung",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2971",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shore Step"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The shallows and tide pools have always called to you and let you pass unhindered. You ignore difficult terrain resulting from shallow water. In addition, if you roll a success on an Acrobatics check to Balance on a slippery or wet surface, or on an Athletics check to Swim, you get a critical success instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-wave-order",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Shore Step",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2972",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Steadying Stone"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The earth has taught you how to remain unyielding and firm. If you roll a success on an Acrobatics check made to Balance on uneven ground composed of earth or rock, you get a critical success instead. As long as you remain on the ground, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Fortitude or Reflex DC against attempts to Shove or Trip you. This bonus also applies to saving throws against spells or effects that would attempt to knock you prone. If you're a rock dwarf, this bonus increases to +3.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stone-order",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Steadying Stone",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2980",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reflective Ripple Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2980#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter a stance of fluid grace as small amounts of water flow with your movements and attacks. You can make flowing wave attacks that deal 1d6 bludgeoning damage. They are in the brawling group and have the agile, disarm, finesse, nonlethal, trip, unarmed, and water traits. While in Reflective Ripple Stance, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to Disarm, Swim, or Trip, and you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Reflex DC to avoid being Disarmed and Tripped.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Reflective Ripple Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Water"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2980#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2981",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stoked Flame Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2981#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter a stance of fast, fiery movements. You can make flashing spark attacks that deal 1d8 slashing damage. They are in the brawling group and have the forceful, nonlethal, sweep, and unarmed traits. If you have access to the flashing sparks' critical specialization effect, you can take an alternate effect instead: if your critical Strike dealt damage, the target takes 1d6 persistent fire damage. While in Stoked Flame Stance, you gain a +5-foot status bonus to your Speed. If you have incredible movement, increase the benefit from incredible movement to a +15-foot status bonus plus 5 feet for every 4 levels beyond 3rd.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Stoked Flame Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Evocation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=2981#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3033",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Arcane Fists"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your physical training encompasses unarmed combat forms. The damage die for your fist changes to 1d6 instead of 1d4. You don't take the normal –2 circumstance penalty when making a lethal attack with your fist or any other unarmed attacks. Your unarmed attacks gain the arcane trait, making them magical. At 5th level, you also gain the critical specialization effects of unarmed attacks in the brawling group and weapons in the brawling group, and the critical specialization effect uses your spell DC instead of your class DC.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Arcane Fists",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3034",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Folklorist Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are a master archivist and entertainer, capable of pulling wisdom from the tales you tell and weaving your allies and enemies into a powerful narrative. You gain the Spin Tale action. Spin Tale [one-action] (auditory, linguistic) Frequency once every 10 minutes; Effect You tell a story, designating one of your allies (but not yourself) as the hero of the story, and one enemy as the villain; both must be within 60 feet. The hero gains a +1 status bonus to attack rolls and saving throws against the villain until the start of your next turn. If you Spin a Tale on your next turn, the story continues for another round, for a maximum of 10 rounds. While the tale continues, minor, crude illusions spring into being in your space; these are arcane illusion effects that have no mechanical impact other than illustrating your tale.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-performance",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Folklorist Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3035",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Folktales Lore"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can pull bits of wisdom from any tale. You become trained in Folktales Lore, a special Lore skill that can be used only to Recall Knowledge, but on any topic. If you fail a check to Recall Knowledge with Folktales Lore, you get the effects of the Dubious Knowledge skill feat. If you are legendary in the Performance skill, you gain expert proficiency in Folktales Lore, but you can't increase your proficiency rank in Folktales Lore by any other means.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-folklorist-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Folktales Lore",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3036",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Narrative Conduit"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You act as a conduit for your companions just as your stories are a conduit between teller and listener. When you Spin a Tale and the hero of your tale Casts a Spell against the villain, you warp the world, allowing the hero to calculate range and cover to the villain from your space instead of their own if they prefer. The hero must choose to calculate both range and cover from the same space; they can't use one space for range and the other for cover.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-folklorist-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Narrative Conduit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3037",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rule of Three"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3037#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Heroes learn from their previous failures, often succeeding on the third attempt. You narrate a tale of the hero's success, granting them a +2 circumstance bonus to their AC or saving throw against the triggering effect. If the villain has used the same effect against the hero on both of their last two turns, and you used Rule of Three on that effect last turn as well, the bonus increases to +4.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-folklorist-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Rule of Three",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3037#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3038",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Communal Tale"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Stories are an experience meant to be shared as a group. When you Spin a Tale, you can designate up to six non-minion allies as the heroes of your story. Each hero, once during the tale, can continue the story in your stead by spending an action to Spin the Tale; if they do, the story continues for another round, as if you had Spun the Tale at the start of your turn. This could allow the story to continue for up to 6 additional rounds, if all possible allies Spin the Tale, though you can continue to Spin the Tale on your own as normal.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-folklorist-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Communal Tale",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3039",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Nantambu Chime-Ringer Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've studied the basics of harmony and resonance in magic, exemplified by the ringing of chimes. You gain a single arcane or occult cantrip of your choice, heightened to a spell level equal to half your level, rounded up. If you weren't already, you become trained in that tradition's spell DCs and spell attack rolls, with Intelligence as your spellcasting ability if you choose arcane or Charisma as your spellcasting ability if you choose occult. Regardless of your choice, you also either become trained in Arcana or Occultism, or an expert in one of these skills if you are already trained in both.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-performance-and-society",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Nantambu Chime-Ringer Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3040",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fleet Tempo"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3040#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "To rush after a criminal or reach someone in need, you ring a sprightly tone. You and all allies within 30 feet gain a +10-foot status bonus to all Speeds for 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-nantambu-chime-ringer-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Fleet Tempo",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Transmutation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3040#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3041",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Deny the Songs of War"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "To keep the peace, you disrupt those who seek to break it. You can cast deafness and 4th-level silence once per day each as innate spells. The tradition of these spells is the one you chose for the Nantambu Chime-Ringer Dedication feat.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-nantambu-chime-ringer-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Deny the Songs of War",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3042",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sing to the Steel"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3042#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You strike magical tones that can turn the tide of combat. You and your allies within 30 feet gain the effects of one of the following runes until the end of your next turn: corrosive, disrupting, flaming, frost, ghost touch, shock, or thundering. The effects apply to a single weapon the creature is holding or one of the creature's unarmed attacks. You choose the rune and the effect applies to all creatures. You can use an action, which has the concentrate trait, to extend the duration of the rune for 1 additional round up to a maximum of 1 minute. If this would give a weapon or unarmed attack more property runes than its normal maximum, an existing property rune (as the creature chooses) is suppressed until the spell ends.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-nantambu-chime-ringer-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Sing to the Steel",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Evocation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3042#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3043",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Song of Grace and Speed"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3043#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You instill great swiftness into your allies. You and all allies within 30 feet become quickened for 1 minute and can use the additional action to Strike, Stride, or Step.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-nantambu-chime-ringer-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Song of Grace and Speed",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Transmutation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3043#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3045",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Explosive Leap"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3045#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You aim an explosion from your innovation downward to launch yourself into the air. You jump up to 30 feet in any direction without touching the ground. You must land on a space of solid ground, or else you fall after using your next action. As normal for effects where you fall after using your next action, you still fall at the end of your turn, even if you don't use any further actions that turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Explosive Leap",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor",
            "aonprd:Trait-Move",
            "aonprd:Trait-Unstable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3045#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3049",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tamper"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3049#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You tamper with a foe's weapon or armor, using a free hand. Choose either a weapon held by an enemy in your reach or a suit of armor worn by an enemy in your reach. Attempt a Crafting check against the enemy's Reflex DC. Critical Success Your tampering is incredibly effective. If you tampered with a weapon, the enemy takes a –2 circumstance penalty to attack rolls and damage rolls with that weapon. If you tampered with armor, the armor hampers the enemy's movement, making the enemy flat-footed and inflicting a –10-foot penalty to its Speeds. The effect lasts until the enemy Interacts to remove it, regardless of which one you used. Success Your tampering is temporarily effective. As critical success, but the effect ends at the start of your next turn, even if the enemy doesn't Interact to end it. Critical Failure Your tampering backfires dramatically, creating a small explosion from your own tools or gear. You take fire damage equal to your level.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Tamper",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3049#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3051",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Collapse Armor"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3051#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You've modified your armor innovation to collapse into a more compact form so you can don or remove it in an instant. If you’re wearing your innovation when you Collapse your Armor, you remove it instantly, and it compresses into its compact form, after which it latches onto your body, typically by attaching to a belt, bandoleer, or other convenient carrying surface as a nondescript satchel. If your armor is stowed and carried on your person in its compact form when you take this action, it unfolds back into its armor form onto your body. In compact form, your armor innovation is easier to carry, with a Bulk 1 lower than the Bulk listed for it, to a minimum of light Bulk (carried armor normally has a Bulk 1 higher than listed in the armor entry).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-armor-innovation",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Collapse Armor",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Modification"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3051#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3054",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Searing Restoration"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3054#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "They told you there was no way that explosions could heal people, but they were fools… Fools who didn't understand your brilliance! You create a minor explosion from your innovation, altering the combustion to cauterize wounds using vaporized medicinal herbs. You or a living creature adjacent to you regains 1d10 Hit Points. In addition, the creature you heal can attempt an immediate flat check to recover from a single source of persistent bleed damage, with the DC reduction from appropriate assistance. At 3rd level, and every 2 levels thereafter, increase the healing by 1d10.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Searing Restoration",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Unstable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3054#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3055",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced Construct Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've upgraded your construct companion's power and decision-making ability. It becomes an advanced construct companion. During an encounter, even if you don't use the Command a Construct action, your construct companion can still use 1 action on your turn that round to Stride or Strike.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-construct-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced Construct Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3057",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dual-Form Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've built your innovation with replaceable interlocking pieces that you can use to transform it into another type of weapon entirely. When you select this feat, choose a level 0 or 1st-level simple or martial weapon. It must be either a common weapon or another to which you have access. This weapon becomes your innovation's second configuration. Select a new set of weapon modifications for this new configuration. You can spend two Interact actions to switch your weapon innovation between the two configurations. These actions don't need to be taken consecutively, but if you've provided the first and not the second, the weapon is non-functional as it is stranded between states. Your weapon's Bulk is always the greater Bulk of the two configurations, regardless of which configuration it's in—if one weapon is smaller than the other, you still need to keep any weapon parts on hand. Any runes on your weapon innovation affect the second weapon configuration as long as it would normally qualify for them.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-weapon-innovation-expert-overdrive",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Dual-Form Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor",
            "aonprd:Trait-Modification"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3059",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Megaton Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3059#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You activate gears, explosives, and other hidden mechanisms in your innovation to make a powerful attack. You make a Strike, dealing an extra die of weapon damage. If you're at least 10th level, increase this to two extra dice, and if you're at least 18th level, increase it to three extra dice. The type of Strike you can make depends on your innovation. Armor You Strike with a melee unarmed attack or a melee weapon. To use a melee weapon for this, you must have prepared it in advance with special contraptions when you make your daily preparations.Construct Your minion innovation Strikes.Weapon You Strike with your weapon innovation. Unstable Function You put even more force into the Strike, though you risk stress fractures to your innovation. Add the unstable trait to Megaton Strike. The Strike deals another extra damage die, for a total of two extra dice at 4th level, three at 10th level, and four at 18th level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-armor-construct-or-weapon-innovation",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Megaton Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3059#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3060",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Clockwork Celerity"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3060#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can use unstable clockwork devices in your innovation to push your invention to act more quickly. You are quickened for this turn. How you can use the extra action depends on your innovation. Armor You can use the extra action to Step, Stride, or use another movement action granted by your innovation (such as Swim if you have the Diving Armor feat).Construct You can use the extra action to Command your construct innovation (or to provide 1 of the actions if you spend 2 actions to Command your construct).Weapon You can use the extra action to Strike with your innovation or Reload your innovation.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-armor-construct-or-weapon-innovation",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Clockwork Celerity",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Unstable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3060#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3062",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Megavolt"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3062#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You bleed off some electric power from your innovation in the shape of a damaging bolt. Creatures in a 20-foot line from your innovation take 3d4 electricity damage, with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. The electricity damage increases by 1d4 at 8th level and every 2 levels thereafter. Unstable Function You overload and supercharge the voltage even higher. Add the unstable trait to Megavolt. The area increases to a 60-foot line and the damage increases from d4s to d12s. If you have the breakthrough innovation class feature, you can choose a 60-foot or 90-foot line for the area when you use an unstable Megavolt; if you also have the revolutionary innovation class feature, you can choose a 60-foot, 90-foot, or 120-foot line.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Megavolt",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Electricity",
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3062#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3064",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Gigaton Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you use a full-power Megaton Strike, you can knock your foe back. When you succeed at your Strike while using an unstable Megaton Strike, your target must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC. Critical Success The creature is unaffected. Success The creature is pushed back 5 feet. Failure The creature is pushed back 10 feet. Critical Failure The creature is pushed back 20 feet.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-megaton-strike",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Gigaton Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3066",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Manifold Modifications"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've modified your innovation using clever workarounds, so you can include another initial modification without compromising its structure. Your innovation gains an additional initial modification from the list for innovations of its type.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-initial-modification",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Manifold Modifications",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor",
            "aonprd:Trait-Modification"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3070",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Electrify Armor"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3070#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You electrify your armor to punish foes who dare to attack you. For 1 round, any creature that touches you, or that hits you with a melee unarmed attack or a non-reach melee weapon attack, takes 1d4 electricity damage. The effect ends if you cease wearing your armor innovation. If you have the revolutionary innovation class feature, the damage increases to 2d4. Unstable Function You create an unstable chain reaction, sending countless sparks dancing across your armor. Add the unstable trait to Electrify Armor. The effects last for 1 minute instead of 1 round, and the damage dice increase from d4s to d12s.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-armor-innovation",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Electrify Armor",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3070#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3071",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Helpful Tinkering"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3071#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You don't just tinker with your own innovation, you fiddle with your allies' weapons as well (for their benefit, of course). Choose an ally in your reach and one of their weapons. Attempt a Crafting check against a high DC for your level. Success For 1 minute, the chosen ally's Strikes with the chosen weapon gain the same offensive boost your innovation has. Critical Failure Your ally takes damage of the type and amount that your offensive boost normally deals on a successful Strike.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-offensive-boost",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Helpful Tinkering",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3071#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3076",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Gigavolt"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you unleash electricity from your innovation, you can bounce it off obstacles, creating a field of electric death. When you use Megavolt, each time your line of electricity hits a solid barrier, such as a wall, it bounces off at an angle of your choice and continues until you have reached the full length of the line. Even if a creature is in the area from multiple bounces, it takes the damage only once.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-megavolt",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Gigavolt",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3081",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unstable Redundancies"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3081#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You've built triple redundancies into your innovation and added all sorts of buffers to protect it from the harm of your unstable experiments. You automatically succeed at the triggering flat check. You can't rely on your Unstable Redundancies again until you spend 10 minutes setting them back up. If you spend 10 minutes retuning your innovation so you can use unstable actions again, you can set up your Unstable Redundancies during the same time.",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Unstable Redundancies",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3081#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3083",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Persistent Boost"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your innovation sets foes on fire, covers them in acid, leaves barbed thorns behind, or otherwise deals persistent damage to your foes that sticks around long after you deliver your boosted attack. When you or your construct innovation damage a foe with offensive boost, that foe also takes 1d8 persistent damage of the same damage type as the offensive boost damage.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-offensive-boost",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Persistent Boost",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3085",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Devastating Weaponry"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3085#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You release a volley of projectiles from your weapon, or power it to fly in every direction across the battlefield and Strike multiple creatures. Make a Strike with your weapon innovation against each foe within 30 feet of you. Don't increase your multiple attack penalty until after making all the attacks. If your innovation is a melee weapon and any of the attacks are outside your reach, you Release the weapon before the Strikes, and it returns to your grasp after all of them. If your hands are full when the weapon returns, it falls to the ground in your space. As normal, if your weapon innovation requires one or more actions to reload between Strikes, you can't use it to make multiple attacks with Devastating Weaponry.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-weapon-innovation",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Devastating Weaponry",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Inventor"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3085#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=311",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Animal Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the service of a young animal companion that travels with you on your adventures and obeys any simple commands you give it to the best of its abilities. See Animal Companions for more information. Ranger: When you Hunt Prey, your animal companion gains the action's benefits and your hunter's edge benefit if you have one.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-animal-order",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Animal Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=312",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Leshy Familiar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You call a minor spirit of nature into a plant body, creating a leshy companion to aid you in your spellcasting. You gain a familiar, which has your choice of either the plant or fungus familiar ability; this doesn't count against your usual limit of familiar abilities (typically 2). The spirit you call has a more tenuous connection to its plant body than fully independent leshies, so it is Tiny in size like other familiars.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-leaf-order",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Leshy Familiar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=314",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Storm Born"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are at home out in the elements, reveling in the power of nature unleashed. You do not take circumstance penalties to ranged spell attacks or Perception checks caused by weather, and your targeted spells don’t require a flat check to succeed against a target concealed by weather (such as fog).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-storm-order",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Storm Born",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=315",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Widen Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=315#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You manipulate the energy of your spell, causing it to spread out and affect a wider area. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that has an area of a burst, cone, or line and does not have a duration, increase the area of that spell. Add 5 feet to the radius of a burst that normally has a radius of at least 10 feet (a burst with a smaller radius is not affected). Add 5 feet to the length of a cone or line that is normally 15 feet long or smaller, and add 10 feet to the length of a larger cone or line.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Widen Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=315#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3155",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cover Fire"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3155#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You lay down suppressive fire to protect allies by forcing foes to take cover from your wild attacks. Make a firearm or crossbow Strike; the target must decide before you roll your attack whether it will duck out of the way. If the target ducks, it gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against your attack, or a +4 circumstance bonus to AC if it has cover. It also takes a –2 circumstance penalty to ranged attack rolls until the end of its next turn. If the target chooses not to duck, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your attack roll for that Strike.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Cover Fire",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Gunslinger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3155#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3158",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Munitions Crafter"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Bullets and bombs can be scarce in some parts, so you’ve learned to make your own. You become trained in Crafting and gain the advanced alchemy benefits. You can use the advanced alchemy benefits to create a number of daily consumables equal to 4 + half your level (rounded up); these consumables must be bombs or alchemical ammunition. You gain a formula book that includes the formula for black powder and four 1st-level types of common or uncommon alchemical ammunition or bombs of your choice. When crafting alchemical ammunition, including black powder in doses or rounds, using advanced alchemy, you create the ammunition in batches of 4 (meaning that if you were 4th level and used all of your advanced alchemy consumables to create alchemical ammunition, you could create a maximum of 24 rounds). You cannot use advanced alchemy to Craft horns or kegs of black powder.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Munitions Crafter",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Gunslinger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3159",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sword and Pistol"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You're comfortable wielding a firearm or crossbow in one hand and a melee weapon in the other, combining melee attacks with shots from the firearm. When you make a successful ranged Strike against an enemy within your reach with your one-handed firearm or one-handed crossbow, that enemy is flat-footed against your next melee attack with a one-handed melee weapon. When you make a successful melee Strike against an enemy with your one-handed melee weapon, the next ranged Strike you make against that enemy with a one-handed firearm or one-handed crossbow doesn't trigger reactions that would trigger on a ranged attack but not a melee attack, such as Reactive Strike. Either of these benefits is lost if not used by the end of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Sword and Pistol",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Gunslinger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=316",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Untamed Form"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are one with the wild, always changing and adapting to meet any challenge. You gain the untamed form order spell, which lets you transform into a variety of shapes that you can expand with druid feats.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-untamed-order",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Untamed Form",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3161",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fake Out"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3161#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With a skilled flourish of your weapon, you force an enemy to acknowledge you as a threat. Make an attack roll to Aid the triggering attack. If you dealt damage to that enemy with the same weapon since the start of your last turn, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to this roll.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Fake Out",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Gunslinger",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3161#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3162",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Pistol Twirl"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3162#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your quick gestures and flair for performance distract your opponent, leaving it vulnerable to your follow-up attacks. You Feint against an opponent within the required weapon’s first range increment, rather than an opponent within melee reach. If you succeed, the foe is off-guard against your melee and ranged attacks, rather than only your melee attacks. On a critical failure, you’re off-guard against the target’s melee and ranged attacks, rather than only its melee attacks.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Pistol Twirl",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Gunslinger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3162#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3163",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Risky Reload"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3163#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You've practiced a technique for rapidly reloading your firearm, but attempting to use this technique is a dangerous gamble with your firearm's functionality. Interact to reload a firearm, then make a Strike with that firearm. If the Strike fails, the firearm misfires.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Risky Reload",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Gunslinger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3163#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3165",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemical Shot"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3165#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You've practiced a technique for mixing alchemical bombs with your loaded shot. You Interact to retrieve the bomb (if it's not already in your hand) and pour its contents onto your ammunition, consuming the bomb, then resume your grip on the required weapon. Next, Strike with your firearm. The Strike deals damage of the same type as the bomb (for instance, fire damage for alchemist's fire), and it deals an additional 1d6 persistent damage of the same type as the bomb. If the Strike is a failure, you take 1d6 damage of the same type as the bomb you used, and the firearm misfires. The persistent damage increases to 2d6 if the bomb is 11th level or higher, or 3d6 if it's 17th level or higher.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemical Shot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Gunslinger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3165#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3166",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Black Powder Boost or [two-actions]"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3166#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You fire your weapon as you jump, using the kickback to go farther. You Leap and discharge your firearm to add a +10-foot status bonus to the distance traveled. If you spend 2 actions for Black Powder Boost, you High Jump or Long Jump instead.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Black Powder Boost or [two-actions]",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Gunslinger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3166#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3168",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Paired Shots"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3168#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your shots hit simultaneously. Make two Strikes, one with each of your two ranged weapons, each using your current multiple attack penalty. Both Strikes must have the same target. If both attacks hit, combine their damage and then add any applicable effects from both weapons. You add any precision damage, only once, to the attack of your choice. Combine the damage from both Strikes and apply resistances and weaknesses only once. This counts as two attacks when calculating your multiple attack penalty.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Paired Shots",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Gunslinger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3168#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=317",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Call of the Wild"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You call upon the creatures of nature to come to your aid. You can spend 10 minutes in concert with nature to replace a spell you’ve prepared in one of your druid spell slots with a summon animal or summon plant or fungus spell of the same rank.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Call of the Wild",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=318",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Enhanced Familiar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You infuse your familiar with additional primal energy, increasing its abilities. You can select four familiar or master abilities each day, instead of two.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-a-familiar",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Enhanced Familiar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=321",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Form Control"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=321#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With additional care and effort, you can take on an alternate shape for a longer period of time. If your next action is to cast untamed form, the spell’s rank is 2 lower than normal (minimum 1st rank), but you can remain transformed for up to 1 hour or the listed duration (whichever is longer). You can still Dismiss untamed form as normal.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-untamed-form",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Form Control",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=321#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=325",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Forest Passage"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can always find a path, almost as if foliage parted before you. You ignore any difficult terrain caused by plants and fungi, such as bushes, vines, and undergrowth.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-leaf-order",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Forest Passage",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=326",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Plant Empathy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have a connection to flora that allows you to communicate with them on a rudimentary level. You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with plants and fungus.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Plant Empathy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3267",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spellshot Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You cast arcane spells like a wizard, gaining a spellbook with four common arcane cantrips of your choice. You gain the Cast a Spell activity. You can prepare two cantrips each day from your spellbook. You’re trained in the spell attack modifier and spell DC statistics. Your key spellcasting attribute for spellshot archetype spells is Intelligence, and they are arcane spells. You become trained in Arcana; if you were already trained in Arcana, you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. This counts as the wizard archetype for the benefits of Basic Wizard Spellcasting.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-way-of-the-spellshot",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Spellshot Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Class",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3268",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fulminating Shot"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3268#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You channel potent magic into your next shot, empowering it with a blast of crackling energy. Choose acid, cold, electricity, or fire. If you hit with your next attack roll using a firearm or crossbow before the end of your turn, you deal 1d6 additional damage of this type. At 12th level, this increases to 2d6 additional damage, and at 18th level, it increases to 3d6 additional damage.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-spellshot-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Fulminating Shot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3268#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=327",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Insect Shape"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your understanding of life expands, allowing you to mimic a wider range of creatures. Add the shapes in insect form to your untamed form list. Whenever you use untamed form to polymorph into the non-flying insect shapes listed in pest form, the duration is 24 hours instead of 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-untamed-form",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Insect Shape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=329",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Storm Retribution"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=329#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You lash out, directing a burst of storming fury toward a creature that has harmed you. You cast tempest surge on the triggering opponent and push that creature, moving it 5 feet away from you if it fails its Reflex save, or 10 feet if it critically fails. This movement is forced movement.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-storm-order-tempest-surge-order-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Storm Retribution",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=329#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3329",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Executioner Weapon Training"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your Gray Gardener training has made you deeply skilled with the weapons that execute with a swift chop to the neck. You become trained with the following weapons: battle axe, falchion, greataxe, and scimitar. Whenever you gain a class feature that grants you expert or greater proficiency with a given weapon or weapons, you also gain that proficiency for these weapons.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-vigilante-dedication-member-of-the-gray-gardeners",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Executioner Weapon Training",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=333",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Soaring Shape"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Wings free you from the shackles of the ground below. Add the bat and bird shapes in aerial form to your untamed form list. If you have Insect Shape, you also add the wasp shape to your untamed form list. If you have Ferocious Shape, you also add the pterosaur shape to your untamed form list. Whenever you use untamed form to take a shape that grants you a specific Acrobatics modifier, you gain a +1 status bonus to Acrobatics checks.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-untamed-form",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Soaring Shape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3330",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Harsh Judgment"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3330#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Choose one creature you can see, and loudly declare the creature's life forfeit by your judgment. That creature becomes your condemned foe until they are defeated, you use Harsh Judgment on a different creature, or the encounter ends. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to Seek your condemned foe and on Intimidation checks to Demoralize them. You have a –1 circumstance penalty to Perception checks to Seek creatures other than your condemned foe and on Intimidation checks to Demoralize anyone other than your condemned foe. You typically can use Harsh Judgment only during an encounter, and if you try to use it to declare someone's life forfeit during exploration or downtime, you are likely to start an encounter.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-vigilante-dedication-member-of-the-gray-gardeners",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Harsh Judgment",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vigilante"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3330#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3331",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Voice of Authority"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You easily command the attention of others, and when the time comes to turn threats into action, your authoritative voice causes foes to falter. Your voice can be heard easily by any creatures within 300 feet if you wish, regardless of the level of ambient noise, although your voice can't penetrate silence or similar efect. If you roll Intimidation for initiative, on the frst round of combat, creatures that haven't acted yet are flat-footed to you.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-intimidation-vigilante-dedication-member-of-the-gray-gardeners",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Voice of Authority",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vigilante"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3332",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Discerning Gaze"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have a sense for when people are lying. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus on your secret Perception checks to Sense Motive. If you use Sense Motive on a creature you have currently condemned with Harsh Judgment, your GM rolls the Perception check twice and takes the higher result (this is a fortune effect).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-vigilante-dedication-member-of-the-gray-gardeners",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Discerning Gaze",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3333",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Frightful Condemnation"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3333#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your willingness to follow through on your pitiless judgment is frightful to the person you have condemned, and they begin to dread what you will do to them next. Your condemned foe is frightened 1, or frightened 2 if the triggering Strike was a critical hit.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-harsh-judgment-vigilante-dedication-member-of-the-gray-gardeners",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Frightful Condemnation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fear",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vigilante"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3333#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3334",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Accurate Swing"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You strike cleanly with wide, sweeping attacks to inflict maximum damage, taking advantage of your judged foe's fear to land a felling blow. If you Strike a creature you condemned with Harsh Judgment that has the frightened condition with a sweep melee weapon or a sweep unarmed attack, you gain a circumstance bonus to the Strike's damage equal to the number of weapon damage dice your weapon deals.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-vigilante-dedication-harsh-judgment-member-of-the-gray-gardeners",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Accurate Swing",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vigilante"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3335",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Gardener's Resolve"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3335#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The Gray Gardeners are known for having nerves of steel and an unbreakable resolve. When you would be overwhelmed by terror, you can draw upon this resolve to keep your composure and remain undaunted. You take mental damage equal to twice your level, and the saving throw is a success.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-vigilante-dedication-member-of-the-gray-gardeners",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Gardener's Resolve",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vigilante"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3335#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3336",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reminder of the Greater Fear"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3336#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You give a target a stern glower to remind them that it is you, and no one else, they should truly fear. Reduce the value of the frightened condition the creature would take by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-intimidation-vigilante-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Reminder of the Greater Fear",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vigilante"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3336#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3337",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Strident Command"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The common folk heed your demands, and though your true foes rarely bend to your commands, when they do the hesitation can cost them the battle. You can cast command once every 10 minutes as a 1st-level occult innate spell. If you're in your vigilante identity, you can command the target only to approach you, drop prone, or stand in place. If you're in your social identity, you can command the target only to run away or release what the target is holding.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-intimidation-vigilante-dedication-voice-of-authority-member-of-the-gray-gardeners",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Strident Command",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3338",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Execution"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3338#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You swing wide, attempting to behead your condemned foe. Make a melee Strike against your condemned foe. If you hit, your condemned foe takes 8d6 extra precision damage with a basic Fortitude save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. If the condemned foe is reduced to 0 Hit Points by the execution and requires a head to live, they die. For creatures with multiple heads, this usually kills the creature only if you sever its last head. The creature then becomes temporarily immune to your Execution for 1 day.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-harsh-judgment-vigilante-dedication-member-of-the-gray-gardeners",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Execution",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vigilante"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3338#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3339",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Terrifying Countenance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3339#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can erect a magical cowl that terrorizes your enemies. Once per day, you can cast mask of terror as an innate occult spell, targeting yourself. If you critically hit a creature that's temporarily immune to the spell, the creature's temporary immunity ends.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-vigilante-dedication-member-of-the-gray-gardeners",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Terrifying Countenance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vigilante"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3339#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=334",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Wind Caller"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You bid the winds to aid you, carrying you through the air and allowing you passage through the strongest headwinds. You gain the stormwind flight order spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-storm-order",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Wind Caller",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=338",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Plant Shape"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can take the shape of a plant creature. If you don't have untamed form, you can cast plant form once per day, heightened to the same rank as your highest-rank druid spell slot. If you do have untamed form, add the shapes listed in plant form to your untamed form list, and whenever you're polymorphed into another shape using untamed form, you gain resistance 5 to poison.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-leaf-order-or-untamed-form",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Plant Shape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3406",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cloud Walk"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your growing link to cloud dragons has granted you the ability to walk on clouds. Once per hour, you can cast air walk on yourself as an innate arcane spell, but only to walk on clouds or fog.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dragon-disciple-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Cloud Walk",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3407",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shape of the Cloud Dragon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've discovered how to transform yourself into a cloud dragon. Once per day, you can cast 7th-level dragon form as an innate arcane spell, transforming into a cloud dragon. The spell automatically heightens to 8th level if you're 16th level and 9th level if you're 18th level. On a critical hit with an unarmed Strike gained from dragon form, you recharge the spell's breath weapon immediately. While in this form, you gain the following cloud dragon–specific abilities: Cloud cloud walk (you can walk on clouds or fog); Melee [one-action] jaws, Damage 2d10 piercing plus 1d12 electricity; Melee [one-action] claw (agile), Damage 3d10 slashing; Melee [one-action] tail (reach 10 feet), Damage 3d10 bludgeoning; Melee [one-action] horn (reach 10 feet), Damage 3d8 piercing; breath weapon 30-foot cone, 6d12 electricity.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dragon-disciple-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Shape of the Cloud Dragon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3408",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Deflecting Cloud"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3408#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You've mastered a defensive technique unique to the ancient dragons of Bloodsalt: beating your wings to create a billowing cloud of mist. You become momentarily hidden from the triggering attack if vision is the attacker's only precise sense. Normally this means the attacker must succeed at a DC 11 flat check to target you. You also gain a +4 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dragon-disciple-dedication-dragon-wings-sorcerer-bloodline-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Deflecting Cloud",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3408#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3409",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mighty Wings"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your dragon wings are now a permanent part of your body, giving you a fly Speed equal to your Speed. If you spend 1 Focus Point to cast dragon wings, your fly Speed increases to 90 feet for the duration, unless your Speed is faster, and you gain the effects of dragon claws for the duration.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dragon-disciple-dedication-dragon-wings-sorcerer-bloodline-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Mighty Wings",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=341",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Green Tongue"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You share a special kinship with all things green and living. You (and your leshy familiar, if you have one) are constantly under the effects of speak with plants. Most non-creature plants recognize you as a druid of the leaf order and are friendly to you.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-green-empathy",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Green Tongue",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3410",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Blessing of the Sun Gods"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The Old Sun Gods share their power with you. Select the ambition, cities, darkness, dreams, family, fire, freedom, healing, moon, passion, or sun domain. You gain an initial domain spell for that domain. If you don't already have one, you gain a focus pool of 1 Focus Point, which you can regain using the Refocus activity to pray to the Old Sun Gods; if you already have a focus pool, increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1. Your Bright Lion focus spells are divine spells; you become trained in divine spell attacks and spell DCs, using Charisma as your spellcasting ability score.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bright-lion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Blessing of the Sun Gods",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3411",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lion's Might"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've trained with the weapons of the Bright Lions. You gain access to lion scythes and sun slings. Whenever you gain a class feature that grants you expert or greater proficiency in certain weapons, you also gain that proficiency rank with lion scythes and sun slings.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bright-lion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Lion's Might",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3412",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lion's Fury"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain access to the lion scythe's and sun sling's critical specialization effects.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-lions-might",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Lion's Fury",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3413",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Greater Sun Blessing"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your connection to the Old Sun Gods grows stronger. You gain an advanced domain spell from a domain you chose with Blessing of the Sun Gods. Increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-blessing-of-the-sun-gods",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Greater Sun Blessing",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=342",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Primal Focus"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your connection to nature is particularly strong, and the spirits of nature flock around you, helping you replenish your focus. Whenever you Refocus, completely refill your focus pool.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Primal Focus",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3422",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "All of the Animal"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You know how to make the best and most efficient use of a hunted animal's carcass. Choose a Large or larger corpse of an animal that died within the past day. While using Survival to Subsist near the carcass, you always receive enough food for yourself and one additional Medium creature, using up the meat from the carcass to do so. Since you're using all of the animal, others can't use the carcass's meat for any other purpose, including their own use of All of the Animal.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-survival",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "All of the Animal",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3423",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spirit Speaker"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You know that when an animal dies, its spirit lingers briefly before moving on. Using low chants, body language that shows respect, and special movements that demonstrate to the spirit that you are an ally, you glean information from a spirit before it departs. This is a 1-minute activity. You must begin the activity while adjacent to the body of an animal or beast that died within the last 1 minute. As part of the activity, you ask one simple question of the spirit. Attempt a Nature check at a DC determined by the GM (normally, this is the appropriate DC for the level of the animal or beast when it was alive). Regardless of the result of your check, the spirit immediately departs and can't be used for Spirit Speaker again. If the creature had the confused or frightened condition when it died, you can't get a result better than a critical failure. Only one creature can use Spirit Speaker on a given dead animal, as the effort takes the spirit's full attention. Critical Success The spirit answers you truthfully. The spirit's answer is likely to be terse or cryptic compared to normal communication with an animal, and it can pertain only to things the creature directly experienced or considered important. The spirit doesn't remember anything that happened more than 1 day ago. Success As critical success, but the spirit doesn't recall anything that happened more than 1 hour ago. Failure The spirit doesn't answer you. Critical Failure The spirit is wracked with misery or bewilderment and gives you an erroneous answer.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-nature",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Spirit Speaker",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Necromancy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Secret",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3424",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tame Animal"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Animals born and raised far from humanoid settlements rarely get along with two-legged beings, whom they assume to be dangerous predators. In spite of this, you know how to approach and entreat a wild animal so that it's more receptive to your presence and requests. To use this feat, choose a wild animal that isn't actively hostile to you and which isn't confined to an area smaller than its Speed in diameter (animals held in place or trapped are typically too scared to be tamed). Attempt a Nature check against a DC determined by the GM; this is usually the animal's Will DC, but circumstances might adjust the precise DC. This attempt usually takes an hour, but you can perform it in 10 minutes if you have expert proficiency in Nature, 1 minute if you have master proficiency, or as a three-action activity if you have legendary proficiency. Critical Success You form a friendly bond with the animal. As long as it isn't starving, the animal won't attack you or creatures obviously allied with you, even if they're creatures the animal would normally prey upon. This effect is permanent. Success As critical success, but the effect lasts for 1 month. If you or an ally teach the animal a basic action during that time with the Train Animal skill feat, the effect is permanent. Failure You fail to make any kind of meaningful impression on the animal. Critical Failure The animal does its best to attack you and is immune to Tame Animal for 1 month.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-nature",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Tame Animal",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exploration",
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3425",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Game Hunter Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are skilled at tracking big game animals and similar creatures. You gain the Hunt Prey action, but you can designate only animals, beasts, and dragons as prey. In addition to the other benefits of Hunt Prey, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Stealth checks against your hunted prey. When you succeed at a Strike against your hunted prey while it's flat-footed, it must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC. On a failure, the prey's Speeds are each reduced by 10 feet for 1 round; on a critical failure, the duration of this effect is 1 minute. The prey is then temporarily immune to this effect for 10 minutes. If you already have Hunt Prey, you become an expert in Survival. You apply the Stealth bonus and the Speed reduction only when your prey is an animal, beast, or dragon.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-survival",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Game Hunter Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3426",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Big Game Trapper"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can set snares specifically for big prey, leaving smaller creatures unscathed. Each time you set a snare, you can choose Small, Medium, Large, or Huge. That snare can be triggered only by creatures of that size or larger.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-game-hunter-dedication-snare-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Big Game Trapper",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3427",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Keep Pace"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3427#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "When your hunted prey tries to bolt, you follow. You Stride up to your Speed, following your hunted prey and keeping it in reach throughout its movement until it stops moving or you've moved your full Speed. You can use Keep Pace to Burrow, Climb, Fly, or Swim instead of Stride if you have the appropriate movement type.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-game-hunter-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Keep Pace",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3427#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3428",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Positioning"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3428#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You're always ready to get the jump on your target. You Step up to twice.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-game-hunter-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Positioning",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3428#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3429",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Pyrophilic Recovery"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You rely on fire and extreme heat to sprout and regrow. Whenever you take fire damage, at the beginning of your next turn, you regain Hit Points equal to half your character level (minimum 1). The total number of Hit Points you recover in this way, including any adjustments that increase the effects of healing, can't exceed half the Hit Points you lost from the fire damage you took. For example, if an effect deals 15 fire damage and you have fire resistance 5, you would take 10 fire damage and Pyrophilic Recovery could recover at most 5 Hit Points, regardless of any other effects that increase healing. If you take fire damage more than once before your next turn, the Hit Points recovered from Pyrophilic Recovery are cumulative, though still no more than half the fire damage taken each time.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Pyrophilic Recovery",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Leshy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3430",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Climate Adaptation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Like evergreen trees, which stay healthy and vibrant from winter through summer, you too can adapt to a variety of extreme climates. You're unaffected by mild cold or heat environmental effects, and when you're in severe cold or heat, you take the effects of mild cold or heat instead (see Table 10–13). This doesn't protect you from extreme or incredible cold or heat.",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Climate Adaptation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Leshy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3431",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Defensive Needles"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your body is covered in sharp needles or spines which you can use to defend yourself. Each time you become grabbed by a creature or an adjacent creature hits you with an unarmed attack, you twist and thrash your body around, dealing 2 piercing damage to that creature. This damage increases to 3 at 9th level, 4 at 13th level, and 5 at 17th level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-cactus-leshy-or-pine-leshy",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Defensive Needles",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Leshy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3432",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Towering Growth"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You're capable of growing as tall as a pine tree for a short time. You gain 2nd-level enlarge as a primal innate spell. You can cast this spell twice per day and you must target yourself.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-pine-leshy",
          "aonprd:level": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Towering Growth",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Leshy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3433",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cunning Trickster Mask"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mask carries the legacy of Verdant Spider, the Speaker of Needs, allowing you to deceive and outwit your foes. You can attempt to Feint a target from up to 30 feet away, and if you succeed or critically succeed in your Feint attempt, the target of your Feint takes a –2 circumstance penalty to saving throws against your spells until the start of your next turn. If you don't have the Conceal Spell feat, you gain it as a bonus feat, allowing you to disguise your spellcasting from others' eyes. If you already have the Conceal Spell feat, you can use Conceal Spell once per round as a free action instead of as a single action.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-dedication-or-wizard-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Cunning Trickster Mask",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3434",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Emancipator's Mask"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mask grants you the abilities of Whistling Kite, the Vigilant Seer, who emancipated thousands. When you are attempting a check to free someone else from an effect that immobilizes, paralyzes, or controls them, roll twice and take the higher result; this is a fortune effect. The GM might decide that this fortune effect applies when attempting checks to remove other conditions or effects to free another. Immediately after you Cast a non-cantrip Spell that targets only one creature, you can choose to permit the target to make an attempt to Escape.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-dedication-or-wizard-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Emancipator's Mask",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3435",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Grand Medic's Mask"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mask is infused with restorative magic associated with Ibex, the Flourishing Field, so it constantly repairs itself. You gain fast healing 5. If you lose a limb or other body part, it regrows within 1 day. Immediately after you Cast a non-cantrip Spell that targets only one creature, you can choose to have the spell also give that creature temporary Hit Points equal to the spell's level until the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-dedication-or-wizard-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Grand Medic's Mask",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3436",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Protective Spirit Mask"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mask carries the protective instincts of White Bull, the Horn Forger, and no one will hurt your allies while you have anything to say about it. Immediately after you Cast a non-cantrip Spell that targets only one ally, you can choose to have the spell also give that creature a +1 circumstance bonus to AC until the start of your next turn. You also gain the Protector's Interdiction reaction. Protector's Interdiction [reaction] Trigger An adjacent ally is hit or critically hit by an attack; Effect You interpose yourself between your ally and the attack. The attack hits you instead, or critically hits you if it critically hit your ally.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-dedication-or-wizard-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Protective Spirit Mask",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3437",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sky Master Mask"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mask holds the legacy of Black Heron, the Wings of Knowledge, who united the aeromancers of the Shory Empire. You can harness residual magical power to fly. You gain a fly Speed equal to your Speed. Immediately after you Cast a non-cantrip Spell that targets only you, your fly Speed doubles until your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-dedication-or-wizard-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Sky Master Mask",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3438",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stalking Feline Mask"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Like Azure Leopard, the Patient Warden, your mask makes you most at home in the night and teaches you how to use the darkness to hunt. You gain greater darkvision. Immediately after you Cast a non-cantrip Spell with the shadow or darkness trait, you can attempt to Hide or Sneak as a free action. You must still meet the usual requirements of the action you choose, such as having cover or concealment to Hide and being undetected or hidden to Sneak.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-dedication-or-wizard-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Stalking Feline Mask",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3439",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Storyteller's Mask"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mask remembers the stories of Shifting Frog, Storyteller of the Past and Future. You can cast foresight once per day as an innate spell, either arcane if you have Wizard Dedication or primal if you have Druid Dedication, but the duration is 10 minutes instead of 1 hour. Immediately after you Cast a non-cantrip Spell that targets only a single foe, you can Recall Knowledge about that foe.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-dedication-or-wizard-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Storyteller's Mask",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3440",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Thick Hide Mask"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mask grants you the toughness of Elephant, the Conjured Chronicle. Increase your maximum number of Hit Points by 20. Immediately after you Cast a non-cantrip Spell that targets only you, you gain resistance 10 to all physical damage until the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-dedication-or-wizard-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Thick Hide Mask",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3441",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tireless Guide's Mask"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mask hosts the legacy of Golden Snake, the Tireless Guide, allowing you to guide others with ease. Your allies can use Follow the Expert to follow you for any of your trained skills, in addition to skills in which you are an expert or better. When they follow you when you use a trained skill, their circumstance bonus is +1. Immediately after you Cast a non-cantrip Spell that targets only one ally, that ally can Stride as a free action.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-dedication-or-wizard-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Tireless Guide's Mask",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3442",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vigilant Mask"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mask grants the extraordinary magical senses of Carmine Jaws, the Hyena who Looks Between. You gain scent as a precise sense to a range of 60 feet. If you already have scent as a precise sense, increase its range by 60 feet. You can sometimes catch a faint whiff of magic itself. Immediately after you Cast a non-cantrip Spell, your scent extends between worlds, like Carmine Jaws's own. This causes you to be able to smell ethereal creatures, those in an extradimensional space with an aperture that's within your scent range, incorporeal creatures and objects, and other creatures and objects that are insubstantial or not fully in phase with reality. Unlike your normal scent, this is an imprecise sense.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-dedication-or-wizard-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Vigilant Mask",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3443",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mammoth Lord Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've undertaken the ultimate challenge of the Mammoth Lords and tamed a megafauna. You gain a megafauna you tamed as a young animal companion. Your megafauna animal companion must be a megafauna appropriate to the Realm of the Mammoth Lords; see the What Counts as Megafauna? sidebar for guidance and examples. While an animal companion usually starts as Small, you can begin with a Medium version of that animal (changing no statistics other than its size). Contrary to the usual rules for animal companions, this feat can give you a second animal companion. If you have more than one animal companion, you can adventure with only one of them at a time. You can switch between them like a beastmaster does. You gain the Call Companion action, as the beastmaster archetype, and you follow all the other rules found in the Call Companion sidebar.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ride",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Mammoth Lord Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3444",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mammoth Charge"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3444#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You Command an Animal to order your megafauna companion to Stride twice. At any point during this movement, you can make a melee Strike against one enemy within reach.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mammoth-lord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Mammoth Charge",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3444#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3445",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mature Megafauna Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've raised your megafauna companion to be a more powerful force on the battlefield than most of its kind. The companion you gained through the Mammoth Lord Dedication feat becomes a mature animal companion, granting it additional capabilities. During an encounter, even if you don't use the Command an Animal action, your megafauna animal companion can still use 1 action on your turn to Stride or Strike.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mammoth-lord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Mature Megafauna Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3446",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Megafauna Veterinarian"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "By heeding the wise advice of elders in your following— and aided by your own experience—you've learned how to provide medical care to the megafauna of the Mammoth Lord followings. You can attempt a Nature check instead of a Medicine check for any of Medicine's trained and untrained uses, provided the subject of your medical care is a megafauna. If you're attempting an action that requires a particular proficiency rank in Medicine (such as Treat Wounds), use your proficiency rank in Nature instead. If the subject of your care is your megafauna and you roll a success on your check, you get a critical success instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mammoth-lord-dedication-expert-in-nature",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Megafauna Veterinarian",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3447",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Speech of the Mammoth Lords"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've learned the ancient tongue spoken by the creatures of the far north. You can ask questions of, receive answers from, use the Diplomacy skill with, and Coerce megafauna. In most cases, megafauna of the Realm of the Mammoth Lords will hear you out.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mammoth-lord-dedication-master-in-diplomacy-or-intimidation",
          "aonprd:level": "7",
          "aonprd:name": "Speech of the Mammoth Lords",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3448",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Incredible Megafauna Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Under your care and training, your megafauna companion has realized its innate potential. Your companion becomes an indomitable or savage animal companion (your choice), gaining additional abilities determined by the type of companion.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mature-megafauna-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Incredible Megafauna Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3449",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stalwart Mind"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3449#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "When necessary to avoid a magical compulsion or curse, you can be as stubborn as your megafauna companion. Attempt a new Will save against the triggering effect.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mammoth-lord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Stalwart Mind",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3449#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3450",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Staggering Blow"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3450#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You've trained your megafauna companion to stagger its enemies, impeding their ability to fight back. You Command an Animal to order your megafauna companion to spend both its actions making a single, powerful Strike. The attack deals an extra die of weapon damage, and if the attack hits and deals damage, the target is slowed 1 until the end of its next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mammoth-lord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Staggering Blow",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3450#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3451",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unbreakable Bond"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You and your megafauna companion are bound together; as long as you live, it's much harder for your companion to die. If your megafauna companion gains the dying condition, it automatically succeeds at the recovery check to stabilize at 0 Hit Points on its turn. Additionally, your megafauna companion only dies at dying 5 rather than dying 4. Finally, the first time each day your megafauna companion would reach dying 5 and die, as long as you're still alive, your companion's dying value decreases to 0 instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mammoth-lord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Unbreakable Bond",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Necromancy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3452",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Gigantic Megafauna Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The mammoths and other megafauna ridden by your people are larger than any ordinary beast. Your megafauna companion increases in size to Huge but doesn't otherwise change its statistics.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mammoth-lord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Gigantic Megafauna Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3453",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Specialized Megafauna Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've trained your mammoth or other megafauna companion to perform in unusual or extreme situations, granting it abilities far beyond others of its kind. Your megafauna gains your choice of the bully, racer, tracker, or wrecker specialization.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mammoth-lord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Specialized Megafauna Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=349",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Monstrosity Shape"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can transform into a powerful magical creature. Add the cave worm and sea serpent shapes listed in monstrosity form to your untamed form list. If you have Soaring Shape, also add the phoenix shape to your untamed form list.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-untamed-form",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Monstrosity Shape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=350",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Invoke Disaster"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can invoke nature’s fury upon your foes. You gain the storm lord order spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-wind-caller",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Invoke Disaster",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3568",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alkenstar Agent Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You put on the persona of a rough and tumble outlaw, but your real goals are to report threats to Alkenstar back to the grand duchess. You become an expert in Deception and trained in your choice of Underworld Lore or Legal Lore; if you were already trained, you become an expert instead. You gain the Lie to Me skill feat.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-at-least-one-firearm-trained-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Alkenstar Agent Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3569",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Loose Cannon"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3569#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your unpredictable gunfire often catches enemies off guard or hits unprotected areas. Make a ranged Strike with a firearm against a creature that you haven't already attacked on this turn. You gain a circumstance bonus to damage on this Strike equal to the number of weapon damage dice. The Strike gains the following failure effect. Failure The firearm misfires, but it doesn't cause the other critical failure effects listed below. Critical Failure The firearm misfires and also explodes. It becomes broken, and it deals its normal weapon damage to all creatures in a 20-foot burst centered on the firearm, with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. This damage includes any from the weapon's fundamental and property runes.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-alkenstar-agent-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Loose Cannon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3569#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3570",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Prepare Papers"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You're practiced at creating forgeries that establish your outlaw credentials or augment your legal authority. You can Create a Forgery as an exploration activity. It takes you about 1 hour per page of the document that you're forging. This time is reduced to 10 minutes per page if you're legendary in Society.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-alkenstar-agent-dedication-master-in-society",
          "aonprd:level": "7",
          "aonprd:name": "Prepare Papers",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3571",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Flash your Badge"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3571#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You make a fearsome show of your authority. Roll Intimidation checks to Demoralize each creature in a 30-foot cone. When you do so, Demoralize gains the visual trait, and creatures are affected if they can see you. If a target creature hasn't broken a law in the past week (as determined by the GM), the result of your check against that creature is one degree of success worse than the result you rolled.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-alkenstar-agent-dedication-master-in-intimidation",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Flash your Badge",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3571#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3572",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Black Powder Flash"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3572#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You ignite a pinch of black powder in a foe's face. Choose an adjacent creature. It must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC. Critical Success The creature is unaffected. Success The creature is dazzled for 1 round. Failure The creature is blinded for 1 round and dazzled for 1 minute. The creature can rub its eyes as an Interact action to end this blinded condition. Critical Failure The creature is blinded for 1 round and dazzled for 1 hour.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-powder-punch-stance",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Black Powder Flash",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3572#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3573",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Inured to Alchemy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've developed control over how your body processes alchemical poisons and drugs. Each of your successful saving throws against an alchemical poison, a drug, or an addiction reduces the stage by 2, or by 1 for a virulent alchemical poison, drug, or addiction. Each critical success reduces the stage by 3, or by 2 for a virulent alchemical poison, drug, or addiction.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-fortitude-saves",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Inured to Alchemy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3574",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Pain Tolerance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain resistance to mental damage equal to half your level and a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against effects that would make you clumsy, drained, or enfeebled.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-fortitude-saves",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Pain Tolerance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3575",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Powder Punch Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You infuse your handwraps with black powder. On your first melee Strike each round with an unarmed attack, knuckle duster, or black powder knuckle duster, you deal an additional 1 fire damage. If you critically succeed at an attempt to Shove while in this stance, the target is pushed back an additional 5 feet.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-martial-artist-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Powder Punch Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3576",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Thunder Clap"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3576#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You slam your hands together to unleash a deafening blast. Creatures in a 15-foot cone take 3d6 sonic damage, with a basic Fortitude save against your class DC. Creatures that critically fail their save are also deafened for 1 minute. You can't use this ability again for 1d4 rounds as your hands recover from the thunderous vibrations. At 8th level, and every 2 levels thereafter, the damage from Thunder Clap increases by 1d6.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-powder-punch-stance",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Thunder Clap",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sonic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3576#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3644",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Glass Skin"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Even if vitrumancy is a mystery to you, your blood and flesh know the secrets of the art of arcane glass. Patches of your skin to flicker into glass without warning. By focusing the effect, you can concentrate the glass into a powerful protective layer of magical obsidian. Once per day, you can cast stoneskin on yourself as an innate primal spell, though the spell covers you in a layer of glass instead of stone. During this innate stoneskin, you gain the Shatter Glass reaction. At 18th level, the stoneskin is heightened to 6th level instead of 4th. Shatter Glass [reaction] Trigger An adjacent creature Strikes you with a melee weapon or unarmed attack and deals damage; Requirements Your innate stoneskin from Glass Skin is active; Effect You shatter some of the glass on your skin to damage your attacker. The attacker takes 3d10 damage and the duration of the stoneskin decreases by 1 minute. At 14th level, the damage increases to 4d10, and at 18th level, the damage increases to 5d10.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-you-were-present-at-the-death-of-the-medusa-alethsia-whose-vitrumantic-powers-were-passed-on-to-you-in-the-wake-of-her-destruction",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Glass Skin",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Abjuration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Aftermath",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3645",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Clockwork Reanimator Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can animate corpses through cunning engineering. You gain a prototype construct companion to serve as a minion. Unlike normal construct companions, yours is a corpse animated by clockwork gears and technological prowess.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Clockwork Reanimator Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3646",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced Reanimated Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your corpselike construct companion becomes much more powerful and can act with limited autonomy to follow your greater directives. It becomes an advanced construct companion. During an encounter, even if you don't use the Command a Minion action, your construct companion can still use 1 action on your turn that round to Stride or Strike.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-clockwork-reanimator-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced Reanimated Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3647",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hijack Undead"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3647#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your clockwork devices can commandeer the bodies of undead, bending them to your will. Make a melee Strike against an adjacent undead creature. On a success, instead of taking damage, the target becomes controlled by you if its level is equal to or lower than your level – 3. It can attempt a Will saving throw against the higher of your class DC or spell DC to resist being controlled by you. If the target is already under someone else's command, the controlling creature also rolls a saving throw, and the undead uses the better result. Critical Success The target is unaffected and temporarily immune for 24 hours. Success The target is unaffected. Failure The undead creature becomes a minion under your control for 1 minute. The control ends if you or an ally attacks the minion undead. Critical Failure As failure, but the duration is 1 hour.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-clockwork-reanimator-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Hijack Undead",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3647#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3648",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "It's Alive!"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've mastered the use of electrical energy to power your clockwork creations. Whenever your construct companion takes electricity damage, it gains temporary Hit Points equal to either half the electricity damage it took or your level, whichever is lower. These temporary Hit Points last for up to 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-clockwork-reanimator-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "It's Alive!",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3649",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Incredible Reanimated Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You imbue the necrotized flesh of your reanimated construct companion with strange chemicals and fine-tune the clockwork within, enhancing all its capabilities. It becomes an incredible construct companion.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-advanced-reanimated-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Incredible Reanimated Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3650",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Self-Destruct"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3650#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You've installed a self-destruct device within your construct companion, which you can trigger with a special device from up to 60 feet away. When you activate the device, your reanimated construct companion explodes, dealing 2d6 fire damage per level to all creatures in a 30-foot radius. Creatures caught in the blast can attempt a basic Reflex save, with a DC equal to the higher of your class DC or spell DC.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-clockwork-reanimator-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Self-Destruct",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3650#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3651",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Improved Hijack Undead"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Undead creatures find it all but impossible to resist your commands. When you use Hijack Undead, if the undead fails its save, it becomes your minion for 10 minutes. If it critically fails, it becomes your minion for 24 hours.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-clockwork-reanimator-dedication-hijack-undead",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Improved Hijack Undead",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3652",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Paragon Reanimated Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have reached the pinnacle of necromantic science, creating a mechanical zombie unlike any the world has seen before. Your reanimated construct companion becomes a paragon construct companion.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-incredible-reanimated-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Paragon Reanimated Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3653",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unwind Death"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3653#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Combining necromancy with the mysterious temporal powers of clockwork, you wind a creature backward from the moment of its death. Attempt a DC 40 Crafting check to revive a dead creature that has been dead for no more than 3 rounds. If you succeed, the target returns to life with the effects of raise dead, except it still has the wounded condition it had before dying, increased by 1 (or wounded 1 if it wasn't wounded before dying). Whether you succeed or fail, the target is then temporarily immune to Unwind Death for 1 day.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-clockwork-reanimator-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Unwind Death",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3653#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3654",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Zombie Horde"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3654#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You built your reanimated construct companion of modular components from various corpses. Its unique makeup enables your companion to split into dozens or even hundreds of much smaller corpse constructs. Acting as one, this shambling swarm can overwhelm your enemies. You Command your reanimated construct companion. Instead of its normal actions, the companion splits into a horde of Small and Tiny construct companions within a 30-foot emanation from its original space. The horde makes a Strike against each foe within the emanation with a +2 circumstance bonus to its attack rolls. The multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after the companion makes all the attacks. The miniature companions recombine into a single companion of their original size at any location within the emanation.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-clockwork-reanimator-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Zombie Horde",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3654#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3660",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mental Balm"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your spells release soothing mental waves. Use this amp in place of a psi cantrip's normal amp entry. You can use this amp only on a psi cantrip that targets or affects you or one or more of your allies and doesn't target or affect any enemies.Amp You or one ally within 30 feet gains a +2 status bonus to Will saves against emotion effects for 1 minute. You can also have the amped psi cantrip attempt to counteract one effect imposing the frightened condition on yourself or the chosen ally, or an effect imposing the stupefied condition that has a duration of 1 hour or less. If you successfully counteract the effect, you remove only the frightened and stupefied conditions, not any other part of the effect.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Mental Balm",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Amp",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3661",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Psi Burst"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3661#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With a passing thought, you direct violent psychic energies at a nearby creature. Target one creature within 30 feet. It takes 1d4 bludgeoning damage with a basic Reflex save. At 3rd level and every 2 levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d4.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Psi Burst",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mindshift",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psyche",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3661#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3662",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Warp Space"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You use your magic to bend space, causing your spell to strike from a strange vector. Use this amp in place of a psi cantrip's normal amp entry. The amped psi cantrip must have a range.Amp Choose a square within 30 feet to which you have line of effect and line of sight. Determine your spell’s line of effect and line of sight from there, as well as whether creatures have cover against the spell. The spell can exceed its normal range as measured from you, as long as it’s within its normal range from the square you chose.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Warp Space",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Amp",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3663",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Astral Tether"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3663#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You spin out a thread of psychic energy that connects you to an ally, using it as a conduit for your abilities. Choose a willing creature within 60 feet and connect to it. Whenever you would gain a benefit from a psychic amp, you can have the amp affect the tethered creature instead. You can do so only if the amp grants a distinct benefit, not if it alters the amped spell. The tether can't be severed physically but breaks if the distance between you and the tethered ally ever exceeds 60 feet, if you become unconscious, or if you use Astral Tether again.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Astral Tether",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3663#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3664",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Homing Beacon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As your spell strikes a target, you plant a beacon in the target's mind that announces its presence to those nearby. Use this amp in place of a psi cantrip's normal amp entry. The amped cantrip must be one that has one or more targets and must either require a spell attack roll or have a saving throw.Amp Choose one creature hit by the spell (if the spell has a spell attack roll) or that fails its save against the spell (if the spell requires a save). A psychic beacon emits from the creature's location, making it easier to notice the creature as the mind and attention of onlookers is subtly drawn to it. For 1 minute, if the target would be invisible, it's instead merely concealed, and if it would be concealed, it's no longer concealed.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Homing Beacon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Amp",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3667",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Violent Unleash"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3667#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The force of your mind unleashing itself releases a violent shock wave that batters your enemies. You deal 2d6 force damage to all creatures in a 20-foot emanation, with a basic Reflex save. At 5th level and every 2 levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d6.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Violent Unleash",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mindshift",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3667#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3671",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Strain Mind"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3671#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You strain your body beyond its limits to use an amp even when your mental power is depleted. You add an amp that costs 1 Focus Point to the spell. Instead of paying the normal Focus Point cost, you lose Hit Points equal to four times the spell rank of the amped psi cantrip as you bleed from your nose or suffer some other visible sign of strain.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Strain Mind",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3671#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3676",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Thoughtsense"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can detect the flickers of mental activity let off by all thinking creatures. You gain thoughtsense as a vague sense that has a range of 30 feet—like all vague senses, it's only about as precise as an average human's sense of smell, meaning you generally can predict only if a creature is present. Your thoughtsense detects only thinking creatures, so a creature that is unthinking or otherwise immune to mental effects (such as many constructs and oozes) can't be perceived using your thoughtsense, regardless of how precise it is. While your Psyche is Unleashed, your thoughtsense upgrades to an imprecise sense, letting you use it to Seek out creatures.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Thoughtsense",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3677",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Whispering Steps"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your spell leaves a lingering connection between you and a creature—one through which you can nudge the creature's mind this way or that. The amped cantrip must take 2 or more actions to cast, target one or more creatures, and either require a spell attack roll or have a saving throw. Use this amp in place of the psi cantrip's normal amp entry.Amp Choose one enemy who is a target of the spell. If that enemy fails its save or the spell hits it, you whisper in the creature's mind, forcing it to Stride up to half its Speed in a direction of your choosing; as this is forced movement, you can't force the creature to move into hazardous terrain, off a ledge, or the like. After it moves, the creature becomes temporarily immune to this amp for 24 hours.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Whispering Steps",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Amp",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3699",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Diverse Lore"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your wandering studies mean you've heard rumors or theories about almost every topic... though admittedly, your sources aren't always the most reliable. You can take a –2 penalty to your check to Recall Knowledge with Esoteric Lore to Recall Knowledge about any topic, not just the usual topics available for Esoteric Lore. Additionally, when you succeed at your check to Exploit a Vulnerability, compare the result of your Esoteric Lore check to the DC to Recall Knowledge for that creature; if that number would be a success or a critical success, you gain information as if you had succeeded at the Recall Knowledge check.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Diverse Lore",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3700",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Divine Disharmony"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3700#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "From your collection of religious trinkets, you pull out opposing divine objects—such as the religious symbols of two deities that are hated enemies—and combine them in a display that causes discordant clashes of divine energy that are especially distracting to the faithful. Roll your choice of a Deception or Intimidation check against the Will DC of a creature you can see within 60 feet, with the following results. If the creature is particularly devoted to a deity, such as a cleric, celestial, monitor, fiend, or other creature with divine spells, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your skill check. The GM might determine that a creature that despises all deities, such as an alghollthu, is unaffected. Critical Success The creature is off-guard to your attacks until the end of your next turn. Success The creature is off-guard to your attacks until the end of your current turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Divine Disharmony",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3700#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3702",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Root to Life or [two-actions]"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3702#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Marigold, spider lily, pennyroyal—many primal traditions connect flowers and plants with the boundary between life and death, and you can leverage this association to keep an ally on this side of the line. You place a small plant or similar symbol on an adjacent dying creature, immediately stabilizing them; the creature is no longer dying and is instead unconscious at 0 Hit Points. If you spend 2 actions instead of 1, you empower the act further by uttering a quick folk blessing to chase away ongoing pain, adding the auditory trait to the action. When you do so, attempt flat checks to remove each source of persistent damage affecting the target; due to the particularly effective assistance, the DC is 10 instead of the usual 15.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Root to Life or [two-actions]",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3702#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3705",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Esoteric Warden"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you apply antithetical material against a creature successfully, you also ward yourself against its next attacks. When you succeed at your check to Exploit a Vulnerability, you gain a +1 status bonus to your AC against the creature's next attack and a +1 status bonus to your next saving throw against the creature; if you critically succeed, these bonuses are +2 instead. You can gain these bonuses only once per day against a particular creature, and the benefit ends if you Exploit Vulnerability again.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-exploit-vulnerability",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Esoteric Warden",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3706",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Talisman Esoterica"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You know how to assemble the supernatural objects in your esoterica into a number of temporary talismans. Each day during your daily preparations, you can make two talismans with an item level no higher than half your level. You must know each talisman's formula. A talisman created this way is a temporary item and loses its magic the next time you make your daily preparations. You know the formulas for all common talismans in GM Core of your level or lower. You remember your talisman formulas through oral tradition or mnemonics, so you don't need a formula book for them.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Talisman Esoterica",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3707",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Turn Away Misfortune"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3707#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You perform a superstition, such as casting salt over your shoulder to ward off bad luck. Turn Away Misfortune's fortune trait cancels out the misfortune effect, causing you to roll normally. As normal, you can apply only one fortune ability to a roll, so if you Turned Away Misfortune on an attack roll, you couldn't also use an ability like Halfling Luck to alter the roll further.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Turn Away Misfortune",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3707#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3709",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Instructive Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3709#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You attack your foe and analyze how it reacts. Make a Strike. On a hit, you can immediately attempt a check to Recall Knowledge about the target. On a critical hit, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the check to Recall Knowledge.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Instructive Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3709#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3710",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Paired Link"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You break a trinket, such as a lodestone or jade pendant, in two, creating a sympathetic link between the halves that bridges distance. During your daily preparations, you perform a short ceremony where you gift one of the two halves to a willing ally. On that ally, you can cast spells and use thaumaturge abilities targeting your paired ally as though you are adjacent to each other, and the ally can cast spells targeting you in the same way. These effects last as long as you and the ally have their half; if either half leaves either of your possessions for even a moment, or if you establish a link with a new ally during your next daily preparations, the link breaks.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Paired Link",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3716",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Elaborate Talisman Esoterica"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As you continue to collect talismanic esoterica, you improve your ability to create temporary talismans. You can create four temporary talismans each day instead of two.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-talisman-esoterica",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Elaborate Talisman Esoterica",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3722",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shared Warding"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You ward your allies from the attacks of your foes whenever you apply those protections to yourself. When you gain a status bonus to AC and saves from Esoteric Warden, you can choose to grant the same benefit to all allies within 30 feet.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-esoteric-warden",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Shared Warding",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3725",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Grand Talisman Esoterica"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've gained the ability to place multiple talismans on an item. Normally, affixing more than one talisman to an item causes the talismans to be suppressed, but when you Affix a Talisman, you can specially treat one item you're working on, allowing it to have two active talismans at once. This special treatment ends if you use Affix a Talisman to treat a new item with this ability.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-talisman-esoterica",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Grand Talisman Esoterica",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3728",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Seven-Part Link"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Many traditions hold the number seven as significant. By exchanging pieces of a seven-part set of esoterica, you create a magical web by which your allies can affect each other at a distance. When you use Paired Link during your daily preparations, you can exchange linking esoterica with up to six willing allies, keeping one piece for yourself. In addition to the normal effects of Paired Link, if a linked ally casts a spell with a range of touch, they can target linked allies within 30 feet with that spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-paired-link",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Seven-Part Link",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3729",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sever Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3729#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You apply a frayed thread, a pinch of fulu ash, or a similar undone charm to your weapon, and swing to break a spell. Make a Strike against an enemy. If you hit and deal damage, you attempt to counteract a single spell active on the target (your choice). Your counteract rank is equal to half your level (rounded up), and your counteract check modifier is equal to your class DC – 10.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Sever Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Arcane",
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3729#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3780",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Blasting Beams"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3780#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "A directed beam of heat or an arc of lightning is one of the simplest ways to project energy. You fire a blast or beam from one hand. Make an attack roll against a creature within 30 feet. If you succeed, the beam deals 1d6 damage to the target for every 2 levels you have, or double damage on a critical success. Awakening Your beams blast through targets. Instead of making an attack roll to damage a single creature within 30 feet, you can use Blasting Beams as a 2-action activity to damage all creatures in a 60-foot line, with a basic Reflex save. Awakening You can choose to launch smaller, quicker beams from your eyes instead. These beams deal d4s instead of d6s, but the attack has the agile trait, and you don’t need a hand free to make it, though your eyes must be uncovered.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Blasting Beams",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Attack",
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3780#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3782",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Storming Breath"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3782#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You spit out a freezing breath or sonic scream. You deal 4d6 damage, plus 1d6 damage for every level you have beyond 6th, to all creatures in a 30-foot cone, with a basic Reflex save. Awakening Your blast powerfully batters your foes. A creature that critically fails its save is knocked prone. Awakening The kickback of your blast helps you make a speedy escape. When you use this ability, you Fly backward 15 feet in a straight line directly opposite your blast. This movement doesn’t trigger reactions based on movement.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Storming Breath",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3782#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3786",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "High-Speed Regeneration"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3786#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your wounds knit together with barely a thought. You regain Hit Points equal to double your level. When you gain this deviation, the GM secretly selects one type of energy damage or precious material, such as fire or cold iron. When you take damage of that type, your wound smokes until the end of your next turn, preventing you from using High-Speed Regeneration. Awakening Your regeneration can automatically save you from the brink of death. Once per day, you can use High-Speed Regeneration when your Hit Points would be reduced to 0 instead of the usual trigger. You avoid being knocked out and remain at the number of HP you regained. Awakening Regrowth invigorates you. You gain a +10-foot status bonus to your Speed until the end of your turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "High-Speed Regeneration",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3786#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3788",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Eerie Flicker"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3788#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your body flickers momentarily into the Ethereal Plane. You become concealed for 1 round, and the flat check for concealment applies to the Strike that would have hit you. If the flat check fails, the Strike misses you. Awakening When your body flickers, you momentarily assume a terrifying form. If a creature fails the flat check against concealment from your Eerie Flicker, it becomes frightened 1, and it doesn’t reduce the frightened condition from this effect at the end of the same turn it gained the condition. Awakening You can choose to compress your flickering movement into a single moment, increasing your chance to avoid the triggering attack in exchange for a shorter- lived effect. If you choose to do so, the flat check for concealment against the triggering attack increases to DC 9, but the concealment affects only the triggering Strike.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Eerie Flicker",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3788#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3883",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Corpse Tender Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have a connection to mindless undead that allows you to communicate your intentions to them on a rudimentary level. You can use Diplomacy to Make an Impression on mindless undead and to make very simple Requests of them; their mindless trait doesn't grant immunity to these mental effects. Most mindless undead are likely hostile toward you by default and must be kept at a safe distance to give you time to Make an Impression. You become trained in Diplomacy; if already trained, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-evil-alignment-trained-in-religion",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Corpse Tender Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3884",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Command Corpse"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the Command Undead feat, but you can use it only to transform the effects of harm spells you cast on mindless undead. These spells can control creatures with a level equal to or lower than your level – 1 (instead of your level – 3).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-corpse-tender-dedication-ability-to-cast-harm",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Command Corpse",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3885",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Corpse Tender's Font"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You easily tend to the wounds of the dead. You can cast harm as a divine innate spell once per day. This spell is heightened to half your level, rounded up. You can target only mindless undead with this spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-corpse-tender-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Corpse Tender's Font",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3886",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Improved Command Corpse"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you use Command Undead on a mindless undead, if the undead succeeds at its save but doesn't critically succeed, it becomes your minion for 1 round. If the undead fails its save, it becomes your minion for 1 hour. If it critically fails, it becomes your minion for 24 hours.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-command-corpse",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Improved Command Corpse",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3887",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Imbue Mindlessness"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You grasp the mind of an undead creature and temporarily wipe it as empty as a zombie's brain. You can target any undead with your divine innate harm spell, not just mindless undead. When you target one non-mindless undead creature with this spell, you can transform its effects. Instead of harm's normal effects, the target must attempt a Will save. Critical Success The target is unaffected. Success The target is stupefied 1 for 1 round. Failure The target is stupefied 2 for 1 minute. While it is stupefied, you can use your Corpse Tender feats on the target as though it were mindless. Critical Failure As failure, except the target is stupefied 3 for 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-command-corpse",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Imbue Mindlessness",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3888",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Flailtongue"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your tongue has mutated into a lashing weapon reminiscent of Kabriri's bone-laden flail. You can use a free action to unhinge your lower jaw and sprout rigid bones from your tongue. You gain an unarmed attack that deals 1d6 bludgeoning damage. Until you use an Interact action to reset your jaw and retract your tongue, you can't make a jaws Strike. Your flailtongue is in the flail weapon group and has the disarm, sweep, and trip traits.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ghoul-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Flailtongue",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3889",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Competitive Eater"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Gorging on flesh after your stomach is full fortifies you, making you hardy enough to withstand more punishment. When you become fully satiated, you gain an amount of temporary Hit Points equal to 10 + your level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-glutton-for-flesh",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Competitive Eater",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3890",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Secret Eater"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have discovered and found favor with the cult within the church of Kabriri known as the Secret Eaters. You have maggots that writhe under your skin with the power to wriggle out from between your teeth, glean secrets from those you devour, and whisper them telepathically into your mind. Once per hour when you Consume Flesh, you can select a single Intelligence-, Wisdom-, or Charisma-based skill whose secrets you wish to uncover. You become subject to the effects of corpse communion as if you had critically succeeded at casting the ritual: you learn a significant piece of lore, a forgotten secret, or some other tantalizing nugget of knowledge that is of immediate use to you.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ghoul-dedication-worshipper-of-kabriri",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Secret Eater",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Necromancy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3891",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tunneling Claws"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have elongated claws and enhanced senses, making you uncanny at digging the underground passageways needed to construct ghoul warrens and rob graves without arousing suspicion. You gain a burrow Speed of 15 feet and a tremorsense (imprecise) of 60 feet. You can Burrow through any earthen matter, including rock, while moving at your full burrow Speed. When you move in this way, you can choose either to leave tunnels behind you that are large enough to allow creatures of your size or smaller to move through them or move through the ground while leaving no tunnels or signs of your passing.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ghoul-dedication-trained-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Tunneling Claws",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3892",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bodysnatcher"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your secret-stealing maggots reveal how to devour more than just the flesh and secrets of a victim; you can ingest and assume their whole physical appearance. When you Consume Flesh of a creature of your size or smaller, you can assume the physical form of the creature immediately after becoming satiated or fully satiated. Using Bodysnatcher counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. Your transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine you are a member of the ancestry or creature type into which you transformed, and you gain a +4 circumstance bonus to your Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through your disguise. You do not gain the special abilities, skills, voice, memories, or other characteristics of the creature you consumed, only their physical form. Unlike Change Shape, Bodysnatcher can be used to gain the appearance of a specific individual whose flesh you've consumed. This effect lasts until you are no longer satiated and can only be used once per individual creature.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-secret-eater",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Bodysnatcher",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Polymorph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Transmutation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3893",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Graveshift"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The maggots inhabiting your body impart you with the knowledge to travel from grave to grave, drawing upon the mystical power of the labyrinthine network of magical warrens and tunnels that connect Everglut to the Material Plane. You can spend 10 minutes channeling this power to transport you and all target creatures or objects that are inside the grave you are standing in to a chosen grave you are aware of (unoccupied or occupied) within 100 miles. When you target an occupied or filled grave, you and all transported creatures and objects appear scattered aboveground around the targeted grave (or belowground in adjacent tunnels or passageways if available).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-secret-eater",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Graveshift",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Conjuration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Teleportation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3894",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Breath of Hungry Death"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3894#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have uncovered occult mysteries that allow you to unleash the devastating hunger of Kabriri upon your foes with a single exhalation, releasing a massive cloud of flesh-eating gas that glows with a sickly green light. You deal 7d6 acid and 7d6 negative damage to all creatures within a 30-foot cone (basic Reflex save with a DC equal to your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher). A creature that gets a critical failure on this Reflex save is also paralyzed for 1 round. A creature that succeeds at this save becomes temporarily immune to Breath of Hungry Death for 24 hours. When a creature is killed using Breath of Hungry Death, its body is reduced to a smoldering pile of ash wafting with necrotic fumes. You can use a reaction to immediately inhale these fumes and become satiated or fully satiated as if you had used Consume Flesh.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-secret-eater",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Breath of Hungry Death",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Acid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Incapacitation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Necromancy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3894#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3895",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Wrath of the First Ghoul"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3895#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The ravenous maggots inside you become capable of exploding forth from your attacks into the wounds of an opponent, whispering telepathic words of destruction that invoke horrific flashbacks of Kabriri's transformation from elf to ghoul or psychic images of hundreds of maggots bursting from the victim's flesh all at once. Make a melee Strike against a target creature. If it hits, in addition to taking damage from the Strike, the target is affected by a 10th-level casting of power word kill. If Wrath of the First Ghoul is used against a target elf, Leng ghoul, or worshipper of Pharasma and does not instantly kill the creature, the target takes double damage.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-secret-eater",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Wrath of the First Ghoul",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Death",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Enchantment",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=3895#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4077",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Jellyfish Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4077#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You relax your posture and loosen your joints, allowing yourself to move with incredible fluidity. You can make stinging lash attacks that deal 1d6 slashing damage. These attacks are in the brawling group, and have the finesse, nonlethal, reach, and unarmed traits. While in Jellyfish Stance, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Reflex saves and on checks to Escape and Squeeze.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Jellyfish Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4077#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4078",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sixth Pillar Mastery"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You align your magical and physical potential. Whenever you succeed at an unarmed Strike against an opponent, they have a -1 status penalty to saves against your spells until the start of your next turn. Whenever you cast a spell using spell slots, you gain a +1 status bonus to attack rolls with your unarmed Strikes until the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-sixth-pillar-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Sixth Pillar Mastery",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4079",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Touch Focus"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4079#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can redirect a spell's power through you to deliver it within striking distance. If your next action is to Cast a Spell with 1 or more targets and a range farther than touch, you change the range to touch. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the attack. This only allows you to touch a single target with the spell, even if the spell originally affected more than 1 target. As long as your spell attack is successful, the target is knocked prone in addition to the spell's normal effects.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-sixth-pillar-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Touch Focus",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Metamagic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4079#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=41",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Goblin Scuttle"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=41#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You take advantage of your ally's movement to adjust your position. You Step.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Goblin Scuttle",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Goblin"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=41#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4153",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Harrower Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You become trained in Occultism; if you are already trained in this skill, you become trained in a different skill of your choice instead. You also become trained in Fortune-Telling Lore, and you learn the harrowing ritual. In addition, once a day when you perform your daily preparations, you can perform a harrow reading for yourself if you have access to a harrow deck. Draw a card from your harrow deck—that card's suit becomes your active harrow omen for the next 24 hours and modifies several other harrower feats as detailed on the following pages. You gain the Avoid Dire Fate reaction. Avoid Dire Fate [reaction] (fortune) Requirements you have an active harrow omen; Trigger you fail or critically fail a check associated with your harrow omen's suit; Effect Treat the failure as a success or a critical failure as a failure. You no longer have an active harrow omen.Associated Suit ChecksSuitAssociated Check 1—Hammers (Str)Strikes (both melee and ranged) 2—Keys (Dex)Reflex saving throws 3—Shields (Con)Fortitude saving throws 4—Books (Int)Skill checks 5—Stars (Wis)Will saving throws 6—Crowns (Cha)All other checks (including flat checks)",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Harrower Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4154",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Experienced Harrower"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you perform the harrowing ritual, the DC for the Primary Check is never more than the standard DC by level, and the cost for the ritual is halved. If you use a fine harrow deck, the cost for the ritual is removed entirely.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Experienced Harrower",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4155",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Harrow Casting"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4155#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You draw a card from your harrow deck just before you cast a spell to infuse your magic with its destined potential. If your next action is to Cast a Spell, the suit of the card you draw enhances the spell in one of the following ways. If the card you draw matches the suit of your active harrow omen, the effect is enhanced further as detailed below. When you Harrow Cast, attempt a DC 11 flat check. If you fail this check, you lose your active harrow omen at the end of your turn. Hammer The force of the spell is enhanced. This effect only enhances single-target offensive spells that require you to make a successful spell attack or require a saving throw from the target to resist. If you hit the target, or if they fail their saving throw, the spell inflicts additional force damage equal to the spell's level. This additional damage doubles if your harrow omen is Hammers.Key Some of the magic remains behind, infusing your defenses. Until the start of your next turn, you gain a +1 status bonus to your AC and all saving throws. If your harrow omen is Keys, this increases to a +2 status bonus.Shield As the spell's magic takes effect, it heals you as well, restoring Hit Points equal to 2d6 + the spell's level. If your harrow omen is Shields, the Hit Points restored increases to 4d6 + twice the spell's level.Book The spell's magic infuses your mind with sudden insights about the target. You can attempt to Recall Knowledge about the target as a free action, using your spell attack roll to make the check. You gain a +2 status bonus to this roll if Books is your harrow omen.Star The spell's magic bolsters those it aids. This effect only enhances single-target spells cast on willing subjects. The magic restores Hit Points to the affected target equal to 2d6 + the spell's level. If your harrow omen is Stars, the magic also grants the target a +2 status bonus to all saving throws until the start of your next turn.Crown The spell's magic is hidden and subtle, and observers may not realize you're doing anything more than manipulating cards in your harrow deck. Attempt a Fortune-Telling Lore check against all observer's Perception DCs. If your check is successful against an observer's Perception DC, that observer doesn't notice you are Casting a Spell, even though normally spells have sensory manifestations. This hides only the spell's spellcasting actions and manifestations, not its effects. If your harrow omen is Crowns, you gain a +2 status bonus to your Fortune-Telling Lore check.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Harrow Casting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Metamagic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4155#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4156",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Restore Omen"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You spend 10 minutes meditating with your harrow deck, then draw a card. The suit of the card grants you a new harrow omen.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Restore Omen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exploration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4157",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Benevolent Spirit Deck"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4157#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You manifest a ghostly deck of harrow cards that seek to protect you or an ally. Select one willing target within 30 feet; the cards move through the air to surround that target, protecting them from harm and granting a +1 status bonus to AC and resistance 5 to a type of damage associated with your active harrow omen (see below). This resistance increases to 10 if you're at least 10th level and 15 if you're 15th level. This effect lasts as long as you sustain it, up to 1 minute, or until you no longer have an active harrow omen. Once the effect ends, you lose your active harrow omen. Hammers: cold damageKeys: fire damageShields: poison damageBooks: electricity damageStars: mental damageCrowns: acid damage",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Benevolent Spirit Deck",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4157#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4158",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Harrow Ritualist"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You immediately learn two of the following rituals: astral projection, call spirit, commune, commune with nature, legend lore, or planar binding. When you perform any ritual, you can incorporate harrow cards into the ritual to gain a +2 status bonus to all skill checks made to resolve the effects of the ritual. You can take this feat more than once; each time you do, you learn two new rituals.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Harrow Ritualist",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4159",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vengeful Spirit Deck"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4159#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You manifest a ghostly deck of harrow cards. Draw a card from a harrow deck, then select a target within 60 feet. The card flies through the air to strike at that target, inflicting 4d6 damage, with a basic saving throw against your class DC. The type of damage inflicted is determined by your active harrow omen; if the card drawn is in the same suit as your active harrow omen, the target takes a –2 status penalty to its saving throw. The damage increases to 6d6 if you're 10th level and 8d6 if you're 15th level. You can continue to throw cards at targets on your turn as long as you Sustain the Vengeful Spirit Deck—throwing a card takes two actions. This effect lasts as long as you Sustain it, up to 1 minute, or until you no longer have an active harrow omen. Once the effect ends, you lose your active harrow omen.Hammers: cold damageKeys: fire damageShields: poison damageBooks: electricity damageStars: mental damageCrowns: acid damage",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Vengeful Spirit Deck",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Metamagic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4159#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4160",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reading the Signs"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have a knack for drawing the right card, be it from a harrow deck, in a game of cards, or even when drawing from a Deck of Many Things. When you're attempting a skill check involving the drawing of cards or resolving the effects of a divination effect (including attempting a saving throw against a hostile divination effect against you), you gain a +2 status bonus to the check. When you draw a card to determine your harrow omen, perform Harrow Casting, cast harrowing, or if you activate a magical deck of cards, draw 2 cards, and choose the one you prefer as your actual card drawn. You can even use this ability when drawing from a Deck of Many Things, but only once per deck. The unused card is shuffled back into the stack.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Reading the Signs",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4161",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Axuma's Awakening"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Choose two cantrips from the arcane spells list. You can cast these cantrips at will as arcane innate spells. A cantrip is heightened to a spell level equal to half your level rounded up. Then, choose one 1st-level spell and one 2nd-level spell from the arcane spells list. You can cast each of these spells once per day as arcane innate spells. Spells gained from this feat must be common spells or spells to which you have access.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-exposure-to-the-well-of-axuma",
          "aonprd:level": "11",
          "aonprd:name": "Axuma's Awakening",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4162",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Axuma's Vigor"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your vigor grants anyone using Medicine checks to Administer First Aid to you, or use any of the Treat actions on you, a +2 circumstance bonus to their check. During the Long-Term Rest activity, you heal at twice the normal rate.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-exposure-to-the-well-of-axuma",
          "aonprd:level": "11",
          "aonprd:name": "Axuma's Vigor",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4193",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Two-Element Infusion"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4193#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Slamming one element into another, you combine their strengths. If the next action you use is an Elemental Blast, choose two of your kinetic elements instead of one. The blast gains the traits of both elements and uses the highest range and damage die among the two elements. Half the blast's damage is the damage type of one element, and the other half is the damage type of the other element. If the total damage is an odd number, you choose which element deals the higher damage. Determine the damage amounts before altering the amount due to halving, doubling, resistances, weaknesses, and other calculations. If either element can deal more than one type of damage, you can still choose which damage type to use. You gain any added effects of both elements, such as their critical blast junction effects.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-two-or-more-kinetic-elements",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Two-Element Infusion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Infusion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Kineticist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4193#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4208",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Four Winds"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4208#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Mimicking the anemoi—monarchs of the four winds—you propel four creatures. Target up to four willing creatures within 30 feet of you. Each of those creatures can Stride up to half its Speed. If it has a fly Speed, it can instead Fly up to half its fly Speed.Level (10th) The targets move up to full Speed instead of half.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Four Winds",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Air",
            "aonprd:Trait-Impulse",
            "aonprd:Trait-Kineticist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4208#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4209",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Whisper on the Wind"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4209#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You speak in a whisper, a soft wind carrying your words far away. This has the effect of the message spell with a range of 500 feet, and it can target only a creature surrounded by air. If you start your message with the target's name, you and the target don't need to be able to see each other, nor do you need line of effect.Level (4th) The range is 1 mile. Level (14th) The range is planetary plus the Plane of Air.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Whisper on the Wind",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Air",
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Illusion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Impulse",
            "aonprd:Trait-Kineticist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4209#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4232",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rock Rampart"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4232#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Drawing on your connection to the Plane of Earth, you form a wall of rock and earth. This has the effect of wall of stone, but the wall's maximum length is 40 feet. The wall lasts until the end of your next turn, but you can Sustain it up to 1 minute.Level (+4) The maximum length of the wall increases by 10 feet, and the Hit Points of each section increase by 5.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Rock Rampart",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Earth",
            "aonprd:Trait-Impulse",
            "aonprd:Trait-Kineticist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Overflow",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4232#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4238",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Flying Flame"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4238#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "A Tiny shape of flame appears, taking a form of your choice—such as a bird, an arrow, or a simple sphere. It Flies from you up to 30 feet in a path you choose. Each creature it passes through takes 1d6 fire damage with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. A creature attempts only one save, even if the flame passes through it multiple times.Level (+2) The damage increases by 1d6.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Flying Flame",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Impulse",
            "aonprd:Trait-Kineticist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4238#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=426",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Impossible Volley"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=426#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You fire a volley at all foes in an area. Make one Strike with a –2 penalty against each enemy within a 10-foot-radius burst centered at or beyond your weapon’s volley range. Roll the damage only once for all targets. Each attack counts toward your multiple attack penalty, but do not increase your penalty until you have made all your attacks.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Impossible Volley",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=426#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4263",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alloy Flesh and Steel"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4263#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Elemental energy replaces every cell of your body with raw metal. You gain the benefits of the ferrous form spell (except you can't cast needle darts) until the end of your next turn. You can Sustain the impulse up to 1 minute, and when you do, you can Raise a metal Shield if you're wielding one. Your metal Elemental Blasts deal an additional die of damage. If you suspend any conditions with Alloy Flesh and Steel, when it ends, you're temporarily immune to Alloy Flesh and Steel for 1 hour.Level (16th) The resistance is 15.",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Alloy Flesh and Steel",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Impulse",
            "aonprd:Trait-Kineticist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Metal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Polymorph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4263#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4274",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Call the Hurricane"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4274#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Massive waves spiral around you, with you as the eye of the hurricane. The waves appear in a 20-foot emanation, or a 30-foot emanation if you're in a body of water. Each creature in the area takes 6d8 bludgeoning damage with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. A creature that fails its save is battered by the waves and pushed 10 feet (or 20 feet on a critical failure).Level (+2) The damage increases by 1d8.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Call the Hurricane",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Impulse",
            "aonprd:Trait-Kineticist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Overflow",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Water"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4274#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4285",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ravel of Thorns"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4285#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Thorny vines grow in geometric patterns on surfaces in your kinetic aura. A creature that starts its turn in the thorns takes a –10-foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds until it leaves the area. The thorns are hazardous terrain. A creature takes 2 piercing damage each time it moves into one of these squares. If any square the thorns grow on is water or soil, double the hazardous terrain damage for all thorns. If you move, the thorns disappear; new thorns grow at the end of your turn.Level (+4) The damage increases by 1.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Ravel of Thorns",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Impulse",
            "aonprd:Trait-Kineticist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Plant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wood"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4285#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4333",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Kineticist Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You become trained in kineticist class DC and impulse attack rolls. Choose one element to be your kinetic element (air, earth, fire, metal, water, or wood). You gain a kinetic aura and the Channel Elements action, though you don't get to use an Elemental Blast or stance impulse when you take that action. You gain the Elemental Blast action. Your Elemental Blast does not automatically gain additional damage dice every four levels, instead requiring you to take the Improved Elemental Blast feat. You become trained in Nature; if you were already trained in Nature, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-constitution-2",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Kineticist Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Multiclass"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4357",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Worm Caller Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You pledge yourself to understanding and emulating one of the most powerful creatures of the Darklands: the mighty cave worm. You gain the following action. Shake It Off [one-action] (fortune, primal) Frequency once per day; Trigger You fail or critically fail a saving throw against a condition or adverse effect (such as baleful polymorph); Effect You reroll the triggering save and use the better result.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-nature-or-cave-worm-lore",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Worm Caller Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4358",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Worm Sense"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You emulate the senses of the cave worm. You gain darkvision and tremorsense as an imprecise sense within 5 feet. The range of the tremorsense increases to 10 feet at 8th level and to 15 feet at 12th level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worm-caller-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Worm Sense",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4359",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Wormskin"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your flesh grows thick and bloated, protecting you against harm. You gain resistance equal to half your level versus one of the following types of damage, chosen when you take the feat: fire, cold, or bludgeoning. This choice cannot be changed. When you're unarmored, your flesh gives you a +2 item bonus to AC with a Dexterity cap of +3. You can apply with armor potency runes and property runes directly to your flesh, though excruciatingly painful.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worm-caller-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Wormskin",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4360",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Inexorable"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You imbue yourself with the resilience of the cave worm. When you gain the paralyzed, slowed, or stunned condition, roll a DC 15 flat check. On a success you ignore the condition. When using Worm Form you are immune to penalties to your Speed and the immobilized condition, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Fortitude or Reflex DC against attempts to Shove or Trip you, and you ignore difficult terrain and greater difficult terrain.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worm-caller-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Inexorable",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4361",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Worm's Feast"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4361#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You call forth a brood of infantile cave worms to feast on your enemy's flesh. Choose a creature within 30 feet; the creature must attempt a Fortitude save. At 8th level and every 2 levels above that, the persistent piercing damage taken on a failure increases by 1d6. Critical Success The worms writhe away harmlessly. Success The target takes 2d6 piercing damage and 2d6 persistent piercing damage. Failure The target takes 6d6 piercing damage and 2d6 persistent piercing damage. Critical Failure As failure, plus the target is flat-footed as long as it takes persistent piercing damage.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worm-caller-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Worm's Feast",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Conjuration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4361#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4362",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Worm Empathy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can connect with cave worms (and other worm-related creatures, at the GM's discretion) on a rudimentary level. You can use Diplomacy to Make an Impression on cave worms and to make simple Requests of them. In most cases, the cave worm's starting attitude is indifferent and they will give you time to establish contact.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worm-caller-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Worm Empathy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4363",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Azure Fins"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When submerged in water or another liquid, you form small fin-like arms along your body, granting you far greater maneuverability while swimming. You gain a swim Speed equal to your land Speed. Furthermore, while swimming on the surface of a liquid, you can Leap out of the liquid and do not fall until the end of your turn, allowing you to spend the rest of the turn above the surface.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worm-caller-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Azure Fins",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4364",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Call Worm Spirit"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4364#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You call forth a ghostly manifestation of the worm spirit. Choose an intersection on the ground within 60 feet; the ghostly maw of a worm emerges from the ground, attacking all creatures in a 10 foot burst. Each creature in the area must attempt a Reflex save. Critical Success The target is unaffected. Success The target takes 1d10+13 bludgeoning damage as it is battered by the worm's body. Failure The target takes 3d10+15 piercing damage as it is bitten by the worm. The target is immobilized until the end of its next turn. Critical Failure As failure, but the damage increases to 6d10+30 and the target is knocked prone.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worm-caller-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Call Worm Spirit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Conjuration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4364#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4365",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tunnel"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain a burrow speed of 10 feet.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worm-caller-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Tunnel",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4366",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Crimson Breath"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4366#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You gain a fire breath weapon similar to that of a crimson worm. You breathe a blast of flame in a 30-foot cone that deals 12d6 fire damage to all creatures in the area (basic Reflex save). This damage increases by 2d6 at 14th level and every 2 levels thereafter.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worm-caller-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Crimson Breath",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Evocation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4366#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4367",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Venomous Touch"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've learned to channel the sting of the worm. You gain purple worm sting as an innate primal spell that you can cast once per day.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worm-caller-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Venomous Touch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4368",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Worm Form"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4368#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You take on the form of a purple worm or transform into a humanoid-worm hybrid, retaining your own head but with a worm's body, transforming into a Huge battle form. You must have enough space to expand into or the ability is lost. While in this form, you gain the animal trait. You can Dismiss the form. You gain the following statistics and abilities regardless of which battle form you choose: AC = 20 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.40 temporary Hit Points.Darkvision.One or more unarmed melee attacks specific to the battle form you choose, which are the only attacks you can Strike with. You're trained with them. Your attack modifier is +25, and you use the listed damage. Melee attacks are Strength based (for the purpose of the enfeebled condition, for example). If your unarmed attack modifier is higher, you can use it instead.Athletics modifier of +30, unless your own modifier is higher. You also gain specific abilities based on the type of monster you choose: Purple Worm Speed 40 feet, burrow 30 feet, swim 20 feet; Melee [one-action] jaws (deadly 2d10, reach 15 feet), Damage 3d10+15 piercing; Melee [one-action] stinger (agile, poison, reach 15 feet), Damage 2d12+15 piercing plus 2d6 persistent poison; Melee [one-action] body (reach 15 feet) Damage 1d10+13 bludgeoningHybrid Speed 40 feet; Melee [one-action] stinger (agile, poison, reach 10 feet), Damage 2d12+15 piercing plus 1d6 persistent poison; Melee [one-action] body (reach 10 feet), Damage 1d10+13 bludgeoning; Hybrid Caster You retain the ability to speak, and can cast spells as long as they don't have somatic or material components.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-worm-caller-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Worm Form",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Polymorph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Transmutation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4368#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4369",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Call the Worm"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain summon animal, heightened to 9th level, as an innate primal spell that you can cast once per day, but can only summon a purple worm. At 20th level, you can summon an elite purple worm instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-call-worm-spirit",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Call the Worm",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4371",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stone Brawler Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've learned to call the primal power of elemental stone to your aid. You gain the Stonestrike Stance action. Stonestrike Stance [one-action] Requirements You are standing on the ground; Effect You enter the stance of unyielding stone and draw upon the power of the living rock, encasing your fists in stone and allowing you to make stonestrike attacks. These deal 1d8 bludgeoning damage, are in the brawling group, and have the forceful, magical, and unarmed traits.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-constitution-14",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Stone Brawler Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4372",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stoney Skin"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your skin takes on the hardness of stone. You gain resistance to physical damage (except adamantine) equal to your number of class feats from the Stone Brawler archetype.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stone-brawler-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Stoney Skin",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4373",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stoney Deflection"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4373#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You gather the resiliency of stone to block attacks against you. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to AC and to any defenses against being Shoved or Tripped until the beginning of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stone-brawler-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Stoney Deflection",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4373#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4374",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ore Fists"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you enter the Stonestrike Stance, your fists appear to be covered with veins of unrefined ore. Your stonestrike attacks count as cold iron and silver when determining weaknesses and bypassing resistances.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stone-brawler-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Ore Fists",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4375",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stonebane"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your stonestrike attacks deal 1d6 additional damage against constructs, creatures with the earth trait, and earthen objects, such as a stone door.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stone-brawler-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Stonebane",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4376",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Adamantine Fists"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You imbue your unarmed strikes with one of the strongest metals. Your stonestrike attacks are treated as adamantine.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ore-fists",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Adamantine Fists",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4377",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stonebound Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You bind yourself to the very essence of stone. You become trained in Plane of Earth Lore and learn the Terran language. If you are already trained in Plane of Earth Lore, you become trained in a skill of your choice. If you already speak Terran, you learn a common language of your choice. Increase your maximum Hit Points by your level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-constitution-14",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Stonebound Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4378",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Elemental Existence"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your body becomes infused with elemental earth. You gain the Adopted Ancestry feat and gain a 1st level oread ancestry feat as a bonus feat, ignoring the limitations of the lineage trait. When you gain new ancestry feats, you can select oread feats in addition to feats allowed by your ancestry and heritage.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stonebound-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Elemental Existence",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4379",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stone Guardian"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn to call a powerful guardian of earth and stone to your side. You can cast summon elemental as an innate primal spell once per day, and can only summon elementals with the earth trait. This spell is automatically heightened to half your level rounded up.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stonebound-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Stone Guardian",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4380",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stone Blood"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your blood becomes thick and sluggish, but no less effective at oxygenating your cells. You can selectively stop your bleeding with ease. Reduce the DC of flat checks to stop persistent bleed damage from 15 to 10, and you can use a single action that has the concentrate trait to gain an early flat check without physically binding the wounds. You recover from the drained condition twice as quickly as normal.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stonebound-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Stone Blood",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4381",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stonebound Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've learned to manifest your connection to stone by conjuring it to your side. You gain scatter scree as a primal innate cantrip. At 8th level, you gain meld into stone as a primal innate spell once per day. At 10th level, you gain shape stone as a primal innate spell once per day. At 12th level, you gain wall of stone as a primal innate spell once per day.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stonebound-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Stonebound Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4382",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Statue"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4382#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your body and equipment appear to be made of stone as you hold perfectly still. Until the next time you act, you appear to be a statue and do not need to eat, drink, or breathe, but you are flat-footed. Your Deception DC to pass as a statue is equal to 10 + your proficiency bonus (do not apply any other bonuses, penalties, or modifiers).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stonebound-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Statue",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4382#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4383",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rocky Flesh"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your flesh takes on the hardness of stone. You gain resistance to physical damage (except adamantine) equal to your number of class feats from the Stonebound archetype.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stonebound-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Rocky Flesh",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4384",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Living Stone"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your body becomes living stone. You don't need to eat or drink and need only 6 hours of rest to feel well rested. You must still rest at least 8 hours and spend 1 hour of preparation to regain resources usable only a limited number of times per day, such as spell slots. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to saving throws against diseases, poisons, and effects that would cause the paralyzed or stunned conditions. When you roll a successful saving throw against a disease or poison, you get a critical success instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-stonebound-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Living Stone",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4573",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bardic Lore"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your studies make you informed on every subject. You are trained in Bardic Lore, a special Lore skill that can be used only to Recall Knowledge, but on any topic. If you have legendary proficiency in Occultism, you gain expert proficiency in Bardic Lore, but you can’t increase your proficiency rank in Bardic Lore by any other means.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-enigma-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Bardic Lore",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4575",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lingering Composition"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "By adding a flourish, you make your compositions last longer. You learn the lingering composition focus spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-maestro-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Lingering Composition",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4576",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Martial Performance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your muse has taught you how to handle a wider variety of weapons than most bards, empowering you to effortlessly blend your performance into combat tools. When you have a courageous anthem composition cantrip active, and you damage an enemy with a Strike, the spell’s duration is extended by 1 round. You can extend an individual casting only once in this way. If you gain the rallying anthem or song of strength composition cantrips, you can apply this benefit to those cantrips as well.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warrior-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Martial Performance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4577",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reach Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4577#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can extend your spells’ range. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that has a range, increase that spell’s range by 30 feet. As is standard for increasing spell ranges, if the spell normally has a range of touch, you extend its range to 30 feet.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Reach Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4577#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4578",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Versatile Performance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can rely on the grandeur of your performances rather than ordinary social skills. You can use Performance instead of Diplomacy to Make an Impression and instead of Intimidation to Demoralize. You can also use an acting Performance instead of Deception to Impersonate. In addition, you can use your proficiency rank in Performance to meet the prerequisites of skill feats that require a particular proficiency rank in Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-polymath-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Versatile Performance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4585",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Multifarious Muse"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your muse doesn’t fall into a single label. Choose a type of muse other than that of your own. You gain a 1st-level feat that requires that muse, and your muse is now also a muse of that type, allowing you to take feats with the other muse as a prerequisite. You don’t gain any of the other effects of the muse you chose.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Multifarious Muse",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4587",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Uplifting Overture"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn the uplifting overture composition cantrip, which aids your allies’ skills with the inspiring nature of your performance.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-maestro-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Uplifting Overture",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4594",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Triple Time"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn the triple time composition cantrip, which speeds up you and your allies for a round.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Triple Time",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4602",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Steady Spellcasting"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You don’t lose spells easily. If a reaction would disrupt your spellcasting action, attempt a DC 15 flat check. If you succeed, your action isn’t disrupted.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Steady Spellcasting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric",
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4607",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Know-It-All"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you succeed at a check to Recall Knowledge, you gain additional information or context. When you critically succeed at a check to Recall Knowledge, you get additional information or context or can ask an additional follow-up question (the GM chooses which).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bard-enigma-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Know-It-All",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4614",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quickened Casting"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4614#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "If your next action is to cast a cantrip or a spell that is at least 2 ranks lower than the highest-rank spell slot you have, reduce the number of actions to cast it by 1 (minimum 1 action).",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Quickened Casting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4614#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4622",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Allegro"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can quicken your allies with a fast-paced performance. You learn the allegro composition cantrip.",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Allegro",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4629",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Effortless Concentration"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4629#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can maintain a spell with hardly a thought. You immediately gain the effects of the Sustain action, allowing you to extend the duration of one of your active spells.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Effortless Concentration",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Summoner",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4629#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4642",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Deadly Simplicity"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you are wielding your deity’s favored weapon, increase the damage die size of that weapon by one step. If your deity’s favored weapon is an unarmed attack (such as a fist, if you worship Irori) and its damage die is smaller than d6, instead increase its damage die size to d6.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-deity-with-a-simple-or-unarmed-attack-favored-weapon-trained-with-your-deitys-favored-weapon",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Deadly Simplicity",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4644",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Domain Initiate"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your deity bestows a special spell related to their powers. Select one domain—a subject of particular interest to you within your religion—from your deity’s list. You gain an initial domain spell for that domain, a spell unique to the domain and not available to other clerics. Domain spells are a type of focus spell. It costs 1 Focus Point to cast a focus spell, and you start with a focus pool of 1 Focus Point. You refill your focus pool during your daily preparations, and you can regain 1 Focus Point by spending 10 minutes using the Refocus activity to pray to your deity or do service toward their causes. Focus spells are automatically heightened to half your level rounded up, much like cantrips. Focus spells don’t require spell slots, and can’t be cast using spell slots. Your focus pool can hold one Focus Point for each focus spell you have, up to 3 points. The full rules for focus spells appear here.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Domain Initiate",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4649",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Emblazon Armament"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Carefully etching a sacred image into a physical object, you steel yourself for battle. You can spend 10 minutes emblazoning a symbol of your deity upon a weapon or shield. The symbol doesn’t fade until 1 year has passed, but if you Emblazon an Armament, any symbol you previously emblazoned, and any symbol already emblazoned on that item instantly disappears. The emblazoned item is a religious symbol of your deity in addition to its normal purpose, and it gains another benefit determined by the type of item. The benefit applies only to followers of the deity the symbol represents, but others can use the item normally. Shield The shield gains a +1 status bonus to its Hardness. (This causes it to reduce more damage with the Shield Block reaction.).Weapon The wielder gains a +1 status bonus to damage rolls with the weapon.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Emblazon Armament",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exploration"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4650",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Panic the Dead"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Vitality strikes terror in the undead. When you use a heal spell to damage undead, any undead that fails its saving throw is also frightened 1. If it critically failed, the creature also gains the fleeing condition until the start of your next turn. Mindless undead are not immune to this effect due to being mindless.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Panic the Dead",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fear",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4663",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Divine Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4663#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You siphon residual spell energy into a weapon you’re wielding. Until the end of your turn, the weapon deals an additional 1d4 spirit damage. If you are holy or unholy, Strikes with the weapon also gain that trait, and the additional damage increases to 2d4 against creatures of the opposing trait.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Divine Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4663#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4665",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Selective Energy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As you call down divine power, you can prevent some enemies from benefiting or some allies from being hurt. When you cast a version of harm or heal that has an area, you can designate up to 5 creatures in the area. They are not targeted by the spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Selective Energy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cleric"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4708",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Animal Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the service of a young animal companion that travels with you on your adventures and obeys any simple commands you give it to the best of its abilities. See Animal Companions for more information. Ranger: When you Hunt Prey, your animal companion gains the action's benefits and your hunter's edge benefit if you have one.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-druid-animal-order",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Animal Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4710",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Leshy Familiar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You call a minor spirit of nature into a plant body, creating a leshy companion to aid you in your spellcasting. You gain a familiar, which has your choice of either the plant or fungus familiar ability; this doesn't count against your usual limit of familiar abilities (typically 2). The spirit you call has a more tenuous connection to its plant body than fully independent leshies, so it is Tiny in size like other familiars.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-leaf-order",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Leshy Familiar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4711",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Plant Empathy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have a connection to flora that allows you to communicate with them on a rudimentary level. You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with plants and fungus.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Plant Empathy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4712",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Storm Born"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are at home out in the elements, reveling in the power of nature unleashed. You do not take circumstance penalties to ranged spell attacks or Perception checks caused by weather, and your targeted spells don’t require a flat check to succeed against a target concealed by weather (such as fog).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-storm-order",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Storm Born",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4713",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Untamed Form"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are one with the wild, always changing and adapting to meet any challenge. You gain the untamed form order spell, which lets you transform into a variety of shapes that you can expand with druid feats.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-untamed-order",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Untamed Form",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4715",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Widen Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4715#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You manipulate the energy of your spell, causing it to spread out and affect a wider area. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that has an area of a burst, cone, or line and does not have a duration, increase the area of that spell. Add 5 feet to the radius of a burst that normally has a radius of at least 10 feet (a burst with a smaller radius is not affected). Add 5 feet to the length of a cone or line that is normally 15 feet long or smaller, and add 10 feet to the length of a larger cone or line.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Widen Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4715#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4716",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Call of the Wild"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You call upon the creatures of nature to come to your aid. You can spend 10 minutes in concert with nature to replace a spell you’ve prepared in one of your druid spell slots with a summon animal or summon plant or fungus spell of the same rank.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Call of the Wild",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4717",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Enhanced Familiar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You infuse your familiar with additional primal energy, increasing its abilities. You can select four familiar or master abilities each day, instead of two.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-a-familiar",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Enhanced Familiar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4722",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Forest Passage"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can always find a path, almost as if foliage parted before you. You ignore any difficult terrain caused by plants and fungi, such as bushes, vines, and undergrowth.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-leaf-order",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Forest Passage",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4723",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Form Control"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4723#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With additional care and effort, you can take on an alternate shape for a longer period of time. If your next action is to cast untamed form, the spell’s rank is 2 lower than normal (minimum 1st rank), but you can remain transformed for up to 1 hour or the listed duration (whichever is longer). You can still Dismiss untamed form as normal.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-untamed-form",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Form Control",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4723#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4730",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Insect Shape"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your understanding of life expands, allowing you to mimic a wider range of creatures. Add the shapes in insect form to your untamed form list. Whenever you use untamed form to polymorph into the non-flying insect shapes listed in pest form, the duration is 24 hours instead of 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-untamed-form",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Insect Shape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4732",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Storm Retribution"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4732#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You lash out, directing a burst of storming fury toward a creature that has harmed you. You cast tempest surge on the triggering opponent and push that creature, moving it 5 feet away from you if it fails its Reflex save, or 10 feet if it critically fails. This movement is forced movement.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-storm-order-tempest-surge-order-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Storm Retribution",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4732#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4739",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Soaring Shape"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Wings free you from the shackles of the ground below. Add the bat and bird shapes in aerial form to your untamed form list. If you have Insect Shape, you also add the wasp shape to your untamed form list. If you have Ferocious Shape, you also add the pterosaur shape to your untamed form list. Whenever you use untamed form to take a shape that grants you a specific Acrobatics modifier, you gain a +1 status bonus to Acrobatics checks.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-untamed-form",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Soaring Shape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4740",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Wind Caller"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You bid the winds to aid you, carrying you through the air and allowing you passage through the strongest headwinds. You gain the stormwind flight order spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-storm-order",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Wind Caller",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4744",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Plant Shape"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can take the shape of a plant creature. If you don't have untamed form, you can cast plant form once per day, heightened to the same rank as your highest-rank druid spell slot. If you do have untamed form, add the shapes listed in plant form to your untamed form list, and whenever you're polymorphed into another shape using untamed form, you gain resistance 5 to poison.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-leaf-order-or-untamed-form",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Plant Shape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4751",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Primal Focus"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your connection to nature is particularly strong, and the spirits of nature flock around you, helping you replenish your focus. Whenever you Refocus, completely refill your focus pool.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Primal Focus",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4760",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Monstrosity Shape"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can transform into a powerful magical creature. Add the cave worm and sea serpent shapes listed in monstrosity form to your untamed form list. If you have Soaring Shape, also add the phoenix shape to your untamed form list.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-untamed-form",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Monstrosity Shape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4762",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Invoke Disaster"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can invoke nature’s fury upon your foes. You gain the storm lord order spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-wind-caller",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Invoke Disaster",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4768",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Combat Assessment"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4768#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You make a telegraphed attack to learn about your foe. Make a melee Strike. On a hit, you can immediately attempt a check to Recall Knowledge about the target. On a critical hit, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the check to Recall Knowledge. The target is temporarily immune to Combat Assessment for 1 day.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Combat Assessment",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4768#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4771",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Point Blank Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4771#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You take aim to pick off nearby enemies quickly. When using a ranged volley weapon while you are in this stance, you don’t take the penalty to your attack rolls from the volley trait. When using a ranged weapon that doesn’t have the volley trait, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to damage rolls on attacks against targets within the weapon’s first range increment.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Point Blank Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4771#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4772",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reactive Shield"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4772#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can snap your shield into place just as you would take a blow, avoiding the hit at the last second. You immediately use the Raise a Shield action and gain your shield’s bonus to AC. The circumstance bonus from the shield applies to your AC when you’re determining the outcome of the triggering attack.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Reactive Shield",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4772#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4773",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Snagging Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4773#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You combine an attack with quick grappling moves to throw an enemy off balance as long as it stays in your reach. Make a Strike while keeping one hand free. If this Strike hits, the target is off-guard until the start of your next turn or until it’s no longer within the reach of your hand, whichever comes first.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Snagging Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4773#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4774",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sudden Charge"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4774#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With a quick sprint, you dash up to your foe and swing. Stride twice. If you end your movement within melee reach of at least one enemy, you can make a melee Strike against that enemy. You can use Sudden Charge while Burrowing, Climbing, Flying, or Swimming instead of Striding if you have the corresponding movement type.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Sudden Charge",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4774#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4775",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vicious Swing"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4775#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You unleash a particularly powerful attack that clobbers your foe but leaves you a bit unsteady. Make a melee Strike. This counts as two attacks when calculating your multiple attack penalty. If this Strike hits, you deal an extra die of weapon damage. If you’re at least 10th level, increase this to two extra dice, and if you’re at least 18th level, increase it to three extra dice.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Vicious Swing",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4775#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4781",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dueling Parry (Fighter)"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4781#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can parry attacks against you with your one-handed weapon. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to AC until the start of your next turn as long as you continue to meet the requirements.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Dueling Parry (Fighter)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4781#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4783",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lightning Swap"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4783#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have practiced quickly switching between combat styles and the equipment needed for them. You Interact to stow any number of items from your hands, then draw up to two weapons or a shield and a weapon.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Lightning Swap",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4783#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4788",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Double Shot"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4788#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You shoot twice in blindingly fast succession. Make two Strikes, each against a separate target and with a –2 penalty. Both attacks count toward your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn’t increase until after you’ve made both of them.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Double Shot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4788#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4794",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Slam Down"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4794#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You make an attack to knock a foe off balance, then follow up immediately with a sweep to topple them. Make a melee Strike. If it hits and deals damage, you can attempt an Athletics check to Trip the creature you hit. If you’re wielding a two-handed melee weapon, you can ignore Trip’s requirement that you have a hand free. Both attacks count toward your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn’t increase until after you’ve made both of them.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Slam Down",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4794#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4800",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Disarming Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4800#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You adopt a fencing stance that improves your control over your weapon. While you are in this stance, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to Disarm and a +2 circumstance bonus to your Reflex DC when defending against checks to Disarm you. In addition, you can attempt to Disarm creatures up to two sizes larger than you.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Disarming Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4800#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4801",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Furious Focus"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve learned to maintain your balance even when swinging furiously. When you make a Vicious Swing with a melee weapon you’re wielding in two hands, it counts as one attack toward your multiple attack penalty instead of two.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-vicious-swing",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Furious Focus",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4803",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reflexive Shield"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can use your shield to fend off explosions and the like. When you Raise your Shield, you gain your shield’s circumstance bonus to Reflex saves.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Reflexive Shield",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4808",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Triple Shot"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can quickly fire multiple shots with greater control. When you use Double Shot, you can make the attacks against the same target. You can add an additional action to Double Shot to make three ranged Strikes instead of two. If you do, the penalty is –4. All attacks count toward your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn’t increase until after you’ve made all of them.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-double-shot",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Triple Shot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4809",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Blind-Fight"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your battle instincts make you more aware of concealed and invisible opponents. You don’t need to succeed at a flat check to target concealed creatures. You’re not off-guard to creatures that are hidden from you (unless you’re off-guard to them for reasons other than the hidden condition), and you need only a successful DC 5 flat check to target a hidden creature. While you’re adjacent to an undetected creature of your level or lower, it is instead only hidden from you",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-perception",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Blind-Fight",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4815",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Positioning Assault"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4815#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With punishing blows, you force your opponent into position. Make a Strike with the required weapon. If you hit, you Reposition the target 5 feet.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Positioning Assault",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4815#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4823",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Debilitating Shot"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4823#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Aiming for a weak point, you impede your foe with a precise shot. Make a ranged weapon Strike. If it hits and deals damage, the target is slowed 1 until the end of its next turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Debilitating Shot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4823#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4824",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Disarming Twist"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4824#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "After your initial attack redirects your foe’s defenses, your follow-up wrests their weapon from their grasp. Make a melee Strike with a one-handed melee weapon. In addition to its other effects, this Strike gains the success and critical success effects of the Disarm action. The Strike also has the following failure effect. Failure The target becomes off-guard until the end of your current turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Disarming Twist",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Press"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4824#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4832",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Brutal Finish"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4832#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your final blow can make an impact even if it rebounds off a foe’s defenses. Make a Strike with a melee weapon you’re wielding in two hands. After the Strike, your turn ends. The Strike deals one additional weapon damage die, or two additional weapon damage dice if you’re at least 18th level. The Strike also gains the following failure effect. Failure You deal damage equal to one weapon damage die of the required weapon. Increase this to two dice if you’re at least 18th level.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Brutal Finish",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Press"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4832#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4834",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dueling Dance (Fighter)"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4834#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Using a free hand as pivot and balance, you both attack and defend with your weapon. While you are in this stance, you constantly have the benefits of Dueling Parry",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dueling-parry-fighter",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Dueling Dance (Fighter)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4834#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4845",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Opening Stance (Fighter)"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4845#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "At the first sign of trouble, often before you consciously realize the danger, you drop into a stance with a mere thought. Use an action that has the stance trait.",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Opening Stance (Fighter)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4845#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4847",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Whirlwind Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4847#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You lash out in a blur of motion, attacking all nearby adversaries. Make a melee Strike against each enemy within your melee reach. Each attack counts toward your multiple attack penalty, but you do not increase your penalty until you have made all your attacks.",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Whirlwind Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4847#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4849",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Improved Reflexive Shield"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your shield can help save nearby allies. When you use Shield Block against damage resulting from a Reflex save, adjacent allies who would take damage due to Reflex saves against the same effect also benefit from the damage reduction.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-reflexive-shield",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Improved Reflexive Shield",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4850",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Master of Many Styles"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4850#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You move fluidly between stances, using your mastery of combat to always adopt the best tactics. You use an action with the stance trait.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-fighter-opening-stance-fighter-monk-reflexive-stance",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Master of Many Styles",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4850#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4851",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Multishot Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4851#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You lock yourself in a stable position so you can fire swiftly and accurately. While you are in this stance, your penalty for Double Shot is reduced to –1. If you move from your position, this stance ends.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-triple-shot",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Multishot Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4851#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4854",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Impossible Volley"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4854#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You fire a volley at all foes in an area. Make one Strike with a –2 penalty against each enemy within a 10-foot-radius burst centered at or beyond your weapon’s volley range. Roll the damage only once for all targets. Each attack counts toward your multiple attack penalty, but do not increase your penalty until you have made all your attacks.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Impossible Volley",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4854#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4855",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Savage Critical"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The wounds you inflict are grievous. When you Strike with a weapon or unarmed attack for which you have legendary proficiency, you critically succeed if you roll a 19 on the die as long as that result would be a success. This has no effect on a 19 if the result would be a failure.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Savage Critical",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fighter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4871",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Companion's Cry"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can urge your companion to do its utmost. You can spend 2 actions to Command an Animal instead of 1 when commanding your animal companion. If you do, your animal companion uses an additional action.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-an-animal-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Companion's Cry",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4879",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mature Animal Companion (Ranger)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your animal companion becomes a mature animal companion and gains additional capabilities. Your animal companion has greater independence. During an encounter, even if you don't use the Command an Animal action, your animal companion can still use 1 action that round on your turn to Strike or Stride (or Burrow, Climb, Fly, or Swim if it has that Speed). It can do this at any point during your turn, as long as you aren’t currently taking an action. If it does, that’s all the actions it gets that round—you can’t Command it later.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Mature Animal Companion (Ranger)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4888",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Incredible Companion (Ranger)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your animal companion continues to grow and develop. It becomes a nimble or savage animal companion (your choice), gaining additional capabilities determined by the type of companion.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mature-animal-companion-ranger",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Incredible Companion (Ranger)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4896",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Side by Side (Ranger)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You and your animal companion fight in tandem. Whenever you and your animal companion are adjacent to the same foe, you are both flanking that foe with each other, regardless of your actual positions.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-an-animal-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Side by Side (Ranger)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4905",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Specialized Companion (Ranger)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your animal companion continues to grow in power and ability, and it is now cunning enough to become specialized. Your animal companion gains one specialization of your choice.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-incredible-companion-ranger",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Specialized Companion (Ranger)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4909",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Masterful Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your animal companion shares your incredible hunting skills, allowing it to take down your shared prey with ease. When you Hunt Prey, your animal companion gains the masterful hunter benefit associated with your hunter’s edge, rather than just your original hunter’s edge benefit.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-masterful-hunter-animal-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Masterful Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=492",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hunted Shot"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=492#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You take two quick shots against the one you hunt. Make two Strikes against your prey with the required weapon. If both hit the same creature, combine their damage for the purpose of resistances and weaknesses. Apply your multiple attack penalty to each Strike normally",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Hunted Shot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=492#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4922",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "You're Next"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4922#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "After downing a foe, you menace another. Attempt to Demoralize a creature within 60 feet, with a +2 circumstance bonus. If you have legendary proficiency in Intimidation, you can use this as a free action with the same trigger.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-intimidation",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "You're Next",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fear",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue",
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4922#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4923",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Brutal Beating"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your critical hits shakes your foes’ confidence. Whenever your Strike is a critical hit and deals damage, the target is frightened 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ruffian-racket",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Brutal Beating",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fear",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=493",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Monster Hunter"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You quickly assess your prey and apply what you know. As part of the action used to Hunt your Prey, you can attempt a check to Recall Knowledge about your prey. When you critically succeed at identifying your hunted prey with Recall Knowledge, you note a weakness in the creature’s defenses in addition to any other benefits. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your next attack roll against that prey, and any ally you tell gains the same benefit. You can give bonuses from Monster Hunter only once per day against a particular creature.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Monster Hunter",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4931",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Head Stomp"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4931#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Make an unarmed melee Strike against a prone target. If it hits, until the end of your next turn the target is stupefied 1 (or stupefied 2 on a critical hit) and off-guard.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Head Stomp",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4931#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4966",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vicious Debilitations"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The debilitations you dish out seriously impair your foes. Add the following debilitations to the list you can choose from when you use Debilitating Strike. Debilitation The target gains weakness 5 to your choice of bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage.Debilitation The target becomes clumsy 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ruffian-racket-debilitating-strike",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Vicious Debilitations",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4978",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stay Down!"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4978#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have ways of keeping your foes down. Attempt an Athletics check against the triggering foe’s Fortitude DC. On a success, the action is disrupted, causing the creature to remain prone. On a critical success, the creature also can’t Stand until its next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Stay Down!",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4978#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=498",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Draw"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=498#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You draw your weapon and attack with the same motion. You Interact to draw a weapon, then Strike with that weapon.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Draw",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Gunslinger",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=498#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4984",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reconstruct The Scene"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You spend 1 minute surveying a small location (such as a single room) to get an impression of events that occurred there in the last day. This involves moving about the area and studying footprints, spilled drinks or blood, and so forth. You get an indistinct mental impression of significant events that happened there. This gives you clues and details of the past, including the overall events and their time frame, but it’s not a perfect record. This also isn’t enough to identify who was involved in these events if you weren’t already aware the person was there. As determined by the GM, you also pick out various seemingly small details that could serve as important clues, like a memorable weapon someone used for a murder or the type of cloak someone wore when passing through.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Reconstruct The Scene",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4988",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Powerful Sneak"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve learned to exploit your enemies’ openings. Your sneak attack damage ignores any immunity or resistance the target has to precision damage. In addition, when you Sneak, you can designate one creature you’re undetected by at the end of that action. On the next attack you make against that creature before the end of your next turn, any sneak attack die you roll that’s less than 3 is a 3 instead. This has no benefit if your next attack against the creature doesn’t deal sneak attack damage, and if you designate a new creature you lose the benefit on any previous one.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Powerful Sneak",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4992",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cackle"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your patron’s power fills you with confidence, letting you sustain a magical working even as a quick burst of laughter leaves your lips. You learn the cackle hex.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Cackle",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4993",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cauldron"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can brew magic in your cauldron, creating useful magical concoctions. You can use the Craft activity to create oils and potions. You immediately gain the formulas for four common 1st-level oils or potions. At 4th level and every 2 levels beyond that, you gain the formula for a common oil or potion of that level or lower (a 4th-level potion if you’re 4th level, a 6th-level potion if you’re 6th level, and so on). If you have a familiar, you can have your familiar learn these formulas rather than storing them in a formula book. Your familiar can learn new formulas in the same way it learns new spells, and these formulas are transferred from a slain familiar to a new familiar in the same way spells are. During your daily preparations, you can create one temporary oil or potion using a formula you know. If you have master proficiency in spell DC, you can create a batch of two temporary oils or potions during your daily preparations, and if you have legendary proficiency, you can create a batch of three. Any items you create this way become inert bottles of liquid the next time you make your daily preparations, and any remaining effects of the temporary items end. A temporary oil or potion has no value.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Cauldron",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4996",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Basic Lesson"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your patron grants you a special lesson, revealing a hidden facet of its nature. Choose a basic lesson from the list here. You gain its associated hex, and your familiar learns the associated spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Basic Lesson",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4997",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Conceal Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4997#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Through sheer mental effort, you can simplify the incantations and gestures needed to spellcast, leaving them barely noticeable. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell, the spell gains the subtle trait, hiding the shining runes, sparks of magic, and other manifestations that would usually give away your spellcasting. The trait hides only the spell's spellcasting actions and manifestations, not its effects, so an observer might still see a ray streak out from you or see you vanish into thin air.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Conceal Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=4997#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=500",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Companion's Cry"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can urge your companion to do its utmost. You can spend 2 actions to Command an Animal instead of 1 when commanding your animal companion. If you do, your animal companion uses an additional action.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-an-animal-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Companion's Cry",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5002",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Greater Lesson"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your patron grants you greater knowledge. Choose a greater or basic lesson from the list here. You gain its associated hex, and your familiar learns the associated spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Greater Lesson",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5004",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Incredible Familiar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your familiar is imbued with even more magic than other familiars. You can select a base of six familiar or master abilities each day, instead of four.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-enhanced-familiar",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Incredible Familiar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5005",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Murksight"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your vision pierces through non-magical fog, mist, rain, and snow. You don’t take circumstance penalties to ranged attacks or Perception checks caused by non-magical precipitation, and your targeted attacks don’t require a flat check to succeed against a target concealed only by such effects.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Murksight",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5008",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Witch’s Bottle"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You spend 10 minutes and 1 Focus Point brewing a special potion containing the power of one of your hexes that targets a creature. A creature that consumes this potion is targeted by the hex. If the hex has a sustained duration and you have cackle, you can cast cackle into the bottle just before you seal it. If you do, the hex's duration is extended as if you had cast cackle the round after the hex was cast (typically this extends the duration by 1 round). Your cackling laugh sounds out when the potion is unsealed. Any potion you create this way loses its power the next time you make your daily preparations. While the potion is in your possession, you can render it inert using a single action that has the concentrate trait. You can't regain the Focus Point you spent to create the potion (or the Focus Point you spent to cast cackle) until the potion is consumed or loses its magic.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-cauldron",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Witch’s Bottle",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5010",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Major Lesson"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your patron grants you even greater secrets. Choose a major, greater, or basic lesson from the list here. You gain its associated hex, and your familiar learns the associated spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Major Lesson",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5013",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hex Focus"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your patron’s teachings have allowed you to achieve a deeper focus. Whenever you Refocus, completely refill your focus pool.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Hex Focus",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=502",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Far Shot"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your experience in the field has taught you how to focus your aim at a distance, increasing your accuracy. Double your weapons’ range increments.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Far Shot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5024",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Familiar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You make a pact with a creature that serves you and assists your spellcasting. You gain a familiar.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Familiar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5028",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bespell Strikes"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5028#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You siphon spell energy into one weapon you’re wielding, or into one of your unarmed attacks, such as a fist. Until the end of your turn, the weapon or unarmed attack deals an extra 1d6 force damage and gains the associated trait (see below) if it didn’t have it already. If the spell dealt a different type of damage, the Strike deals this type of damage instead (or one type of your choice if the spell could deal multiple types of damage). Oracle: Your strike gains the divine trait. Sorcerer: Your strike gains the trait of your bloodline’s magical tradition. Wizard: Your strike gains the arcane trait.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Bespell Strikes",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5028#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5032",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Convincing Illusion"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5032#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You use your deceptive skills to make your illusions seem even more real. Attempt a Deception check against the target’s Perception DC. If you succeed, the target fails to disbelieve the illusion.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Convincing Illusion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5032#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5036",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced School Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain access to the advanced teachings of your arcane institution, learning a powerful new school spell. You gain the advanced school spell for your arcane school.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced School Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5044",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Magic Sense"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have a literal sixth sense for ambient magic in your vicinity. You can sense the presence of magic auras as though you were always using a 1st-rank detect magic spell. This detects magic in your field of vision only. When you Seek, you gain the benefits of a 3rd-rank detect magic spell on things you see (in addition to the normal benefits of Seeking). You can turn this sense off and on with a free action at the start or the end of your turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Magic Sense",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Arcane",
            "aonprd:Trait-Detection",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=506",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Snare Specialist"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You specialize in creating quick traps to obstruct your enemies on the battlefield. If your proficiency rank in Crafting is expert, you gain the formulas for three common or uncommon snares. If your rank is master, you gain 6. If your rank is legendary, you gain 9. Each day during your daily preparations, you can prepare four snares from your formula book for quick deployment; if they normally take 1 minute to Craft, you can Craft them with 3 Interact actions. The number of snares increases to six if you have master proficiency in Crafting and eight if you have legendary proficiency in Crafting. Snares prepared in this way don't cost you any resources to Craft.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-crafting-snare-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Snare Specialist",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=508",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mature Animal Companion (Ranger)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your animal companion becomes a mature animal companion and gains additional capabilities. Your animal companion has greater independence. During an encounter, even if you don't use the Command an Animal action, your animal companion can still use 1 action that round on your turn to Strike or Stride (or Burrow, Climb, Fly, or Swim if it has that Speed). It can do this at any point during your turn, as long as you aren’t currently taking an action. If it does, that’s all the actions it gets that round—you can’t Command it later.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Mature Animal Companion (Ranger)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=510",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Skirmish Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=510#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your feet and weapon move in tandem. Either Step and then Strike, or Strike and then Step.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Skirmish Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=510#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5117",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemical Crafting"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can use the Craft activity to create alchemical items. When you select this feat, you immediately add the formulas for four common 1st-level alchemical items to your formula book.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemical Crafting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5125",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Battle Medicine"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5125#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can patch up wounds, even in combat. Attempt a Medicine check with the same DC as for Treat Wounds and restore the corresponding amount of HP; this doesn’t remove the wounded condition. As with Treat Wounds, you can attempt checks against higher DCs if you have the minimum proficiency rank. The target is then immune to your Battle Medicine for 1 day. This does not make them immune to, or otherwise count as, Treat Wounds.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-medicine",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Battle Medicine",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5125#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5131",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cat Fall"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your catlike aerial acrobatics allow you to cushion your falls. Treat falls as 10 feet shorter. If you’re an expert in Acrobatics, treat falls as 25 feet shorter and 50 feet if you’re a master. If you’re legendary in Acrobatics, you always land on your feet and don’t take damage, regardless of the distance of the fall.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-acrobatics",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Cat Fall",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=514",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Deadly Aim"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=514#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You aim for your prey’s weak spots, making your shot more challenging but dealing more damage if you hit. Make a ranged Strike against your hunted prey at a –2 penalty. You gain a +4 circumstance bonus to damage on that Strike. This bonus increases to +6 at 11th level and +8 at 15th level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-weapon-specialization",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Deadly Aim",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=514#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5140",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Diehard"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "It takes more to kill you than most. You die from the dying condition at dying 5, rather than dying 4.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Diehard",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5147",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fascinating Performance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you Perform, compare your result to the Will DC of one observer. If you succeed, the target is fascinated by you for 1 round. If the observer is in a situation that demands immediate attention, such as combat, you must critically succeed to fascinate it and the Perform action gains the incapacitation trait. You must choose which creature you're trying to fascinate before you roll your check, and the target is then temporarily immune for 1 hour. If you're an expert in Performance, you can fascinate up to four observers; if you're a master, you can fascinate up to 10 observers; and if you're legendary, you can fascinate any number of observers at the same time.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-performance",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Fascinating Performance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5159",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Impressive Performance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your performances inspire admiration and win you fans. You can Make an Impression using Performance instead of Diplomacy. If you spend at least 10 minutes performing in front of an audience, you can Make an Impression targeting up to 10 members of the audience who were there for the whole performance, without taking the normal penalty. The number of targets increases to 20 for a 1-hour performance and 50 for a 2-hour performance.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-performance",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Impressive Performance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5182",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Natural Medicine"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can apply natural cures to heal your allies. You can use Nature instead of Medicine to Treat Wounds, including higher Nature proficiency letting you attempt more difficult checks. It doesn’t replace Medicine for uses of the skill other than Treat Wounds or for feat prerequisites. If you’re in the wilderness, you might have easier access to fresh ingredients, allowing you to gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your check to Treat Wounds using Nature, subject to the GM’s determination.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-nature",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Natural Medicine",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5184",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "No Cause for Alarm"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5184#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You attempt to reduce panic. Attempt a Diplomacy check, comparing it to the Will DC of creatures in a 10-foot emanation around you who are frightened. Each of them is temporarily immune for 1 hour. Critical Success Reduce the creature's frightened value by 2. Success Reduce the creature's frightened value by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-diplomacy",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "No Cause for Alarm",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5184#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5186",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Pet"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have a pet-a Tiny animal of a type you choose, such as a cat, bird, or rodent. It has the minion trait, meaning it gains 2 actions during your turn if you use the Command an Animal action to command it; this replaces the usual effects of Command an Animal, and you don't need to attempt a Nature check. A pet can't take attack actions except to Escape or Force Open. Level Your pet's level is equal to yours. Modifiers and AC Your pet's save modifiers and AC are equal to yours before applying circumstance or status bonuses or penalties. It uses 3 + your level as its modifier for Perception, Acrobatics, and Stealth, and just your level as its modifier for other skill checks. It doesn't have or use its own attribute modifiers and can never benefit from item bonuses. Hit Points Your pet has 5 Hit Points per level. Senses Your pet has low-light vision and can gain additional senses from pet abilities. Speed Your pet has a Speed of 25 feet. You can choose to instead have an aquatic pet, which breathes in water instead of air and has the aquatic trait, no land Speed, and a swim Speed of 25 feet. Pet Abilities When you gain your pet, choose two of the following abilities. If your pet is an animal that naturally has one of these abilities (for instance, an owl has a fly Speed), you must select that ability. Your pet can't be an animal that naturally has more pet abilities than the maximum. In some cases, the GM might add some familiar abilities described on pages 212–213 to the pet abilities you can choose.Amphibious It gains the amphibious trait, allowing it to breathe in both air and water, and has both a land Speed and a swim Speed, each equal to its highest land Speed or swim Speed.Burrower It gains a burrow Speed of 5 feet, allowing it to dig Tiny holes.Climber It gains a climb Speed of 25 feet.Darkvision It gains darkvision.Echolocation Your pet can use hearing as a precise sense within 20 feet.Fast Movement Increase one of the pet's Speeds from 25 feet to 40 feet.Flier It gains a fly Speed of 25 feet.Manual Dexterity It can use up to two of its limbs as if they were hands to perform manipulate actions.Scent Your pet can use scent as an imprecise sense within 30 feetTough Your pet's max HP increase by 2 per level.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Pet",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5195",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Identification"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can Identify Magic swiftly. You take only 1 minute when using Identify Magic to determine the properties of an item, ongoing effect, or location, rather than 10 minutes. If you’re a master, it takes a 3-action activity, and if you’re legendary, it takes 1 action.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-arcana-nature-occultism-or-religion",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Identification",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5196",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Jump"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can use High Jump and Long Jump as a single action instead of 2 actions. If you do, you don’t perform the initial Stride (nor do you fail if you don’t Stride 10 feet).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Jump",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=520",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Incredible Companion (Ranger)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your animal companion continues to grow and develop. It becomes a nimble or savage animal companion (your choice), gaining additional capabilities determined by the type of companion.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mature-animal-companion-ranger",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Incredible Companion (Ranger)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5212",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shield Block"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5212#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You snap your shield in place to ward off a blow. Your shield prevents you from taking an amount of damage up to the shield’s Hardness. You and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Shield Block",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5212#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=522",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Penetrating Shot"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=522#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You shoot clear through an intervening creature to hit your prey. Choose a target that is giving lesser cover to your hunted prey. Make a single ranged Strike with the required weapon against the chosen target and your hunted prey. This attack ignores any lesser cover the chosen target provides your hunted prey. Roll damage only once, and apply it to each creature you hit. A Penetrating Shot counts as two attacks for your multiple attack penalty",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Penetrating Shot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=522#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=525",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Distracting Shot"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The sheer power of your attacks, or the overwhelming number of them, leaves an enemy flustered. If you critically hit your hunted prey with a ranged weapon, or hit it at least twice on the same turn with a ranged weapon, it’s off-guard until the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Distracting Shot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=529",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Side by Side (Ranger)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You and your animal companion fight in tandem. Whenever you and your animal companion are adjacent to the same foe, you are both flanking that foe with each other, regardless of your actual positions.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-an-animal-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Side by Side (Ranger)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=538",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Specialized Companion (Ranger)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your animal companion continues to grow in power and ability, and it is now cunning enough to become specialized. Your animal companion gains one specialization of your choice.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-incredible-companion-ranger",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Specialized Companion (Ranger)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5415",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Zoophonic Communication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your studies have expanded your ability to parley and negotiate into the animal realm. You can Request from animals using Performance instead of Diplomacy as though you shared a language, although this gives you no special ability to understand their responses. You can also use Performance instead of Nature to Command an Animal.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-zoophonia-muse",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Zoophonic Communication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=543",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Masterful Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your animal companion shares your incredible hunting skills, allowing it to take down your shared prey with ease. When you Hunt Prey, your animal companion gains the masterful hunter benefit associated with your hunter’s edge, rather than just your original hunter’s edge benefit.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-masterful-hunter-animal-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Masterful Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ranger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=551",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Trap Finder"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have an intuitive sense that alerts you to the presence of traps. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to find traps, to AC against attacks made by traps, and to saves against traps. Even if you aren’t Searching, you get a check to find traps that normally require you to be Searching. You still need to meet any other requirements to find the trap. You can disable traps that require a proficiency rank of master in Thievery. If you have master proficiency in Thievery, you can disable traps that require a proficiency rank of legendary instead, and your circumstance bonuses against traps increase to +2.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Trap Finder",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=553",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "You're Next"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=553#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "After downing a foe, you menace another. Attempt to Demoralize a creature within 60 feet, with a +2 circumstance bonus. If you have legendary proficiency in Intimidation, you can use this as a free action with the same trigger.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-intimidation",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "You're Next",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fear",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue",
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=553#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=555",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Distracting Feint"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your Feints are far more distracting than normal. While a creature is off-guard by your Feint, it also takes a –2 circumstance penalty to Perception checks and Reflex saves.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-scoundrel-racket",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Distracting Feint",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=561",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dread Striker"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You capitalize on your enemies’ fear to slip past their defenses. Any creature that has the frightened condition is also off-guard against your attacks.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Dread Striker",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=562",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Magical Trickster"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Whether you’re using magic items, wielding innate magic, or dabbling in spellcasting, you can sneak spells past your foes’ defenses as easily as any blade. When you succeed at a spell attack roll against a flat-footed foe’s AC and the spell deals damage, you can add your sneak attack damage to the damage roll. If your single spell leads to multiple separate damage rolls, apply your sneak attack damage only once per target.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Magical Trickster",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5760",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemical Familiar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have used alchemy to create life, a simple creature formed from alchemical materials, reagents, and a bit of your own blood. You gain a familiar, which has the construct familiar ability; this is permanent, doesn't require the familiar to have the tough familiar ability, and doesn't count against your usual limit of familiar abilities (typically 2). The familiar uses your Intelligence modifier to determine its Perception, Acrobatics, and Stealth modifiers.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemical Familiar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5764",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Bomber"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5764#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You keep your bombs and bomb-related reagents in easy-to-reach pouches from which you draw without thinking. You Interact to draw a bomb, draw a versatile vial, or use Quick Alchemy to create a bomb, then Strike with the bomb. If you have the ability to create more than one bomb at a time with Quick Alchemy (such as from the double brew class feature), you can Strike with only one of the bombs you create with this action.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Bomber",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5764#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5765",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Soothing Vials"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The healing chemicals in your versatile vials also help calm a patient's mind. When a living creature affected by a mental effect regains Hit Points from one of your versatile vials, it can immediately attempt a new Will saving throw to end one mental effect of its choice. It gains a +1 item bonus to the saving throw.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-chirurgeon-research-field",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Soothing Vials",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5766",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Clotting Elixirs"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your restorative concoctions have a clotting effect on the drinker's blood. When a living creature drinks an infused elixir with the healing trait that you have created, it can immediately attempt a DC 10 flat check to remove any persistent bleed damage.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Clotting Elixirs",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5769",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Revivifying Mutagen"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5769#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You metabolize a mutagen to heal yourself. You regain 1d6 Hit Points for every 2 levels you have, but the mutagen's duration immediately ends.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Revivifying Mutagen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5769#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5770",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Smoke Bomb"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can add a tarry additive to an alchemical bomb to make it emit smoke. When thrown, in addition to its normal effects, the bomb creates a cloud of smoke in a 10-foot burst. You choose which corner of the target's space (or the space in which the bomb lands) the cloud is centered on. Creatures within that area have the concealed condition, and all other creatures are concealed to them. The smoke lasts for 1 minute or until dissipated by a strong wind.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Smoke Bomb",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Additive",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5774",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Invigorating Elixir"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can mix an aromatic salve into an elixir with the healing trait to soothe physical maladies. In addition to its normal effects, the elixir can be imbibed by a creature prevented from doing so (such as a sickened creature). In addition to its other effects, the elixir attempts to counteract an effect imposing one of the following conditions of the imbiber's choice: clumsy, enfeebled, sickened, or stupefied. Use half your level rounded up for the counteract rank and your class DC – 10 for the counteract modifier. The imbiber is then temporarily immune to the effects of this additive for 10 minutes. The additive can't counteract curses, diseases, or conditions that are part of the creature's normal state.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Invigorating Elixir",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Additive",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5775",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Regurgitate Mutagen"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5775#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You redirect a mutagen within your body to spit a stream of stomach acid at a foe. A creature within 30 feet takes 1d6 acid damage for every 2 levels you have, with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. On a failure, the creature is also sickened 1 (or sickened 2 on a critical failure). The mutagen's duration immediately ends.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Regurgitate Mutagen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5775#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5777",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Combine Elixirs"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can add the full ingredients of a second elixir to an elixir you make to create a hybrid concoction. You must expend an additional versatile vial to make this combined elixir, and the ingredients must be for an elixir of the same level or lower that you could create with Quick Alchemy. When this combination elixir is consumed, both the constituent elixirs take effect. For example, you can combine two lesser elixirs of life to create a combined elixir that heals twice the normal amount, or you can combine a lesser darkvision elixir with a lesser eagle-eye elixir to both gain darkvision and find secret doors.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Combine Elixirs",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Additive",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5779",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Directional Bombs"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can lob bombs with great force and a precise trajectory to angle the splash in a cone that sprays in a single direction, potentially allowing you to avoid allies and splash deeper into enemy lines. When throwing an alchemical bomb with the splash trait, instead of splashing all squares adjacent to the target, you can create a splash in a 15-foot cone. You choose the cone's direction, but its first square must be a square in the target's space.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Directional Bombs",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5783",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Improved Invigorating Elixir"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Choose physical invigoration or mental invigoration, and add the listed conditions to those you can choose for an invigorating elixir you create to counteract: Physical Invigoration blinded, deafened, drained, paralyzed, slowed; Mental Invigoration confused, controlled, fleeing, frightened, paralyzed, slowed.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-invigorating-elixir",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Improved Invigorating Elixir",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5784",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mutant Physique"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Basic mutagens that affect your physical form can bring out the beast within you, turn you nigh invincible, or make your body more elastic. While you're affected by one of the listed mutagens, you get an additional benefit. Bestial Mutagen You gain the mutagen's item bonus to your Intimidation checks. In addition, you increase the damage die size of your claws and jaws by one step, and they gain the deadly d10 trait.Juggernaut Mutagen You gain resistance to all physical damage equal to half your level.Quicksilver Mutagen You can stretch your legs and Step up to 10 feet, and you can squish and compress your body, allowing you to make it through tight spaces as if you were one size smaller, in addition to any effect from Squeezing.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Mutant Physique",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5786",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sticky Bomb"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can mix in a sticky additive to an alchemical bomb to make its contents adhere and continue to deal damage. A creature hit by a sticky bomb also takes persistent damage equal to and of the same type as the bomb's splash damage. If the bomb already deals persistent damage, combine the two amounts. Use the splash damage amount listed in the bomb's stat block, even if you used an ability to change the splash damage dealt.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Sticky Bomb",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Additive",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5788",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Expanded Splash"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can throw bombs at just the right trajectory to create especially large and powerful explosions. When you throw an alchemical bomb and that bomb has the splash trait, you can have the splash damage affect all creatures within 10 feet of the target instead of 5 feet. If you do, you gain a status bonus to the bomb's splash damage equal to your Intelligence modifier. If you have the bomber 5th-level field discovery, this additional damage applies even if you caused your bomb to deal splash damage equal to your Intelligence modifier instead of the normal amount, allowing your bombs to deal splash damage equal to double your Intelligence modifier.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Expanded Splash",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=579",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sneak Adept"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "It’s almost impossible to spot you. When you roll a failure on a Sneak action, you get a success instead. You can still critically fail.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-stealth",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Sneak Adept",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5792",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Supreme Invigorating Elixir"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "For the purposes of counteracting effects with invigorating elixirs, treat your level as though it were 2 higher. Add the listed conditions to those you can choose for an invigorating elixir you create to counteract: petrified, stunned. You can also choose a disease regardless of what, if any, conditions it imposes.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-invigorating-elixir",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Supreme Invigorating Elixir",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5795",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mutant Innervation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Basic mutagens that affect your mind and thoughts can make you communicate telepathically, protect you from being detected, or let you communicate with anyone. While you're affected by one of the listed mutagens, you get an additional benefit. Cognitive Mutagen You also gain the mutagen's item bonus to Deception, Diplomacy, Intimidation, Medicine, Nature, Performance, Religion, and Survival checks. In addition, you can communicate telepathically with creatures within 60 feet with whom you share a language. The communication is two-way once you establish it, so a creature you contact can also communicate with you.Serene Mutagen Detection, revelation, and scrying effects of 9th rank (or 17th level) or lower detect nothing from you or your possessions and auras. For instance, detect magic would still detect other magic in the area, but not any magic on you.Silvertongue Mutagen Ignore circumstance penalties you would take to Deception, Diplomacy, Intimidation, and Performance checks. In addition, your words transcend linguistic barriers; everyone listening to you speak hears your words as if you were speaking in their own language (though you don't actually speak that language, nor does this ability allow you to understand any additional languages).",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Mutant Innervation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5799",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Persistent Mutagen"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've trained your physical form to remain stable. Once per day, when you consume an alchemical item with the infused and mutagen traits, you can extend its duration to last until the next time you make your daily preparations instead of its normal duration. Unlike with the normal extension from Extend Elixir, this can exceed the duration of an item created with Quick Alchemy beyond its normal 10-minute limit.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-extend-elixir",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Persistent Mutagen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=580",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tactical Debilitations"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn new debilitations that grant you tactical advantages against your foes. Add the following debilitations to the list you can choose from when you use Debilitating Strike. Debilitation The target can’t use reactions.Debilitation The target can’t flank or contribute to allies’ flanking.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-scoundrel-racket-debilitating-strike",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Tactical Debilitations",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5801",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Miracle Worker"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your alchemical mastery can resuscitate the recently slain. You can administer a major or true elixir of life to a creature who has been dead for no more than 2 rounds. When you do, that creature is immediately returned to life with 1 Hit Point and becomes wounded 1.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Miracle Worker",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5803",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemical Revivification"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "If you die while under the effect of at least one elixir, the alchemical compounds in your bloodstream bring you back to life at the start of your next turn. You're affected by an elixir of rejuvenation, then a true elixir of life, then your choice of a major bestial mutagen, major juggernaut mutagen, or major quicksilver mutagen as though you just imbibed it. These automatic reactions don't get any special benefits you add when creating or using these items. Because you died, all other alchemical compounds in your bloodstream are inert. After being revived, you're temporarily immune to Alchemical Rejuvenation for 1d4 hours.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemical Revivification",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5804",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Craft Philosopher's Stone"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your research has paid off, culminating in the legendary philosopher's stone. You learn the formula for the philosopher's stone and can add it to your formula book.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Craft Philosopher's Stone",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5805",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mega Bomb"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can add a highly explosive additive to an alchemical bomb to turn it into a mega bomb. Throwing this bomb takes a 2-action activity instead of a Strike. This isn't a Strike, and you don't make an attack roll. The mega bomb explodes in a 30-foot burst within 60 feet. It deals damage as if each creature were the primary target, with a basic Reflex save. On a failed save, a creature also takes any extra effects that affect a primary target (such as off-guard from bottled lightning). Though all targets in the area take splash damage as primary targets, there is no further splash beyond that area.",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Mega Bomb",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Additive",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5810",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Raging Intimidation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your fury fills your foes with fear. While you are raging, your Demoralize and Scare to Death actions (from the Intimidation skill and an Intimidation skill feat, respectively) gain the rage trait, allowing you to use them while raging. As soon as you meet the prerequisites for the skill feats Intimidating Glare and Scare to Death, you gain these feats.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Raging Intimidation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5814",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Furious Finish"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5814#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Desperate to finish the fight, you pour all your rage into one final blow. Make a Strike. If it hits, you gain a circumstance bonus to damage equal to the number of rounds remaining in your Rage (maximum 10). After this Strike, your Rage immediately ends, and you are fatigued until you rest for at least 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Furious Finish",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5814#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5815",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "No Escape"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5815#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You keep pace with a retreating foe. Stride up to your Speed, following the enemy and keeping it in reach throughout its movement until it stops moving or you've moved your full Speed. You can use No Escape to Burrow, Climb, Fly, or Swim instead of Stride if you have the corresponding movement type.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "No Escape",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5815#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5820",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Scars of Steel"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5820#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "When you are struck with the mightiest of blows, you can flex your muscles to turn aside some of the damage. You gain resistance to the triggering attack equal to your Constitution modifier plus half your level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-fury-instinct",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Scars of Steel",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5820#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5824",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Animal Skin"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your proficiency in unarmored defense increases to expert. When you are raging and unarmored, your skin transforms into a thick hide. You gain a +2 item bonus to AC (+3 if you have the greater juggernaut class feature). The thickness of your hide gives you a Dexterity modifier cap to your AC of +3. This item bonus to AC is cumulative with armor potency runes on your explorer's clothing, mystic armor, and bands of force.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-instinct",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Animal Skin",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Morph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5832",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reactive Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5832#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You lash out at a foe that leaves an opening. Make a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If your attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, you disrupt that action. This Strike doesn't count toward your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Reactive Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5832#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5835",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Animalistic Brutality"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5835#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You deepen the connection into your animal instincts. Your unarmed attack from bestial rage gains one of the following traits until you stop raging: backswing, forceful, parry, razing, or sweep. You can't use this ability again until the next time you Rage. You can choose a different trait each time you use Animalistic Brutality",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-instinct",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Animalistic Brutality",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Morph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5835#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5853",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Terrifying Howl"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5853#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You unleash a terrifying howl. Attempt Intimidation checks to Demoralize each enemy within 30 feet: you don't take a penalty if the creature doesn't understand your language. Regardless of the results of your checks, each target is then temporarily immune to Terrifying Howl for 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Terrifying Howl",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5853#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5857",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Predator's Pounce"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5857#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You close the distance to your prey in a blur, pouncing on the creature before it can react. You Stride up to your Speed and make a Strike at the end of your movement.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-instinct",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Predator's Pounce",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Barbarian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5857#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=586",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spring from the Shadows"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=586#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You leap from hiding and assail your target. You Stride up to your Speed, but you must end your movement next to an enemy you’re hidden from or undetected by. You then Strike that enemy; you remain hidden from or undetected by that creature until after you Strike. You can use Spring from the Shadows while Burrowing, Climbing, Flying, or Swimming instead of Striding if you have the corresponding movement type.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Spring from the Shadows",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=586#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5883",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Deity's Domain"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You embody an aspect of your deity. Choose one of your deity's domains. You gain the domain's initial domain spell as a devotion spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Deity's Domain",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5892",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Divine Grace"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5892#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You call upon your deity's grace, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to the save.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Divine Grace",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5892#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5897",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mercy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your touch soothes the body or mind. You can cast lay on hands targeting a living creature using 2 actions instead of 1. If you do, you can attempt to counteract one condition of your choice affecting the target. When you select this feat, choose one of the following options, which determines the conditions you can choose: Mercy of the Body blinded, dazzled, deafened, enfeebled, sickened; Mercy of Grace clumsy, grabbed, paralyzed; Mercy of the Mind fleeing, frightened, stupefied.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-lay-on-hands",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Mercy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5904",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Greater Mercy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your faith enhances your ability to remove conditions. Add the following options to the list of conditions you can counteract for any type of mercy you can grant. Mercy of the Body drained, slowed; if you're 16th level, add stunned; Mercy of Grace immobilized, restrained, slowed; if you're 12th level, add petrified; if you're 16th level, add stunned; Mercy of the Mind confused, controlled, slowed; if you're 16th level, add doomed and stunned.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mercy",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Greater Mercy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5929",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ultimate Mercy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mercy transcends the bounds of life and death. Add ultimate mercy to the types of mercy you can provide. When you use Mercy, you can target a creature that died since your last turn to return it to life. The target returns to life with 1 Hit Point and becomes wounded 1. You can't return the target to life if it died from disintegrate or a death effect. The creature gains the other benefits of lay on hands after it returns to life.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-mercy",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Ultimate Mercy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Champion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5935",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Flexible Studies"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've collected a cross-section of information on various disciplines you can refer to when preparing for various tasks. During your daily preparations, you can cram on a certain subject to become temporarily trained in one skill of your choice. This proficiency lasts until you prepare again. As this proficiency is temporary, you can't use it as a prerequisite for a permanent character option like a skill increase or a feat.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Flexible Studies",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5936",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Known Weaknesses"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Whenever you Devise a Stratagem, you can also attempt a check to Recall Knowledge as part of that action before rolling the d20. If you critically succeed at the Recall Knowledge check, you notice a weakness and can convey the information to allies to grant each of them a +1 circumstance bonus to their next attack roll against the subject, as long as their attack is made before the beginning of your next turn. If you choose an attack stratagem, this bonus applies to that attack roll too.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Known Weaknesses",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5938",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "That's Odd"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you enter a new location, such as a room or corridor, you immediately notice one thing out of the ordinary. The GM determines what it is, or whether there's nothing reasonable to pick up, skipping obvious clues that can be easily noticed without a check or specifically looking for them. You learn only that an area or object is suspicious, but not why it's suspicious. For example, if you entered a study with a large bloodstain on the ground, the bloodstain is so obviously suspicious it's evident to you already, so the GM might note that there's something suspicious about the desk drawer instead. You would then need to investigate the drawer further to find out what specifically is out of the ordinary. If you wish, you can Pursue a Lead concerning this detail even if you have Pursed a Lead less than 10 minutes ago. That's Odd doesn't reveal whether creatures are suspicious. You don't typically get any benefit when you leave and come back to a place, though if a major change has happened there and time has passed, the GM might determine that you do.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "That's Odd",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5943",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Person of Interest"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5943#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Sometimes, you need to follow the leads as they come in the middle of an investigation. Choose a creature that you can see who isn't, to your knowledge, tied to any of your current investigations. For the next minute, you can Devise a Stratagem against that creature as a free action.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Person of Interest",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5943#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5946",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemical Discoveries"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've devoted extra time in the lab to improve your knowledge of alchemy. You learn the formulas for two alchemical items each time you level up instead of one; these must still be elixirs or tools. The number of versatile vials you can create each day increases by one if you're an expert in Crafting, two if you're a master, or three if you're legendary.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-alchemical-sciences-methodology",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemical Discoveries",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5948",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lie Detector"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You're adept at noticing the tells of a liar—sweat, flushing, a quavering voice, a quickening pulse. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to Sense Motive and to Perception DCs against attempts to Lie to you. When you determine someone is lying to you, you can use their deceit to your advantage to gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the next Deception, Diplomacy, Intimidation, or Performance check you attempt against that creature within the next minute. If you would gain your Pursue a Lead investigation bonus to any of the above checks, that bonus increases by 1 instead of you gaining the +1 bonus listed.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-empiricism-or-interrogation-methodology",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Lie Detector",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=595",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Perfect Distraction"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=595#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You use clever tactics to mislead your foes as you sneak away. You Sneak while leaving a decoy behind. The decoy acts as the spell mislead, though you aren’t invisible, just undetected. You can continue to concentrate to move your decoy, as with the spell, whether or not you remain hidden throughout the duration. Once you use Perfect Distraction, you need to spend 10 minutes to set up another decoy before you can use it again.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-legendary-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Perfect Distraction",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=595#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5950",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Scalpel's Point"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your stratagems benefit from your precise knowledge of anatomy. When you critically hit with an attack on which you substituted your attack roll due to Devising a Stratagem, if your attack dealt piercing or slashing damage, you also deal 1d6 persistent bleed damage to your target.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-forensic-medicine-methodology",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Scalpel's Point",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5953",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Predictive Purchase"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have just the thing for the situation. You gain the Prescient Planner and Prescient Consumable feats. When using Prescient Planner, you can pull out the item as a 2-action activity to remove your backpack (or a similar container) and draw the item, rather than taking 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Predictive Purchase",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5954",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Thorough Research"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have comprehensive knowledge in your fields of interest. When you succeed at a Recall Knowledge check, you gain additional information or context. When you critically succeed at a check to Recall Knowledge, you get additional information or context or can ask an additional follow-up question (the GM chooses which).",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Thorough Research",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=596",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Implausible Infiltration"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=596#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You find tiny imperfections and somehow fit yourself through them, possibly moving directly through the wall or floor. Your movement attempt fails if the wall or floor is made of something other than wood, plaster, or stone; is thicker than 10 feet; or contains even a thin layer of metal. If you have a climb Speed, you can use this ability to attempt to move through a ceiling.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-legendary-in-acrobatics-quick-squeeze",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Implausible Infiltration",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Move",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rogue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=596#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5961",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Empiricist's Eye"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Sharp and piercing, your eyes see all and convey more. Your Point Out actions lose the auditory trait, and you don't need to be heard to convey the information to your allies. In addition, a creature you Point Out is off-guard to your allies until the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-empiricism-methodology",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Empiricist's Eye",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5967",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Surgical Shock"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5967#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With a few well-placed jabs with your fist or weapon, you render your opponent disoriented or ungainly. Attempt a Medicine check against the Fortitude DC of a target within your reach. The result of your check determines the severity of the condition you inflict. Critical Success The target is either clumsy 3 or stupefied 3 until the end of your next turn. The target is then immune to Surgical Shock for 1 hour. Success As critical success, but the target is either clumsy 2 or stupefied 2. Failure The target is minorly inconvenienced. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the next attack action you attempt against it before the end of your turn. Critical Failure The target is unaffected and you overextend yourself, triggering reactions as if you had used a manipulate action.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-forensic-medicine-methodology",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Surgical Shock",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Attack",
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5967#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5969",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Strategic Bypass"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your plans account for your foes' resistances, enabling you to strike a telling blow. When you hit with a Strike on which you substituted your attack roll due to Devising a Stratagem, you ignore an amount of resistance equal to your Intelligence modifier for each resistance that applies against your attack.",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Strategic Bypass",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5971",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Implausible Purchase"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "It seems impossible, but you've analyzed every angle and are able to just keep pulling out exactly the item you need, even in far-flung locations. You can use Prescient Planner even if you have already used it after purchasing goods, and you can use it as a single action instead of a 2-action activity, during which you Interact to draw the item. In addition, five times per day, you can use Prescient Planner to pull out a common consumable item up to 6 levels lower than your level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-predictive-purchase",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Implausible Purchase",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Investigator"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5976",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Crane Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5976#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your arms flutter like a crane's wings. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC, but the only Strikes you can make are crane wing attacks. These deal 1d6 bludgeoning damage; are in the brawling group; and have the agile, finesse, nonlethal, and unarmed traits. While in Crane Stance, reduce the DC for High Jump and Long Jump by 5, and when you Leap, you can move an additional 5 feet horizontally or 2 feet vertically.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Crane Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5976#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5977",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dragon Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5977#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter the stance of a dragon and make powerful leg strikes like a lashing dragon's tail. You can make dragon tail attacks that deal 1d10 bludgeoning damage. They are in the brawling group and have the backswing, nonlethal, and unarmed traits. While in Dragon Stance, you can ignore the first square of difficult terrain while Striding.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Dragon Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5977#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5980",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mountain Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5980#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter the stance of an implacable mountain—a technique created by dwarven monks—allowing you to strike with the weight of an avalanche and block blows with your garments. The only Strikes you can make are falling stone unarmed attacks. These deal 1d8 bludgeoning damage; are in the brawling group; and have the forceful, nonlethal, and unarmed traits. While in Mountain Stance, you gain a +4 item bonus to AC and a +2 circumstance bonus to any defenses against Reposition, Shove, Trip, and other forced movement effects. You have a Dexterity modifier cap to your AC of +0, meaning you don't add your Dexterity to your AC, and your Speeds are all reduced by 5 feet. The item bonus to AC from Mountain Stance is cumulative with armor potency runes on your explorer's clothing, mystic armor, and bands of force.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Mountain Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5980#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5981",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Qi Spells"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have cultivated your qi to produce magical effects. You gain inner upheaval, qi rush, or another 1st-rank monk qi spell you have access to.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Qi Spells",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5982",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stumbling Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5982#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter a seemingly unfocused stance that mimics the movements of the inebriated—bobbing, weaving, leaving false openings, and distracting your enemies from your true movements. While in this stance, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Deception checks to Feint. The only Strikes you can make are stumbling swing unarmed attacks. These deal 1d8 bludgeoning damage; are in the brawling group; and have the agile, backstabber, finesse, nonlethal, and unarmed traits. If an enemy hits you with a melee Strike while in this stance, it becomes off-guard against the next stumbling swing Strike you make against it before the end of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Stumbling Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5982#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5983",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tiger Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5983#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter the stance of a tiger and can make tiger claw attacks. These deal 1d8 slashing damage; are in the brawling group; and have the agile, finesse, nonlethal, and unarmed traits. On a critical success with your tiger claws, if you deal damage, the target takes 1d4 persistent bleed damage. As long as your Speed is at least 20 feet while in Tiger Stance, you can Step 10 feet.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Tiger Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5983#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5984",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Wolf Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5984#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter the stance of a wolf, low to the ground with your hands held like fangs. You can make wolf jaw unarmed attacks. These deal 1d8 piercing damage; are in the brawling group; and have the agile, backstabber, finesse, nonlethal, and unarmed traits. If you're flanking a target while in Wolf Stance, your wolf jaw unarmed attacks also gain the trip trait.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Wolf Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5984#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5987",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Elemental Fist"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can color your qi in bright elemental energy. When you cast inner upheaval, in addition to the damage types normally available, you can deliver the extra damage with elemental magic, adding the element's trait and changing the damage type to the listed one: air electricity (sparking gust), earth bludgeoning (chunk of stone), fire fire (flickering flame), metal slashing (flying metal shards), water cold (wave of frigid water), or wood bludgeoning (pummeling pine cones).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-inner-upheaval",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Elemental Fist",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5990",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cobra Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5990#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter a tightly coiled stance, with your hands poised as venomous fangs. While in this stance, the only Strikes you can make are cobra fang unarmed attacks. These deal 1d4 piercing damage; are in the brawling group; and have the agile, deadly d10, finesse, unarmed, and venomous traits. While in Cobra Stance, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Fortitude saves and your Fortitude DC, and you gain poison resistance equal to half your level.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Cobra Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5990#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5995",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Harmonize Self"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can restore your health by tapping into your qi. You gain the harmonize self qi spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-qi-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Harmonize Self",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=5998",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced Qi Spells"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your talent at controlling your qi has reached new heights. You gain qi blast, shrink the span, or another 3rd-rank qi spell you have access to.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-qi-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced Qi Spells",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6010",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Clinging Shadows Initiate"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn a mystical stance that transforms your qi into sticky smoke that shrouds your limbs. You gain the clinging shadows stance qi. While entering the stance is a qi spell, the shadow grasp attacks it grants are not, so you can use them as often as you like while in the stance.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-qi-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Clinging Shadows Initiate",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6011",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ironblood Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6011#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter the stance of impenetrable iron, refusing to yield to any blow. You can make iron sweep unarmed attacks. These deal 1d8 bludgeoning damage; are in the brawling group; and have the nonlethal, parry, sweep, and unarmed traits. While in Ironblood Stance, you gain resistance 2 to all damage. The resistance increases to 3 at 12th level, to 4 at 16th level, and to 5 at 20th level.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Ironblood Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6011#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6015",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tangled Forest Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6015#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You extend your arms like gnarled branches to interfere with your foes' movements. You can make lashing branch unarmed attacks. These deal 1d8 slashing damage; are in the brawling group; and have the agile, finesse, nonlethal, and unarmed traits. While you're in Tangled Forest Stance and can act, every enemy in your reach that tries to move away from you must succeed at a Reflex save, Acrobatics check, or Athletics check against your class DC or be immobilized for that action. If you prefer, you can allow the enemy to move.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Tangled Forest Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6015#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6017",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Wild Winds Initiate"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn a stance that lets you attack from a distance. You gain the wild winds stance qi spell. Though entering the stance is a qi spell, the wind crash Strikes the stance grants are not, so you can use them as often as you like while in the stance.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-qi-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Wild Winds Initiate",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6028",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Meditative Focus"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your meditation is so effective that you can achieve a deep focus with the world around you. When you Refocus, you regain all your Focus Points instead of 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-qi-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Meditative Focus",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=603",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dangerous Sorcery"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your legacy grants you great destructive power. When you Cast a Spell from your spell slots, if the spell deals damage and doesn’t have a duration, you gain a status bonus to that spell’s damage equal to the spell’s level.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Dangerous Sorcery",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=604",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Familiar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You make a pact with a creature that serves you and assists your spellcasting. You gain a familiar.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Familiar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6040",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Master Qi Spells"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have achieved near-total mastery of your qi. You gain medusa's wrath, touch of death, or another 8th-rank qi spell you have access to.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-qi-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Master Qi Spells",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6044",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Grandmaster Qi Spells"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have unlocked a qi technique achievable only by those who attain complete mastery of both their body and their spirit. You gain embrace nothingness, qi form, or another 9th-rank qi spell you have access to.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-qi-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Grandmaster Qi Spells",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6053",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Foretell Harm"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6053#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your magic echoes ominously as you glimpse injury in the target's future. At the beginning of your target's next turn, it takes damage equal to twice the triggering spell's rank as a seemingly random and minor misfortune finds it. The damage and type of misfortune is of a type matching the spell; for instance, if you dealt fire damage, a flame might spontaneous ignite on them or they might burn a hand on their torch. The target is then temporarily immune to Foretell Harm for 24 hours.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Foretell Harm",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6053#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6055",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Nudge the Scales"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6055#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You lay a finger on the scales of life and death to heal a creature, regardless of whether it's living or undead. You restore Hit Points equal to 2 + double your level to one creature within 30 feet. In addition, you can mediate during your daily preparations to place yourself on one side of the scales. Choose life or death. If you align yourself with life, you can be targeted and healed by vitality healing effects, as normal for most living creatures; if you align yourself with death, you gain the void healing ability, and can instead be targeted and healed by void effects and other effects that restore Hit Points to undead creatures.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Nudge the Scales",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spirit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6055#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6056",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Oracular Warning"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6056#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have a premonition about impending danger that you use to warn your allies. Each ally within 20 feet gains a +2 status bonus to their initiative roll and gains temporary Hit Points equal to half your level, which last for 1 minute. If you are cursebound 2 when you use Oracular Warning, the bonus increases to +3, and if you are cursebound 3, the bonus increases to +4.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Oracular Warning",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6056#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6057",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Whispers of Weakness"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6057#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Voices whisper to you how to best lay a creature low. You target one creature within 60 feet; if it has any weaknesses, you learn them, as well as which of its saving throw modifiers is lowest. You also come to understand its movements, gaining a +2 status bonus to your next attack roll (or skill check made as part of an attack action) against that foe before the end of your turn. The target is then temporarily immune for 1 day.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Whispers of Weakness",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6057#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6059",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Domain Acumen"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Every oracle's mystery touches on a divine domain of the deities that fuel it; you can access that power. Choose one of the domains associated with your mystery for which you don't already have an initial domain spell. You gain an initial domain spell from that domain, which you cast as a revelation spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Domain Acumen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6060",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Meddling Futures"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6060#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You open yourself to the guidance of whatever spirits or powers deign to help you. Roll 1d4 to see what type of spirit is drawn to you. Your next action must be the type of action the spirit prefers, but you also gain the listed benefit for the action as the spirit guides you. If you attempt to use a different action, you must succeed at a DC 6 flat check or the action is lost. 1 Warrior You must attempt a Strike. You gain a +1 status bonus to your attack roll and a +2 status bonus to damage, or a +6 status bonus to damage if you are at least cursebound 3. 2 Adept You must attempt a Perception check or a skill action. You gain a +1 status bonus to the check, or a +2 status bonus if you are cursebound 3. 3 Sage You must attempt to Cast a Spell. You gain a status bonus to the spell's damage or healing equal to the spell's rank, or equal to the spell's rank + 3 if you are at least cursebound 3. 4 Wanderer You must attempt a Stride action, or a Fly, Climb, or Burrow action if you have the relevant speed. You gain a +10- foot status bonus to your Speed for the action, or a +20-foot status bonus if you are at least cursebound 3.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Meddling Futures",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6060#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6061",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Knowledge of Shapes"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6061#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Inspiration lets you surpass your preconceptions of your spells' limits. You use Reach Spell or Widen Spell as a free action.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-widen-spell-or-reach-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Knowledge of Shapes",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6061#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6062",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Thousand Visions"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6062#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You open your senses to numerous visions of the immediate future. The visions grant you subtle details of your immediate surroundings within 30 feet. Within this range, you don't need to succeed at a flat check to target a concealed creature, you're not off-guard to creatures that are hidden from you (unless you're off-guard to them for reasons other than the hidden condition), and you need only a successful DC 5 flat check to target a hidden creature. Beyond 30 feet, the visions become overwhelmed with too many possible futures, making all of your senses imprecise beyond this range. The visions persist for 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Thousand Visions",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Prediction"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6062#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6063",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced Revelation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Divine power reveals greater mysteries to you. You learn the advanced revelation spell associated with your mystery.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-initial-revelation-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced Revelation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6064",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Gifted Power"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mystery grants you additional magic. You have an extra spell slot of your highest rank, which you can use only to cast one of your mystery's granted spells, heightened to this rank.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Gifted Power",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6067",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Read Disaster"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You spend 10 minutes and open yourself to the divine mysteries of the world, peering into the most sinister portents of the future. You gain the effects of augury, except you learn only about the dangers ahead; any results of “good” are instead “nothing,” and results of “mixed” are instead “bad.” If you are legendary in Religion, you take only 1 minute to Read Disaster.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Read Disaster",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exploration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Prediction"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6068",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Surging Might"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6068#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You focus the power of your spell to overcome enemies' resistances. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell, the spell ignores an amount of the target's resistance equal to your level against the following types of damage: spirit, vitality, and void. This applies to all damage the spell deals, including persistent damage and damage caused by an ongoing effect of the spell. This doesn't cause the spell to ignore immunities, only resistances.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Surging Might",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6068#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6069",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Water Walker"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When in the throes of your curse, your steps take on a supernatural buoyancy. When you are cursebound 1, you can Stride across liquids that don't support your weight, but you must end your movement on a surface that can support you or you fall into the liquid as normal. When you are cursebound 2 or worse, you gain the effects of water walk.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Water Walker",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6072",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Trial by Skyfire"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6072#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your lips murmur as you portend a great disaster, one you hope you survive. A rain of blazing bolts begins to fall from the heavens in a 10-foot emanation, centered on you, that deals 2d6 fire damage to all creatures in the emanation at the end of each of your turns (basic Reflex save); you can't exclude yourself from the emanation. The skyfire persists for 1 minute; while you can't Dismiss it, you can suppress the effect for 1 round with a Sustain action. The rain of fire is suppressed if you fall unconscious. If you become cursebound 3 or 4 at any point during Trial by Skyfire's duration, the emanation increases to 15 feet and the damage increases to 4d6.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-cosmos-mystery-or-flame-mystery",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Trial by Skyfire",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6072#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6073",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Waters of Creation"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6073#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Water is the source of life, and you draw upon this primordial force to heal your allies' wounds. A gentle ring ripples out from you in a 15-foot emanation, restoring 5d6 Hit Points to creatures in the area. At 12th level and every two levels thereafter, the amount restored increases by 1d6. If you are cursebound 3 when you use Waters of Creation, the amount healed increases to d8s.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-life-mystery-or-tempest-mystery",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Waters of Creation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vitality",
            "aonprd:Trait-Water"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6073#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6074",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Domain Fluency"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You command a deep understanding of the domains related to your mystery. Choose one of the domains associated with your mystery for which you have an initial domain spell. You gain an advanced domain spell from that domain, which you cast as a revelation spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-domain-acumen",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Domain Fluency",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6075",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Epiphany at the Crossroads"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6075#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The crossroads between life and death is a place that can reveal many secrets. You gain the effects of an augury spell in a strange, near-death vision. Empowered by the realization, you then lose the dying condition (becoming wounded 1 or increasing your wounded value by 1, as normal), regain a number of Hit Points equal to twice your level, and can Stand.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Epiphany at the Crossroads",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6075#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6076",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Greater Revelation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You unlock deeper revelations hidden within your mystery. You gain your mystery’s greater revelation spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-initial-revelation-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Greater Revelation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6082",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Diverse Mystery"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have broadened your understanding of the divine and can tap into the wonders of a different mystery. Select one revelation spell from a mystery other than your own. You can choose only an initial revelation spell or an advanced revelation spell. This spell gains the cursebound trait for you, and when you cast it, you gain the cursebound 1 effects of its mystery in addition to your normal curse effects. Any ability that lets you use a cursebound ability without increasing the severity of your curse also prevents you from gaining this additional curse effect. You can't cast your chosen revelation spell if any of the following conditions are true: its mystery's curse effects directly conflict with or negate the effects of your own mystery's curse, the curse would have no effect on you (for example, removing an ability from your original mystery that you lack), or if either of these criteria would be met once you finish Casting the Spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Diverse Mystery",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6098",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Split Shot"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6098#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You fragment a ranged spell. If your next action is to Cast a Spell without a duration that requires an attack roll against a single target, you can choose a second target within range. You roll a single attack roll and compare the result to the AC of both targets. This counts as one attack for your multiple attack penalty. To the second target, the spell deals half the amount of damage it would normally deal and has no effects beyond the spell's initial damage (such as imposing conditions or penalties).",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Split Shot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6098#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6099",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced Bloodline"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You draw more power from your bloodline. You gain the advanced bloodline spell associated with your bloodline.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bloodline-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced Bloodline",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6106",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Explosion of Power"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your magic explodes. You know the following blood magic effect. Blood Magic—Explosion of Power Raw power explodes outward from you. Each creature within a 5-foot emanation takes 1d6 damage per rank of the spell you just cast (basic Reflex save). The type of damage depends on the tradition of your bloodline. If you cast arcane spells, you deal force damage. If you cast divine spells, you deal spirit damage. If you cast occult spells, you deal mental damage. If you cast primal spells, you deal fire damage.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Explosion of Power",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6108",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Greater Bloodline"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You uncover the greater secrets of your bloodline. You gain the greater bloodline spell associated with your bloodline.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bloodline-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Greater Bloodline",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=611",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Divine Evolution"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The divine might provided by your bloodline flows through you. You gain an additional spell slot of your highest rank, which you can use only to cast your choice of heal or harm. You can cast either of these spells using that spell slot, even if they aren't in your spell repertoire.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bloodline-that-grants-divine-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Divine Evolution",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6111",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bloodline Focus"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "By listening to the beating of your heart, your focus recovers faster. Whenever you Refocus, completely refill your focus pool.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bloodline-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Bloodline Focus",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=613",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Primal Evolution"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can call upon the creatures of the wild for aid. You gain an additional spell slot of your highest rank, which you can use only to cast summon animal or summon plant or fungus. You can cast either of these spells using that spell slot, even if they aren't in your spell repertoire.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bloodline-that-grants-primal-spells",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Primal Evolution",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6132",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Goading Feint"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your tricks make foes overextend their attacks. On a Feint, you can use the following success and critical success effects instead of any other effects you would gain when you Feint; if you do, other abilities that adjust the normal effects of your Feint no longer apply. You can choose whether to use the Goading Feint benefits or the normal benefits each time you Feint a given foe. Critical Success The target takes a –2 circumstance penalty to all attack rolls against you before the end of its next turn. Success The target takes a –2 circumstance penalty to its next attack roll against you before the end of its next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Goading Feint",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=614",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced Bloodline"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You draw more power from your bloodline. You gain the advanced bloodline spell associated with your bloodline.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bloodline-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced Bloodline",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6142",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tumble Behind (Swashbuckler)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your tumbling puts your foes on the back foot. When you Tumble Through successfully, the foe you Tumbled Through is off-guard against the next attack you make before the end of your turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Tumble Behind (Swashbuckler)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=616",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bloodline Resistance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your magical blood makes you more resistant to magic. You gain a +1 status bonus to saving throws against spells and magical effects.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Bloodline Resistance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6164",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reflexive Riposte"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can riposte almost without a thought. At the start of each of your turns when you regain your actions, you gain an additional reaction that can be used only to perform an Opportune Riposte.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-opportune-riposte",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Reflexive Riposte",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6176",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Felicitous Riposte"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You take advantage of your foe's openings with uncanny odds. When you make an Opportune Riposte, roll twice on the attack roll and take the better result.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Felicitous Riposte",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Swashbuckler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=618",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Greater Bloodline"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You uncover the greater secrets of your bloodline. You gain the greater bloodline spell associated with your bloodline.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bloodline-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Greater Bloodline",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=621",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bloodline Focus"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "By listening to the beating of your heart, your focus recovers faster. Whenever you Refocus, completely refill your focus pool.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bloodline-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Bloodline Focus",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=622",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Magic Sense"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have a literal sixth sense for ambient magic in your vicinity. You can sense the presence of magic auras as though you were always using a 1st-rank detect magic spell. This detects magic in your field of vision only. When you Seek, you gain the benefits of a 3rd-rank detect magic spell on things you see (in addition to the normal benefits of Seeking). You can turn this sense off and on with a free action at the start or the end of your turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Magic Sense",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Arcane",
            "aonprd:Trait-Detection",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sorcerer",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6266",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shield Salvation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can save your shield from total destruction, even after a devastating attack. If a shield would be destroyed due to damage taken during your Shield Block, the shield remains intact at 1 Hit Point instead. Its construction is weakened until you take the time to repair it thoroughly, preventing you from using Shield Salvation to save the same shield until your next preparations.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bastion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Shield Salvation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6328",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Familiar Master Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have forged a mystical bond with a creature. This might have involved complex rituals and invocations, such as meditating under the moon until something crept out of the forest. Or maybe you just did each other a good turn, such as rescuing the beast from a trap or a foe, and then being rescued in turn. Whatever the details, you are now comrades until the end. You gain a familiar. If you already have a familiar, you gain the Enhanced Familiar feat.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Familiar Master Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=640",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Conceal Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=640#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Through sheer mental effort, you can simplify the incantations and gestures needed to spellcast, leaving them barely noticeable. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell, the spell gains the subtle trait, hiding the shining runes, sparks of magic, and other manifestations that would usually give away your spellcasting. The trait hides only the spell's spellcasting actions and manifestations, not its effects, so an observer might still see a ray streak out from you or see you vanish into thin air.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Conceal Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Witch",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=640#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=644",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Silent Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=644#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve learned how to cast many of your spells without speaking the words of power you would normally need to provide. If the next action you use is Casting a Spell that has a verbal component and at least one other component, you can remove the verbal component. This makes the spell quieter and allows you to cast it in areas where sound can’t carry. However, the spell still has visual manifestations, so this doesn’t make the spell any less obvious to someone who sees you casting it. When you use Silent Spell, you can choose to gain the benefits of Conceal Spell, and you don’t need to attempt a Deception check because the spell has no verbal components.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-conceal-spell",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Silent Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Metamagic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=644#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6466",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bon Mot"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6466#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You launch an insightful quip at a foe, distracting them. Choose a foe within 30 feet and roll a Diplomacy check against the target's Will DC. Critical Success The target is distracted and takes a –3 status penalty to Perception and Will saves for 1 minute. The target can end the effect early with a retort to your Bon Mot. This can either be a single action that has the concentrate trait or an appropriate skill action to frame their retort. The GM determines which skill actions qualify, though they must take at least 1 action. Typically, the retort needs to use a linguistic Charisma-based skill action. Success As critical success, but the penalty is –2. Critical Failure Your quip is atrocious. You take the same penalty an enemy would take had you succeeded. This ends after 1 minute or if you issue another Bon Mot and succeed.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-diplomacy",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Bon Mot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6466#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=647",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced School Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain access to the advanced teachings of your arcane institution, learning a powerful new school spell. You gain the advanced school spell for your arcane school.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced School Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Wizard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6472",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Dirty Trick"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6472#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You hook a foe's bootlaces together, pull their hat over their eyes, loosen their belt, or otherwise confound their mobility through an underhanded tactic. Attempt a Thievery check against the target's Reflex DC. Critical Success The target is clumsy 1 until they use an Interact action to end the impediment Success As critical success, but the condition ends automatically after 1 round. Critical Failure You fall prone as your attempt backfires.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-thievery",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Dirty Trick",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Attack",
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6472#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6483",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Forensic Acumen"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You understand principles of forensic medicine, making you better at examining a body to determine the cause of death or injury. You can perform a forensic examination on a body, as described under Recall Knowledge in the Medicine skill, in half the normal amount of time (to a minimum of 5 minutes). If you succeed at your check, you can attempt an immediate check to Recall Knowledge to follow up on something you found, with a +2 circumstance bonus. This check is usually related to the cause of injury or death, such as a Crafting check to identify a poison or weapon used or an additional Medicine check to identify a specific disease. If you prefer, you can instead attempt to Recall Knowledge about the type of creature whose body you examined, using the appropriate skill and gaining the same circumstance bonus. The circumstance bonus increases to +3 if you have master proficiency in Medicine and +4 if you have legendary proficiency.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-medicine",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Forensic Acumen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6506",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Snare Crafting"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can use the Craft activity to create snares. When you select this feat, you immediately add the formulas for four common 1st-level snares to your formula book.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Snare Crafting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6519",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Red Mantis Assassin Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have learned how to stalk your foes and slay them with a sawtooth saber. You become trained in Stealth and Assassin Lore; if you were already trained, you become an expert instead. Whenever your proficiency in any weapon increases to expert or beyond, you also gain that new proficiency with sawtooth sabers. You become bound by Achaekek's anathema and can receive his sanctification.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-sawtooth-sabers-worshipper-of-achaekek-member-of-the-red-mantis-assassins",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Red Mantis Assassin Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6520",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Basic Red Mantis Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have learned limited divine magic from your Red Mantis training. You gain the Cast a Spell activity. You can prepare two common cantrips each day from the divine spell list or any other divine cantrips you have access to. You also gain the basic spellcasting benefits. You're trained in the spell attack modifier and spell DC statistics. Your key spellcasting attribute for the Red Mantis archetype spells is Charisma, and they are divine Red Mantis spells. If you gain a Focus Pool from any Red Mantis Assassin class feats, you can Refocus by praying to Achaekek or researching your assigned kill. You also have access to the Red Mantis magic school. In addition to preparing spells from the divine spell list, you can prepare spells from this school. Regardless of their usual magic tradition, when you prepare spells from this school, they are divine spells, as are any Red Mantis focus spells you gain.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-red-mantis-assassin-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Basic Red Mantis Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6521",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Crimson Shroud"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6521#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You swathe yourself in a veil of red mist for 1 minute. While the shroud is active, you gain fast healing equal to half your level. You can Interact with your shroud, swirling it around you, to gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC until the beginning of your next turn. Finally, if you die while the shroud is active, you can choose to have your entire body vanish into red mist, leaving behind only your gear; you make this choice when you activate Crimson Shroud. At 10th level, you can use this ability once per hour instead of once per day.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-red-mantis-assassin-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Crimson Shroud",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6521#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6522",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Red Mantis School Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the Red Mantis magic school's initial school spell. If you don't already have one, you gain a focus pool of 1 Focus Point.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-basic-red-mantis-magic",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Red Mantis School Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6523",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Achaekek's Grip"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You sense if a creature you have slain in the last year has been restored to life, as long as you and that creature are on the same plane. You also gain the Achaekek's clutch focus spell. If you don't already have one, you gain a focus pool of 1 Focus Point.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-basic-red-mantis-magic",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Achaekek's Grip",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6524",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mantis Form"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the mantis form focus spell. If you don't already have one, you gain a focus pool of 1 Focus Point.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-basic-red-mantis-magic",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Mantis Form",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6525",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fading"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6525#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You partially fade from reality. The attacker must attempt a DC 11 flat check; on a failure, the attack passes harmlessly through the image of your body that remains behind. An instant later you return to reality, and your Crimson Shroud ends",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-crimson-shroud",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Fading",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Teleportation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6525#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6526",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Expert Red Mantis Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the expert spellcasting benefits.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-religion-basic-red-mantis-magic",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Expert Red Mantis Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6527",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vernai Training"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "To resurrect a creature you've slain, a spellcaster must counteract your influence on its death. The DC of this check is equal to your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. In addition, you've undergone training to better make use of your magic. Increase the spell slots you gain from Red Mantis assassin archetype feats by 1 for each spell rank other than your two highest Red Mantis spell slots. You can prepare only spells from the Red Mantis magic school curriculum in these extra slots.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-achaekeks-grip-basic-red-mantis-magic",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Vernai Training",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6528",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Prayer Attack"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6528#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You've mastered the signature assassination style of the Red Mantis. Attempt to Feint an enemy within 30 feet. If your Feint is successful, when you use Prayer Attack on subsequent turns you automatically make the target flat-footed against your melee attacks for that turn without rolling a check to Feint, so long as you remain visible to the target and the target remains within 30 feet of you. If you use your Prayer Attack against a different target, you must attempt to Feint the target normally. When you use Prayer Attack, your next successful Strike with a sawtooth saber that turn deals 2d6 persistent bleed damage to the target.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-red-mantis-assassin-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Prayer Attack",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6528#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=6529",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Master Red Mantis Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the master spellcasting benefits.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-legendary-in-religion-basic-red-mantis-magic",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Master Red Mantis Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=667",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Alchemy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the Quick Alchemy action. Quick Alchemy [one-action] Alchemist Manipulate Source Core Rulebook pg. 72 Cost 1 batch of infused reagents Requirements You have the formula for the alchemical item you're creating, and you're either holding or wearing alchemist's tools.You swiftly mix up a short-lived alchemical item to use at a moment's notice. You create a single alchemical consumable item of your advanced alchemy level or lower that's in your formula book without having to spend the normal monetary cost in alchemical reagents or needing to attempt a Crafting check. This item has the infused trait, but it remains potent only until the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-alchemist-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Alchemy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7106",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rushing Goat Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7106#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter the stance of an unruly goat, lowering your body and preparing to butt heads with your foes. The only Strikes you can make are ramming horn attacks. These strikes deal 1d8 bludgeoning damage, are in the brawling group, and have the forceful, nonlethal, shove, and unarmed traits. When you make a ramming horn attack and your previous action was to Climb, Stride, or Leap, you gain a circumstance bonus to damage equal to the number of weapon damage dice. You can make ramming horn Strikes while Climbing even if you don’t have a free hand.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Rushing Goat Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7106#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7107",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Twisting Petal Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7107#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your body moves like a petal twisting on the wind, confounding your opponents while using their energy against them. You can make gale blossom strikes that deal 1d6 slashing damage. These strikes are in the brawling group and have the agile, finesse, nonlethal, shove, and unarmed traits. While in Twisting Petal Stance, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to Shove and a +2 circumstance bonus to your Fortitude DC to avoid being Shoved. You also gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Deception checks to Feint and a +2 circumstance bonus to your Perception DC to resist an opponent’s Feint attempt.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Twisting Petal Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7107#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7110",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Kaiju Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7110#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your encounter with one of the rare forces of nature known as kaiju has imbued you with knowledge of a martial art that allows you to emulate a fraction of their power. When you enter Kaiju Stance, you become Large and are clumsy 1. The only Strikes you can make are shattering earth attacks. These strikes deal 1d8 bludgeoning damage, are in the brawling group, and have the backswing, fatal d12, reach, and unarmed traits. On a critical success with a shattering earth attack, all creatures other than you that are within 10 feet of the target, including the target itself, take 1 point of bludgeoning splash damage per weapon damage die. While in Kaiju Stance, you ignore difficult terrain.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Kaiju Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Polymorph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7110#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7120",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Apparition Sense"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can see and interact with things others can’t. You have apparition sight, an imprecise sense that allows you to detect the presence of invisible or hidden spirits, haunts, and undead within 30 feet of you. You can allow a spirit or undead otherwise incapable of speech to speak through you as long as you are in direct contact with it. As an activity that takes 10 minutes, you can act as a link between disembodied souls and their mortal bodies. As long as you are in contact with both a spirit and a living body that belonged to it in life during that entire time, the spirit can use you to return to that body; this does not allow you to bring the dead back to life, but can assist in restoring a disembodied soul to a still-living body. If the body is occupied by another spirit or soul, that entity must succeed at a Will save against your spell DC or be cast from the body when its original owner is returned.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Apparition Sense",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7121",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Circle of Spirits"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7121#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With a thought, word, or gesture, you reach your mind out to another spirit. Choose another apparition from among those you’ve attuned to; it becomes your primary apparition, replacing your current one.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Circle of Spirits",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Apparition",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7121#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7122",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Relinquish Control"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7122#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your apparition takes over and shields you from outside influence. Until the start of your next turn, you gain a +4 status bonus on saves against spells and effects that give you the controlled condition or attempt to influence your actions (such as charm, command, or a nosoi’s haunting melody). However, the only actions you can take are to Recall Knowledge, Step, Strike, Cast an apparition Spell, Cast a vessel Spell, Sustain a vessel spell, or use an action that has the apparition trait. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus on all Recall Knowledge checks made using Lore skills granted by your attuned apparitions.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Relinquish Control",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Apparition"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7122#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7123",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spirit Familiar (Animist)"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you attune to your apparitions during your daily preparations, you can choose to dedicate a small amount of your life force to allow one of them to physically manifest as a familiar, which gains the spirit trait. If your familiar is slain or destroyed, you lose all other benefits from the apparition until you remanifest the familiar during your next daily preparations. If you disperse the apparition you have manifested as a familiar, the familiar is destroyed.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Spirit Familiar (Animist)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7126",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spiritual Expansion Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7126#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your apparitions manifest to scatter the energy of your spell. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that has an area of a burst, cone, or line and does not have a duration, increase the area of that spell. Add 5 feet to the radius of a burst that normally has a radius of at least 10 feet (a burst with a smaller radius is not affected). Add 5 feet to the length of a cone or line that is normally 15 feet long or smaller, and add 10 feet to the length of a larger cone or line. You can also use this feat to increase the radius of an emanation spell with a duration by 5 feet by dedicating your primary apparition to maintaining the spellshape; dedicating the apparition to the spell prevents you from using the apparition’s vessel spell, apparition skills, or avatar form for the duration of the modified spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Spiritual Expansion Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Apparition",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7126#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7127",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Apparition's Enhancement"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7127#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Spiritual power encases your weapon or unarmed attack. Until the end of your turn, one wielded weapon or unarmed attack you have deals an extra 1d6 spirit damage and gains the divine trait, if it didn’t have it already.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Apparition's Enhancement",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Apparition",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spirit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7127#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7131",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Blazing Spirit"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7131#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your apparition grants fiery defenses. You gain resistance equal to your level against the triggering damage, and the triggering creature takes 1d6 fire damage and 1 persistent fire damage. This damage increases to 2d6 fire damage and 2 persistent fire damage at 12th level, and 3d6 fire damage and 3 persistent fire damage at 18th level.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Blazing Spirit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Apparition",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wandering"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7131#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7133",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Medium's Awareness"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your apparitions watch over you. You gain a +2 status bonus to Perception checks made to Seek and when using Perception for your initiative roll. At 12th level, this status bonus increases to +3, and at 20th level, to +4.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Medium's Awareness",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Apparition",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wandering"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7136",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Instinctive Maneuvers"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you allow an apparition control over your body, it might vent its fury against your foes. When you Relinquish Control, you add Grapple, Reposition, Shove, and Trip to the list of actions you can take. You gain a +2 status bonus to the Athletics check to attempt these actions.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-relinquish-control",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Instinctive Maneuvers",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Apparition"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7137",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spirit Walk"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your allied apparitions ward you against the predations of their restless peers. You and allies in a 30-foot emanation gain a +2 status bonus to Recall Knowledge checks about spirits, haunts, and undead. While you’re Searching or Detecting Magic in exploration mode, this bonus also applies to AC and saves against reactions any of you trigger from haunts and spirits. During your first turn in an encounter, you and allies in the aura have resistance equal to half your level against damage dealt by haunts or spirits.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-apparition-sense",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Spirit Walk",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Apparition",
            "aonprd:Trait-Aura",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exploration"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7139",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Apparition's Quickening"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7139#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "If your next action is to cast a cantrip or a spell that is at least 2 ranks lower than the highest-rank spell slot you have, you can draw power from one of your attuned apparitions to reduce the number of actions to cast it by 1 (minimum 1 action). The chosen apparition is dispersed until you can re-attune to it at your next daily preparations, but you can’t disperse an apparition in this way if you would no longer be attuned to any apparitions afterward.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Apparition's Quickening",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Apparition",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7139#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7142",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shadows Within Shadows"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7142#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your apparition possesses a furtive and elusive nature that can influence and blend with your spiritual energy to form a protective and nearly impenetrable shroud of nondetection around you. The enemy must reroll the triggering check and take the lower result.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Shadows Within Shadows",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Apparition",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Misfortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wandering"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7142#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7151",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spirit's Sacrifice"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7151#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your attuned apparition gathers all of the energy it can through your shared bond and uses that power to disperse itself while channeling the energy back into you, saving your life. You can use Spirit’s Sacrifice even while unconscious or otherwise unable to act. Choose one apparition you have attuned; you do not die, your wounded condition is reduced to 1 if it would be higher, and you regain a number of Hit Points equal to twice your level. The chosen apparition is dispersed until you can re-attune to it at your next daily preparations.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Spirit's Sacrifice",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Animist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Apparition"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7151#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7154",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Energized Spark"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The energy of your spirit manifests as crackling lightning, the chill of winter, or the power of an element. Choose one of the following traits: air (slashing), cold, earth (bludgeoning), electricity, fire, metal (slashing), poison, sonic, vitality, void, water (bludgeoning), or wood (piercing). You can choose for any spirit damage dealt by your exemplar abilities to instead gain the trait and deal the corresponding damage type.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Energized Spark",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7155",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sanctified Soul"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve drawn a line in the sand in the cosmic struggle between good and evil and chosen a side. You gain either the holy trait or the unholy trait. All your exemplar abilities that deal spirit damage gain the sanctified trait, allowing you to apply your holy or unholy trait to them to better affect your chosen enemies",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Sanctified Soul",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7157",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vow of Mortal Defiance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7157#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Having seen the wreckage left by the gods and their servitors as they play in their great war of good and evil, you’ve come to the only reasonable conclusion: they all must be cut from their silken thrones. You swear a vow to defeat one creature within 60 feet that has the holy or unholy trait. The first time each round that you deal damage to that creature, you deal an additional 1d6 spirit damage. You can’t use Vow of Mortal Defiance again until you or the target is defeated, flees, or the encounter ends.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-you-are-not-sanctified-with-the-holy-or-unholy-trait",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Vow of Mortal Defiance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7157#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7159",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Leap the Falls"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Reinforcing your legs with divine energy, you can leap the battlefield as powerfully as a salmon clearing a waterfall. The imbued ikon gains the following ability. Immanence You gain the Powerful Leap and Quick Jump skill feats, allowing you to jump further and faster, even if you do not meet the prerequisites for them.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Leap the Falls",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7160",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Red-Gold Mortality"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "By channeling your divinity into a creature along with a strike, you can disrupt their ability to recover. The imbued ikon gains the following ability. Immanence When you successfully damage an enemy with the ikon, a marking appears around the wound, painted in the red of mortal blood and the gold of divine ichor. When the target would regain Hit Points, such as from a healing effect or an ability like fast healing or regeneration, it must attempt a Will save against your class DC to determine the effects, and then the marking fades. The marking otherwise fades after 1 minute. Success The creature regains the full number of Hit Points that would be healed. Failure The creature regains only half the number of Hit Points as the contradictory energies swirl within it. Critical Failure The creature doesn’t regain any Hit Points.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Red-Gold Mortality",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Void"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7161",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Only the Worthy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can designate your ikons as movable by only your own hand, leaving them fixed in place as surely as if they were lodged in stone. Whenever you Release an ikon, you can spend an action to command it to remain motionless. While motionless, the ikon can be moved only if 8,000 pounds of pressure are applied to it or if a creature uses Athletics to Force Open the ikon with a DC equal to your class DC. You can Release your ikon over an adjacent prone enemy to hold them down with the ikon’s motionlessness—while so Released, you can’t use the ikon, but the enemy must succeed at the Athletics check to Stand or to move. The ikon automatically flies back to your hand when the effect is broken or if you spend an Interact action to hold out a hand and draw it back.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Only the Worthy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7162",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Steel on Steel"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The ring of divinely empowered steel assails your enemies. Transcendence—Ringing Challenge [two-actions] (sonic, spirit, transcendence) You clang your ikon against a weapon, shield, or the ground, emitting a shock wave that deals 1d4 spirit damage and 1d4 sonic damage to all creatures in a 30-foot cone or 15-foot emanation (basic Fortitude save). A creature that critically fails its saving throw is deafened for 1 minute. At 6th level and every 2 levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d4 spirit damage and 1d4 sonic damage.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Steel on Steel",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7163",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Through the Needle's Eye"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your weapon strikes with the perfection your will demands. Transcendence—Blinding of the Needle [two-actions] (transcendence) You aim your weapon in a superficial cut above your opponent’s eye. Make a Strike with the imbued ikon. If that Strike is successful, the target must succeed at a Fortitude save against your class DC or become blinded for 1 round or until it uses an Interact action to clear the blood from its vision.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Through the Needle's Eye",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7164",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Binding Serpents Celestial Arrow"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As you prepare to shoot your weapon, you invoke divine serpents that bind your enemies. The imbued ikon gains the following ability. Transcendence—Coiling Serpents [two-actions] (transcendence) Make a ranged Strike with your ikon. If the Strike hits, the target must succeed at a Reflex save against your class DC or the arrow transforms into a multitude of ethereal snakes that coil around the target, immobilizing it until it succeeds at an Escape attempt against your class DC.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Binding Serpents Celestial Arrow",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7166",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Motionless Cutter"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your weapon is so sharp even an insect alighting upon its still blade would be severed. Your weapon ikon gains the following ability. Transcendence—Sever Four Dragonfly Wings [three-actions] (transcendence) Make a Strike that deals slashing damage with your weapon ikon. If that Strike is successful, you can immediately make an additional Strike against a different target within your reach. You can continue making Strikes in this manner, each against a different target, until you have made a total of four Strikes or you miss with a Strike, whichever comes first. Each attack counts toward your multiple attack penalty, but you do not increase your penalty until you have made all your attacks.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Motionless Cutter",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7167",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Additional Ikon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your story has grown rich enough that three ikons can’t contain its full complexity. You gain a fourth ikon, which can be of any type.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Additional Ikon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7168",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Battle Hymn to the Lost"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7168#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your movements in combat are an artistic dirge to those spirits who could not fight to see another day. You make a Strike. Regardless of whether the Strike succeeds, spirits of warriors who died gloriously in battle surge out to attack with you. They appear in a 30-foot cone if you make a melee Strike or in a 10-foot emanation around your target if you made a ranged Strike. Each enemy in the area takes 2d10 damage with a basic Reflex save against your class DC; you choose whether the damage is bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing. At 12th level and every 4 levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d10. As they join the battle, the spirits call your fallen allies back to the fight. Any of your allies in the area who are dying regain Hit Points equal to the damage you rolled. This is a divine, healing, vitality effect.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-of-verse-unbroken-or-peerless-under-heaven",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Battle Hymn to the Lost",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7168#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7169",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Raise Island"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7169#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You churn the sea and fish up stone so your enemies together can receive their punishment. Each enemy in a 30-foot emanation must succeed at a Fortitude save against your class DC or be swept up to 15 feet to another location of your choice within the affected area and become off-guard until the start of your next turn. Then, if you’re on a surface, a pillar of earth rises underneath you and lasts for 1 minute. The pillar is 10 feet tall, and its surface includes your space and a 5-foot emanation around you. After the pillar rises, you can attempt a melee Strike against one enemy in reach.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-born-of-the-bones-of-the-earth-or-restless-as-the-tides",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Raise Island",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7169#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7171",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Breath of Vital Ash"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Reddish ash stains your ikon, impossible to clean off. Every time you exhale, a tinge of red and a scent of spiced smoke float upon your breath. The imbued ikon gains the following ability. Transcendence—Mark the Center [one-action] (transcendence) You hold a hand to your lips and exhale, releasing enchanted red ash in a 15-foot cone. The ash clings to the vital areas of each enemy in the area for 1 minute. When a creature marked by the ash is hit and dealt damage by a Strike, it takes an additional 4d6 precision or vitality damage, then its mark ends. The damage type is whichever is worse for the creature, as determined by the GM. At 13th level and every 3 levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d6.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Breath of Vital Ash",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7173",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fish from the Falls' Edge"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7173#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Seeing your ally fall, you let out a cry, sending your divine spark to them temporarily to keep them from tumbling down the River of Souls. You prevent the triggering creature from dying and restore 5d8 Hit Points to them. The ally is invigorated by the touch of your divine power, gaining a +1 status bonus to their saving throws and AC for 1 round. Your divine spark remains with your ally, preventing you from gaining any of your ikons’ immanence effects until the start of your next turn, when it returns to an ikon of your choice.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Fish from the Falls' Edge",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vitality"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7173#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7174",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Journey Of the Sky Chariot"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Small wings, flaming wheels, or another signifier of flight sprout from your ikon as it gains the power to lift you from the ground. Your ikon gains the following effects. Immanence Your ikon keeps you hovering even without conscious effort. You can remain in the air at the end of this turn, even if you didn’t use a Fly action. Transcendence—Race the Skies [one-action] (concentrate, transcendence) You take your place among the heavens. For 1 minute, you gain a fly Speed equal to your Speed or 20 feet, whichever is greater.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Journey Of the Sky Chariot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7241",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rising Blood Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The power within your blood grows. You gain the basic spellcasting benefits. Each time you gain a spell slot of a new rank from the bloodrager archetype, add a common spell of the appropriate tradition and rank to your repertoire. In addition, when you Cast a Spell from your repertoire and you are at least drained 1, increase the extra damage dealt by that spell from Rage by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bloodrager-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Rising Blood Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7416",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Legacy of Monarchs"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "No matter what might happen to you, your legacy shall never die. If you’re slain, any of your knights who touches your corpse can choose to take up your mantle; over the course of 10 minutes, they don your equipment, replace their attribute modifiers with yours, replace their skills and feats with yours, and become you for all intents and purposes, retaining only their ancestry, heritage, and ancestry feats. If you’re later returned to life, you can choose to reclaim your mantle from your former knight; if you do so, they revert to their previous state, and you reclaim all that was yours. Otherwise, you can choose to live a new life, retraining all your skills and feats while adopting a new name and identity.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-prophesied-monarch-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Legacy of Monarchs",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7492",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Flood Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7492#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The lessons of the flood teach a stance that distributes and circulates a single breath through the body and allows your punches to contain the focused power of a torrent of water. While in this stance, you hold your breath for up to 10 minutes and leave the stance if you stop holding your breath. You do not lose additional air if you attack, are critically hit, or critically fail a save. You still lose all remaining air if you speak, including to Cast a Spell. The only Strikes you can make are flooded river unarmed attacks. These deal 1d8 bludgeoning damage; are in the brawling group; have the nonlethal, trip, unarmed, and water traits; and don’t take the normal penalty for being used underwater. They also gain the forceful trait while you’re underwater.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Flood Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Water"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7492#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7493",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reflective Ripple Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7493#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You enter a stance of fluid grace as small amounts of water flow with your movements and attacks. You can make flowing wave attacks that deal 1d6 bludgeoning damage. They are in the brawling group and have the agile, disarm, finesse, nonlethal, trip, unarmed, and water traits. While in Reflective Ripple Stance, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to Disarm, Swim, or Trip, and you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Reflex DC to avoid being Disarmed and Tripped.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Reflective Ripple Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Monk",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Water"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7493#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7505",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Battle Harbinger Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have trained extensively in combat, battlefield tactics, and stamina, focusing on being an exceptional warrior for your faith in exchange for less time studying the traditional spells and scriptures. You become trained in your choice of Athletics or Acrobatics, if you are already trained in both skills, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Toughness general feat. If you already have this feat, you gain another general feat of your choice.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-battle-creed",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Battle Harbinger Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Class",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=752",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemical Crafting"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can use the Craft activity to create alchemical items. When you select this feat, you immediately add the formulas for four common 1st-level alchemical items to your formula book.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemical Crafting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=756",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Assurance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Even in the worst circumstances, you can perform basic tasks. Choose a skill you’re trained in. You can forgo rolling a skill check for that skill to instead receive a result of 10 + your proficiency bonus (do not apply any other bonuses, penalties, or modifiers).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-at-least-one-skill",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Assurance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=760",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Battle Medicine"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=760#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can patch up wounds, even in combat. Attempt a Medicine check with the same DC as for Treat Wounds and restore the corresponding amount of HP; this doesn’t remove the wounded condition. As with Treat Wounds, you can attempt checks against higher DCs if you have the minimum proficiency rank. The target is then immune to your Battle Medicine for 1 day. This does not make them immune to, or otherwise count as, Treat Wounds.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-medicine",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Battle Medicine",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=760#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7606",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Verduran Shadow Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your awareness of primal energies allows you to explore forests with preternatural ease. You become an expert in Survival. You can substitute your proficiency in Survival for your proficiency in Stealth when meeting feat prerequisites and gaining additional benefits from feats for being an expert, master, or legendary in Stealth; however, unless you also fulfill the Stealth prerequisite, you can only use those feats in forest terrain. While in forests, you can use your Survival modifier in place of your Stealth modifier when you Avoid Notice, Hide, Sneak, or would use Stealth to roll initiative.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-stealth-and-survival",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Verduran Shadow Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7607",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Canopy Predator"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are as at home in the treetops as you are beneath their branches. You gain a climb Speed of 15 feet when moving through trees, vines, and other foliage. Whenever you succeed at an Athletics check to Climb a tree or an Acrobatics check to Balance on a branch, you get a critical success instead. You aren’t off-guard while Climbing or Balancing on a tree.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-verduran-shadow-dedication-trained-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Canopy Predator",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7608",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Underbrush Trailblazer"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the Terrain Stalker feat, selecting the underbrush terrain; if you already have Terrain Stalker for underbrush, you can select a different type of difficult terrain. If you Avoid Notice while exploring, and if any allies use Follow the Expert to follow you as you do so, you can extend your Terrain Stalker feat’s benefits to one ally so long as they remain within 10 feet of you. If you have master proficiency in Stealth, you can extend the effect to two allies. If you have legendary proficiency in Stealth, you can extend it to four allies.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-verduran-shadow-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Underbrush Trailblazer",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7609",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Verduran Ambush"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7609#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You prepare to ambush a foe. You Ready an activity that takes 2 actions, though that activity must either be Death from Above or an activity with the requirement that you be hidden or undetected by all your opponents (such as Scout’s Pounce). After using the reaction, you cannot use this feat again for 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-verduran-shadow-dedication-expert-in-stealth",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Verduran Ambush",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7609#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7610",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Death from Above"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7610#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You leap down on your target, using their body to cushion your fall and your momentum to empower your attack. Attempt an Athletics check to Leap to a space adjacent to the target. If you land adjacent to the target, compare the Athletics check result against your target’s Reflex DC. When you leap onto a creature in this way, you do not also deal damage for falling on a creature. Regardless of your result, the target is temporarily immune to your Death from Above for 1 minute. Critical Success The target falls and lands prone, reducing the falling damage you take by an amount equal to twice your level. You then can make a melee Strike against the target. The Strike gains the deadly d8 weapon property and deals an additional 1d6 bludgeoning damage. This additional damage increases to 2d6 if you are a master in Athletics, and to 3d6 if you are legendary in Athletics. Success The target is off-guard until the beginning of your next turn, reducing the falling damage you take by an amount equal to your level. You can then make a melee Strike against the target, adding the deadly d8 weapon property to the attack. Failure You can make a Strike against the target. Critical Failure You fall prone, whether you take falling damage or not.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-canopy-predator-verduran-shadow-dedication-expert-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Death from Above",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7610#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7611",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sense the Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7611#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You sense how an incoming attack moves through ambient primal energy, predicting how best to dodge. The triggering attack targets your Survival DC instead of your AC. Though this allows you to avoid taking penalties to your AC, it doesn’t remove any conditions or other effects causing such penalties. For example, an enemy with sneak attack would still deal extra damage to you for being off-guard, even though you wouldn’t take the –2 circumstance penalty when defending against the attack.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-verduran-shadow-dedication-master-in-survival",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Sense the Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7611#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7612",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Caustic Nectar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have specialized glands inside your throat, which produce acidic nectar that you can spit long distances. You gain a nectar ranged unarmed attack with a range increment of 20 feet that deals 1d4 acid damage. On a critical hit, the target is additionally sickened 1. Your nectar doesn’t add critical specialization effects. You’re immune to your own nectar.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ardande-plant-or-wood-trait",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Caustic Nectar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7613",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unbowed, Unbroken"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your connection to elemental wood manifests as resilience—towering trees, rough bark, deep roots, and patient determination. You gain the Unwavering Resilience reaction. Unwavering Resilience [reaction] Trigger You attempt a saving throw against a poison, disease, or mental effect, but you haven’t rolled yet. EffectYou tap into the power of the Plane of Wood, gaining strength and mental fortitude. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus on the triggering save. If you critically succeed at this saving throw, you become bolstered by your success; blossoms and new growth temporarily sprout all over your body, and you gain a number of temporary Hit Point equal to your level. These temporary Hit Points last for one minute. When there temporary Hit Points are lost, the verdant growth subsides.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Unbowed, Unbroken",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Ardande",
            "aonprd:Trait-Lineage",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7614",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Wilderness Born"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’re at home in the wilderness and easily disappear into it. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Hide and Sneak in natural terrain, and a +1 circumstance bonus to Sense Direction in natural terrain. While in natural terrain, you’re always considered to be Covering Tracks, even if you chose a different activity in exploration mode.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ardande-plant-or-wood-trait",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Wilderness Born",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7615",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Root"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7615#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You react instinctively, sprouting roots from your legs and plunging them deep into the ground to keep your footing. If a force would move you, you move half that distance, to a minimum of 5 feet. If you would be knocked prone, resolve the effect, then you Stand.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ardande-plant-or-wood-trait",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Root",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7615#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7616",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Grow Tool"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7616#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You grow a simple tool from your own body, coaxing flowers, vines, roots, and wood to grow and sprout from your flesh into the desired shape. You create a one level 0 common simple tool with no intricate parts or written text, such as a crowbar, rope, or shovel. You can’t replicate a tool kit or weapon with this ability. This item lasts for 1 minute, or until you create another tool with this ability, whichever comes first. When duration runs out, the item crumbles to mulch.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ardande-plant-or-wood-trait",
          "aonprd:level": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Grow Tool",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Plant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7616#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7617",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Pollinate"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7617#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "As you’re hit, you emit a dense cloud of pollen, obscuring you from sight. You become concealed until the beginning of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ardande-plant-or-wood-trait",
          "aonprd:level": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Pollinate",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7617#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7618",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "One with the Wild"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You naturally blend in with the wilderness, becoming camouflaged. In natural terrain, you can Hide and Sneak even without cover or being concealed.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-wilderness-born",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "One with the Wild",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7619",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unfettered Growth"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "By tapping into the limitless power of the Plane of Wood, you can experience sudden, dramatic growth for a short time. Select one of the following benefits when you gain this feat. This choice is permanent and can’t be changed. You gain 2nd-rank enlarge as a primal innate spell. You can cast this spell twice per day and must target yourself. The spell’s duration is 30 minutes.You gain 4th-rank enlarge as a primal innate spell. You can cast this spell once per day and must target yourself.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ardande-plant-or-wood-trait",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Unfettered Growth",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=762",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bonded Animal"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You forge strong connections with animals. You can spend 7 days of downtime regularly interacting with a normal animal (not a companion or other special animal) that is friendly or helpful to you. After this duration, attempt a Nature check against the animal's Will DC. If successful, you bond with the animal. The animal is permanently bonded to you until you form a bond with a different animal or do something egregious to break your bond. A helpful animal is easier to direct. If your bonded animal is level –1, it gains the minion trait, allowing you to command it more efficiently. The maximum level of creature that can be your minion increases to 3 if you're a master in Nature and to 11 if you're legendary.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-nature",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Bonded Animal",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Downtime",
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7620",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Irresistible Bloom"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7620#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You bloom, sprouting flowers and releasing a pleasant smell, becoming irresistible. All creatures in a 30-foot emanation must attempt a Will save with a DC equal to your Class DC or Spell DC, whichever is higher. On a failure, a creature becomes fascinated with you, and must spend at least one of its actions on its next turn moving toward you. On a critical failure, you acting hostile to that creature allows them to attempt another save, rather than automatically ending the fascination. These effects last until the beginning of your next turn. You can spend one action at the beginning of your turn to Sustain the effects for an additional round. You can Sustain it in this way for a maximum of 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ardande-plant-or-wood-trait",
          "aonprd:level": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "Irresistible Bloom",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Incapacitation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Olfactory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7620#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7621",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Potent Nectar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your nectar becomes particularly dangerous. Select one of the following benefits when you gain this feat. This choice is permanent and can’t be changed. Your nectar is sticky, and clings to your target. Your nectar unarmed attack deals an additional 1d4 persistent acid damage to the target. This persistent damage isn’t multiplied on a critical hit.Your nectar is shot at a high velocity, and splashes upon contact. Your nectar unarmed attack additionally deals 1d4 acid splash damage. This splash damage isn’t multiplied on a critical hit.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-caustic-nectar",
          "aonprd:level": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "Potent Nectar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7622",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fungal Exhalation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can conjure toxic spores to infect enemies. You gain the fungal exhalation order spell. Increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-spore-order",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Fungal Exhalation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Focus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7623",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hedge Prison"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You cultivate plants to entrap your foes. You gain the hedge prison order spell. Increase the number of Focus Points in your focus pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-cultivation-order",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Hedge Prison",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid",
            "aonprd:Trait-Focus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7624",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Born to the Trees"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You adapt a creature to live among the trees, improving its ability to climb, balance, and leap. Target a willing creature within 30 feet. For 10 minutes, it gains a climb Speed equal to its Speed and a +1 circumstance bonus to Acrobatics checks to Balance and Athletics checks to Long Jump and High Jump. When it Leaps, it increases the distance it can Leap horizontally by 5 feet and vertically by 2 feet. If you use Born to the Trees again, any existing one ends.Level (6th) You can target up to 5 willing creatures.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Born to the Trees",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Impulse",
            "aonprd:Trait-Kineticist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Morph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wood"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7625",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "The Thousand Lashes of the Weeping Willow"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You conjure a massive willow tree, which lashes your foes with a thousand branches. The trunk of the weeping willow tree is 10-feet in diameter and appears in an unoccupied space within 500 feet. The tree whips its branches at all your enemies within a 30-foot-radius emanation centered on the willow’s trunk, dealing 10d8 slashing damage with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. A creature that fails its save is also overcome with sorrow, becoming slowed 1 for as long as the willow remains, as it weeps uncontrollably. The willow doesn’t target you or your allies. The willow tree remains until the end of your next turn, but you can Sustain it up to 1 minute. The first time you Sustain the impulse each round, the weeping willow attacks again, dealing 4d8 slashing damage to all enemies in the area with a basic reflex save. If you use this impulse again, the previous one ends.Level (20th) The initial damage is 14d8, and the Sustained damage is 5d8.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "The Thousand Lashes of the Weeping Willow",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Impulse",
            "aonprd:Trait-Kineticist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Overflow",
            "aonprd:Trait-Plant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wood"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7626",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Release Spores"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7626#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You create a miasma of spores. These spores fill a 20-foot burst within 100 feet and remain for 1 round per level you have. All creatures within the spores become concealed, and all creatures outside the spores become concealed to creatures within it. You can see through the spores without difficulty. You can Dismiss the spores. Awakening The spores smell disgusting. Creatures in the area are sickened 1 for as long as they remain in the area, plus 2 rounds. Awakening The spores are toxic. The miasma deals 1 poison damage per 2 levels you have to creatures in the area when you Release Spores, to creatures who begin their turn in the area, and to creatures who enter the area.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Release Spores",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fungus",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Poison",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7626#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7627",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rotten Slurry"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7627#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You expel a glob of rotten, foul-smelling slurry from your torso, hand, or mouth at a foe. Make a ranged attack roll against a creature within 30 feet. If you succeed, the slurry deals 1d4 bludgeoning damage to the target for every two levels you have, or double damage on a critical success. A creature that’s damaged by the attack is sickened 1 (sickened 2 on a critical success). Awakening The slurry bursts, showering bystanders. The attack deals an additional 1d4 poison splash damage for every four levels you have. Awakening The slurry is caustic, and bores into the flesh of those it touches. The attack deals an additional 1d4 Persistent acid damage.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Rotten Slurry",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Attack",
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7627#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7628",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Irradiate"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7628#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You exude an aura of radiation, making everyone around you ill. All creatures in a 15-foot emanation must succeed at a Fortitude save or become sickened 1. On a critical failure, they’re also fatigued for 1 minute. You’re immune to your own radiation. The value of this sickened condition increases by 1 for every 5 levels you have beyond 6th. Awakening You become more efficient at exuding this aura of radiation. The radius of the emanation becomes 60 feet. Awakening Your radiation becomes more potent. Creatures in the area take an additional 1d4 poison damage for every 2 levels you have, with a basic Fortitude save (roll this Fortitude save once and apply it to both the damage and the sickened condition).",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Irradiate",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Poison",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7628#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7629",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unleash the Blight"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7629#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You unleash the rot infecting you, spreading the blight to those nearby. All living creatures in a 60-foot emanation take 1d6 void damage for every 2 levels you have, with a basic Fortitude save. Awakening The blight is infectious. Creatures damaged by your blight take an additional 1d6 persistent void damage, as they begin to decompose. Awakening The blight is debilitating. Creatures damaged become drained 1 for one round on a success, drained 1 for 1 minute on a failure, and drained 2 for 1 minute on a critical failure.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Unleash the Blight",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Negative",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7629#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7630",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sprout Fruit"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7630#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The plants covering your body sprout a single, ripe fruit. A creature other than you who eats this fruit as a three-action activity (1 Interact action to pluck the fruit and 2 Interact actions to eat it) is healed 1d4 Hit Points for every 2 levels you have. Awakening The fruit is more potent. Increase the healing from d4s to d6s. Awakening The fruit is plentiful. You sprout one additional fruit for every 5 levels you have beyond 2. Also, those who eat a fruit may reduce a condition affecting them by 1.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Sprout Fruit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Plant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7630#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7631",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vine Lash"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7631#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "A long vine sprouts from your arm, which you can temporarily wield like a whip. Make a melee attack roll against a creature within 30 feet. If you succeed, the vine deals 1d6 slashing damage for every 2 levels you have to the target, or double damage on a success. Awakening The vine coils around your foes, squeezing them lifeless. On a successful hit, the target is grabbed by the vine. The DC to Escape the vine is equal to your Class DC or Spell DC, whichever is higher. Each round on your turn, if the target is still grabbed, the vine squeezes them, dealing 1d6 bludgeoning damage for every 2 levels you have. Awakening Rather than lash at your foes with a single vine, dozens of writhing vines emerge from your hands, lashing all creatures in a large area. You can use Vine Lash as a 2-action activity to damage all creatures in a 30-foot cone, with a basic Reflex save.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Vine Lash",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Attack",
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Plant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7631#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7632",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Defensive Growth"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7632#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You grow a shield of woven flowers and branches, then Raise that Shield to defend yourself from the triggering attack. If you would take damage from the attack, you immediately Shield Block. This is a wooden shield. The shield remains in your possession for a number of rounds equal to your level, or until it’s destroyed. Awakening The shield becomes stronger. It has Hardness 5, HP 40, BT 20. Awakening The shield takes on a mind of its own and lashes out vengefully when destroyed. When the shield is destroyed, is explodes, dealing 4d6 piercing damage to your attacker, with a basic Reflex save.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Defensive Growth",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Plant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Wood"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7632#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7633",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Disperse into Petals"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7633#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You merge with the blossoms sprouting from you and disperse, becoming a visible cloud of blossoms and petals. You’re amorphous. You lose any item bonus to AC and all other effects and bonuses from armor, and you use your proficiency modifier for unarmored defense. You gain resistance to physical damage equal to half your level and are immune to precision damage. You can’t cast spells, activate items, or use actions that have the attack or manipulate trait. You gain a fly Speed of 10 feet. You can remain in this form for up to 1 minute. You can Dismiss this effect. Awakening You can maintain your form for a longer time. You can remain in this form for up to 1 hour. Awakening You’ve learned to harm others, even while in your blossom state. You can occupy the same space as someone else. While occupying someone else’s space, you can spend 1 action to spin around in a vortex of blossoms, dealing 1d4 slashing damage for every 5 levels you have to the creature, with a basic Reflex save.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Disperse into Petals",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Plant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Polymorph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7633#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7634",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Gladiator's Roar"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7634#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can project your voice into a high-pitched screech that damages your foes. Your roar can be heard twice as far as normal, and creatures within a 15-foot-cone take 6d10 sonic damage and must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. If your Gladiator’s Roar triggers Play to the Crowd, you gain a +2 status bonus to your Performance check to do so. Critical Success The creature is unaffected. Success The creature takes half damage and becomes frightened 1. Failure The creature takes full damage and becomes frightened 2. Critical Failure The creature takes double damage, becomes frightened 3, and is stunned 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-gladiator-dedication-master-in-intimidation",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Gladiator's Roar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fear",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sonic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7634#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7635",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Operatic Adventurer"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your training has focused you for the opera, and it certainly shows. You become master in Performance, and at 15th level your skill in Performance increases to Legendary. You also become expert in Theater Lore or become master in Theater Lore if you were already expert. When you’re on a stage, in an arena, or otherwise at the focus of a crowd there to see you perform, your eagerness to begin grants a +3 circumstance bonus to initiative rolls if you roll Acrobatics, Intimidation, or Performance for initiative.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-acrobat-celebrity-dandy-or-gladiator-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Operatic Adventurer",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7636",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Perfect Pitch"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your ear for harmony has enhanced your ability with musical magic. You can use Performance to Learn a Spell or Identify Magic spells and effects that are musical in nature. In addition, you gain the Pitch-Perfect Projection action. Pitch-Perfect Projection [one-action] (auditory, spellshape) By using your perfect pitch, you can amplify your voice to cause magical auditory effects to reach further. If your next action this round is to Cast a Spell or use an action that creates an auditory effect with a range, increase that range by 30 feet.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-celebrity-or-dandy-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Perfect Pitch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7637",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Play to the Crowd"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have a knack for knowing just how to manipulate groups by saying exactly what needs to be said. When you Lie in a public area in front of a crowd, you can gauge the reactions of the crowd as you speak to know how your Lie is working, and Lie loses its secret trait. You gain the Reactive Falsehood reaction. Reactive Falsehood [reaction] (fortune) Frequency once per hour; Trigger You fail to Lie to a creature in public; Effect As your target sees through your lie, you spin your falsehood in a way that utilizes the crowd’s reaction to bolster believability. Re-roll your Deception check to Lie with a +2 status bonus and use this check’s result as the actual result to Lie.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-dandy-dedication-master-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Play to the Crowd",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7638",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Primadonna"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7638#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The spotlight should always be on you and you alone. Attempt a Performance check against the Will DCs of all enemies within 30 feet who can see or hear you. On a success, the targets focus on you and gain a +1 circumstance bonus to hit you, but they’re off-guard to all creatures other than yourself. On a critical success, the effect lasts for 3 rounds.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-celebrity-dedication-master-in-performance",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Primadonna",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7638#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7639",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Virtuosic Dancer"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You're so fond of using your Acrobatic feats on the stage that you've begun adding your own flair to these dances on the big stage. When you Perform, if you do a performance that is either related to dance, acting or opera, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the roll. If you're legendary in Acrobatics, this increases to a +2 circumstance bonus. You gain the Dancing Dodge reaction. Dancing Dodge [reaction] (move) Trigger You're hit by a Strike during the first round of combat; Effect You take advantage of the fact that your foe isn't ready to anticipate your dance-like moves in combat. Add a +3 circumstance bonus to your Armor Class against the triggering Strike to determine the Strike's actual result.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-acrobat-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Virtuosic Dancer",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7640",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Costume Change"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Enough of your life has been spent performing that you’ve mastered the art of the quick change—especially when it comes to armor or invested items. You can remove any armor as a 3-action Interact activity. You can don light armor in 2 rounds, or in 1 minute for medium or heavy armor. You gain the Impromptu Investment activity. Impromptu Investment (1 minute) Frequency once per 10 minutes; Effect You can remove investiture from an item you currently have invested, and this investiture does not count against your daily limit. You can invest a new item in this item’s place.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-acrobat-celebrity-dandy-or-gladiator-dedication-quick-disguise-master-in-performance",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Costume Change",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7641",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fit for the Role"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Not only are you a flamboyant performer, but you’ve mastered an occult secret that allows you to outfit yourself and your companions with magical visages. You gain the ability to cast illusory disguise as a 7th-rank innate occult spell once per day.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-acrobat-or-dandy-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Fit for the Role",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7642",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "It's Not Over"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7642#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "In the world of drama, the finale of any performance doesn’t have to be the end, and for you, this now extends to life itself. When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points, you can use this reaction to suddenly spring back into action. Instead of gaining the dying condition and falling unconscious, you regain a number of Hit Points equal to 10 + your level + your Constitution modifier.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-celebrity-or-gladiator-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "It's Not Over",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7642#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7643",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tempo Shift"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7643#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You are always ready to embrace to a change in tempo and adapt your actions to take advantage of unforeseen developments. When you return to the initiative order after you Delay, you do so in an unpredictable way. All enemies are off-guard to you until the start of your next turn, and you become Quickened for the current round but can only use the extra action to Stride or Strike.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-celebrity-or-gladiator-dedication-legendary-in-acrobatics",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Tempo Shift",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7643#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7644",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fight Choreography"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve spent enough time training in stage fighting and teaching a wide range of stunts that you can prepare your companions with directions on how to avoid peril in battle. You can Aid an ally’s Acrobatics or Athletics check with a Theater Lore check. You gain the Swift Choreography reaction. Swift Choreography [reaction] (auditory, linguistic) Trigger An ally within 30 feet would become grabbed, immobilized, off-guard, prone, or restrained; Effect You call out a quick reminder to your ally about a special move you’d suggested to them at some point in the past, allowing the ally to avoid the triggering effect completely.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-acrobat-or-gladiator-dedication-master-in-theater-lore",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Fight Choreography",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7645",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tragic Lament"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7645#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You dramatically cry out in poetic verse about the tragedies that led to your doom at this very moment, instilling guilt in your attacker. The Strike deals normal damage rather than critical damage as your foe relents on their attack at the last moment as they’re moved by your words, though other effects that happen on a critical hit still occur. The creature that made the triggering Strike must then succeed on a Will save against your Class DC or be slowed 1 for 1 round by guilt at its actions against you.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-celebrity-or-dandy-legendary-in-performance",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Tragic Lament",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7645#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7646",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "More Real than Real"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your performances aren’t just well-known, they’re famous across the land and beyond. Your ability to make people believe the stories you perform has taken on supernatural power. You gain the ability to cast fabricated truth once per day as an occult innate spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-acrobat-celebrity-dandy-or-gladiator-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "More Real than Real",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7647",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tattooed Historian Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You become trained in Diplomacy or Performance; if you are already trained in both skills, you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain access to all uncommon magical tattoos with the orc trait. You gain a storied skin for free upon gaining this feat (or another magical tattoo of 2nd level or lower if you already have storied skin). You cannot have more than one storied skin tattoo, but the frequency of its Living History ability increases by one use per minute for every three tattooed historian feats you have. For every two tattooed historian feats you have, you can invest one magical tattoo that does not count against the maximum number of items you can have invested at one time.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-constitution-1-trained-in-orc-lore-belkzen-lore-or-orc-pantheon-lore-or-at-the-gms-discretion-a-related-lore-skill",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Tattooed Historian Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7648",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Aurochs-Headed"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your words and body language can subconsciously unsettle orcs, giving you an advantage when convincing them to see things your way. Many with this feat use it to travel freely between holds, warning all but the toughest orcs to waylay weaker prey. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to skill checks to Make an Impression or Coerce creatures with the orc trait. Enemy orcs who can see you at the start of combat take a –1 penalty to initiative rolls.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-diplomacy-or-intimidation",
          "aonprd:level": "3",
          "aonprd:name": "Aurochs-Headed",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7649",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spell Survivor"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Once you’ve resisted an opponent’s magic, anything else they throw your way becomes less effective. When you attempt a saving throw against a spell using Orc Superstition or Pervasive Superstition and critically succeed, you gain resistance 1 to all damage dealt by that triggering spell’s caster until the end of their next turn. At 9th level and every 4 levels thereafter, the resistance increases by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-orc-superstition",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Spell Survivor",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Orc",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7650",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Agent of All Holds"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Orcs across Belkzen recognize you as an honored lorekeeper. You’re adept at leveraging this status and showing off your tattoos to resolve conflicts, change minds, or distract others from a faux pas. You get a failure on the check, rather than a critical failure. If the triggering check was made against a creature with the orc trait, you can instead add the fortune trait to this ability and reroll the check, treating any critical failure as a failure.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-tattooed-historian-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Agent of All Holds",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7651",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Inked Panoply"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7651#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your tattoos can briefly animate and extend from your skin, granting you a spectral shieldbearer who protects you from harm. Doing so expends one use of your storied skin, granting you a +1 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack. In addition, you gain resistance to mental, spirit, and void damage equal to twice your number of tattooed historian feats against the triggering attack.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-tattooed-historian-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Inked Panoply",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7651#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7652",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Infused with Belkzen's Might"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7652#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your tattoos immortalize the conquests of orc war leaders, such as Belkzen besieging the dwarven Sky Citadel of Koldukar. You can expend one use of your storied skin’s Living History ability to channel this power into your own weapons. Until the end of your next turn, you deal additional spirit damage with weapons and unarmed attacks equal to 1 plus half the number of Tattooed Historian feats you have.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-tattooed-historian-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Infused with Belkzen's Might",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7652#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7653",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Inscribed with Elders' Deeds"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your tattoos commemorate unique exploits that (according to legends) only an orc could accomplish. During your daily preparations, you can reconfigure part of your storied skin to depict a specific orc hero, granting you a 1st-level ancestry feat with the orc trait until you prepare again; this ancestry feat cannot require any physiological feature you lack, as determined by the GM. Since this feat is temporary, you can’t use it as a prerequisite for permanent character options, such as for a feat. At 13th level, you can instead gain a 5th-level ancestry feat with the orc trait.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-tattooed-historian-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Inscribed with Elders' Deeds",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7654",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Wrath of the Hold"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7654#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your tattoos carry the strength of an innumerable horde, and you can expend one use of your storied skin’s Living History ability to animate your tattoos as ghostly assailants that swarm your foes. These spirits attack all foes in a 30-foot cone, dealing 4d6 spirit damage. The damage increases by 1d6 at 10th level and every 2 levels thereafter. Each affected creature must attempt a basic Will saving throw against the higher of your class DC or spell DC.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-tattooed-historian-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Wrath of the Hold",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7654#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7655",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Political Acumen"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have spent years following the political maneuvering and secret alliances of elves in Iadara. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks made to Sense Motive against other elves and to your Perception DC against Lies spoken by agents of Tanglebriar.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-perception",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Political Acumen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Elf",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7656",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Traditional Ways"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are a fervent follower of the long-standing elven traditions established when your people returned to Kyonin. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Nature, Society, and Lore skill checks related to Kyonin or the elves that live there, as well as a +1 circumstance bonus to saves against enchantment effects that would force you to act against your will.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Traditional Ways",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Elf",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7657",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shame the Sin"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7657#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your conviction against the sins that all demons grow from is so strong that you can force a demon to suffer from its sins when you strike a sound blow against them. In addition to doing the normal damage for your critical hit, the demon also suffers the effects of its special vulnerability. If the demon has no special vulnerability, it instead takes an additional 1d6 mental damage. This increases to 2d6 mental damage at 13th level and to 3d6 mental damage at 17th level.",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Shame the Sin",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Elf",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7657#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7658",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Swamp Stealth"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7658#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "In swamplands, you are particularly skilled at quickly hiding behind bits of underbrush or foliage, or moving quietly through murky water. You Take Cover and then use that cover to Hide.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-stealth",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Swamp Stealth",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Elf",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7658#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7659",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Political Virtuoso"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your mastery of the politics of your home nation is profound. Your circumstance bonus from Political Acumen becomes +4 instead of +2.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-political-acumen",
          "aonprd:level": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Political Virtuoso",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Elf",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7660",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Demon Hunter"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The demons of Tanglebriar have long haunted your dreams, just as they have long threatened Kyonin. You have not only studied these fiendish foes well, but have trained extensively to battle the hordes of demons that serve Treerazer and are particularly adept at striking desperate melee blows against them. When you make your daily preparations, choose one kind of demon, such as succubus, omox, shemhazian, or Treerazer. For the remainder of the day, the first time you hit one of those specific demons in a round with a melee Strike, you also deal 1d6 additional spirit damage. At 13th level, the extra damage increases to 2d6 additional spirit damage, and at 17th level, the extra damage increases to 3d6 spirit damage.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-religion-or-demon-lore",
          "aonprd:level": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Demon Hunter",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Elf",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7661",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Anchoring Arrow"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7661#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can prevent demonic foes from fleeing your wrath via teleportation. Make a bow Strike against a demon. In addition to the normal effects of the Strike, the target must attempt a Will save against your class DC. Critical Success The target avoids any additional effect. Success The target takes a –5 circumstance penalty to all their movement Speeds for 1 round as arcane coils of magic meddle with their mobility. Failure As success, but a –5 foot circumstance penalty for 1 minute. While the target is affected by this, Anchoring Arrow attempts to counteract any teleportation effect that would move the target, or any effect that would transport the target to a different plane. The arrow has a counteract rank of 7th and a +20 modifier to the roll. Critical Failure As failure, except a –10 foot circumstance penalty, and the duration is 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Anchoring Arrow",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Arcane",
            "aonprd:Trait-Elf",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7661#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7662",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cold Iron Stomach"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have steeled yourself against potent odors. Whenever you gain the sickened condition, you reduce the value of that condition by 1; if this reduces the value to 0, you avoid becoming sickened entirely. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to all saving throws against olfactory and poison effects created by demons or environmental hazards associated with the Outer Rifts (including all environmental hazards found in Tanglebriar).",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Cold Iron Stomach",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Elf",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7663",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Treehealer"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can undo the effect of demonic corruption in plants. By spending 10 minutes in contact with a tree that’s been corrupted by demonic presence, you can restore the tree to its original health. This does not prevent that tree from becoming corrupted again in the future. Alternatively, you can spend 10 minutes in contact with a creature with the plant trait. At the end of this time, you restore 7d8+56 Hit Points to that creature and heal half that amount of your own Hit Points. Additionally, you can attempt to counteract any one curse or disease afflicting that plant creature as if you had cast cleanse affliction heightened to 7th rank. Your counteract rank for this is 7, and your counteract check is equal to your Will save or your spell attack modifier, whichever is higher.",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Treehealer",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Elf",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exploration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7664",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Demon Slayer"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7664#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can deliver a melee blow to a demon that creates an explosion of holy light to try to finish the demon off. In addition to the normal damage from your melee Strike, you also inflict 10d6 spirit damage to the demon. The demon can resist this additional damage with a basic Fortitude save against your class DC. If the demon is slain by this strike, it explodes in a blast of holy light that fills a 30-foot emanation. All creatures in this area that have the demon trait take 10d6 spirit damage and must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC. Critical Success The demon takes no damage. Success The demon takes half damage. Failure The demon takes full damage and is dazzled for 1 round. Critical Failure The demon takes full damage and is permanently blinded.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-demon-hunter",
          "aonprd:level": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "Demon Slayer",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Elf",
            "aonprd:Trait-Holy",
            "aonprd:Trait-Light",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7664#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=767",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cloud Jump"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your unparalleled athletic skill allows you to jump impossible distances. Triple the distance you jump on a successful Long Jump (so you could jump 90 feet with an Athletics result of 30). When you successfully High Jump, use the distance jumped and distance limit for a Long Jump but don’t triple the distance. You can jump a distance greater than your Speed by spending additional actions when you Long Jump or High Jump. For each additional action spent, add your Speed to the distance limit.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-legendary-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "15",
          "aonprd:name": "Cloud Jump",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7761",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bloodsense"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’re extraordinarily sensitive to the presence of blood. You gain bloodsense as an imprecise sense with a range of 15 feet. This allows you to sense the presence of creatures, living or dead, that have blood (this includes most creatures that aren’t immune to bleed). You’re similarly able to detect the presence of fresh blood in volumes of one pint or more, so long as it’s no more than 24 hours old.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-perception",
          "aonprd:level": "7",
          "aonprd:name": "Bloodsense",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7762",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sanguine Tenacity"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your blood carries permanent regenerative properties. The penalties from enfeebled and the penalties and lost HP from drained both affect you as if the condition values were 1 lower than they actually are. You also gain resistance 5 to persistent bleed damage and reduce the DC of checks to recover from persistent bleed damage to 11, or 6 if you have particularly effective assistance.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-constitution-4",
          "aonprd:level": "11",
          "aonprd:name": "Sanguine Tenacity",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7763",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vasodilation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Using the power of your own blood, you encourage increased blood flow to nourish damaged tissue or stifle the flow to clot wounds or prevent the spread of poison and disease. You no longer require a healer’s toolkit to Administer First Aid, Treat Disease, Treat Poison, or Treat Wounds, though you take 1 damage each time you take one of these actions without the proper tools from the expenditure of your blood. You can’t reduce or prevent this damage. You gain a +1 item bonus when performing these actions using your blood, which increases to +2 if you’re a master in Medicine and +3 if you’re legendary.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-medicine",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Vasodilation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7764",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sanguimancer Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The life essence in your blood recovers naturally over time. You gain a special type of temporary Hit Points called sanguimancy Hit Points that follow the normal rules for temporary Hit Points with two exceptions: you can spend them to power some sanguimancy feats, and you can never have a greater number of sanguimancy Hit Points than double your level. After a full 8-hour rest, you gain sanguimancy HP equal to your level that last for 8 hours. If someone successfully restores HP to you with Treat Wounds, you also gain 1 sanguimancy HP for every 10 Hit Points recovered (minimum 1 sanguimancy HP).",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Sanguimancer Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7765",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Blood Shield"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7765#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You raise a defensive barrier of your own blood to protect you. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC until the start of your next turn, increasing to a +2 bonus if you spend 10 or more sanguimancy Hit Points. While this bonus is in effect, you can use the Shield Block reaction with your blood shield. The blood shield has Hardness equal to four times the number of sanguimancy Hit Points you spent. After you use Shield Block, the blood shield dissipates, ending the circumstance bonus to AC early.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-sanguimancer-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Blood Shield",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7765#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7766",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Exsanguinate"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7766#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "After one of your attacks, you direct your foe’s blood to spray upon you, infusing you with life energy. You gain a number of sanguimancy HP equal to half your level that last only until the end of your next turn. Exsanguinate works only against active foes who are able to act and aren’t restrained.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-sanguimancer-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Exsanguinate",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7766#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7767",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Transfusion"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7767#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You bring forth the regenerative properties of blood on behalf of an ally or yourself. You touch a willing creature and grant them fast healing 1 for 5 rounds. You can spend an additional 5 sanguimancy Hit Points to increase the fast healing by 1, to a maximum of 8.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-sanguimancer-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Transfusion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7767#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7768",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Venipuncture"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7768#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "A shell made up of hundreds of razor-thin needles of blood forms around you before exploding outward, lacerating foes in a 30-foot emanation. The needles deal piercing damage equal to double the number of sanguimancy Hit Points you spent, to a maximum of 80 damage. Creatures caught in the blast must attempt a basic Reflex save. The DC for this save is your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-sanguimancer-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Venipuncture",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7768#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=777",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Expeditious Search"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have a system that lets you search at great speed, finding details and secrets twice as quickly as others can. When Searching, you take half as long as usual to Search a given area. This means that while exploring, you double the Speed you can move while ensuring you’ve Searched an area before walking into it (up to half your Speed). If you’re legendary in Perception, you instead Search areas four times as quickly.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-perception",
          "aonprd:level": "7",
          "aonprd:name": "Expeditious Search",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=779",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Experienced Smuggler"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You often smuggle things past the authorities. When the GM rolls your Stealth check to see if a passive observer notices a small item you’ve concealed, the GM uses the number rolled or 10—whichever is higher—as the result of your die roll, adding it to your Stealth modifier to determine your Stealth check result. If you’re a master in Stealth, the GM uses the number rolled or 15, and if you’re legendary in Stealth, you automatically succeed at hiding a small concealed item from passive observers. This provides no benefits when a creature attempts a Perception check while actively searching you for hidden items.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-stealth",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Experienced Smuggler",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7792",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Armor Regiment Training"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've trained for grueling marches in full battle kit. You treat heavy armor as being 1 Bulk lighter than it actually is, and you can rest normally while wearing armor of any type. In exploration mode, you and your allies use your normal Speeds without including your armors' Speed penalties to determine your travel Speed.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Armor Regiment Training",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7800",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rapid Assessment"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7800#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You quickly evaluate your enemies. Attempt a check to Recall Knowledge against one creature you are observing.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Rapid Assessment",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7800#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7801",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Set-up Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7801#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your attack makes it difficult for your enemy to defend themselves against your allies' attacks. Attempt a Strike against an enemy. If the Strike is successful, the target is off guard against the next attack that one of your allies attempts against it before the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Set-up Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7801#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7803",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Banner Twirl"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7803#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You spin your banner in an elaborate pattern that your enemies find inscrutable. You and any ally adjacent to you have concealment from ranged attacks until the start of your next turn",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Banner Twirl",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Brandish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7803#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7805",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Observational Analysis"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You are able to rapidly discern relevant details about your opponents in the heat of combat. When you use Combat Assessment against a target that you or an ally has targeted with a Strike or spell since the start of your last turn, you get a +2 circumstance bonus to the Recall Knowledge check (+4 if the Strike from Combat Assessment is a critical hit.)",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-combat-assessment",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Observational Analysis",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=781",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fascinating Performance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you Perform, compare your result to the Will DC of one observer. If you succeed, the target is fascinated by you for 1 round. If the observer is in a situation that demands immediate attention, such as combat, you must critically succeed to fascinate it and the Perform action gains the incapacitation trait. You must choose which creature you're trying to fascinate before you roll your check, and the target is then temporarily immune for 1 hour. If you're an expert in Performance, you can fascinate up to four observers; if you're a master, you can fascinate up to 10 observers; and if you're legendary, you can fascinate any number of observers at the same time.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-performance",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Fascinating Performance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7810",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Efficient Preparation"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve developed techniques for drilling your allies on multiple tactics in a succinct and efficient manner. Increase the number of tactics you can have prepared by 1.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Efficient Preparation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7811",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Defiant Banner"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7811#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You vigorously wave your banner to remind yourself and your allies that you can and must endure. You and all allies within the aura of your commander's banner when you use this action gain resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage equal to your Intelligence modifier until the start of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Defiant Banner",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Brandish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7811#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7812",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Officer's Education"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You know that a broad knowledge base is critical for a competent commander. You become trained in two skills you are not already trained in, become an expert in one skill you are currently trained in, learn one common language you do not already know, and gain any one general feat that you meet the prerequisites for.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Officer's Education",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7817",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Standard-Bearer's Sacrifice"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7817#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Seeing an enemy take aim at your ally, you bravely flourish your banner to redirect their attention to you. The triggering opponent must attempt a Will save against your class DC. Success The opponent completes its attack against your ally. Failure The opponent targets you with the triggering attack instead. Critical Failure As failure, and you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your AC against the triggering attack.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Standard-Bearer's Sacrifice",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Brandish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7817#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7818",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Targeting Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your attack creates an opening in your target's defenses for your allies to capitalize on. When you successfully damage an opponent with either Guiding Shot or Set-Up Strike, the next creature other than you to attack the same target before the start of your next turn deals an amount of additional precision damage equal to your Intelligence modifier.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-guiding-shot-or-set-up-strike",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Targeting Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Commander"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7831",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bodyguard"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You swear a vow to protect one of your allies at all costs, regardless of the risk this might pose to you. During your daily preparations, choose one of your allies as your charge. When you Taunt, the penalty your taunted enemy takes increases to –2 against your charge. You can take 10 minutes to change who your charge is before your next daily preparations.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Bodyguard",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7833",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Long-distance Taunt"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can draw the wrath of your foes even at a great distance. When you use Taunt, you can choose a target within 120 feet.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Long-distance Taunt",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7837",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Covering Stance"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7837#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your very presence on the field of battle protects nearby allies from harm. At the end of each of your turns while you're in this stance, choose one ally adjacent to you to gain lesser cover until the start of your next turn. That ally loses this benefit if they move to a space that is no longer adjacent to you at any point during their move. If you Intercept an Attack that would harm the ally you're covering, that ally can Step as a free action after your reaction is complete.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Covering Stance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7837#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7842",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shielding Taunt"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7842#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "By banging loudly on your shield, you get the attention of even the most stubborn of foes. Raise a Shield, and then Taunt a creature. Your Taunt gains the auditory trait.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Shielding Taunt",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7842#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7843",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Taunting Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7843#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The force of your blow causes your enemy to focus their attention on you. Make a Strike. Regardless of whether the Strike hits, you Taunt the target. Your Taunt gains the visual trait.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Taunting Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7843#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7844",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Area Armor"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The armor you wear protects you and shelters your allies against explosions and other large-scale assaults. While you're wearing medium or heavy armor, allies adjacent to you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Reflex saves against area effects. If you're a master in the armor, the bonus is +2 instead.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Area Armor",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7850",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shielded Attrition"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7850#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You provoke attacks from foes that might otherwise stop your allies from moving. Raise your Shield, then choose whether to Stride up to half your Speed. This movement triggers enemies' reactions as normal. Each enemy who could have reacted to your movement is unable to react to your allies' movement until the start of your next turn (regardless of whether it chose to react to your movement).",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Shielded Attrition",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7850#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7854",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Retaliating Rescue"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7854#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "When an ally is in danger, you can hustle to reach them and punish the foe threatening them. Stride up to your Speed. You must end this movement adjacent to an ally who is within an enemy's reach. Then, you push your ally up to 5 feet (as normal for forced movement, this movement doesn't trigger reactions) and make a melee Strike against an enemy within your reach. If your ally was in that enemy's reach and your push moved them out of it, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your attack roll.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Retaliating Rescue",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7854#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7856",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stomp Ground"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7856#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You bring your booted foot down on the ground with enough force to rattle your foes. Each creature in a 5-foot emanation must attempt a Reflex saving throw against your class DC. Critical Success The creature is unaffected. Success The creature is off-guard until the end of your turn. Failure The creature is knocked prone. Critical Failure The creature is knocked prone and takes 1d6 bludgeoning damage from the fall.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Stomp Ground",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7856#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7858",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Juggernaut Charge"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7858#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "As you move forward in a rush, you put the weight of your armor behind an attack that can drag a foe with you. You Stride. If you end your movement within melee reach of at least one enemy, you can make a melee Strike against that enemy, then Stride again. If your Strike hit and dealt damage, that enemy is pulled with you and is moved the same direction and distance as your second Stride.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Juggernaut Charge",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7858#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7860",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shield from Arrows"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7860#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You place your shield in the path of an oncoming projectile. Your adjacent ally gains a +4 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack. If the attack misses, you have deflected it with your shield.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Shield from Arrows",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7860#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7863",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Get Behind Me!"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When saving your allies from harm, you push them behind you to better protect them. When you use Intercept Attack to protect an ally, you can move that ally up to 10 feet if they’re willing. You can’t move the ally to a position outside your reach, you can’t move them into or through obstacles, and you must move them farther away from the source of the attack if possible. This movement doesn’t trigger reactions.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-intercept-attack",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Get Behind Me!",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7866",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tough Cookie"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7866#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Though you've taken a lot of punishment, you aren't easily brought down. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to half your maximum Hit Points that last for 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Tough Cookie",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7866#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7871",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Scattering Charge"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7871#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You charge into a group of enemies to send them flying. Stride up to your Speed. At the end of your movement, you can Shove up to three creatures within your reach. You don't need a hand free to do so. You attempt a separate Athletics check for each one; each attempt counts toward your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until after you've made all the attempts. Regardless of your results, you can't Stride to follow any of the targets.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Scattering Charge",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7871#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7874",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bloody Denial"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7874#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You strike a foe with force to prevent them from reacting. Make a Strike. If you hit, the target must attempt a Fortitude saving throw against your class DC. If your Strike was a critical hit, the result of the save is one degree of success worse. Critical Success The creature is unaffected. Success Choose an ally. Until the start of your next turn, the creature can't use reactions against that ally. Failure The creature can't use reactions until the start of your next turn. Critical Failure As failure, plus the creature is stunned 1.",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Bloody Denial",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7874#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7878",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Clobber"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7878#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With a mighty blow, you send an enemy flying backward and onto the ground. Strike a foe. This Strike deals an extra die of weapon damage. If you hit and deal damage, you can automatically Shove the target, with the same benefits as the Shove action (including the critical success effect, if your Strike was a critical hit). The target then falls prone. This counts as two attacks when calculating your multiple attack penalty.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Clobber",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7878#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7879",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Never!"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The idea that you would hurt your companions, even when you've lost your reason, is unthinkable. Each time you would attack an ally due to being confused or controlled, you can attempt another saving throw against the effect that caused you to be confused or controlled with a +4 circumstance bonus to the save. If you succeed, you don't make the attack, though you still expend any actions it would have taken. If your save ends the effect making you confused or controlled, you can take any remaining actions during your turn as normal. Failing or critically failing this additional save doesn't increase the effect's duration or otherwise worsen it.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Never!",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=788",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Group Coercion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can strong-arm people effectively, even when you don’t have them isolated. When you Coerce, you can compare your Intimidation check result to the Will DCs of up to five targets instead of one. It’s possible to get a different degree of success for each target. The number of targets you can Coerce in a single action increases to 10 if you’re an expert, 25 if you’re a master, and 50 if you’re legendary.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-intimidation",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Group Coercion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7880",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Demolish Defenses"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7880#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With a powerful blow, you crack a foe's armor or tough hide, opening it up for further attacks. Make a melee Strike. This Strike deals one additional weapon die of damage; if the target is your taunted enemy, this increases to two additional weapon die of damage. This counts as two attacks for the purposes of calculating your multiple attack penalty. If you hit and deal damage, the target must attempt a Fortitude saving throw against your class DC. Critical Success The target takes no additional effect. Success The target is off-guard until the end of your next turn. Failure The target is clumsy 2 until the end of your next turn. Once it loses this clumsy condition, it's off-guard for 1 round. Critical Failure As failure, but the target is clumsy 3.",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Demolish Defenses",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7880#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7883",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shield from Spells"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your prowess with a shield allows you to block magic and more. You can use Shield from Arrows against ranged spell attacks and other ranged attacks, not just physical ranged Strikes.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-shield-from-arrows",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Shield from Spells",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Guardian"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=790",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hefty Hauler"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can carry more than your frame implies. Increase your maximum and encumbered Bulk limits by 2.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Hefty Hauler",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=7958",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Munitions Master Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have drilled enough with your light mortar to operate it with unrivaled efficiency. You gain the Engineer's Efficiency action. Engineer's Efficiency [one-action] Frequency once per turn; Requirements You are adjacent to your light mortar; Effect You Aim your light mortar and then either Load or Launch it.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-light-mortar-innovation",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Munitions Master Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Class",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=796",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Intimidating Glare"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can Demoralize with a mere glare. When you do, Demoralize loses the auditory trait and gains the visual trait, and you don’t take a penalty if the creature doesn’t understand your language.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-intimidation",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Intimidating Glare",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8006",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Myth Hunter"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8006#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your ancestors confronted and bested mythic beasts of Iblydan antiquity. Through a combination of hearing these tales and channeling a hint of those warriors' mythic power, you've developed a knack for bypassing a mythic creature's fabled defenses. The next time you successfully Strike the triggering creature, your Strike treats its mythic resistance as 2 lower. You treat its resistance as 4 lower if your Hero-God Lore or Legendary Beast Lore proficiency rank is expert, 6 lower if your rank is master, and 8 lower if your rank is legendary. If your Strike would already ignore mythic resistance (because you are a mythic character or wield a mythic weapon), your next successful Strike against the creature instead deals an additional 1d6 precision damage. This additional damage increases to 1d8 if your Hero-God Lore or Legendary Beast Lore proficiency rank is expert, 1d10 if your rank is master, or 1d12 if your rank is legendary.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-hero-god-lore-or-legendary-beast-lore",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Myth Hunter",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8006#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8007",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fiery Rebirth"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8007#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "When you escape death, you return to life with retributive fire that burns those who harmed you. You expend 1 Mythic Point, return to consciousness, Stand, and regain additional Hit Points equal to your level. You then erupt in flames, dealing fire damage equal to twice your level to adjacent foes, with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. Foes that critically fail the save are also pushed 5 feet away from you.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Fiery Rebirth",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fire",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8007#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8008",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Follow the Threads of Fate"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8008#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "A norn’s thread—spun from fate itself—runs through or wraps around your ikon. Transcendence—Unravel the Future [one-action] (fortune, transcendence) You pluck a single thread from your ikon, which ties itself in three loops about your wrist, where it remains for the next minute. If you fail an attack roll or skill check, and a +1 status bonus would change your failure into a success or your success into a critical success, you gain a +1 status bonus to this check retroactively, changing the outcome appropriately as the thread pulls you to the future you desire. The thread then falls from your wrist. You can have only one thread in existence at a time.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Follow the Threads of Fate",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8008#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8009",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Topple the Titans"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8009#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Even the greatest titans of the world are easier to kill when they’re lying on the ground. You’ve made it your mission to topple such giants and can make others fall with a force that shakes the very earth. The triggering creature’s toppling body shakes the ground, emitting a quake in a 10-foot emanation from their space. Apply the result of your triggering Athletics check against the Reflex DC of each creature in the emanation to Trip them as well. You do not need to have a hand free, and you do not lose your balance if any of your attempts to Trip are a critical failure.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Topple the Titans",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8009#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8010",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Riddle the Sphinx"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve learned the secrets of the sphinx’s riddles and empowered your ikon with them. You can voice these mysteries, forcing others to overcome them as you did. Transcendence—Tangle in Riddle [one-action] (auditory, mental, transcendence) You speak a bizarre koan that transcends language and is understood by only one creature within 30 feet. The target must attempt a Will save against your class DC. It’s then immune to this ability for 1 hour. Critical Success The target is unaffected. Success The target is stupefied 1 for 1 round. Failure The target is stupefied 1 for 1d4 rounds. Critical Failure The target is stupefied 1 and confused for 1d4 rounds.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Riddle the Sphinx",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8011",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shield of Stone"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You stole a gorgon’s gaze and trapped it in your ikon. You’ve learned how to brandish it for your advantage, subduing the rage of the trapped gaze by turning it on your enemies. Transcendence—Brandish the Gorgon’s Gaze [one-action] (earth, transcendence, visual) Effect You Raise your mirrored aegis, though it seems to lose some of its usual luster in favor of the dull sheen of stone. If you Shield Block a melee attack with the mirrored aegis before the beginning of your next turn, the gorgon’s eyes upon it flash at the triggering creature, who must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC. On a failure, they are slowed 1 for 1 minute as their body partially petrifies. Regardless of the outcome, that creature is temporarily immune to this effect for 24 hours.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Shield of Stone",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Ikon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8012",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "As a Thousand Soldiers"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8012#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Though you may have stolen from the hive, you’ve nothing but respect for the armies guarding it, and you borrow their strength to overwhelm your foes. Your body transforms into a swarm of bees. You Fly up to twice your Speed; during this movement you can pass through any space that would be small enough for a single insect, and your movement does not trigger reactions. If you pass through an enemy’s space, you can inflict a storm of stings that deals 3d4 piercing damage and 3d4 poison damage, with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. At the end of your movement, you return to your original form. At 10th level and every two levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d4 piercing damage and 1d4 poison damage.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-plunderer-of-the-hives-riches",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "As a Thousand Soldiers",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Polymorph",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8012#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8013",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Forward Gaze into Life"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8013#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Despite the constant cold of death at your back, you keep your gaze forward into the realm of life. You release two 15-foot cones, aimed exactly opposite each other, one ahead of you that deals 5d10 vitality damage and one behind you that deals 5d10 void damage, each with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. Creatures that critically fail also take 5 persistent damage, of the same damage type dealt.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trespasser-in-deaths-realm",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Forward Gaze into Life",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exemplar",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Vitality",
            "aonprd:Trait-Void"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8013#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8014",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Heroic Weakness"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As word of your faith spreads, so too does word of your foibles and weaknesses. Where originally these disadvantages may have been myths themselves, or simply manifestations of ill fortune or chance, when you take this feat, one of those weaknesses becomes real. Work with your GM to choose your heroic weakness—it must be to a specific damage type and must be associated with a specific condition, both of which must be elements that are going to be significant parts of your story’s future. For example, you could choose for a weakness to be spirit damage caused to you by a follower of a rival god, physical damage from a specific category of weapon, void damage caused by a specific kind of undead, or fire damage taken in a certain part of the world or from creatures from that part of the world. The amount of weakness you gain to this damage is equal to twice your level. But with this new weakness comes a new source of power, for when your foes would take advantage of your weakness, you can use the pain and humiliation to bolster your own resolve. You gain the following reaction. Makes Me Stronger [reaction] Trigger You take damage from your heroic weakness and are not reduced to fewer than 1 Hit Point by the damage; Effect You make a show of powering through your weakness, be it by flexing your muscles, issuing a challenging roar, laughing off the pain, or simply acting as if the damage doesn’t worry you in the slightest. Your spells gain a status bonus to damage against the triggering creature equal to twice their rank; this lasts until the next time you use this reaction. In addition, the creature that damaged you with your heroic weakness must attempt a Will save against your class or spellcasting DC, whichever is higher, to avoid becoming frightened 1 (frightened 2 on a critical failure).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-godling-dedication-hero-god-accomplishment",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Heroic Weakness",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8015",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Myth of Quick-Thinking"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your myth includes amusing parables of clever plans and sly maneuvers, often applied to small things in life such as disguising yourself as a sheep to ambush a wolf or tricking a snake into shedding its skin. You can Lie as a two-action activity, regardless of how elaborate your tale. When you attempt a Deception check, you can spend a Mythic Point to do so at mythic proficiency. If you succeed at a Deception check while in the presence of your hierophant, any of your worshippers that you can see automatically succeed at an attempt to Impersonate or Lie in such a way that supports your story (for example, the target of your Lie claiming you are a teacher sees all of your worshippers as students). You also lay claim to one of the following domains of your choice: confidence, secrecy, or trickery.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-godling-dedication-hero-god-accomplishment",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Myth of Quick-Thinking",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8016",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Myth of Realm-Walking"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your myth speaks of distant travel to countless countries, planes, or dimensions. When any effect attempts to anchor you to a plane (such as planar tether) or to banish you from the current plane (such as banishment), that effect gains the incapacitation trait. If it already has the incapacitation trait, you gain a +4 status bonus to your save against the effect. If you successfully save against such an effect, the creature that attempted to use this effect on you must succeed at a Will save against your class or spell DC (whichever is higher) to avoid becoming stupefied 1 for 1 minute (stupefied 2 on a critical failure). You also lay claim to one of the following domains of your choice: dreams, fate, or travel.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-godling-dedication-hero-god-accomplishment",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Myth of Realm-Walking",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8017",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hero-God's Bond"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "At times, the myth of a hero-god includes a favored partner or a bonded ally, such as the hero-gods of promises and shield-bearers, Upion and Warrick. When you gain this feat, select an ally. They are your bonded partner. While you and your bonded partner are on the same plane, you and your bonded partner always have the same doomed value (defaulting to the highest value), so when your bonded partner’s doomed condition would increase or be set to a specific amount, your doomed value also increases to match (if it is lower than your current doomed value). When either of you are dying, the other knows this immediately, as well as the distance and direction to the dying partner’s location. When either of you attempts a recovery check, as long as the other is on the same plane, reduce the DC of the recovery check by 2. You can communicate telepathically with your bonded partner as long as you are within 60 feet of each other. You can change your bonded partner by spending 1 week of downtime bonding with another ally.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warrior-of-legend-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Hero-God's Bond",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8018",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Martyr's Parry"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8018#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You intercede to absorb the triggering attack. Your bonded partner gains a +2 circumstance bonus to their AC. If the attack still hits, you take the triggering attack’s damage instead of your bonded partner, though the attack still uses your bonded partner’s defenses for the purposes of determining if it hit or critically hit.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-hero-gods-bond",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Martyr's Parry",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8018#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8019",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Grief's Fury"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8019#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "A lost love. A broken spear. Rage burning through a hero-god. When a myth speaks of a wounded partner, the hero-god often rejects the future. Too many find themselves on a battlefield, clutching a body that they swore to protect. In that moment, the wellspring of power ignites. Increase the value of your doomed condition by 1, to a maximum of doomed 3. You gain a +2 status bonus to attack rolls against any creature that attacked or dealt damage to your partner in the last minute. If you reduce a creature to 0 HP that attacked or damaged your partner, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to twice their level. These benefits last until your bonded partner is no longer unconscious or for 1 minute, whichever duration is shorter.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-hero-gods-bond",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Grief's Fury",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8019#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8020",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hydra's Bond"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When the hero-gods built Pol-Sylirica and its seven armies, they feared betrayal from within. They took inspiration from the multi-headed hydra, and bound the seven armies together with supernatural ties to make them behave as if they shared one body. Following these tactics, during daily preparations, you can select a number of willing creatures equal to half your level to be part of your hydra’s bond. Members of the same hydra’s bond always know if another member is telling the truth. When a member of the hydra’s bond saves against an effect that would have them act against their allies (such as the confused condition, a dominate spell, or other mental effects that would give an ally the controlled condition), you can spend a Mythic Point to allow that character to attempt the save at mythic proficiency. If a member of the hydra’s bond fails a save against such an effect, other members automatically know that the target is controlled or under the influence of a mental effect. In addition, all members of the hydra’s bond gain a +2 circumstance bonus to any roll made to counteract that effect.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Hydra's Bond",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8021",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fool's Fleeting Plan"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When Aercelys, hero-god of fools and fire, dove into the funeral pyre of his beloved daughter, he seemed a fool without thought for his safety. Yet when he returned with her body, he showed the slow rise of her chest, and those who doubted became the fools. You carry Aercelys’s spark within you, which protects you from rash decisions. You do not trigger reactions when you use an action that you gained from being quickened.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Fool's Fleeting Plan",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8022",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stages of Fate"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "At one time, the hero-gods could not tell their own prophecies. Ongalte, hero-god of deicide, defied this rule and cemented why it should be upheld. Those that can reach into the web of fates and pluck out a string are forbidden from speaking of their own myth. Yet nothing forbids them from speaking the myths of others. You peer through the world around you to see the delicate threads connecting others to their fate when they become afflicted. Choose a creature within 30 feet that you can see and who you know is affected by an ongoing affliction that progresses through stages, such as most diseases or poisons. Spend 1 Mythic Point, then attempt a Religion check at mythic proficiency against that affliction’s DC. Critical Success The next time the afflicted creature attempts a saving throw against the affliction, they automatically gain a critical success. If this results in the affliction coming to an end, you gain 1 Mythic Point. Success The next time the afflicted creature attempts a saving throw against the affliction, they gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the roll and increase the result of the saving throw by one degree of success. Failure The next time the afflicted creature attempts a saving throw against the affliction, they gain a +1 circumstance bonus. Critical Failure You share the afflicted’s fate, and are exposed to their affliction. You must immediately save against the affliction’s effect.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Stages of Fate",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8023",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Windborne Shove"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The hero-god of phalanxes and winds, grand Konebrys, led a force of dozens against an army of thousands. They gathered their soldiers in tight ranks, then marched against the wind to take the enemy by surprise. When a gust pushed the foes back, they struck their victorious blow. You emulate Konebrys’s tactics in pushing small forces against mighty foes. Whenever you are adjacent to an ally, creatures that attempt to Tumble Through your space take a –2 circumstance penalty to their Acrobatics check. When you critically succeed on a melee Strike against an enemy, you can immediately attempt to Shove your target as a free action. You can spend a Mythic Point on this Shove attempt to do so at mythic proficiency.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-guardians-calling",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Windborne Shove",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8024",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Awakened Power"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your power spontaneously evolves or reconfigures itself. You gain one awakening benefit for a deviant feat of 4th level or lower.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Awakened Power",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8025",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Greater Awakened Power"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your power undergoes yet another awakening. You gain one awakening benefit for a deviant feat of 10th level or lower.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Greater Awakened Power",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8026",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Blasting Beams"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8026#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "A directed beam of heat or an arc of lightning is one of the simplest ways to project energy. You fire a blast or beam from one hand. Make an attack roll against a creature within 30 feet. If you succeed, the beam deals 1d6 damage to the target for every 2 levels you have, or double damage on a critical success. Awakening Your beams blast through targets. Instead of making an attack roll to damage a single creature within 30 feet, you can use Blasting Beams as a 2-action activity to damage all creatures in a 60-foot line, with a basic Reflex save. Awakening You can choose to launch smaller, quicker beams from your eyes instead. These beams deal d4s instead of d6s, but the attack has the agile trait, and you don’t need a hand free to make it, though your eyes must be uncovered.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Blasting Beams",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Attack",
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8026#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8027",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Consume Energy"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8027#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your connection to energy is so much stronger than the offending display in front of you, allowing you to claim it for yourself. Attempt a counteract check against the triggering effect as you draw it into your body. If you successfully counteract the ability, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to double the counteract level of the ability, which last for 1 minute. Awakening The energy you consume helps empower your abilities. The next ability from the dragon classification that you use increases its range by 30 feet if it has a range, or increases its area by 10 feet if it’s a cone or line. If you don’t use this benefit within 1 minute, it fades. Awakening You channel some of the seized energy into your next attack. Choose one of your weapons or unarmed attacks. Until the end of your next turn, Strikes with the chosen weapon or unarmed attack deal an additional 1d6 damage of a type matching the energy you consumed.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Consume Energy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8027#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8028",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Storming Breath"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8028#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You spit out a freezing breath or sonic scream. You deal 4d6 damage, plus 1d6 damage for every level you have beyond 6th, to all creatures in a 30-foot cone, with a basic Reflex save. Awakening Your blast powerfully batters your foes. A creature that critically fails its save is knocked prone. Awakening The kickback of your blast helps you make a speedy escape. When you use this ability, you Fly backward 15 feet in a straight line directly opposite your blast. This movement doesn’t trigger reactions based on movement.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Storming Breath",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8028#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8029",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Propulsive Leap"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8029#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "By expelling flames from your feet or levitating through electrical repulsion, you propel yourself through the air. For 1 minute, you gain a fly Speed equal to your Speed or 20 feet, whichever is greater. If you aren’t on solid ground at the end of your turn, you must attempt another backlash check for your deviation, though you remain airborne even if you fail your check unless the damage from the check renders you unconscious. Awakening You blast through the air at great speed, gaining a +15-foot status bonus to your Fly speed from Propulsive Leap. Awakening You can use your propulsion as a makeshift weapon. The first time each round you Fly starting from the ground, all creatures adjacent to you take 1d4 damage for every 2 levels you have, with a basic Reflex save.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Propulsive Leap",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8029#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8030",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sonic Dash"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8030#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You bounce up and down once, then sprint forward. You Stride twice in a straight line. You can use Sonic Dash while Burrowing, Climbing, Flying, or Swimming instead of Striding if you have the corresponding movement type. Awakening Your Sonic Dash generates a sonic boom, dealing 1d4 sonic damage for every two levels you have to all creatures other than you in a 5-foot emanation at the point you end your Sonic Dash, with a basic Fortitude save. Creatures that fail are deafened for 1 round, or 1 minute on a critical failure. Awakening Your speed generates a slipstream that allows you to reposition your allies. You can dash through a willing ally’s space during your Sonic Dash, causing them to be drawn by winds alongside you. You deposit them in any unoccupied space adjacent to you at the end of your Sonic Dash.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Sonic Dash",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8030#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8031",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Overclock Senses"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8031#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your senses speed up to the point that time seems to stand still, allowing you to catch details and incoming attacks. You Seek. After you Seek, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your AC against ranged attacks and to Reflex saving throws until the beginning of your next turn. Awakening When you use Overclock Senses, you can focus even more on the present moment, allowing you more apparent time to observe and plot at the expense of defense. When you use Overclock Senses, you do so with the benefits of darkvision, or if you are at least 14th level, with the benefits of truesight. You can attempt a Recall Knowledge check as a free action after Seeking. Your senses spent, you then do not gain the normal bonuses to AC and Reflex saving throws. Awakening You hone your senses even further, letting you react to attacks almost before they happen. While you have the bonuses from Overclock Senses, if you would be hit by a ranged attack, you can spend a reaction to have the attacker roll the attack again (this is a misfortune effect), and if you would fail a Reflex save, you can spend a reaction to roll the save again (this is a fortune effect). You must take the second result, even if it is worse.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Overclock Senses",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8031#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8032",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unstable Gearshift"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8032#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You shift your body into a higher gear, your speed compounding further and further. You gain a +10-foot status bonus to all your Speeds, which lasts until the end of your next turn. At any time during your next turn, you can use Unstable Gearshift again, increasing the status bonus by another 5 feet and prolonging the effect for another round. You can keep using Unstable Gearshift in this way until you can no longer use your deviant abilities. Awakening When moving at high speed, your form blurs. You have concealment for the duration of any move action you take while you are affected by Unstable Gearshift. Awakening Your high-speed form has become partially out of phase with reality. While you are affected by Unstable Gearshift, you are not affected by physical difficult terrain (such as rubble), you do not trigger traps that use weight or pressure plates as a trigger, and you can move through enemy spaces without making checks to Tumble Through, as you simply phase through them.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Unstable Gearshift",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8032#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8033",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lightspeed Assault"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8033#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You zoom from enemy to enemy, striking each in an instant. Stride to an enemy and attempt a Strike against it. If successful, you can add another action to Lightspeed Assault. Stride again and attempt another Strike; if this second Strike is successful, you can spend another action to Stride again and attempt a third Strike. You can use Lightspeed Assault while Burrowing, Climbing, Flying, or Swimming instead of Striding if you have the corresponding movement type. You attempt a backlash check for your deviation only once, regardless of how many actions you end up spending on your Lightspeed Assault. Awakening Your speed allows you to slip the bonds of space. Instead of Striding, you simply teleport to your desired destination. Lightspeed Assault gains the teleportation trait. Awakening You move so quickly that you might as well be in multiple places at once. When you use Lightspeed Assault, you can decide to spend one, two, or three actions up front, selecting your targets ahead of time. You can flank with yourself for any of these Strikes, and if you deal damage to a target more than once, you can add all the damage together for the purpose of overcoming resistances, if it would be more beneficial to you.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Lightspeed Assault",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8033#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8034",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Draining Touch"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8034#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You reach out your arm, grasping hungrily for a source of energy. Attempt a melee Strike. If you succeed, you deal 1d8 cold damage for every 2 levels you have to the target, or double damage on a critical success. Awakening You drain enough energy from a creature to leave it with lingering aftereffects. Your Draining Touch also leaves a creature clumsy 1, or clumsy 2 if your attack was a critical success. Awakening You can pull away not just physical energy, but a creature’s spirit as well. Your Draining Touch can deal your choice of cold, spirit, or void damage, changing the cold trait to spirit or void as appropriate.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Draining Touch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Attack",
            "aonprd:Trait-Cold",
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8034#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8035",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Borrowed Ability"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8035#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your touch opens a conduit into the mind of your target, the emptiness within you pulling skills and memories through. You touch an adjacent creature and choose any skill you believe they are trained or better in. If you choose a skill that they are trained or better in, you borrow their proficiency in that skill, becoming trained in that skill for 1 minute. If they are not trained in the skill you choose, the GM chooses the next most applicable skill (for instance, choosing Acrobatics instead of Athletics). At 12th level, you can become an expert in the skill if the target is as well. If the target of Borrowed Ability is unwilling, the effects depend on the target’s Will save. Critical Success The target resists your touch completely. Success Your borrowing is unstable. At the beginning of each of your turns, you must either relinquish your hold on the borrowed skill (as a free action), or attempt another backlash check for your deviation; the ability ends if you fail. Failure Borrowed Ability lasts for its full duration. Awakening You gain some of the target’s defensive abilities. When you use Borrowed Ability, you also gain a +1 circumstance bonus to one of your saving throws for the duration, matching the target’s highest saving throw. You can choose to apply a –1 circumstance penalty to the target’s saving throw when you do so. Awakening Your touch establishes a lingering link through which you can sense what your target does. When you use Borrowed Ability, you gain any special senses—such as darkvision, scent, or tremorsense—that the target possesses. If the target does not have a sense that you normally have (for instance, an ooze that has no vision), you lose those senses as well. Your senses remain altered for the duration of Borrowed Ability.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Borrowed Ability",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8035#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8036",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Kinetic Dampening"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8036#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You feed off energy in your immediate surroundings, allowing you to dampen the force imparted by incoming blows. Until the beginning of your next turn, you gain resistance 5 to physical damage. At 10th level, and every 4 levels thereafter, the resistance increases by 5. Any blows that strike you during this time make no sound as their energy is drained. Awakening You can extend your dampening field around you to create a safe haven for your allies. If you spend an additional action when using Kinetic Dampening, your field extends in a 15-foot emanation around you. You can choose which creatures within the emanation are affected. Awakening You dampen a greater variety of wavelengths. When you use this feat, you also gain resistance to your choice of fire, electricity, or sonic damage.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Kinetic Dampening",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8036#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8037",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Feed the Void"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8037#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The void within you manages to manifest itself temporarily, a black hole opening over your heart and threatening to draw everything in. A 60-foot cone becomes filled with screaming winds that rush in toward you. All creatures in the cone must attempt a Fortitude saving throw. Critical Success The creature is unaffected. Success The creature is pulled 10 feet toward you. Failure The creature is pulled 20 feet toward you. Critical Failure The creature is pulled 30 feet toward you. Creatures that would be pulled into your square contact the void, which deals 5d6 spirit damage with no saving throw, and are then spat back out in a square adjacent to you of your choice. At 12th level, and every 2 levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d6. Awakening The void feeds upon the creature’s spirit, transferring you some of their vitality. If one or more creatures are pulled into the void, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to the level of the highest-level creature pulled in. These temporary Hit Points last for 10 minutes. Awakening The void’s suction draws in heat and light as well. The first 30 feet of the cone becomes covered in ice as temperatures drop, making the area difficult terrain, and is also plunged into darkness, with the effects of darkness heightened to half your level. Both effects last until the beginning of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Feed the Void",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Extradimensional",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spirit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8037#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8038",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bone Spikes"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8038#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Sharp shards of bone tear forth from your elbows, wrists, or other parts of your body. For 1 minute, you can make bone spike unarmed Strikes that deal 1d6 piercing damage and have the versatile S and sweep traits. When you take the Bone Spikes action, you can choose one weapon on your person and duplicate its weapon runes onto your bone spikes (with the exception of any runes that couldn’t apply to the bone spikes). Awakening Your bones grow longer, lashing flexibly at range. While you have bone spikes, you can Interact to give your bone spikes reach 10 feet until the end of the current turn. Awakening Grooves in your bone spikes form a channel for venom. Your bone spikes deal 1d4 persistent poison damage, which increases to 2d4 at 10th level and 3d4 at 18th level.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Bone Spikes",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8038#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8039",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Titan Swing"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8039#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your limbs tense as you deliver a mighty swing. Make a melee Strike. If it hits, you deal an extra die of weapon damage and push the target back by 5 feet. If you’re at least 10th level, increase this to two extra dice and push the target by 10 feet, and if you’re at least 18th level, increase it to three extra dice and push the target by 15 feet. Awakening On a critical hit, you push the target back double the normal distance and knock it prone. Awakening On a hit, you deal 1d6 persistent bleed damage. This increases to 2d6 at 10th level and 3d6 at 18th level.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Titan Swing",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8039#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8040",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "High-Speed Regeneration"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8040#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your wounds knit together with barely a thought. You regain Hit Points equal to double your level. When you gain this deviation, the GM secretly selects one type of energy damage or precious material, such as fire or cold iron. When you take damage of that type, your wound smokes until the end of your next turn, preventing you from using High-Speed Regeneration. Awakening Your regeneration can automatically save you from the brink of death. Once per day, you can use High-Speed Regeneration when your Hit Points would be reduced to 0 instead of the usual trigger. You avoid being knocked out and remain at the number of HP you regained. Awakening Regrowth invigorates you. You gain a +10-foot status bonus to your Speed until the end of your turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "High-Speed Regeneration",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8040#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8041",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tectonic Stomp"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8041#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You cause minor tremors that topple your enemies. All creatures in a 30-foot emanation who are touching the ground take 1d6 bludgeoning damage for every 2 levels you have, with a basic Reflex save. A creature that fails its save also falls prone. Awakening Your stomp also ejects large fragments from the ground. You raise up to three stone chunks from the ground in unoccupied squares in the emanation; the stones can’t be adjacent to one another. The chunks are 5 feet tall, block movement, and are large enough to Take Cover behind. They have AC 10, Hardness 8, and Hit Points equal to your level. They are immune to critical hits and precision damage. A stone chunk crumbles away when it has 0 Hit Points, and all of them crumble after 1 minute or when you use Tectonic Stomp again. Awakening Your stomp rattles those who fail horribly. A creature that critically fails its save is also stunned 1.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Tectonic Stomp",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8041#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8042",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Eerie Flicker"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8042#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your body flickers momentarily into the Ethereal Plane. You become concealed for 1 round, and the flat check for concealment applies to the Strike that would have hit you. If the flat check fails, the Strike misses you. Awakening When your body flickers, you momentarily assume a terrifying form. If a creature fails the flat check against concealment from your Eerie Flicker, it becomes frightened 1, and it doesn’t reduce the frightened condition from this effect at the end of the same turn it gained the condition. Awakening You can choose to compress your flickering movement into a single moment, increasing your chance to avoid the triggering attack in exchange for a shorter- lived effect. If you choose to do so, the flat check for concealment against the triggering attack increases to DC 9, but the concealment affects only the triggering Strike.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Eerie Flicker",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8042#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8043",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ghostly Grasp (Deviant)"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8043#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "An invisible arm extends from you to grab and manipulate objects. The arm reaches up to 15 feet, grabs an unattended object of 1 Bulk or less, and immediately deposits it in one of your free hands or at your feet. Alternatively, it reaches up to 15 feet and performs a simple Interact action like pushing open a window, though it can’t perform actions that require significant mechanical dexterity. For every 5 levels you have, the amount the hand can lift increases by 1 Bulk, and the arm’s range increases by 15 feet. Being ghostly, the arm can affect ghosts, spirits, and other incorporeal entities, though in most cases, you need an awakening for this to be useful. Awakening Your invisible arm can grab on to an unsuspecting target. You can modify the power’s target to be 1 creature within range. You make an attack roll against the creature’s Fortitude DC and add the attack trait to the action. On a success, the target is grabbed by the arm (or restrained on a critical success). This lasts for 1 round or until the creature Escapes. Awakening You summon additional ghostly arms that entwine together to push targets. You can modify the power’s target to be 1 creature within range. You make an attack roll against the creature’s Fortitude DC and add the attack trait to the action. On a success, you can move the target 5 feet in any direction (10 feet on a critical success).",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Ghostly Grasp (Deviant)",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8043#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8044",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Enervating Wail"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8044#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You release a terrible wail that tears at the spirits of all nearby. All living creatures in a 20-foot emanation take void damage with a basic Fortitude save. The damage is 4d6, plus 1d6 for every level you have beyond 6th. Awakening Your scream echoes in the mind. You can choose to emit a silent psychic wail instead, which changes the damage type to mental, changes the save to a Will save, removes the auditory trait, and adds the mental trait. Awakening Your wail saps your foes’ strength. In addition to the normal effects, living creatures in the area are enfeebled 1 for 1 round on a success (but not a critical success), enfeebled 1 for 1 minute on a failure, and enfeebled 2 for 1 minute on a critical failure.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Enervating Wail",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8044#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8045",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Distant Wandering"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8045#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your body falls unconscious and your spirit projects out of it. While in spirit form, you can’t consciously move your body, and you are invisible and inaudible, though a creature still might notice the signs of your presence and passing, just like for an invisible creature affected by silence, or a scouting eye. You can freely move about, though you can’t touch or move anything, cast spells, attack, or otherwise affect anything around you. Despite your ghostly form, you are not incorporeal and can’t pass through barriers you couldn’t in your body. Most effects can’t harm your spirit form, though some spells, like spirit blast and spirit song, explicitly damage a creature’s spirit. You can return to your body as a free action. If you are in spirit form at the beginning of your turn, you must attempt another backlash check for your deviation, returning to your body if you fail. Awakening Your spirit moves at the speed of thought. You gain a fly Speed and a +20-foot status bonus to your Speed while in spirit form. Awakening Time seems to pass more slowly while you are projecting your spirit. When you enter spirit form, you can Recall Knowledge or Seek. You are quickened while in spirit form and can use the extra action only to Recall Knowledge or Seek.",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Distant Wandering",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Deviant",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8045#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8112",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Oatia Skysage Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your study of the stars unlocks supernatural insights and magic. You either become trained in Astronomy Lore or an expert in Occultism. You learn to cast spontaneous spells and gain the Cast a Spell activity. You gain a spell repertoire with two of the following cantrips of your choice: detect magic, guidance, know the way, or read aura. You cast these spells as occult spells as you draw on the stars and night sky. You’re trained in occult spell attack rolls and spell DCs. Your key spellcasting ability for these spells is Intelligence.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-occultism",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Oatia Skysage Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8113",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Basic Skysage Divination"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The stars move, granting you a sliver of their magic. Choose one of the following 1st-rank spells to your spell repertoire: object reading or sure strike. You can Cast this Spell as an occult Oatia skysage spell. At 6th level, choose one of the following 2nd-rank spells to add to your spell repertoire: augury or see the unseen. At 8th level, you choose one of the following 3rd-rank spells to add to your spell repertoire: clairaudience or locate.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-oatia-skysage-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Basic Skysage Divination",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8114",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stargazer's Eyes"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Long hours in darkened observatories have sharpened your senses. If you don’t have low-light vision or darkvision, you gain low-light vision, or if you already have low-light vision, you gain darkvision.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-oatia-skysage-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Stargazer's Eyes",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8115",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Night's Glow"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The stars and moon lend you their light. You gain your choice of the moonbeam or zenith star domain spell. Like your Oatia skysage spells, you cast this focus spell as an occult spell. It costs 1 Focus Point to cast a focus spell. This feat grants a focus pool of 1 Focus Point that you can recover by using the Refocus to reflect upon or gaze at the stars.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-oatia-skysage-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Night's Glow",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8116",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Minor Omen"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8116#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The stars warn you of danger in the nick of time. Reroll the failed save and use the new result.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-oatia-skysage-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Minor Omen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8116#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8117",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Scholar's Hunch"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8117#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Scholarly debates have taught you to think on your feet. Reroll the failed check and use the new result.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-oatia-skysage-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Scholar's Hunch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8117#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8118",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Starlit Spells"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The stars reveal and punish your enemies. You can cast revealing light and 3rd-level holy light as occult innate spells, each once per day.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-oatia-skysage-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Starlit Spells",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8119",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Expert Skysage Divination"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your studies of the stars have taught you about the mysteries of the cosmos. You choose one of the following 4th-rank spells to add to your spell repertoire: clairvoyance or read omens. At 12th level, choose one of the following 5th-rank spells to add to your spell repertoire: mind probe or scouting eye. At 14th level, choose one of the following 6th-rank spells to add to your spell repertoire: scrying or truesight. You become an expert with spell attack rolls and spell DCs for occult spells.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-basic-skysage-divination",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Expert Skysage Divination",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=812",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Magical Crafting"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can Craft magic items, though some have other requirements, as listed in GM Core. When you select this feat, you gain formulas for four common magic items of 2nd level or lower.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Magical Crafting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8120",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Night's Shine"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your power from the moon and stars becomes strong enough to illuminate the night sky. You gain your choice of the asterism or touch of the moon domain spell. Increase the number of Focus Points in your pool by 1.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-oatia-skysage-dedication-nights-glow",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Night's Shine",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8121",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Night's Warning"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8121#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Portents written in the night sky show you how to avoid an attack. The triggering attack roll targets your Occultism DC instead of your AC. Though this allows you to avoid taking penalties to your AC, it doesn’t remove any conditions or other effects causing such penalties. For example, an enemy with sneak attack would still deal extra damage to you for being off-guard, even though you wouldn’t take the –2 circumstance penalty when defending against the attack.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-oatia-skysage-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Night's Warning",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8121#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8122",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Starlight Armor"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8122#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You armor yourself in the light of distant suns, shielding yourself from harm. The armor grants you resistance 7 to piercing, bludgeoning, and slashing damage. The armor also sheds bright light for 20 feet (and dim light for the next 20 feet). Whenever an adjacent creature attacks you, the attacker must attempt a Will save against your spell DC at the end of its action. On a failure, it becomes dazzled until the end of its next turn. Regardless of the result of the save, the attacker is temporarily immune until the end of its next turn. The dazzling effect has the light and visual traits. When you reach 17th level, the resistance increases to 10.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-oatia-skysage-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Starlight Armor",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8122#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8123",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Master Skysage Divination"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You unlock the most powerful secrets hidden in the stars above. You choose one of the following 7th-rank spells to add to your spell repertoire: retrocognition or true target. At 18th level, add pinpoint to your spell repertoire, and at 20th level, add foresight to your spell repertoire. You gain master proficiency with spell attack rolls and spell DCs for occult spells.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-skysage-divination",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Master Skysage Divination",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8124",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Scion of Domora Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain a spirit guide ally. Your familiar takes on the form of a spirit guide specific familiar.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-familiar-master-dedication-you-have-befriended-a-spirit-guide-and-it-bonded-with-you-using-its-bond-to-mortal-ability",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Scion of Domora Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8125",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spiritual Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8125#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your spirit guide enhances your attacks with occult power. Make a Strike with a weapon that has at least one fundamental rune. This counts as two attacks when calculating your multiple attack penalty. The Strike has the effects of the ghost touch property rune and deals an additional 2d6 force damage. If your weapon has a major striking rune, this Strike instead deals 3d6 force damage.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-scion-of-domora-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Spiritual Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8125#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8126",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Guided Skill"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8126#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You ask your spirit guide for aid. For the next 10 minutes, you gain a +2 status bonus to checks made using Acrobatics, Occultism, Stealth, or Survival.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-scion-of-domora-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Guided Skill",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8126#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8127",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Guardian's Embrace"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8127#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your spirit guide discorporates to surround you in an invisible protective shroud. You gain a +2 status bonus to AC against physical attacks until the beginning of your next turn. If you are hit by a physical attack during this time, you can use a reaction to gain resistance 10 to physical damage dealt by that attack; doing so ends the AC bonus, and you can’t use Guardian’s Embrace again for 10 minutes. Your spirit guide cannot be targeted by effects, cannot be affected by area effects, and cannot take any actions while this ability is active. Your spirit guide appears in a space adjacent to you when the effect ends.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-scion-of-domora-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Guardian's Embrace",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8127#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8128",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Invigorating Breath"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8128#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your spirit guide exhales its sweet-smelling breath on you, granting you the strength to push through your pain. You gain 20 temporary Hit Points for 10 minutes. At 15th level, you instead gain 30 temporary Hit Points for 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-scion-of-domora-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Invigorating Breath",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8128#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8129",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spiritual Flurry"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you use Spiritual Strike, hit targets become off-guard until the end of your current turn. In addition, the additional force damage dealt by the Strike increases by 2d6.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-scion-of-domora-dedication-spiritual-strike",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Spiritual Flurry",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8130",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spiritual Aid"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you call your spirit guide for aid, its presence bolsters your will and agility. You gain the Spiritual Aid reaction. Spiritual Aid [reaction] Trigger You fail a Reflex or Will saving throw; Effect You reroll the triggering saving throw. You must use the second result, even if it’s worse. If you roll a success, you get a critical success instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-scion-of-domora-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Spiritual Aid",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8131",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Spirit Guide Form"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8131#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You fuse with your spirit guide, becoming a hybrid being with enhanced physical and spiritual power. This effect lasts 1 minute; you can end it early as a free action. During this time, you can’t use any other actions granted by this archetype. You gain the following statistics and abilities, regardless of your type of spirit guide. You become incorporeal.You gain resistance 10 to all damage (except force, ghost touch, or spirit; double resistance vs. non-magical).Darkvision.An unarmed melee attack of the same type as your spirit guide (either claws or jaws), which is the only attack you can Strike with. You’re trained with this attack. Your attack modifier is +29 or your normal unarmed attack modifier, whichever is higher. You use the listed statistics for the unarmed attack type:Claws (agile, backstabber, finesse) [one-action] , Damage 3d6+5 slashing plus 1d6 force;Jaws (forceful) [one-action] Damage 3d10+5 piercing plus 1d6 force.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-scion-of-domora-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Spirit Guide Form",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Polymorph"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8131#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8132",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Twilight Speaker Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have carefully studied the histories, customs, and etiquette of many of the younger peoples of Golarion. You become an expert in Society. At 7th level, you become a master in Society, and at 15th level, you become legendary in Society. You can use the Society skill instead of the Diplomacy skill when you attempt to Make an Impression on a non-elven intelligent humanoid creature.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-society-you-are-an-ilverani-elf",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Twilight Speaker Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8133",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Empathetic Envoy"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You believe that treating others with respect is the fastest way into their hearts, and in turn others are more likely to believe in your good intentions and write off bad first impressions as flukes. If a creature’s attitude toward you becomes lower over the course of a social interaction (for example, from friendly to indifferent, or from indifferent to unfriendly), their impression of you returns to its starting level an hour after the social interaction ends. This ability has no effect if the creature you are interacting with becomes hostile.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-twilight-speaker-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Empathetic Envoy",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8134",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Disarming Smile"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8134#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With a wide and sincere smile, you give your attacker pause. You attempt a Diplomacy check against the triggering attacker’s Will DC. After you use Disarming Smile, all creatures who witnessed you use it are temporarily immune to your Disarming Smile for the next 24 hours. Critical Success Your enemy ceases their attack, momentarily taken aback by your disarming smile. The attack fails and the triggering target can’t attempt hostile actions against you until the beginning of its next turn or until you (or your allies) take hostile actions against the enemy (or its allies). You can begin talking to the creature on your next turn to attempt another Diplomacy check; on a success, you sustain the effect until the beginning of your next turn, to a maximum of 1 minute. Talking on subsequent rounds requires that you be able to communicate with the target creature and imparts the auditory and linguistic traits to the action. Success Your foe pauses momentarily. Their attack fails, but they can attempt further attacks against you. Failure The target’s attack is unaffected.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Disarming Smile",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8134#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8135",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Betraying Shank"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8135#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "While your usual diplomacy is well intentioned, you know that sometimes those same skills will need to be turned to deception. In a flash, you draw a sheathed or concealed agile or finesse weapon and make a melee Strike. The target is off-guard against your Strike. You then roll Deception for initiative.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-twilight-speaker-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Betraying Shank",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8135#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8136",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ilverani Purist"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "All twilight speakers are trained to resist the alluring customs of younger peoples, but you have made it your mandate to keep the Ilverani way unchanged. Such dedication has given you a trained eye for subtlety and deception. When you attempt to Sense the Motive of a non-elf humanoid creature and you roll a critical failure, you fail instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-twilight-speaker-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Ilverani Purist",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8137",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "World-Wise Vigilance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your keen study of other cultures gives you insights into the ways those cultures fight. When you use Perception to roll initiative and none of your enemies have the elf trait, you can choose to roll Society instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-twilight-speaker-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "World-Wise Vigilance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8138",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Emphatic Emissary"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8138#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can tell when diplomacy has failed and a meeting is close to unraveling or falling to blows. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus on your initiative roll. During your first turn in combat, you can use your Disarming Smile, targeting every hostile intelligent humanoid creature that can see you but has yet to act. If you choose to sustain your Disarming Smile, you sustain the effect for only one creature, as normal.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-disarming-smile",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Emphatic Emissary",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8138#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8139",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Avenging Runelord Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The call of a long dead runelord has infected your soul and transformed your fate. Choose one of the following sins: envy, gluttony, greed, sloth, or wrath. You become trained in Arcana. If you are already trained in Arcana, you become trained in the skill of your choice. At 14th level, you gain expert proficiency in Arcana. At 16th level, if you gain master proficiency in Arcana. You have familiarity with common weapons in the polearm and spear weapon groups—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as common weapons. When your proficiency for simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons. You learn the Thassilonian language. You gain the ability to cast an arcane spell as an innate spell. This spell must be chosen from the following list: darkvision, mystic armor, runic body, runic weapon, see the unseen, sending, or truesight; alternatively, you can choose any spell of 6th rank or lower from the sin spells listed for your chosen sin (see School of Thassilonian Rune Magic). You can cast this spell as an arcane innate spell once per day. The spell is automatically heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up. Use mythic proficiency to determine any attack rolls or spell DCs. Your obsession with revenge allows you to reflexively lash out at those who harm you with blasts of arcane magic. You gain the Runelord's Response reaction. Runelord's Response [reaction] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 73 Trigger A creature deals damage to you with a spellYou gain a measure of revenge immediately by twisting the magic used by the triggering creature. Spend a Mythic Point. The triggering creature takes 6d8 force damage, with a basic Will saving throw against either your class DC or spell DC using mythic proficiency, whichever is higher. At 14th level, and every 2 levels thereafter, this damage increases by 1d8.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Avenging Runelord Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=814",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Multilingual"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You easily pick up new languages. You learn two new languages, chosen from common languages, uncommon languages, and any others you have access to. You learn an additional language if you are or become a master in Society and again if you are or become legendary.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-society",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Multilingual",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8140",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Expanded Runelord Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your ability to use magic associated with your chosen sin grows. You gain the ability to cast one more arcane spell as an innate spell. This spell must be chosen from those listed in Avenging Runelord Dedication above, as well as contingency, spell riposte, or any 7th-rank spell from your chosen sin’s school. You can cast this spell as an arcane innate spell once per day. The spell is automatically heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up. Use mythic proficiency to determine any attack rolls or spell DCs.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-avenging-runelord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Expanded Runelord Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8141",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reliable Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Magic stored in written form or within wands is more reliable in your capable hands. Whenever you overcharge a wand, reduce the DC of the flat check to avoid destroying the wand by 4. It still gains the broken condition on a success. When you Cast a Spell from a scroll you can spend a Mythic Point as a free action. The spell is cast at mythic proficiency. Once you cast the spell using this ability, attempt a DC 11 flat check. If this check is successful, the scroll is not destroyed, and instead glows with light equivalent to that of a candle for 10 minutes. You can Cast a Spell from this scroll again, but if you do so you cannot enhance it in any way (such as by using this feat), and the scroll is destroyed. If not used before the end of the 10 minutes, the scroll is destroyed.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-avenging-runelord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Reliable Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8142",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shining Runes"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Whenever you Cast a Spell that requires more than one action to cast, the signature Thassilonian runes you trace in the air flicker with light and command attention. They may blaze brightly, leave lingering fog, create discordant noise, or fill the air with an overwhelming scent, such that their presence obfuscates you from onlookers. You gain concealment from enemy creatures until the beginning of your next turn. The DC to identify your spells as you cast them is 2 higher than normal.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-avenging-runelord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Shining Runes",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8143",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Willing Runes"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Magical markings of every kind seem eager to aid your endeavors. Whenever you read text, be it mundane or magical, the writing itself seems to almost to leap into your thoughts. You gain a +2 status bonus to checks to Decipher Writing, Identify Magic, Learn a Spell, or any Research check or Recall Knowledge check involving reading. You gain a +2 status bonus to saving throws and to your AC against effects from hazards that involve reading, such as those created by a rune trap ritual. If you were the one who triggered the hazard by reading the triggering runes, the status bonus increases to +4. If you prepare spells from a spellbook, you gain the following activity. Draw From the Pages [three-actions] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 74 Frequency once per day Requirements you are holding your spellbookSpend a Mythic Point, and then Cast a Spell directly from your spellbook. The spell you cast must be one that takes one or two actions to cast, and it’s automatically heightened to a rank equal to half your level. Use mythic proficiency to determine any attack rolls or spell DCs.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-avenging-runelord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Willing Runes",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8144",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Writhing Runelord Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your prowess with long-hafted weapons catches your opponents by surprise, as it bends or elongates in an obviously supernatural manner. Spend a Mythic Point. Your weapon gains the reach trait until the end of your turn, if it doesn’t have it already. You can Stride and Strike twice, in any order. The movement from your Stride doesn’t provoke reactions. Your Strikes are made at mythic proficiency and gain the critical specialization effect of the weapon. Apply your multiple attack penalty to your Strikes as normal, but the target of your second Strike is off-guard to it.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-avenging-runelord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Writhing Runelord Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Arcane",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8145",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Autonomous Arms"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "A portion of the ancient grasping spirit that infuses your being spills over into a spear or polearm you carry. When you perform your daily preparations, choose one spear or polearm you own. This weapon becomes infused with arcane magic and fragments of thought—it doesn’t become fully intelligent, but it instinctually recognizes you as its wielder and denies its abilities to any other wielder while you live. If your weapon doesn’t possess it already, it gains the effects of the animated property rune. This does not count against the maximum number of property runes your weapon can have at one time. You also gain the following action. Call to Hand [one-action] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 74With a simple flourish of your hand, you cause your autonomous spear or polearm to teleport into your grip, provided you’re on the same plane as your weapon. If you’re level 20, you can call to hand your weapon regardless of where it’s located. If your weapon is wielded by a mythic creature that’s higher level than you, you must spend a Mythic Point to Call to Hand the weapon, otherwise this action fails—you know why it failed, but you don’t learn who has control of your weapon.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-avenging-runelord-dedication-expert-proficiency-in-a-spear-or-polearm",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Autonomous Arms",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8146",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Subjugation"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8146#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have managed to gain a degree of control over the runelord’s ancient soul within your mind, enough that you can project this invasive influence into the minds of others. Spend a Mythic Point. You attempt to send your runelord’s influence into the mind of a creature you can sense within 30 feet. The creature attempts a Will save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. Giants take a –2 status penalty to this saving throw. Regardless of the result, the target is temporarily immune to this ability for 24 hours once the Subjugation ends. Critical Success The creature is unaffected. Success The creature is slowed 1 as it fights off your runelord’s influence. You gain awareness of its abilities and weaknesses as if you achieved a critical success on a Recall Knowledge check to identify the creature. Failure The creature relinquishes control of its faculties and abilities. You gain awareness of its abilities and weaknesses as success. You control the creature until the end of its next turn. Critical Failure As failure, but you control the creature for 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-avenging-runelord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Subjugation",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Complex",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Incapacitation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8146#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8147",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vindictive Thoughts"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8147#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Those who seek to do you personal harm with magic must suffer the same misfortune. Before you attempt your saving throw, spend a Mythic Point. You make this saving throw at mythic proficiency. On any result but a critical failure, the spell’s caster takes 10d6 mental damage (basic Will save against your class DC or spell DC using mythic proficiency, whichever is higher). At 18th level, the mental damage increases to 11d6, and at 20th level, the mental damage increases to 12d6.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-avenging-runelord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Vindictive Thoughts",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Arcane",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8147#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8148",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Advanced Runelord Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your ability to use magic associated with your chosen sin grows. You gain the ability to cast one more arcane spell as an innate spell. This spell must be chosen from those available with Expanded Runelord Magic, in addition to foresight, unrelenting observation, or any spell from your chosen sin’s school. You can cast this spell as an arcane innate spell once per day. The spell is automatically heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up. Use mythic proficiency to determine any attack rolls or spell DCs.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expanded-runelord-magic",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Advanced Runelord Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8149",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Apocalyptic Visions"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8149#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your runelord may not have lived long enough to need to retreat into hiding in the face of Earthfall, but the apocalyptic echoes of this event nevertheless reached their soul all the way in the Boneyard. You’ve learned to endure the invasive thoughts of this empire-ending event, but now you can project that despair into the minds of others. Spend a Mythic Point and target up to 10 creatures within 60 feet that you can sense. You force images into their minds of Earthfall, forcing them to endure a vision of the end of the world and all they hold dear. The creatures must attempt a Will save against your class DC or spell DC using mythic proficiency, whichever is higher. Critical Success The creature is unaffected. Success The creature is so distracted by the visions that they are slowed 1 for 1 round. Failure The creature is slowed 1 and stupefied 1 for 1 minute. Critical Failure The creature is slowed 2 and stupefied 2 for 1 minute. In addition, the creature suffers the effects of the spell nightmare the next time it rests. If the creature fails or critically fails against this effect, the effect repeats each time the creature attempts to sleep until it succeeds on its save or 6 days have passed. You do not need to know the creature’s name or remain on the same planet for the creature to experience these nightmares.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-avenging-runelord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Apocalyptic Visions",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Arcane",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8149#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8150",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Craft Runewell"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Even if the runelord whose soul influences you never did so themselves, you know how to create your own runewell—an artifact that grants you a measure of immortality. You learn the create demiplane ritual. To create your runewell, you must cast create demiplane heightened to 10th-rank. When you do so, you also create an anima focus (an immobile object like a statue or fortification with an appearance you design) at the location you cast the ritual, connecting your other-worldly home to this location. Once you create your runewell, you cannot create another unless the current one is destroyed. While you are located on the same plane that your anima focus is located on, or while you are within your runewell, any doomed value you gain stops at doomed 3. The only way an adversary can destroy your anima focus or runewell is to reduce you to 0 Hit Points and doomed 3 and then reduce your anima focus to 0 Hit Points using arcane magic (or an agent affected by arcane magic) from one of the schools in opposition to your specialized sin chosen when you took Avenging Runelord Dedication. Your anima focus has Hardness equal to twice your level and Hit Points equal to your own. Your anima focus has fast healing equal to twice your Intelligence modifier. Your anima focus is associated with the same sin as your chosen avenging runelord sin. As long as at least one sizable settlement in which this sin is prevalent (subject to the GM’s discretion) is within a hundred miles of it, your anima focus absorbs energy from these sins. As long as it does so and you are on the same plane as the anima focus, you do not age and are immune to effects that rob you of your mental abilities (such as the never mind spell or the confused and stupefied conditions). Other creatures cannot enter your runewell unless they possess a planar key you created and gave to them, or unless they’re adjacent to your anima focus. Your runewell has an exit that allows adjacent creatures within to activate with an Interact action; when they do so, they exit the runewell and appear adjacent to your anima focus. You gain the following activity. Enter Runewell 10 minutes (concentrate, manipulate, teleportation) You and up to 6 willing creatures you’re touching are instantly transported into your runewell, regardless of any distance between you and your anima focus.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-avenging-runelord-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Craft Runewell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8151",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Heroic Scion Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Destiny calls, and the soul of a dead hero reincarnates to take up the fight! Either an old enemy resumes their efforts to affect chaos and violence, or a new threat arises and you feel compelled to stand against it. You’ve stood against evil before, and the time is nigh for you to do so once again. When you select this mythic destiny, work with your GM to determine the best choice for which previous PC or NPC serves as the source of your reincarnation. For the Revenge of the Runelords Adventure Path in particular, any PC who played a role in the Rise of the Runelords, Shattered Star, or Return of the Runelords Adventure Paths makes for a perfect fit—as would any allied NPC who, in your previous campaign, perished before the end. A heroic scion comes into the world when a nemesis from their old adventures returns. In the case of this campaign, the heroic scion’s nemesis are the ancient runelords of Thassilon. In other campaigns, this nemesis can be a specific individual, a coterie of rivals, or an organization you’re destined to oppose. You instinctively know when your nemesis is active in the world. This knowledge may begin as nightmares or a feeling of inevitable conflict but grows stronger and more specific as you contemplate further. You also know when this entity or group has been fully defeated and ceases to operate at all. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to Seek or Sense Motive whenever an ally or servant of your nemesis attempts to Lie to you, escape your notice, or Impersonate someone else. Fate has deemed you incredibly hard to kill. You reduce the DC of recovery checks by 1. Choose one skill that’s not a Lore skill, based on the themes of your reincarnated heroic source. Your GM can help you determine a list of appropriate skills to choose from. When you employ an action using that skill, you may spend a Mythic Point to attempt the associated check at mythic proficiency. Finally, you gain the Additional Lore feat for a special Lore skill subcategory—Incarnation Lore. This Lore skill allows you to become aware of or recall your past exploits. When you increase your proficiency in Incarnation Lore, you remember more about your previous adventures. Certain heroic scion feats require you to attempt an Incarnation Lore check, such as when you attempt the following activity granted you by this feat. Flash of Memory [free-action] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 77Spend a Mythic Point and attempt an Incarnation Lore check at mythic proficiency to Recall Knowledge in place of making any other Lore check (other than Incarnation Lore).",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Heroic Scion Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8152",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Avoid Fate's Gaze"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your past and current enemies may know you by reputation, but spying on you with magic is much more difficult. Whenever you attempt a saving throw against a scrying or effect, you do so at mythic proficiency. Scrying effects that attempt to observe you that don’t allow saving throws to resist (such as clairaudience or clairvoyance) treat you as if you were concealed and actively trying to Hide or Sneak unless they are mythic as well.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Avoid Fate's Gaze",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8153",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "I've Been Here Before"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You adapt quickly to new settings and terrains. When you make your daily preparations in a region you’ve never visited before (such as a city, geographical region, or small demiplane, but not in a dungeon, structure, or other location that focuses on encounter mode play), you spend part of that time introspectively digging into the memories of your past life to get a feel for the adventure that awaits. Choose one of the following Exploration activities: Avoid Notice, Defend, Investigate, Scout, or Search. You perform that exploration activity at full speed rather than at half speed, and any skill check you attempt as a result of this Exploration activity is made at mythic proficiency. These benefits end as soon as you enter a new region, as determined by the GM.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "I've Been Here Before",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Exploration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8154",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Internal Dialogue"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8154#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Past experiences or even past selves whisper words of advice and encouragement when you need them. Roll an Incarnation Lore check and use that result instead of your failed skill check result.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Internal Dialogue",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8154#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8155",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "My Reputation Precedes Me"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Long years of brave exploits haven’t gone unnoticed. Whether you know just the right things to say or those you’re speaking with recognize you as a reincarnated hero, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks made to Gather Information or Make An Impression, and to Intimidation checks made to Coerce. At 18th level, these circumstance bonuses increase to +3. If you spend a Mythic point when you attempt such a check, you do so at mythic proficiency.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "My Reputation Precedes Me",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8156",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reincarnated Companion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’re not alone in having a legendary past life—so too does your companion. This previous life might be the return of an animal companion or familiar a previous PC of yours had that perished, or it could be the reincarnation of an entirely different legendary creature. It could even be the returning spirit of a close friend or ally who stood by your side. If you have an animal companion, it gains one specialization of your choice. If you have a familiar, it gains two additional familiar abilities. If your fated companion is slain, you can replace it at no cost when you perform your daily preparations.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication-familiar-or-nimble-or-savage-animal-companion",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Reincarnated Companion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8157",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "To Thine Own Self"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8157#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Awareness of your past perils protects you from those who would manipulate your thoughts. Attempt to counteract the triggering effect using your Incarnation Lore modifier as your counteract modifier and half your level as your counteract rank.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "To Thine Own Self",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8157#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8158",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Daunting Spell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8158#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your enemies feel the inevitability of defeat once they feel the potency of your magic. If your next action is to Cast a Spell that allows a saving throw, your spell gains the emotion, fear, and mental traits. The spell gains the following success and failure effects in addition to any other effects it would normally have. If the target is your nemesis or an ally of your nemesis, use mythic proficiency to determine your spell’s attack bonus and save DC; if the spell has multiple targets, all targets must be your nemesis or allied with your nemesis for you to use mythic proficiency. Critical Success The target is unaffected by the daunting spell. Success The target is frightened 1. Failure The target is frightened 2 and stupefied 1 for as long as they remain frightened. If the daunting spell has a duration, the affected creature can’t reduce their frightened condition from this effect below 1 until the spell’s duration ends. Critical Failure As failure, but frightened 3 and stupefied 2.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Daunting Spell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8158#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8159",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Let Death Be My Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You recall your death in vivid detail, and the fear, pain, and uncertainty you suffered are blunted by the truth of your reincarnation. Pain and agony brought on by your foes can be endured and even turned back upon them when you feel yourself at death’s door. Whenever you have the doomed, dying, or wounded condition, you gain that condition’s value as a status bonus to damage rolls when you make melee or ranged weapon Strikes. If you have multiple conditions, only the highest value condition counts for setting the amount of this damage bonus. You also gain the following free action. Share Death's Promises [free-action] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 78 Trigger Your turn begins; Requirements You are gaining a bonus to damage from Let Death Be My Weapon;Spend a Mythic Point. You gain a status bonus to damage equal to double the bonus you're receiving from Let Death Be My Weapon that lasts for 1 minute. During this time, this status bonus doesn’t decrease or increase if the value of your doomed, dying, or wounded condition decreases or increases.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Let Death Be My Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8160",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Momentary Respite"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8160#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your sense of destiny manifests as rapid physical healing. Spend a Mythic Point. You regain 8d8 Hit Points and remove any persistent damage condition affecting you. Until the end of your next turn, you’re immune to persistent damage (though you would take any other effects of an attack or spell that would also give you persistent damage).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Momentary Respite",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8160#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8161",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Vigorous Victor"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Long years of success have not only shown you where your limits lie, they’ve expanded them. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to saving throws against effects that would cause you to become drained, enfeebled, fatigued, sickened, or slowed. Whenever you attempt such a save, you can spend a Mythic Point do so at mythic proficiency. The bonus increases to +3 at 18th level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Vigorous Victor",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8162",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "On My Best Day"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8162#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Be they in your current life or your previous one, you’ve had many heroic moments that continue to inspire you. Even past failures or humiliations can become a source of inspiration—or at least, an opportunity to make up for a past error on this new day. Attempt an Incarnation Lore check against a very hard DC of your level. Critical Success You gain a +3 status bonus to AC and resistance to physical damage equal to your level until the end of your next turn. You can Sustain this effect for up to 1 minute. Success As critical success, but the status bonus is +2 and the resistance is equal to half your level. Failure You gain a +1 status bonus to AC until the end of your next turn. Critical Failure You gain a +1 status bonus to AC against the next attack made against you until the end of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "On My Best Day",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8162#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8163",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Telling Blow"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8163#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your determination empowers a telling blow to defeat your most powerful enemies. Spend a Mythic Point. Make a Strike at mythic proficiency. If the Strike hits, you deal an extra die of weapon damage. You can spend additional Mythic Points after determining the outcome of the attack to deal one more die of weapon damage per extra Mythic Point spent. If the target of your attack is your nemesis or an ally of your nemesis, you gain two die of weapon damage per extra Mythic Point spent. If you have no Mythic Points remaining after using this ability, you gain the fatigued condition.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Telling Blow",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8163#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8164",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "To Me!"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8164#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Two lives spent in adventuring groups has given you a special gift for bolstering party morale and pushing your allies to achieve greater ends when they work as a team. Spend a Mythic Point to rally your allies to your side to regroup or push your advantage. Stride and then make a melee Strike. As soon as your turn is over, your allies within 30 feet who can see and hear you may Stride in your direction as a free action, but don’t have to. Your allies control their own movement and may move in such a way as to avoid obstacles or creatures, but if they Stride, they must be at least 5 feet closer to you than where they were when they started by the end of this movement. If yours or an ally’s movement this round triggers reactions, you or your ally uses mythic proficiency to determine their AC or to attempt a saving throw to resist the reaction. If an ally is within melee range of the target of the Strike you made with this ability, that ally may also make a melee Strike against that enemy as a reaction instead of Striding toward you. Any Strikes from To Me! made against your nemesis, be they Strikes you make or Strikes made by allies, use mythic proficiency.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "To Me!",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8164#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8165",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Eternal Hero"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You might be protected by divine intervention or the necessity of cosmic balance. You might be watched over by agents of destiny or fate. You could even be simply someone whose luck and skill have always worked together to ensure your triumph, no matter the odds you might face. Whatever the explanation, you’re almost impossible to kill. You reduce the DC of recovery checks by 1 (this is cumulative with the reduction from the Heroic Scion Dedication feat). Whenever your doomed condition would increase to 4 or more, it doesn’t increase. The first time each day you would be reduced to 0 Hit Points or outright killed by magical means, you instead remain at 1 Hit Point and become immune to all damage until the end of your next turn. If you finally do die, you can spend a Mythic Point as a free action to immediately reincarnate—manifesting in a new body with the same statistics (save for potential changes to your ancestry and ancestry feats) within 15 feet of where your death occurred. Each time you repeat this reincarnation, the cost to do so increases by 1, so that after your third reincarnation, you can no longer swiftly return (as no mythic character can ever have more than 3 Mythic Points at one time).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-heroic-scion-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Eternal Hero",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8166",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Timewracked Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The current of time shifts subtly in your field of view. You have learned to tread these temporal eddies, moving forward and pushing backward in small strokes—sometimes even gaining the ability to move your allies and enemies through time as you choose. Whether or not you’ll ever be fully restored to your proper timeline, you can’t predict—but until then you continue to manipulate your estrangement from time to move unseen, defy your opponents in combat, and occupy future or past versions of yourself to escape distress. With practice you could gain the ability to rehearse a speech at the same tie you deliver it or attack distant foes without spending the time to move between them. Eventually, you might gain the power to vanish from existence altogether while you hop forward and backward in time or even become immortal. Your Speed increases by 5 feet for each mode of movement available to you. You can spend a Mythic Point to roll any check made to determine your initiative at mythic proficiency. If your initiative roll result is tied with an opponent’s initiative roll, you can choose to go first. In addition, you gain the following reaction. Sidestep Through Time [reaction] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 81 Trigger You are about to attempt a Reflex saving throw against an area effectYou slip through time to avoid a dangerous outcome. Teleport up to 10 feet in any direction. If this would take you outside of the area’s effect, you don’t need to attempt the Reflex save against it. You are then off-guard for 1 round.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Timewracked Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8167",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Be Right Back"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8167#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can manipulate time to produce an item in a seemingly impossible fashion. You flicker a few times as you make adjustments to your gear, then solidify again with a specific needed item that you purchased from an alternate timeline using coin you have on your person. This allows you to purchase a single common item with a level no higher than your level and its Bulk must be low enough that carrying it wouldn’t have made you encumbered. You must spend the standard amount to purchase the item, and this money must be carried on your person. You can be wearing or holding the item, as long as you have the required number of hands free, and if the item has the invested trait, you have already Invested in it, provided you haven’t reached your limit of invested items.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-timewracked-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Be Right Back",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8167#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "three-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8168",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Live Off Borrowed Time"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8168#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You tap into the future to steal a bit of time from yourself a few seconds from now that you can use immediately. You become quickened for 1 round, and can use the extra action to take any basic or specialty basic 1-action action. You gain this extra action immediately and can use it this turn. At the end of your turn, you become slowed 1 and are immune to the quickened condition until the end of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-timewracked-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Live Off Borrowed Time",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8168#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8169",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Now You See Me"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8169#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You flash through several possible timelines as you move. Stride up to your Speed. This movement doesn’t provoke reactions, and you are concealed until the end of your turn. All creatures are off-guard to you until the end of your turn. You can use Now You See Me while Burrowing, Climbing, Flying, or Swimming instead of Striding if you have the corresponding movement type.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-timewracked-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Now You See Me",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8169#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8170",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Second Sight"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8170#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You peer into the next several seconds to watch the potential timelines around a nearby creature unfold. Spend a Mythic Point, then make a check to Recall Knowledge at mythic proficiency about a creature you can see. This check gains the following additional effects. Critical Success You learn all the actions the creature will take on its next turn (or in the first round of combat if combat hasn’t begun), such as “Stride toward Seelah” or “Cast shield.” These actions are locked in and the creature must attempt them, even if the situation changes, though it need not perform the actions in the order stated. For instance, if the creature locked in the actions “Stride toward Seelah,” “Make a longsword Strike against Seelah,” and “Raise a shield,” and Seelah spent her turn moving adjacent to the creature, the creature can make the longsword Strike as its first action if it wishes. If the creature is unable to fulfill an action it committed to, it loses that action as it reels from a temporal paradox. If the situation changes drastically (perhaps Seelah becomes invisible and the creature is unaware where Seelah is), the GM determines what happens. Success You gain one additional piece of information about the creature, as if you had critically succeeded at the Recall Knowledge check.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-timewracked-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Second Sight",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Prediction"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8170#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8171",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Temporal Fury"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8171#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You shift and skip through time, vanishing during your movement to appear in unexpected and advantageous locations for combat. Spend a Mythic Point. Strike, then Step up to 10 feet. This movement is affected normally by barriers and difficult terrain; you still move physically through the area, just so swiftly that it appears that you’ve teleported. Then, make another Strike. Apply your multiple attack penalty to both Strikes normally, but this second Strike is made at mythic proficiency and your target is off guard against it.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-timewracked-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Temporal Fury",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8171#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8172",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bolstered Recovery"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Whenever you rest, you recover with remarkable speed. Double the number of Hit Points you regain and the amount by which condition values are reduced from a full night’s rest. You gain the following action. Instant Recovery [one-action] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 82 Frequency once per day;Spend a Mythic Point. You regain Hit Points equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum 1) × your level and remove the fatigued condition. If you’re suffering from any recurring affliction such as poison or disease, attempt a saving throw against the affliction at mythic proficiency to see if you reduce the affliction’s stage. This saving throw cannot increase your affliction’s stage, nor does it change the affliction’s maximum duration.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-timewracked-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Bolstered Recovery",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8173",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Echoing Fury"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You cheat the rules of time to co-locate during your attack. When you use Temporal Fury, your Step can be up to 15 feet. If your second Strike is against the same creature as your first Strike, your second Strike deals an additional die of weapon damage; if both Strikes hit, you combine their damage for the purpose of resistances and weaknesses.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-temporal-fury",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Echoing Fury",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8174",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Preserve the Moment"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8174#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Sometimes, your actions are so successful and impressive that it’s worth going back to them. Note the actions you took during the turn that just ended (excepting the reaction you used to trigger Preserve the Moment), including the die roll results (not the actual check results). Die rolls you made as a result of others’ actions on you or from the environment are not recorded. For example, if you Stride up to a firewyrm, roll a basic Reflex save against its intense heat aura, then Strike the firewyrm with a longsword, and then Climb up an adjacent wall, when you activate Preserve the Moment you record only the Stride action, the Strike action (and the die roll result you roll for the Strike), and the Climb action (and the die roll result you roll for the Athletics check to do so); you do not record your Reflex save against the aura’s effects. Preserve the Moment works best, as a result, when the actions you take are relatively standard and when rolls associated with those are high rolls. You gain the following reaction, which you can use once during the next 24 hours. Restore the Moment [reaction] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 83 Trigger Your turn begins;Spend a Mythic Point. Take the same actions in the same order, using the same die roll results to resolve those actions, as you did in the preserved moment, and apply modifiers to those rolls as they currently exist (not as they were when you recorded the loop) but at mythic proficiency. The exact details of how you accomplish your restored actions can change—you need not move in the exact same pattern or distance with a repeated Stride, for example, nor must you make a repeated Strike against the same foe you attacked in the first set of actions, but you do need to use the same type of movement when you Stride, and you do need to use the same type of weapon to Strike. If at any point during your turn you are unable to take the next action in the loop, your turn ends and you become stunned 1. For example, if you restored the above example against the firewyrm in a round where you were fighting an ogre and you weren’t able to attempt a Strike with a longsword against the ogre as your second action, you would become stunned 1. Likewise, if at the end of your turn there was nothing for you to try to Climb, you would become stunned 1. You can preserve and restore a Cast a Spell action, but if you don’t cast the same spell when you Restore the Moment, you become stunned 1 (you can Cast the Spell at a different rank, though).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-timewracked-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Preserve the Moment",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8174#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8175",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Fracture Time Flow"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your ability to interact with and even observe the flow of time allows you to fracture it slightly in a localized place whenever you land a particularly solid blow on a foe. Whenever you achieve a critical success with a Strike, the target of that Strike must also attempt a Will save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. Critical Success The target is unaffected by the fractured timeflow. Success The target is slowed 1 for 1 round. Failure The target is slowed 2 for 1 round. Critical Failure The target is stunned 3, then slowed 2 for 1 round after they recover from being stunned.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-timewracked-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Fracture Time Flow",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Incapacitation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8176",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Not This Time"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8176#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You reflexively attempt to cycle a creature’s timeline briefly to a reality where it’s less able to succeed. Spend a Mythic Point. The creature that targets you must then attempt a Will save against your class DC or spell DC at mythic proficiency, whichever is higher. Critical Success The spell or ability affects you normally. Success The creature’s attempt to target you is slightly hindered. If your AC is being targeted, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your AC. If you need to attempt a saving throw, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the save. Failure The creature’s attempt to target you is significantly hindered. If your AC is being targeted, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your AC, and a critical hit against you becomes a normal hit. If you need to attempt a saving throw, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the save, and if you critically fail, you fail instead. Critical Failure The creature’s attempt to target you fails, and the actions it used to make the attempt are wasted.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-timewracked-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Not This Time",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8176#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8177",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Timelessness"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Time travelers are rare, but even among them your isolation from time is unique. As long as you remain timewracked, you do not age and cannot die of natural causes. You’re immune to hostile spells and effects related to time or aging, as well as the slowed condition (except for when you gain the slowed condition through this mythic destiny). You reduce the DC of recovery checks by 1. Whenever you roll a flat check to end persistent damage, you roll twice and choose your desired result; this is a fortune effect. In addition, your intimate knowledge of the flow of time gives you a measure of influence over the attempt of another to manipulate it. Whenever an enemy creature that you are aware of and who is within 60 feet of you gains the quickened condition, you gain the quickened condition for 1 round. The actions available to you from the acquired condition are the same as those granted by the ability that quickens your enemy.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-timewracked-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "Timelessness",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8178",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Warshard Warrior Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you became infused with a shard of the god of war, you knew in your gut that your destiny would be one for the ages—yet you may not, at first, know the exact way such a destiny would play out. If you still carry the warshard that empowered you, you might carry it as a token or wear it as jewelry—if indeed it’s not simply embedded into your body. Regardless, the warshard itself no longer has any intrinsic power of its own, and even if you toss the warshard aside, its gifts do not leave you, nor can another benefit from them. If you throw the warshard away or lose it, your destiny remains unaltered; you have, in effect, become the warshard itself. This power manifests through a weapon you wield. When you make your daily preparations, choose one weapon in your possession in which you have at least expert proficiency. That weapon becomes your warshard weapon until you choose a different weapon in your possession during another of your daily preparations. You can choose a mundane nonmagical weapon, a weapon with magical runes, one made of an unusual material, or even a specific magic weapon such as a storm flash or a bloodletting kukri, but not an intelligent weapon or an artifact like the bastard sword Serithtial or one of the seven swords of sin. While you don’t lose access to your warshard warrior feats if your warshard weapon is taken from you or destroyed, note that several of this destiny’s feats require you to be wielding your warshard weapon. You can etch or remove runes from a warshard weapon normally. You can have only one warshard weapon at a time. Your gain the Mythic Strike feat, but you can only use it with your warshard weapon. Whenever you make a Strike with your warshard weapon at mythic proficiency, you double the amount of additional damage you deal with the weapon specialization class feature. When you make Crafting checks to Repair your warshard weapon, your treat your proficiency rank in Crafting as legendary for determining how many Hit Points you restore to the item; in addition, if your Crafting result is a critical failure, you get a failure instead. You also gain the following action. Call Warshard Weapon [one-action] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 85 Requirements You are not holding your warshard weapon, and you have a hand or hands free to be able to wield your warshard weapon;Your warshard weapon teleports into your hand, as long as you and your warshard weapon are on the same planet. At 15th level, you need only be on the same plane as your warshard weapon to call it, and at 18th level, you can call your warshard weapon across any distance. If your warshard weapon is in the possession of a mythic creature that’s higher level than you or placed in an area where teleportation magic doesn’t function, attempt a DC 16 flat check. On a success, your warshard weapon still teleports to your hand.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Warshard Warrior Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8179",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Athlete's Ally"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8179#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You channel the power of your warshard through your weapon to better perform athletic maneuvers. Spend a Mythic Point. For 1 minute, when you attempt Athletics checks to Disarm, Grapple, Reposition, Shove, or Trip with your warshard weapon, you do so at mythic proficiency. Note that this ability doesn’t grant additional weapon traits to your weapon, so your options for which of these maneuvers you can attempt might be limited by your weapon’s existing traits.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warshard-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Athlete's Ally",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8179#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8180",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lightless Sight"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain darkvision as long as you wield your warshard weapon; if you already have darkvision, it becomes greater darkvision. You also gain the following ability. Weaponsight [one-action] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 85Close your eyes and concentrate on your warshard weapon. You perceive the world as if you were observing it from your weapon rather than your own eyes. You can see in all directions simultaneously and therefore can’t be flanked. If you’re not holding your weapon, this ability fails if your warshard weapon is on a different plane than you. If you spend a Mythic Point as part of this action, you attempt saving throws against visual effects at mythic proficiency while observing through your warshard weapon. You can observe through your weapon for up to 1 minute or until you open your eyes as a free action, whichever comes first.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warshard-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Lightless Sight",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8181",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Steadfast Grip"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The connection you have with your warshard weapon strengthens it and assists you in maintaining your grip on it in battle. Your DCs against attempts made to Disarm, Steal, or otherwise remove your warshard weapon from your possession are calculated at mythic proficiency. When you designate a warshard weapon, its Hardness increases by an amount equal to half your level, and its Hit Points increase by an amount equal to your level for as long as it is your warshard weapon.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warshard-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Steadfast Grip",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8182",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Transmute Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you choose a warshard weapon during daily preparations, you can transform the material it’s composed of so that the weapon is made of a precious material (like adamantine, dawnsilver, or cold iron). The material and quality of the material you select must be of a level equal to or less than your character level. You can transmute the weapon into a standard-grade item of that material only if the weapon is at least level 9. You can transmute the weapon into high-grade item of that material only if the weapon is at least level 15.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warshard-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Transmute Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8183",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Warshard Rune"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you choose a warshard weapon during your daily preparations, you can empower it with an additional magical effect. Choose one common weapon property rune that’s of a level equal to or lower than your level. That rune is applied to your warshard weapon as if it were etched onto it normally, but this weapon property does not count against the normal maximum number of property runes a weapon can have. If you empower a weapon with a property rune of the same type, only the highest-level one applies. This additional rune functions only when you wield your warshard weapon and have at least 1 unspent Mythic Point; otherwise, the rune becomes dormant until these conditions are met.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warshard-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Warshard Rune",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8184",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Divide and Conquer"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8184#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "When you face multiple foes, you wield your warshard weapon with vigor. Spend 1 Mythic Point, then Step to a space where you threaten at least two opponents with your warshard weapon. Attempt two Strikes at mythic proficiency, each against a different target. If you hit with both Strikes, you gain an additional effect based on the type of damage you inflict with your weapon. Both attacks count toward your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn’t increase until after you’ve made both of them. If your weapon doesn’t deal one of these three damage types, you can’t use it to Divide and Conquer, and if you deal two different types of damage to each target, you don’t gain any additional effect. • Bludgeoning You knock your enemies around. Each damaged target becomes off-guard until the start of your next turn. • Piercing Your strikes punch through your enemies, leaving bloody wounds. Each damaged target takes 1d8 persistent bleed damage. • Slashing Your slashes leave particularly painful wounds. Each damaged target becomes sickened 2.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warshard-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Divide and Conquer",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8184#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8185",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Indomitable Shot"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8185#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You can fire a single shot that penetrates multiple foes. Spend 1 Mythic Point, then fire a single shot from your ranged warshard weapon. You inflict your weapon’s damage on all creatures in a line, to a maximum distance equal to your weapon’s maximum range or until the line hits a solid object that’s either thicker than 5 feet or has a Hardness in excess of 20, whichever comes first. Each creature in the area attempts a basic Reflex save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher, calculated at mythic proficiency. For each range increment beyond the first, a creature gains a cumulative +2 circumstance bonus to their Reflex save. This ability counts as two attacks when calculating your multiple attack penalty.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warshard-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Indomitable Shot",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Attack",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8185#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8186",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Prescient Parry"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8186#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Spend a Mythic Point. Your warshard weapon intervenes at the last second, rising to deflect the incoming blow. For this attack, calculate your AC at mythic proficiency, then add any item bonus from your weapon to that value. If the attack misses and the target is within your reach, or if your warshard weapon is a ranged weapon and the target is within the weapon’s first range increment, you can Strike the creature who made the triggering attack with your warshard weapon.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warshard-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Prescient Parry",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8186#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8187",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Final Shot Knows the Way"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8187#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You judge a foe’s defenses after attacking them and channel that knowledge into your warshard weapon and its ammunition. Spend a Mythic Point, then Stride twice. At any point during this movement, attempt a ranged Strike at mythic proficiency with your warshard weapon against the same foe you already attacked this round. This Strike ignores any modifiers from cover or concealment the target may have, as the ammunition weaves and twists through the air in an impossible flight. All penalties from range increments are negated during this Strike. If this shot hits its target, the target is so astounded by the shot that they become off-guard until the end of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warshard-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Final Shot Knows the Way",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Press"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8187#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8188",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Throw and Catch"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8188#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You hurl your warshard weapon at an opponent, even though the weapon isn’t designed to be thrown. Spend a Mythic Point. Your weapon gains the thrown trait with a range increment of 40 feet; if your weapon already has the thrown trait, increase its range increment by 40 feet. Make a ranged Strike at mythic proficiency at an opponent within range. For this ranged Strike, apply your full Strength modifier to the damage, as if it were a melee Strike. After the Strike resolves, the weapon flies back to your hand, and you can then attempt a melee Strike (at your normal proficiency, not mythic proficiency) against a target in reach of your weapon. Both attacks count toward your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn’t increase until after you’ve made both attacks.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warshard-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "18",
          "aonprd:name": "Throw and Catch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8188#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8189",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "I Am the Weapon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your supernatural bond with your weapon infuses it with a powerful echo of your sentience, your memory, and even fragments of your very soul. When you would be killed while wielding your warshard weapon, you instead disappear and your warshard weapon falls to the ground. You reappear adjacent to your warshard weapon as soon as any sapient creature picks it up. If the creature is a close ally (such as another PC), you return to life with only 1 Hit Point. However, if a stranger does so, you return to life with full Hit Points. At your discretion, you can delay your return to life for up to 24 hours after a creature picks up the weapon, but you still return to life adjacent to your weapon (or as close to it as possible). If no one picks up your weapon within a week of your death, your soul enters the River of Souls, and you can be brought back to life using other means. No matter how you're brought back to life, you can Call Warshard Weapon as a free action as soon as you regain consciousness. Alternatively, if no one picks up your warshard weapon within a week of your death, you can choose to fuse with your weapon rather than entering the River of Souls. You can no longer be brought back to life, but your soul remains bound to the weapon, and together you are an intelligent item, gaining the same Perception modifier, senses, communication, languages, attribute modifiers, and Will save as you. You retain the same Intelligence-, Wisdom-, and Charisma-based skills. You must still be carried and wielded, and your options are now limited to actions you can take as an intelligent item. You no longer gain or can spend Mythic Points, but as a weapon, you are still mythic. You can spend your actions to attack using the attack modifier with your warshard weapon you had in life, but your damage bonus uses the Strength modifier of your wielder instead of the Strength modifier you had in life. You gain the Impart Martial Wisdom action below, and you might gain other powers at the GM’s discretion, such as the ability to influence or even control your wielder. If you’re destroyed in this weapon form, your soul moves on to the River of Souls and you can be brought back to life using other means, but you must designate a new warshard weapon normally thereafter. Activate—Impart Martial Wisdom [two-actions] (concentrate, mythic, prediction); Frequency once per 10 minutes; Effect You call upon your experience in battle to see how best to attack a foe and give that knowledge to your wielder. Your wielder makes a Strike against a creature within reach or within your first range increment at mythic proficiency. This Strike ignores circumstance penalties to the attack roll and any flat check required due to the target being concealed or hidden.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-warshard-warrior-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "20",
          "aonprd:name": "I Am the Weapon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8190",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Calm and Centered"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your occult connection to the world helps you deal with being frightened or stupefied. When your frightened or stupefied condition values would decrease, decrease the value by 2.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-occultism",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Calm and Centered",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8191",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Comforting Presence"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8191#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your occult connection to your allies lets you take on fear and confusion they feel. Focus on your calmness and pull in nearby allies’ emotions. Reduce the frightened and stupefied condition values of adjacent allies by 1, and increase your frightened and stupefied condition values by the same amount.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-occultism",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Comforting Presence",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8191#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8192",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Go With the Flow"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8192#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You have an occult connection to the world that helps you blend in with the cacophony of life around you. Attempt an Occultism check against the creature’s Perception DC. On a success, the creature mistakenly identifies another creature within 30 feet of you as you instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-master-in-occultism",
          "aonprd:level": "7",
          "aonprd:name": "Go With the Flow",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Secret",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8192#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8193",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Let's Try That Again"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8193#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You feel a sense of deja vu when you’ve made a mistake, almost as if you weren’t so careless in a past life and could certainly do better if given another chance. Reroll the triggering skill check and use the new result, even if it’s worse than your first roll.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Let's Try That Again",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8193#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8194",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Like a Roach"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Living with the bare necessities isn’t terribly hard for someone who has defied death, and like a cockroach, you always know how to survive. When you Subsist during downtime, the DC for your skill check is reduced by 2. You don’t need a minimum proficiency rank to Subsist in unusual environments, nor do you take a –5 penalty if you Subsist after 8 hours or less of exploration.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Like a Roach",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Downtime",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8195",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Weight of Experience"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The experience you’ve accumulated over multiple lifetimes envelops you like a weighted blanket, providing comfort and bestowing confidence under pressure. You gain the trained proficiency rank in one skill of your choice and the Assurance skill feat in that skill as a bonus feat.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Weight of Experience",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8196",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Wisdom From Another Life"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You absorbed a wide variety of facts before you died, and your soul still remembers slivers of this precious knowledge. You gain the trained proficiency rank in one skill of your choice and the Additional Lore skill feat as a bonus feat.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Wisdom From Another Life",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8197",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Animal Soul Siblings"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your eyes have been opened to the spiritual essence suffusing the world. You gain speak with animals as a primal innate spell that you can cast once per day. You get a +1 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks to Gather Information from animals.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Animal Soul Siblings",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8198",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Empathy Incarnate"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Reincarnation has given you a compassionate perspective and enabled you to relate to almost everyone you speak with, putting them at ease and quickly generating trust. Whenever you attempt a Diplomacy check to Make An Impression or Request something, the DC is reduced by 2, and if the creature you’re speaking with is lower level than you, any success is a critical success. Whenever you attempt a Diplomacy check to Gather Information, you can’t critically fail.",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Empathy Incarnate",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8199",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "I've Had Many Jobs"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Finding and excelling at odd jobs is child’s play to one who has worked many occupations during many lives. When you attempt to Earn Income, you function as if you were trained in the skill used. If you’re at least an expert in the skill used, the DC for your skill check is reduced by 2.",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "I've Had Many Jobs",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Downtime",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=820",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Powerful Leap"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can jump 5 feet up with a vertical Leap without making a High Jump. You also increase the horizontal distance when you Leap, including as part of a High Jump or Long Jump, by 5 feet.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Powerful Leap",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8200",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reincarnated Ridiculer"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve practiced the art of taunting an enemy, ensuring they know death will only make you stronger. When you Demoralize an opponent, the target doesn’t become temporarily immune to your attempts to Demoralize it unless you critically fail the check. If the target critically hit you with a Strike on its previous turn, the DC for this check is reduced by 4.",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Reincarnated Ridiculer",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8201",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sleep of the Reborn"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Philosophers compare the cycle of life, death, and rebirth to sleeping, dreaming, and waking. You take it to another level by reliving previous lives in dreams, always waking invigorated and thankful for a new chance at life. Whenever you rest for 8 hours, you gain the effects of a long-term rest. If you’re an ancestry that neither sleeps nor dreams, you still receive this benefit by entering a reflective, meditative state during rest.",
          "aonprd:level": "5",
          "aonprd:name": "Sleep of the Reborn",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8202",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Lingering Echoes"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Not everyone is reincarnated, and you feel a strong connection with the spiritual echoes of those who didn’t receive the same opportunity as you. You gain talking corpse as an occult innate spell that you can cast once per day. You can ask a fourth question of a corpse when you cast this spell. The corpse attempts its Will save against your spell DC or your class DC, whichever is higher.",
          "aonprd:level": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Lingering Echoes",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8203",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Plant Soul Siblings"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’re now able to connect with the spirits present in the greenery of the natural world. You gain speak with plants as a primal innate spell that you can cast once per day. You get a +2 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks to Gather Information from animals or plants.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-animal-soul-siblings",
          "aonprd:level": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Plant Soul Siblings",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8204",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rapid Retraining"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Some feel trapped by their choices and have a tough time reinventing themselves. To you, this dilemma is just a natural part of reincarnation. Retraining other feats or skill increases during downtime only takes 4 days instead of a week, and class features that require a choice can be retrained in a week instead of a month. You also never need to find a teacher to retrain, as the memories of abilities you possessed in past lives are superior to any instructor.",
          "aonprd:level": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "Rapid Retraining",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Downtime",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8205",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "You Seem Somewhat Familiar"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8205#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You fought hundreds of foes in your various past lives, and now and then, something about a new opponent tugs at your memory, almost as if you defeated their grandparent long ago. You get a +2 circumstance bonus to your next attack roll, damage roll, or saving throw against this creature. You only receive this bonus once per creature.",
          "aonprd:level": "9",
          "aonprd:name": "You Seem Somewhat Familiar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8205#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8206",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Clinging to Life"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8206#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "This life still holds much for you, and you aren’t ready to fall back into the River of Souls just yet. When you’re reduced to 0 Hit Points and not immediately killed, you go to 1 Hit Point instead, fall prone, and are unconscious, and you don’t gain the wounded condition.",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Clinging to Life",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8206#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8207",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "I Sense Malevolence"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your time in the River of Souls has given you deep insight into the machinations of those who refuse to move on. You gain spirit senseas a 6th-rank occult innate spell that you can cast once per day.",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "I Sense Malevolence",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8208",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Linguistic Revival"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You achieved fluency in different languages with each reincarnation, and your brain remembers much of the grammar, idioms, and obscenities that you spouted in old lives. You gain truespeech as a 5th-rank occult innate spell that you can cast once a day on only yourself. While the spell is active, you get a +2 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks while speaking to a creature in a language other than Common.",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Linguistic Revival",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8209",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Pain is Temporary"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8209#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Sangpotshi practitioners know that suffering is a fleeting sensation that ultimately strengthens the soul and prepares it for a new reincarnation. Bolstered by this understanding, you’ve learned to temporarily steel yourself against all forms of pain. You gain resistance 10 to all damage until the end of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Pain is Temporary",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8209#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8210",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Stone Soul Siblings"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your connection with nature’s spirits has progressed to the point where you can even have casual conversation with pebbles and boulders. You gain speak with stones as a primal innate spell that you can cast once per day. You get a +2 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks to Gather Information from stones.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-plant-soul-siblings",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Stone Soul Siblings",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8211",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Unbreakable Resolve"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8211#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The experience of coming back after death has granted you a strong sense of resolve; devilish words, slick spells, and conniving trickery can’t easily catch you unprepared. Reroll the triggering save, using the second result only if it’s better.",
          "aonprd:level": "13",
          "aonprd:name": "Unbreakable Resolve",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8211#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8212",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Boneyard Acquaintance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Before your soul returned from death, you interacted with a host of other souls on their way to the Boneyard. One of these acquaintances owes you a favor. You can temporarily summon it to come to your aid, and it appears as a swirling mass of ectoplasm with indiscernible features and a translucent dagger, the favored weapon of Pharasma. This functions as spiritual guardian that you can cast once per day as a 9th-rank divine innate spell.",
          "aonprd:level": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "Boneyard Acquaintance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Force",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8213",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Indomitable Spirit"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8213#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your soul has accumulated countless particles of quintessence over myriad deaths and rebirths, and for one moment, this raw material from the Great Beyond envelops you and your comrades. Until the end of your next turn, you and any allies adjacent to you get a +4 circumstance bonus to AC and are quickened. The additional action can be used only to Strike or Stride.",
          "aonprd:level": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "Indomitable Spirit",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8213#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8214",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Release the Light"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8214#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Many people report seeing a bright light before their death. You’re one of these people, and at rare intervals when hope seems dim, the light exudes outward from your soul. You shed bright light in a 30-foot radius (and dim light for another 30 feet beyond that) until the end of your next turn. Enemy creatures in the area that rely on sight must attempt a Fortitude save equal to your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. Critical Success The creature is unaffected. Success The creature is dazzled for 1 round. Failure The creature is blinded for 1 round and dazzled for 1 minute. Critical Failure The creature is blinded for 2 rounds and dazzled for 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:level": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "Release the Light",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Light",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8214#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8215",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "See You in Hell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8215#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You aren’t sure if you’ll be reincarnated again, so you might as well take this foe with you. A blast of spiritual energy lashes out from the depths of your soul, targeting the creature who attacked you. The creature takes spirit damage equal to the amount that reduced you to 0 Hit Points (basic Will save with a DC equal to your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher).",
          "aonprd:level": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "See You in Hell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8215#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8216",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "This is What It's Like to Die"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "It’s one thing to remember your previous lives. It’s quite another to remember how you died in each of those lives. You can recall dozens, if not more, of excruciating, humiliating, and devastating ends you’ve suffered over the eons, and you can inflict upon your enemies a vision of these pains. You gain phantasmagoria as an occult innate spell that you can cast once per day. When you gain this feat, choose any two of the following damage types: acid, bludgeoning, cold, electricity, fire, piercing, poison, slashing, or sonic. These damage types caused your deaths more often than not in your previous lives, and whenever a creature takes damage from a phantasmagoria spell you cast, you can swap the mental damage that spell normally causes for one of the two damage types you chose.",
          "aonprd:level": "17",
          "aonprd:name": "This is What It's Like to Die",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Reincarnated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=824",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Identification"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can Identify Magic swiftly. You take only 1 minute when using Identify Magic to determine the properties of an item, ongoing effect, or location, rather than 10 minutes. If you’re a master, it takes a 3-action activity, and if you’re legendary, it takes 1 action.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-arcana-nature-occultism-or-religion",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Identification",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=825",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Jump"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can use High Jump and Long Jump as a single action instead of 2 actions. If you do, you don’t perform the initial Stride (nor do you fail if you don’t Stride 10 feet).",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Jump",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=827",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Repair"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "For you, the Repair activity loses the exploration trait and takes 1 minute instead of 10 minutes. If you’re a master in Crafting, it takes 3 actions. If you’re legendary, it takes 1 action.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Repair",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8314",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Mental Balm"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your spells release soothing mental waves. Use this amp in place of a psi cantrip's normal amp entry. You can use this amp only on a psi cantrip that targets or affects you or one or more of your allies and doesn't target or affect any enemies.Amp You or one ally within 30 feet gains a +2 status bonus to Will saves against emotion effects for 1 minute. You can also have the amped psi cantrip attempt to counteract one effect imposing the frightened condition on yourself or the chosen ally, or an effect imposing the stupefied condition that has a duration of 1 hour or less. If you successfully counteract the effect, you remove only the frightened and stupefied conditions, not any other part of the effect.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Mental Balm",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Amp",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8315",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Psi Burst"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8315#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "With a passing thought, you direct violent psychic energies at a nearby creature. Target one creature within 30 feet. It takes 1d4 bludgeoning damage with a basic Reflex save. At 3rd level and every 2 levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d4.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Psi Burst",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mindshift",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psyche",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8315#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8316",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Warp Space"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You use your magic to bend space, causing your spell to strike from a strange vector. Use this amp in place of a psi cantrip's normal amp entry. The amped psi cantrip must have a range.Amp Choose a square within 30 feet to which you have line of effect and line of sight. Determine your spell’s line of effect and line of sight from there, as well as whether creatures have cover against the spell. The spell can exceed its normal range as measured from you, as long as it’s within its normal range from the square you chose.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Warp Space",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Amp",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8317",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Astral Tether"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8317#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You spin out a thread of psychic energy that connects you to an ally, using it as a conduit for your abilities. Choose a willing creature within 60 feet and connect to it. Whenever you would gain a benefit from a psychic amp, you can have the amp affect the tethered creature instead. You can do so only if the amp grants a distinct benefit, not if it alters the amped spell. The tether can't be severed physically but breaks if the distance between you and the tethered ally ever exceeds 60 feet, if you become unconscious, or if you use Astral Tether again.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Astral Tether",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8317#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8318",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Homing Beacon"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As your spell strikes a target, you plant a beacon in the target's mind that announces its presence to those nearby. Use this amp in place of a psi cantrip's normal amp entry. The amped cantrip must be one that has one or more targets and must either require a spell attack roll or have a saving throw.Amp Choose one creature hit by the spell (if the spell has a spell attack roll) or that fails its save against the spell (if the spell requires a save). A psychic beacon emits from the creature's location, making it easier to notice the creature as the mind and attention of onlookers is subtly drawn to it. For 1 minute, if the target would be invisible, it's instead merely concealed, and if it would be concealed, it's no longer concealed.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Homing Beacon",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Amp",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8321",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Violent Unleash"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8321#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "The force of your mind unleashing itself releases a violent shock wave that batters your enemies. You deal 2d6 force damage to all creatures in a 20-foot emanation, with a basic Reflex save. At 5th level and every 2 levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d6.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Violent Unleash",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mindshift",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8321#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8325",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Strain Mind"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8325#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You strain your body beyond its limits to use an amp even when your mental power is depleted. You add an amp that costs 1 Focus Point to the spell. Instead of paying the normal Focus Point cost, you lose Hit Points equal to four times the spell rank of the amped psi cantrip as you bleed from your nose or suffer some other visible sign of strain.",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Strain Mind",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8325#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "free-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8330",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Thoughtsense"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can detect the flickers of mental activity let off by all thinking creatures. You gain thoughtsense as a vague sense that has a range of 30 feet—like all vague senses, it's only about as precise as an average human's sense of smell, meaning you generally can predict only if a creature is present. Your thoughtsense detects only thinking creatures, so a creature that is unthinking or otherwise immune to mental effects (such as many constructs and oozes) can't be perceived using your thoughtsense, regardless of how precise it is. While your Psyche is Unleashed, your thoughtsense upgrades to an imprecise sense, letting you use it to Seek out creatures.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Thoughtsense",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8331",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Whispering Steps"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your spell leaves a lingering connection between you and a creature—one through which you can nudge the creature's mind this way or that. The amped cantrip must take 2 or more actions to cast, target one or more creatures, and either require a spell attack roll or have a saving throw. Use this amp in place of the psi cantrip's normal amp entry.Amp Choose one enemy who is a target of the spell. If that enemy fails its save or the spell hits it, you whisper in the creature's mind, forcing it to Stride up to half its Speed in a direction of your choosing; as this is forced movement, you can't force the creature to move into hazardous terrain, off a ledge, or the like. After it moves, the creature becomes temporarily immune to this amp for 24 hours.",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Whispering Steps",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Amp",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Psychic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=835",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ride"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you Command an Animal you’re mounted on to take a move action (such as Stride), you automatically succeed instead of needing to attempt a check. Any animal you’re mounted on acts on your turn, like a minion. If you Mount an animal in the middle of an encounter, it skips its next turn and then acts on your next turn. Page 301 has more on minions.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Ride",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8354",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Diverse Lore"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your wandering studies mean you've heard rumors or theories about almost every topic... though admittedly, your sources aren't always the most reliable. You can take a –2 penalty to your check to Recall Knowledge with Esoteric Lore to Recall Knowledge about any topic, not just the usual topics available for Esoteric Lore. Additionally, when you succeed at your check to Exploit a Vulnerability, compare the result of your Esoteric Lore check to the DC to Recall Knowledge for that creature; if that number would be a success or a critical success, you gain information as if you had succeeded at the Recall Knowledge check.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Diverse Lore",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8355",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Divine Disharmony"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8355#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "From your collection of religious trinkets, you pull out opposing divine objects—such as the religious symbols of two deities that are hated enemies—and combine them in a display that causes discordant clashes of divine energy that are especially distracting to the faithful. Roll your choice of a Deception or Intimidation check against the Will DC of a creature you can see within 60 feet, with the following results. If the creature is particularly devoted to a deity, such as a cleric, celestial, monitor, fiend, or other creature with divine spells, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your skill check. The GM might determine that a creature that despises all deities, such as an alghollthu, is unaffected. Critical Success The creature is off-guard to your attacks until the end of your next turn. Success The creature is off-guard to your attacks until the end of your current turn.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Divine Disharmony",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8355#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8357",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Root to Life or [two-actions]"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8357#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Marigold, spider lily, pennyroyal—many primal traditions connect flowers and plants with the boundary between life and death, and you can leverage this association to keep an ally on this side of the line. You place a small plant or similar symbol on an adjacent dying creature, immediately stabilizing them; the creature is no longer dying and is instead unconscious at 0 Hit Points. If you spend 2 actions instead of 1, you empower the act further by uttering a quick folk blessing to chase away ongoing pain, adding the auditory trait to the action. When you do so, attempt flat checks to remove each source of persistent damage affecting the target; due to the particularly effective assistance, the DC is 10 instead of the usual 15.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Root to Life or [two-actions]",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Primal",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8357#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8360",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Esoteric Warden"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you apply antithetical material against a creature successfully, you also ward yourself against its next attacks. When you succeed at your check to Exploit a Vulnerability, you gain a +1 status bonus to your AC against the creature's next attack and a +1 status bonus to your next saving throw against the creature; if you critically succeed, these bonuses are +2 instead. You can gain these bonuses only once per day against a particular creature, and the benefit ends if you Exploit Vulnerability again.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-exploit-vulnerability",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Esoteric Warden",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8361",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Talisman Esoterica"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You know how to assemble the supernatural objects in your esoterica into a number of temporary talismans. Each day during your daily preparations, you can make two talismans with an item level no higher than half your level. You must know each talisman's formula. A talisman created this way is a temporary item and loses its magic the next time you make your daily preparations. You know the formulas for all common talismans in GM Core of your level or lower. You remember your talisman formulas through oral tradition or mnemonics, so you don't need a formula book for them.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Talisman Esoterica",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8362",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Turn Away Misfortune"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8362#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You perform a superstition, such as casting salt over your shoulder to ward off bad luck. Turn Away Misfortune's fortune trait cancels out the misfortune effect, causing you to roll normally. As normal, you can apply only one fortune ability to a roll, so if you Turned Away Misfortune on an attack roll, you couldn't also use an ability like Halfling Luck to alter the roll further.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Turn Away Misfortune",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8362#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8364",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Instructive Strike"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8364#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You attack your foe and analyze how it reacts. Make a Strike. On a hit, you can immediately attempt a check to Recall Knowledge about the target. On a critical hit, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the check to Recall Knowledge.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Instructive Strike",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8364#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8365",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Paired Link"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You break a trinket, such as a lodestone or jade pendant, in two, creating a sympathetic link between the halves that bridges distance. During your daily preparations, you perform a short ceremony where you gift one of the two halves to a willing ally. On that ally, you can cast spells and use thaumaturge abilities targeting your paired ally as though you are adjacent to each other, and the ally can cast spells targeting you in the same way. These effects last as long as you and the ally have their half; if either half leaves either of your possessions for even a moment, or if you establish a link with a new ally during your next daily preparations, the link breaks.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Paired Link",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8371",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Elaborate Talisman Esoterica"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As you continue to collect talismanic esoterica, you improve your ability to create temporary talismans. You can create four temporary talismans each day instead of two.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-talisman-esoterica",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Elaborate Talisman Esoterica",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8377",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shared Warding"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You ward your allies from the attacks of your foes whenever you apply those protections to yourself. When you gain a status bonus to AC and saves from Esoteric Warden, you can choose to grant the same benefit to all allies within 30 feet.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-esoteric-warden",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Shared Warding",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8380",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Grand Talisman Esoterica"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've gained the ability to place multiple talismans on an item. Normally, affixing more than one talisman to an item causes the talismans to be suppressed, but when you Affix a Talisman, you can specially treat one item you're working on, allowing it to have two active talismans at once. This special treatment ends if you use Affix a Talisman to treat a new item with this ability.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-talisman-esoterica",
          "aonprd:level": "14",
          "aonprd:name": "Grand Talisman Esoterica",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8383",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Seven-Part Link"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Many traditions hold the number seven as significant. By exchanging pieces of a seven-part set of esoterica, you create a magical web by which your allies can affect each other at a distance. When you use Paired Link during your daily preparations, you can exchange linking esoterica with up to six willing allies, keeping one piece for yourself. In addition to the normal effects of Paired Link, if a linked ally casts a spell with a range of touch, they can target linked allies within 30 feet with that spell.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-paired-link",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Seven-Part Link",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8384",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Sever Magic"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8384#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You apply a frayed thread, a pinch of fulu ash, or a similar undone charm to your weapon, and swing to break a spell. Make a Strike against an enemy. If you hit and deal damage, you attempt to counteract a single spell active on the target (your choice). Your counteract rank is equal to half your level (rounded up), and your counteract check modifier is equal to your class DC – 10.",
          "aonprd:level": "16",
          "aonprd:name": "Sever Magic",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Arcane",
            "aonprd:Trait-Esoterica",
            "aonprd:Trait-Thaumaturge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8384#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "two-actions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=839",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Shield Block"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=839#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You snap your shield in place to ward off a blow. Your shield prevents you from taking an amount of damage up to the shield’s Hardness. You and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Shield Block",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=839#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=843",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Snare Crafting"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can use the Craft activity to create snares. When you select this feat, you immediately add the formulas for four common 1st-level snares to your formula book.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Snare Crafting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=844",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Specialty Crafting"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your training focused on Crafting one particular kind of item. Select one of the specialties listed below; you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Crafting checks to Craft items of that type. If you are a master in Crafting, this bonus increases to +2. If it’s unclear whether the specialty applies, the GM decides. Some specialties might apply only partially. For example, if you were making a morningstar and had specialty in woodworking, the GM might give you half your bonus because the item requires both blacksmithing and woodworking. Specialty CraftingSpecialtyApplicable Items Alchemy*Alchemical items such as elixirs ArtistryFine art, including jewelry BlacksmithingDurable metal goods, including metal armor BookmakingBooks and paper GlassmakingGlass, including glassware and windows LeatherworkingLeather goods, including leather armor PotteryCeramic goods ShipbuildingShips and boats StonemasonryStone goods and structures TailoringClothing WeavingTextiles, baskets, and rugs WoodworkingWooden goods and structures * Requires Alchemical Crafting to Craft.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Specialty Crafting",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=846",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Streetwise"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You know about life on the streets and feel the pulse of your local settlement. You can use your Society modifier instead of your Diplomacy modifier to Gather Information. In any settlement you frequent regularly, you can use the Recall Knowledge action with Society to know the same sorts of information that you could discover with Diplomacy to Gather Information. The DC is usually significantly higher, but you know the information without spending time gathering it. If you fail to recall the information, you can still subsequently attempt to Gather Information normally.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-society",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Streetwise",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=851",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Terrain Expertise"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your experience in navigating a certain type of terrain makes you supremely confident while doing so. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Survival checks in one of the following types of terrain, chosen when you select this feat: aquatic, arctic, desert, forest, mountain, plains, sky, swamp, or underground.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-survival",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Terrain Expertise",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8526",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Trance of Celerity"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8526#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your feet move faster, almost out of your conscious control. You gain a +5-foot status bonus to your Speeds for 1 minute. If you become cursebound 2 at any point during this duration, the bonus increases to a +10-foot status bonus. If you become cursebound 3 at any point during this duration, this bonus increases to +15-foot status bonus instead. Finally, if you become cursebound 4 at any point during this duration, this bonus increases to a +20-foot status bonus.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Trance of Celerity",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Cursebound",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Oracle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8526#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8534",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hellbreaker Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "By joining the League, you've taken on the responsibilities of a Hellbreaker. You gain the Additional Lore general feat for both Devil Lore and Hellknight Lore. If you were already trained in one or both of those Lore skills, you also become trained in a Lore skill of your choice. When you roll initiative, you can attempt a Devil Lore, Hellknight Lore, or Society check to Recall Knowledge about one enemy you can see as a free action, if that skill would be applicable. The GM is the final arbiter of whether or not one of those skills would be appropriate to Recall Knowledge about the enemy.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Hellbreaker Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8535",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Devil you Know"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your knowledge of your enemies gives you an advantage against them, granting you a swift reaction to their devilry. If you know you're fighting against any devils or Hellknights at the beginning of an encounter, you can roll the respective Lore skill for your initiative roll. In addition, whenever you successfully Recall Knowledge about a creature using Devil Lore or Hellknight Lore, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your next skill check against that creature before the end of your next turn. If you're a master in Devil Lore or Hellknight Lore, the bonus increases to +2.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-hellbreaker-dedication-expert-in-devil-lore-or-hellknight-lore",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Devil you Know",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8536",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hellbreaker's Resolve"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8536#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You gird yourself in both mind and body for danger, steeling your resolve. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to your level that last for 1 minute. While you have those temporary Hit Points, you gain a +1 status bonus to Will saves.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-hellbreaker-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Hellbreaker's Resolve",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8536#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8537",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "High Alert"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8537#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You're constantly on guard, keeping watch over your allies against fiendish forces—no one can get the jump on your group while you're around. Choose an ally you can see within 30 feet. They gain a +1 circumstance bonus to their AC and Reflex saving throws against devils and creatures allied with the Chelaxian government (as determined by the GM) until the beginning of your next turn. This action gains the visual trait, the auditory trait, or both, depending on how you alert your ally.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-hellbreaker-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "High Alert",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8537#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8538",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Oppurtune Trickster"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8538#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You aren't above using underhanded tactics to gain an advantage, easily routing your opponents when they attack. Attempt a Deception check against the Perception DC of the creature that's the target of the triggering attack. Regardless of the result, the target is temporarily immune to your attempts to use Opportune Trickster for the next 10 minutes. Critical Success The target is off-guard (including against the triggering attack) until the end of your ally's turn. Success The target is off-guard against the triggering attack. Critical Failure You lose your balance in your attempt to assist your ally and fall prone.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-hellbreaker-dedication-trained-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Oppurtune Trickster",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8538#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "reaction"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8539",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Hell's Bane"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your in-depth knowledge of your foes grants you insight into their weaknesses, granting you an advantage when fighting against them. When you critically succeed at a skill check to Recall Knowledge about a devil or Hellknight, you gain a +4 status bonus to damage against that creature for 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-devil-you-know",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Hell's Bane",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=854",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Titan Wrestler"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can attempt to Disarm, Grapple, Reposition, Shove, or Trip creatures up to two sizes larger than you, or up to three sizes larger than you if you’re legendary in Athletics.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Titan Wrestler",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8540",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Rend Armor"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8540#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your enemies' defenses are no match for you as you wrench your weapon to compromise their armor. The creature takes a –2 circumstance penalty to their AC that lasts until they can take 10 minutes to repair their armor. The creature can also Interact to adjust their armor, which removes this penalty for 1 minute.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-hellbreaker-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Rend Armor",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8540#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8541",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Battle Scars"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You've faced enough opponents that your experience is written across your skin, toughening you against your fiendish foes. You gain resistance to bludgeoning and slashing damage from devils and creatures allied with the Chelaxian government (as determined by the GM) equal to half your level.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-hellbreaker-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Battle Scars",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8542",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Defy Hell"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8542#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Your devotion to your cause gives you endless strength and courage to withstand the enemy's attacks. As long as you're in this stance, you gain a +2 status bonus to saves against mental effects and can make Hellbreaker Strikes. Hellbreaker Strike [two-actions] (holy) Make a weapon or unarmed Strike. This counts as two attacks when determining your multiple attack penalty. If your Strike hits, you deal an additional 2d8 spirit damage. At 18th level, this increases to 3d8 spirit damage.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-hellbreaker-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Defy Hell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8542#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8543",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Return to the Pit!"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can send the fiends who have vexed you back to their home plane where they belong. You can cast banishment once per day as a divine innate spell. When you take this feat, you craft a personal symbol of the Hellbreakers League that's anathema to devils. If you wield this symbol in one hand when you spend an extra action while casting banishment on a devil, you don't need to pay the extra cost to give that creature a –2 circumstance penalty to its save.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-hellbreaker-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Return to the Pit!",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=8544",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Thorn in Hell's Side"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your devotion to the ideals of justice, freedom, and revolution allow you to truly punish those who stand in your way. When you critically succeed at a Hellbreaker Strike, the target must succeed at a Fortitude save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher, or become stunned 1 (stunned 2 on a critical failure). This effect has the incapacitation trait.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-defy-hell",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Thorn in Hell's Side",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=858",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Underwater Marauder"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You’ve learned to fight underwater. You are not off-guard while in water, and you don’t take the usual penalties for using a bludgeoning or slashing melee weapon in water.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-athletics",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Underwater Marauder",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=871",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Pathfinder Agent Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your Pathfinder training has broadened your horizons and made you more flexible at various skills, since you never know when you might need an obscure skill to complete your mission. You become trained in one skill of your choice, or expert in a skill of your choice in which you were trained. You also become trained in Pathfinder Lore, or an expert if you were already trained. When using a skill untrained, your proficiency bonus is equal to your level instead of 0. You gain access to wayfinders.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-member-of-the-pathfinder-society",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Pathfinder Agent Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=900",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Student of Perfection Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have learned the martial arts techniques of your House of Perfection. You become trained in your choice of Acrobatics or Athletics and Warfare Lore; if you were already trained, you become an expert instead. You gain the Ki Strike monk class feat, which grants you the ki strike ki spell and a focus pool of 1 Focus Point that you can recover using the Refocus activity as a monk does. Your ki spells from Student of Perfection are occult spells.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-powerful-fist-or-expert-in-unarmed-attacks-member-of-a-house-of-perfection",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Student of Perfection Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=92",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemical Familiar"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have used alchemy to create life, a simple creature formed from alchemical materials, reagents, and a bit of your own blood. You gain a familiar, which has the construct familiar ability; this is permanent, doesn't require the familiar to have the tough familiar ability, and doesn't count against your usual limit of familiar abilities (typically 2). The familiar uses your Intelligence modifier to determine its Perception, Acrobatics, and Stealth modifiers.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemical Familiar",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=923",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Different Worlds"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your separate experiences in different societies have evolved into entirely separate lives. Create a second identity for yourself with a different name, history, and background. This identity must correspond to one of the ancestries whose ancestry feats you can select. You gain the trained proficiency rank in the Lore skill from the second background you chose (but you don’t gain any of the background’s other benefits), and you gain a +4 circumstance bonus to Deception checks when making a statement that would be true of your second identity or when disguising yourself as your second identity.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ability-to-select-ancestry-feats-from-multiple-ancestries",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Different Worlds",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=924",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Reveal Machinations"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=924#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You reveal that you played a minor but recurring role in another humanoid’s life—or at least convince them that’s the case. Attempt a Deception check against the target’s Will DC. On a success, the revelation makes them frightened 2, and on a critical success they are frightened 3. In addition, you gain information about the subject as though you had attempted to Recall Knowledge about them using an appropriate skill and received the same result on your roll. You can’t use this ability against the same humanoid again until 1 day has passed and you’ve also successfully disguised yourself as a different person.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-legendary-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "15",
          "aonprd:name": "Reveal Machinations",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=924#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=925",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Secret Speech"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Choose a secret society (such as the Lacunafex or the Bellflower Network). You’ve learned that society’s secret cant or jargon, enabling you to share hidden messages when signing or speaking with others who’ve also learned it. If an observer succeeds at a Perception check against your Deception DC when you do this, they realize you are passing a message but fail to discern its content, unless they subsequently succeed at a Society check against your Deception DC. On a critical success, they learn not only the message, but also who you’re passing the message to.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-deception",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Secret Speech",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=926",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Silver's Refrain"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You learn the silver’s refrain composition cantrip, which aids you when fighting devils.",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Silver's Refrain",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Bard",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=927",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tweak Appearances"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You spend 1 minute making quick adjustments to someone’s clothing and appearance, causing their words to carry more weight with an audience of your choice. While speaking to that audience, the target gains a +1 item bonus to Diplomacy and Performance checks. If you have master proficiency in Crafting, the bonus increases to +2; if you have legendary proficiency in Crafting, the bonus increases to +3. This bonus lasts until this ability is used on the target again, the situation they were prepared for ends, or they next change their outfit.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-expert-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Tweak Appearances",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-General",
            "aonprd:Trait-Skill",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=928",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Bellflower Dedication"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You dedicate yourself to freeing slaves and escorting them to freedom. You gain a +5-foot status bonus to your Speed. Choose up to six other people to be your “crop.” Members of your crop can use your Speed for overland travel if it’s higher than their own. Members more than 60 feet from you lose all benefits (from this or other Bellflower tiller feats) of being part of your crop, but they regain those benefits immediately when they return. You can add or remove someone from your crop by spending 10 minutes in conversation with them.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-charisma-14-expert-in-stealth-and-survival-member-of-the-bellflower-network",
          "aonprd:level": "6",
          "aonprd:name": "Bellflower Dedication",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Dedication",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=929",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Scarecrow"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You fight fiercely to protect your crop. When you hit a creature that is adjacent to two or more members of your crop with a weapon or unarmed attack, you gain a circumstance bonus to your damage roll equal to the number of weapon damage dice. When you hit a creature who has a member of your crop grabbed, that member can attempt to Escape using a reaction.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bellflower-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Scarecrow",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=93",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Alchemical Assessment"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can identify alchemical items quickly. When using the Crafting skill to Identify Alchemy on an alchemical item you hold, you can do so as a single action, rather than spending 10 minutes.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-trained-in-crafting",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Alchemical Assessment",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=930",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Garden Path"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can guide your crop to move without notice. When you and any of your crop are Avoiding Notice, you can choose one member of your crop to temporarily gain the benefits of the Quiet Allies skill feat until the group is no longer Avoiding Notice. The group rolls two checks instead of one, using the higher die roll. This is a fortune effect.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bellflower-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Garden Path",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=931",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Practiced Guidance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Making one’s way to safety can be harrowing, but you have extensive practice at helping others along that path. When you roll a success to Aid a member of your crop, you get a critical success instead.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bellflower-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "8",
          "aonprd:name": "Practiced Guidance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=932",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tiller's Drive"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your Speed bonus from Bellflower Dedication increases to +10 feet. Members of your crop receive a +5-foot circumstance bonus to Speed.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bellflower-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Tiller's Drive",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=933",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Tiller's Aid"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can use the Aid reaction to help a member of your crop even if you haven’t prepared to do so.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bellflower-dedication",
          "aonprd:level": "10",
          "aonprd:name": "Tiller's Aid",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=934",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Cut the Bonds"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=934#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "Select a magical effect that has made an adjacent member of your crop clumsy, grabbed, paralyzed, restrained, or slowed. Attempt a counteract check using your attack modifier (including your multiple attack penalty) with a melee weapon with which you have expert proficiency. Your counteract level is half your level rounded up. On a success, you free that member from the effect; on a failure, you can’t attempt to use Cut the Bonds on that effect on that crop member until 24 hours have passed.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-bellflower-dedication-expert-in-a-melee-weapon",
          "aonprd:level": "12",
          "aonprd:name": "Cut the Bonds",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Archetype",
            "aonprd:Trait-Attack",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=934#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=95",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Quick Bomber"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=95#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You keep your bombs and bomb-related reagents in easy-to-reach pouches from which you draw without thinking. You Interact to draw a bomb, draw a versatile vial, or use Quick Alchemy to create a bomb, then Strike with the bomb. If you have the ability to create more than one bomb at a time with Quick Alchemy (such as from the double brew class feature), you can Strike with only one of the bombs you create with this action.",
          "aonprd:level": "1",
          "aonprd:name": "Quick Bomber",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=95#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=96",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Poison Resistance"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your affinity for the natural world grants you protection against some of its dangers. You gain poison resistance equal to half your level, and you gain a +1 status bonus to saving throws against poisons.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Poison Resistance",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Druid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=97",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Revivifying Mutagen"
          },
          "aonprd:actionCost": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=97#actionCost",
          "aonprd:description": "You metabolize a mutagen to heal yourself. You regain 1d6 Hit Points for every 2 levels you have, but the mutagen's duration immediately ends.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Revivifying Mutagen",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=97#actionCost",
          "@type": "aonprd:ActionCost",
          "aonprd:actionSymbol": "one-action"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=98",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Smoke Bomb"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You can add a tarry additive to an alchemical bomb to make it emit smoke. When thrown, in addition to its normal effects, the bomb creates a cloud of smoke in a 10-foot burst. You choose which corner of the target's space (or the space in which the bomb lands) the cloud is centered on. Creatures within that area have the concealed condition, and all other creatures are concealed to them. The smoke lasts for 1 minute or until dissipated by a strong wind.",
          "aonprd:level": "2",
          "aonprd:name": "Smoke Bomb",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Additive",
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/Feats.aspx?ID=99",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Calculated Splash"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You have calculated all the angles to maximize a bomb’s splash. When you throw an alchemical bomb with the splash trait, you can cause the bomb to deal splash damage equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 0) instead of the normal amount.",
          "aonprd:level": "4",
          "aonprd:name": "Calculated Splash",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-common",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Alchemist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=287",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Apocalypse Rider"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "In the darkest hour of the night, a fearsome and terrible steed arrives as a gift from a powerful daemonic patron. You gain an apocalypse mount, which is loyal and follows your commands as long as you work to spread death and destruction. Your apocalypse mount can be any mature animal companion with the mount special ability, though it is obviously touched by daemonic forces. Choose whether your apocalypse mount is a nimble or savage animal companion. During an encounter, even if you don’t use the Command an Animal action, your apocalypse mount can still use 1 action on your turn to Stride or Strike. You also gain the anathema “You forswear any plans to cheat death or build something that will last beyond your own death.” If you break this anathema, you lose access to abilities granted by this archetype until you atone or make amends.",
          "aonprd:name": "Apocalypse Rider",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Death",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Void"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=288",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Archfiend"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Driven by your Calling, you've begun to make plans for your own personal realm from whence you're destined to rule over an army of fiends. Name your realm and describe its eventual appearance. Whether it contains raging hellfire, ponds of caustic acid, or banks of poisonous fog, your realm should be marked by distinctive terrain. Select one of the following damage types associated with your realm's environmental dangers: acid, cold, electricity, fire, or poison. This is your realm's damage type. You gain resistance to the selected damage type equal to half your level. If you already have resistance to this damage type, increase your resistance by 5. The certainty of your will is such that you can temporarily bring forth a portion of your realm into this world. You gain the Manifest Realm ability. Other feats allow you to further manipulate your manifested realm. Manifest Realm [two-actions] (concentrate, divine, manipulate) Frequency once per hour; Effect You corrupt the surrounding area into a manifestation of your realm in a 20-foot-radius burst centered on you. Your manifested realm counts as difficult terrain for your enemies, and your enemies take a –1 penalty to Fortitude saving throws while in your manifested realm. You can Sustain your manifested realm once per round on subsequent rounds, and if you do not, the radius of your manifested realm is reduced by 5 feet. Your realm remains manifested for a maximum of 1 minute, and you can Dismiss your manifested realm. If your manifested realm's radius is ever reduced to 0 feet or if you move beyond 100 feet from the borders of your manifested realm, your manifested realm is automatically Dismissed.",
          "aonprd:name": "Archfiend",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Teleportation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=289",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Ascended Celestial"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your Calling has driven you to perform mortal deeds that will result in your ascension to the ranks of celestials. You’re headstrong and determined and hardly waver in your resolve; once per hour, you can roll twice and use the higher result on a Will saving throw. If you ever become confused, rather than attack wildly, you become stubbornly immobile, wasting all your actions until the condition ends. Additionally, you emanate a nimbus of light. You shed bright light in a 30-foot radius (and dim light to the next 30 feet). You can suppress or reestablish this light as a single action that has the concentrate trait. As long as your nimbus is active, all allies in the area of your nimbus gain a +1 status bonus to saves against fear. You gain the Bless Ally action. Bless Ally [one-action] (concentrate, divine, fortune, mythic) Frequency once per 10 minutes; Requirements Your nimbus is active; Target a willing ally within the bright light of your nimbus; Effect Your radiance grants an ally some of your celestial grace. That ally can roll twice and use the higher result for the next Will save they attempt before the beginning of your next turn.",
          "aonprd:name": "Ascended Celestial",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Divine",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exploration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=290",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Beast Lord"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your Calling has united your destiny with a companion, harnessing a connection between you that links your minds, hearts, and souls. Choose a companion that qualified you for this feat as your united companion. Your united companion increases its Intelligence modifier to +0 or by 1 if its Intelligence modifier is greater than +0. It gains the ability to understand a language that you know and can communicate with you, but only you can understand your companion when it speaks, as it uses chirps, grunts, or other noises to convey its meaning. If you or your united companion are conscious and within 30 feet of each other and either must attempt a saving throw against a mental effect, both you and your united companion attempt the saving throw. The target of the effect uses the best result; this also applies if both you and your united companion must attempt a saving throw against the same effect.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-a-mature-animal-companion-or-an-advanced-construct-companion",
          "aonprd:name": "Beast Lord",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=291",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Broken Chain"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your Calling was sparked by your outrage at tyrants, after having witnessed a brutal act of oppression that you could no longer abide. You may spend a Mythic Point when you attempt an Escape or Force Open check to do so at mythic proficiency. Additionally, you gain the Ultimatum of Liberation action (see below), but you also gain the anathema, “You must not use Ultimatum of Liberation on a creature you don’t believe to be oppressing others or who has conceded their power”. If you break this anathema, you lose access to abilities granted by this archetype until you atone or make amends. Your GM has final say about what constitutes oppression, which can be a difficult and sometimes nebulous concept. In general, oppression is the cruel and unjust use of authority or power. Some examples include performing acts of violence against those without power, removing an individual’s agency through mind control magic, and engaging in organized mistreatment or exploitation of others. When the members of a royal guard assault a beggar just to get him off the street, that is oppression. When a tax collector levies higher charges against the less fortunate because it’s the law, they are participating in a system of oppression. Ultimatum of Liberation [one-action] (auditory, linguistic, mental, mythic) Frequency once per day; Effect You proclaim an ultimatum against a creature you believe is oppressing others and all who follow their orders. All other creatures (including you) who hear your ultimatum, or learn about it later on, are emboldened by your words for 1 day, and gain a +2 status bonus to their Will saving throws against effects produced by the oppressing creature and their allies, which increases to +3 if they are within 30 feet of you. Additionally, the first time each day that creature and each of its allies comes within 30 feet of you, they must succeed on a Will save against your class DC or spell DC (whichever is higher) or become frightened 1 (frightened 2 on a critical failure). This second effect has the emotion, fear, and mental traits. The oppressing creature may end all the effects as a free action by truthfully agreeing to permanently end their oppression. Otherwise, your Ultimatum of Liberation has no duration, though you can have only one Ultimatum of Liberation active at a time. If you pronounce a second Ultimatum of Liberation, the effects of the first one end.",
          "aonprd:name": "Broken Chain",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Death",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Incapacitation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sonic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=292",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Eternal Legend"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "As your renown as a fighter grows, your Calling comes to fruition. Almost nothing can keep you down. During your daily preparations, choose clumsy, drained, or enfeebled. For the remainder of the day, when you roll a success against an effect that would impose that condition on you, you get a critical success instead. In addition, anytime you gain the chosen condition, reduce its value by 1. You can change the chosen condition with a single action that has the concentrate trait.",
          "aonprd:name": "Eternal Legend",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fear",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=293",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Godling"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your Calling allows you to begin walking the path to true deific ascension, inspiring followers as your divine seed grows. Your first follower is your hierophant—the high priest of your new faith—whom you rely on to spread your word and provide an anchoring mortal presence as your perspectives are increasingly pulled toward the cosmic. When you gain this feat, choose one willing ally to be your hierophant. If your hierophant is not trained in spell attack modifier and spell DC, they become trained for as long as they are your designated hierophant. If your hierophant dies or chooses to part ways with you, you can designate a new hierophant by communing with the chosen ally for a period of 24 hours. Your Calling allows you to seize the divine magic typically restricted to deities. Choose one domain to claim (see list of domains here). You learn the initial domain spell for this domain. You gain a pool of Focus Points with 1 Focus Point and you can Refocus by taking 10 minutes to replenish your divine energy from the planes beyond. You gain expert proficiency in spell modifier and spell DC, and your spellcasting ability for these spells is your choice of Wisdom or Charisma, decided when you gain this feat. Your hierophant also gains the Cast a Spell activity and can cast the domain spell you learned with Godling Dedication. When they Cast the Spell in this way, your Focus Point is expended as the cost of the spell. Your hierophant uses their own spellcasting proficiency in spell modifier and spell DC when casting a spell in this way, and they use their own Wisdom or Charisma modifier (matching your choice). If your hierophant has mythic power, they can spend a Mythic Point to cast any divine spell they gain by being your hierophant at mythic proficiency.",
          "aonprd:name": "Godling",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Aura",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sanctified"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=294",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Prophesied Monarch"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Your Calling has culminated in a destiny of rulership, and you’re able to forge a mythic bond with noble knights whose destinies become intertwined with your own. Designate up to five allies as your knights; as long as you’re conscious, your knights’ doomed condition can’t rise above 3, and if they’re ever in mortal peril (such as being unconscious with the dying condition or imprisoned in an enemy fortress), you instantly receive a vision revealing their location and condition. In addition, you gain the Royal Grace exploration activity. Royal Grace (concentrate, exploration, linguistic, mental) You spend 10 minutes conferring with one of your knights who has the doomed condition. By discussing plans for your future kingdom with them and describing the benefits of your rule, you can attempt to soothe their spirits. Attempt a Diplomacy or Society check against a hard DC of your knight's level. Regardless of the result, that knight gains the benefits of the Refocus activity (if they have a focus pool) but is temporarily immune to Royal Grace for 24 hours. Critical Success The knight’s doomed condition is reduced by 2 (minimum 0). Success The knight’s doomed condition is reduced by 1 (minimum 0). Failure The knight’s doomed condition isn’t reduced.",
          "aonprd:name": "Prophesied Monarch",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Death",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Incapacitation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Light",
            "aonprd:Trait-Linguistic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spirit",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=295",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Wildspell"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "You gain the ability to tap into a powerful well of magic. You gain the spellsurge focus spell. This spell is of your main casting tradition.",
          "aonprd:hasPrerequisite": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/feat-ability-to-cast-spells-from-spell-slots",
          "aonprd:name": "Wildspell",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-uncommon",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Light",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Sonic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Stance",
            "aonprd:Trait-Uncommon",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=338",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Avenging Runelord"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The call of a long dead runelord has infected your soul and transformed your fate. Choose one of the following sins: envy, gluttony, greed, sloth, or wrath. You become trained in Arcana. If you are already trained in Arcana, you become trained in the skill of your choice. At 14th level, you gain expert proficiency in Arcana. At 16th level, if you gain master proficiency in Arcana. You have familiarity with common weapons in the polearm and spear weapon groups—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as common weapons. When your proficiency for simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons. You learn the Thassilonian language. You gain the ability to cast an arcane spell as an innate spell. This spell must be chosen from the following list: darkvision, mystic armor, runic body, runic weapon, see the unseen, sending, or truesight; alternatively, you can choose any spell of 6th rank or lower from the sin spells listed for your chosen sin (see School of Thassilonian Rune Magic). You can cast this spell as an arcane innate spell once per day. The spell is automatically heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up. Use mythic proficiency to determine any attack rolls or spell DCs. Your obsession with revenge allows you to reflexively lash out at those who harm you with blasts of arcane magic. You gain the Runelord's Response reaction. Runelord's Response [reaction] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 73 Trigger A creature deals damage to you with a spellYou gain a measure of revenge immediately by twisting the magic used by the triggering creature. Spend a Mythic Point. The triggering creature takes 6d8 force damage, with a basic Will saving throw against either your class DC or spell DC using mythic proficiency, whichever is higher. At 14th level, and every 2 levels thereafter, this damage increases by 1d8.",
          "aonprd:name": "Avenging Runelord",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Arcane",
            "aonprd:Trait-Complex",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Incapacitation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=339",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Heroic Scion"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "Destiny calls, and the soul of a dead hero reincarnates to take up the fight! Either an old enemy resumes their efforts to affect chaos and violence, or a new threat arises and you feel compelled to stand against it. You’ve stood against evil before, and the time is nigh for you to do so once again. When you select this mythic destiny, work with your GM to determine the best choice for which previous PC or NPC serves as the source of your reincarnation. For the Revenge of the Runelords Adventure Path in particular, any PC who played a role in the Rise of the Runelords, Shattered Star, or Return of the Runelords Adventure Paths makes for a perfect fit—as would any allied NPC who, in your previous campaign, perished before the end. A heroic scion comes into the world when a nemesis from their old adventures returns. In the case of this campaign, the heroic scion’s nemesis are the ancient runelords of Thassilon. In other campaigns, this nemesis can be a specific individual, a coterie of rivals, or an organization you’re destined to oppose. You instinctively know when your nemesis is active in the world. This knowledge may begin as nightmares or a feeling of inevitable conflict but grows stronger and more specific as you contemplate further. You also know when this entity or group has been fully defeated and ceases to operate at all. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to Seek or Sense Motive whenever an ally or servant of your nemesis attempts to Lie to you, escape your notice, or Impersonate someone else. Fate has deemed you incredibly hard to kill. You reduce the DC of recovery checks by 1. Choose one skill that’s not a Lore skill, based on the themes of your reincarnated heroic source. Your GM can help you determine a list of appropriate skills to choose from. When you employ an action using that skill, you may spend a Mythic Point to attempt the associated check at mythic proficiency. Finally, you gain the Additional Lore feat for a special Lore skill subcategory—Incarnation Lore. This Lore skill allows you to become aware of or recall your past exploits. When you increase your proficiency in Incarnation Lore, you remember more about your previous adventures. Certain heroic scion feats require you to attempt an Incarnation Lore check, such as when you attempt the following activity granted you by this feat. Flash of Memory [free-action] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 77Spend a Mythic Point and attempt an Incarnation Lore check at mythic proficiency to Recall Knowledge in place of making any other Lore check (other than Incarnation Lore).",
          "aonprd:name": "Heroic Scion",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Auditory",
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Emotion",
            "aonprd:Trait-Exploration",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Fortune",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mental",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare",
            "aonprd:Trait-Spellshape",
            "aonprd:Trait-Visual"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=340",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Timewracked"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "The current of time shifts subtly in your field of view. You have learned to tread these temporal eddies, moving forward and pushing backward in small strokes—sometimes even gaining the ability to move your allies and enemies through time as you choose. Whether or not you’ll ever be fully restored to your proper timeline, you can’t predict—but until then you continue to manipulate your estrangement from time to move unseen, defy your opponents in combat, and occupy future or past versions of yourself to escape distress. With practice you could gain the ability to rehearse a speech at the same tie you deliver it or attack distant foes without spending the time to move between them. Eventually, you might gain the power to vanish from existence altogether while you hop forward and backward in time or even become immortal. Your Speed increases by 5 feet for each mode of movement available to you. You can spend a Mythic Point to roll any check made to determine your initiative at mythic proficiency. If your initiative roll result is tied with an opponent’s initiative roll, you can choose to go first. In addition, you gain the following reaction. Sidestep Through Time [reaction] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 81 Trigger You are about to attempt a Reflex saving throw against an area effectYou slip through time to avoid a dangerous outcome. Teleport up to 10 feet in any direction. If this would take you outside of the area’s effect, you don’t need to attempt the Reflex save against it. You are then off-guard for 1 round.",
          "aonprd:name": "Timewracked",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Concentrate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Flourish",
            "aonprd:Trait-Healing",
            "aonprd:Trait-Incapacitation",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Occult",
            "aonprd:Trait-Prediction",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://squashage.dev/instance/aonprd/MythicDestinies.aspx?ID=341",
          "@type": "aonprd:Feat",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@language": "en",
            "@value": "Warshard Warrior"
          },
          "aonprd:description": "When you became infused with a shard of the god of war, you knew in your gut that your destiny would be one for the ages—yet you may not, at first, know the exact way such a destiny would play out. If you still carry the warshard that empowered you, you might carry it as a token or wear it as jewelry—if indeed it’s not simply embedded into your body. Regardless, the warshard itself no longer has any intrinsic power of its own, and even if you toss the warshard aside, its gifts do not leave you, nor can another benefit from them. If you throw the warshard away or lose it, your destiny remains unaltered; you have, in effect, become the warshard itself. This power manifests through a weapon you wield. When you make your daily preparations, choose one weapon in your possession in which you have at least expert proficiency. That weapon becomes your warshard weapon until you choose a different weapon in your possession during another of your daily preparations. You can choose a mundane nonmagical weapon, a weapon with magical runes, one made of an unusual material, or even a specific magic weapon such as a storm flash or a bloodletting kukri, but not an intelligent weapon or an artifact like the bastard sword Serithtial or one of the seven swords of sin. While you don’t lose access to your warshard warrior feats if your warshard weapon is taken from you or destroyed, note that several of this destiny’s feats require you to be wielding your warshard weapon. You can etch or remove runes from a warshard weapon normally. You can have only one warshard weapon at a time. Your gain the Mythic Strike feat, but you can only use it with your warshard weapon. Whenever you make a Strike with your warshard weapon at mythic proficiency, you double the amount of additional damage you deal with the weapon specialization class feature. When you make Crafting checks to Repair your warshard weapon, your treat your proficiency rank in Crafting as legendary for determining how many Hit Points you restore to the item; in addition, if your Crafting result is a critical failure, you get a failure instead. You also gain the following action. Call Warshard Weapon [one-action] Source Pathfinder Adventure Path #219: Lord of the Trinity Star pg. 85 Requirements You are not holding your warshard weapon, and you have a hand or hands free to be able to wield your warshard weapon;Your warshard weapon teleports into your hand, as long as you and your warshard weapon are on the same planet. At 15th level, you need only be on the same plane as your warshard weapon to call it, and at 18th level, you can call your warshard weapon across any distance. If your warshard weapon is in the possession of a mythic creature that’s higher level than you or placed in an area where teleportation magic doesn’t function, attempt a DC 16 flat check. On a success, your warshard weapon still teleports to your hand.",
          "aonprd:name": "Warshard Warrior",
          "aonprd:rarity": "aonprd:Rarity-rare",
          "aonprd:trait": [
            "aonprd:Trait-Attack",
            "aonprd:Trait-Destiny",
            "aonprd:Trait-Magical",
            "aonprd:Trait-Manipulate",
            "aonprd:Trait-Mythic",
            "aonprd:Trait-Press",
            "aonprd:Trait-Rare"
          ]
        },
